ource NVIDIA Corporation 2026-07-07; from nvblog:hugging-face-lerobot-models-frameworks-open-robotics 2026-07-07] NVIDIA plans to integrate Cosmos 3 into Hugging Face’s LeRobot library soon.\\n    Quote: with NVIDIA Cosmos 3 , a frontier model for physical AI, planned soon.\",\n   \"- e166 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source Palantir ; from gnews:1a116fecd5de1747cc5a06b1 2026-07-07] Palantir announced it is combining its intelligence engine with Nvidia’s Nemotron models to deliver mission-focused AI for U.S. government agencies and major infrastructure operators.\\n    Quote: Earlier this week, Palantir announced that it is combining its new intelligence engine and Nvidia's Nemotron open AI models to deliver mission-focused AI for government agencies and major infrastructure operators in the U.S.\",\n   \"- e167 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com, recounting a CNBC interview; original source Alex Karp, CEO of Palantir 2026-07-01; from gnews:1a116fecd5de1747cc5a06b1 2026-07-07] Palantir CEO Alex Karp said Anthropic and OpenAI provide limited protection for clients’ intellectual property.\\n    Quote: In a CNBC interview, Karp said that the frontier AI model developers, Anthropic and OpenAI, have limited protections for their clients' intellectual property.\",\n   \"- e169 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source Amazon and Alphabet ; from gnews:ce5daf57bdca5da657e5f677 2026-07-07] Amazon and Alphabet are extending access to their in-house processors, increasing competition for NVIDIA’s AI computing products.\\n    Quote: The move comes as the company faces rising competition from specialized AI chips from cloud providers, including Amazon and Alphabet, which are extending access to in-house processors.\",\n   \"- e174 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source SpaceX ; from gnews:9026c944c63575a080ce7ba9 2026-07-07] SpaceX plans to use Nvidia as an initial hardware supplier for its orbital data centers; the item gives no date or amount.\\n    Quote: Nvidia is set to serve as an initial supplier of hardware for SpaceX's orbital data centers.\",\n   \"- e175 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source SpaceX ; from gnews:9026c944c63575a080ce7ba9 2026-07-07] SpaceX plans for its first orbital data-center satellites, called AI1, to use Nvidia chips; the item gives no date or amount.\\n    Quote: SpaceX's first version of the satellites it plans to use as data centers in space is called AI1 and will use Nvidia chips.\",\n   \"- e182 [fact; 24/7 Wall St.; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] NVIDIA Data Center revenue was $75.246 billion in Q1 FY2027, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue reached $75.246 billion (+92% YoY) in Q1 FY27, and CEO Jensen Huang described “the largest infrastructure expansion in human history”.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e116; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e183 [party_statement; 24/7 Wall St.; original source Lisa Su, AMD CEO ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] AMD CEO Lisa Su said customer engagement for MI450 Series and Helios is strengthening, with leading-customer forecasts above AMD’s initial expectations.\\n    Quote: CEO Lisa Su has said “customer engagement around MI450 Series and Helios is strengthening, with leading customer forecasts exceeding our initial expectations.”\",\n   \"- e184 [fact; 24/7 Wall St.; original source Broadcom ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] Broadcom reported Q2 AI semiconductor revenue of $10.8 billion, up 143% year over year, and guided Q3 revenue to $16.0 billion.\\n    Quote: Q2 AI semiconductor revenue was $10.8 billion, +143% YoY, with Q3 guided to $16.0 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e109; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e185 [third_party_view; 24/7 Wall St.; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] Bloomberg Intelligence forecasts a 27% compound annual growth rate for the custom ASIC market through 2033.\\n    Quote: Bloomberg Intelligence forecasts 27% CAGR for the custom ASIC market through 2033.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e108; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e186 [fact; 24/7 Wall St.; original source Google ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] Google Cloud revenue rose 63%, its backlog nearly doubled to more than $460 billion, and Google guided 2026 capital expenditures to $190 billion.\\n    Quote: Google Cloud revenue rose 63% with backlog nearly doubling to over $460 billion, and 2026 capex is guided up tp $190 billion.\",\n   \"- e188 [party_statement; NVIDIA; original source id Software and Bethesda Softworks ; from gnews:2f1cb54b7a3da28d093523b6 2026-07-07] NVIDIA said DOOM: The Dark Ages | Revelations would launch on July 7, 2026, with DLSS Multi Frame Generation, Ray Reconstruction and path tracing support.\\n    Quote: Later today, the DOOM: The Dark Ages | Revelations expansion launches with support for DLSS Multi Frame Generation and Ray Reconstruction, and path tracing.\",\n   \"- e189 [party_statement; NVIDIA; original source Ubisoft ; from gnews:2f1cb54b7a3da28d093523b6 2026-07-07] NVIDIA said Assassin’s Creed Black Flag Resynced would launch on July 9, 2026, with DLSS Multi Frame Generation, Super Resolution and ray tracing support.\\n    Quote: On Thursday, Assassin’s Creed Black Flag Resynced launches with DLSS Multi Frame Generation and Super Resolution, and ray tracing.\",\n   \"- e190 [fact; NVIDIA; original source MADFINGER Games ; from gnews:2f1cb54b7a3da28d093523b6 2026-07-07] NVIDIA said Gray Zone Warfare had added its latest DLSS Dynamic Multi Frame Generation and Super Resolution models for GeForce RTX GPUs.\\n    Quote: Now, the latest DLSS Dynamic Multi Frame Generation and Super Resolution models have been added to further enhance frame rates and image quality on GeForce RTX GPUs.\",\n   \"- e191 [rumour; mlq.ai; original source Three people with knowledge of the matter, as cited by Reuters 2026-07-06; from gnews:9f430c6ce2e8d551fe1f063a 2026-07-07] DeepSeek is developing a custom AI inference chip, according to three people cited by Reuters.\\n    Quote: DeepSeek, the Hangzhou-based AI startup behind some of China's most advanced large language models, is developing its own custom AI chip, Reuters reported on Monday, citing three people with knowledge of the matter [1] . The chip is designed for inference — the phase where trained models generate responses to user queries — rather than for training new models.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e195; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e192 [fact; mlq.ai; original source The U.S. government ; from gnews:9f430c6ce2e8d551fe1f063a 2026-07-07] U.S. export controls bar Chinese companies from accessing the most advanced overseas foundries and restrict shipments of high-bandwidth memory.\\n    Quote: U.S. export controls that bar access to the most advanced overseas foundries and restrict shipments of high-bandwidth memory — a component critical to inference chip performance [2].\",\n   \"- e193 [third_party_view; mlq.ai; original source Richard Windey ; from gnews:9f430c6ce2e8d551fe1f063a 2026-07-07] Analyst Richard Windey said U.S. export rules have effectively zeroed out Nvidia's China revenue and limit DeepSeek's ability to manufacture or sell advanced silicon outside China.\\n    Quote: Analyst Richard Windey highlighted the constraint: the same export rules that have effectively zeroed out Nvidia's China revenue also limit DeepSeek's ability to manufacture or sell advanced silicon outside China [3].\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e122, e198; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e194 [third_party_view; mlq.ai; original source Industry surveys ; from gnews:9f430c6ce2e8d551fe1f063a 2026-07-07] Industry surveys indicate Chinese firms plan to allocate 46% of their AI-accelerator budgets to domestic suppliers within 12 months, versus about 30% currently.\\n    Quote: Industry surveys indicate Chinese firms plan to shift 46% of their AI-accelerator budgets to domestic suppliers within 12 months, up from roughly 30% today [5].\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e157; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e195 [rumour; idnfinancials.com; original source Three unnamed sources familiar with DeepSeek's plans, cited by Reuters ; from gnews:2957e5c79a365952140c8cce 2026-07-07] Unnamed sources cited by Reuters said DeepSeek is developing chips specifically for AI inference.\\n    Quote: According to Reuters , citing three sources familiar with the plans, DeepSeek's chips are being designed specifically for inference, the stage where trained AI models generate responses for users.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e191; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e196 [rumour; idnfinancials.com; original source Unnamed Reuters sources ; from gnews:2957e5c79a365952140c8cce 2026-07-07] Unnamed Reuters sources said DeepSeek's early-stage chip project has involved discussions over the past year with chip design firms, foundries and memory suppliers.\\n    Quote: According to Reuters sources, DeepSeek's chip development project remains at an early stage. Over the past year, the company has been communicating with chip design firms, foundries and memory suppliers to support the development of the semiconductors.\",\n   \"- e197 [rumour; idnfinancials.com; original source idnfinancials.com ; from gnews:2957e5c79a365952140c8cce 2026-07-07] DeepSeek increased recruitment of chip design engineers in recent months, without publicly posting the openings on general recruitment platforms.\\n    Quote: DeepSeek has also increased recruitment of chip design engineers in recent months. The hiring process has been conducted discreetly, without publicly posting job openings on general recruitment platforms.\",\n   \"- e198 [third_party_view; Richard Windsor, Radio Free Mobile; original source Richard Windsor, Radio Free Mobile ; from gnews:2957e5c79a365952140c8cce 2026-07-07] Analyst Richard Windsor said Nvidia's position in China is effectively zero and will remain so, and that DeepSeek is unlikely to sell chips outside China without access to advanced manufacturing technology; he said DeepSeek's development would not affect Nvidia.\\n    Quote: \\\"Nvidia's position in China is effectively at zero and will remain that way. DeepSeek has almost no chance of selling chips outside China unless it gains access to advanced manufacturing technology,\\\" said analyst Richard Windsor of Radio Free Mobile, adding that the development would not affect the chipmaker.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e193; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e199 [third_party_view; idnfinancials.com; original source idnfinancials.com ; from gnews:2957e5c79a365952140c8cce 2026-07-07] Huawei now controls around half of China's AI chip market, which is valued at approximately US$50 billion.\\n    Quote: Huawei has expanded its domestic market share and now controls around half of China's AI chip market, which is valued at approximately US$50 billion.\",\n   \"- e102 [fact; TradingView; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reported total revenue of $81.62 billion in fiscal 2027 Q1, up 85% year over year; non-GAAP EPS was $1.87, up 140%.\\n    Quote: First-quarter fiscal 2027 revenues climbed 85% year over year to $81.62 billion, while non-GAAP earnings per share jumped 140% to $1.87.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e225; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e105 [fact; Danielle Liverance; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reported revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year, and data-center revenue of $75.2 billion, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Revenue rose 85% year over year to $81.6 billion, with data center up 92% to $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e89, e116, e226; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e159 [third_party_view; businesstimes.com.sg, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence’s survey; original source Bloomberg Intelligence 2026-07-07; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] Bloomberg Intelligence’s survey expects Nvidia’s market share in China to shrink as H20 chips become harder to find and local suppliers take over; it says Beijing has urged Chinese technology firms not to use H20 chips.\\n    Quote: While Nvidia’s products remain popular, the Santa Clara-based firm’s market share is expected to shrink as its H20 chips, which Beijing has urged its tech firms not to use , become harder to find and local firms take over, according to the survey.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e220; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e161 [third_party_view; businesstimes.com.sg, reporting Bloomberg News; original source Bloomberg News ; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] Bloomberg News reported that domestic companies will supply at least 80% of China’s core technologies, including chips.\\n    Quote: At least 80 per cent of core technologies, such as chips, will be supplied by domestic companies, Bloomberg News reported.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e221; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e162 [third_party_view; businesstimes.com.sg, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence’s report; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] Bloomberg Intelligence’s report says a global memory-chip shortage is likely to cap growth at Chinese AI firms such as SMIC, while ChangXin Memory Technologies is positioned to benefit.\\n    Quote: But a global memory chip shortage is likely to cap the growth of Chinese AI firms like Semiconductor Manufacturing International Corporation, with ChangXin Memory Technologies poised to reap the benefits.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e222; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e200 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source LangChain ; from nvblog:nemotron-langchain-agents-open-stack 2026-07-08] LangChain tuned its Deep Agents harness for NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Ultra, making the tuned harness available for enterprises to use.\\n    Quote: By tuning its Deep Agents harness specifically for NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Ultra, it allows for high-performing agents that complete more tasks, run faster and give enterprises a fully open stack they can customize, own and run anywhere.\",\n   \"- e201 [party_statement; NVIDIA Corporation; original source Abridge, Amdocs, Box and EY ; from nvblog:nemotron-langchain-agents-open-stack 2026-07-08] Abridge, Amdocs and Box are embedding specialized agents into their platforms, while EY is expanding its NVIDIA implementation capabilities around NemoClaw blueprints for LangChain Deep Agents.\\n    Quote: Abridge, Amdocs and Box are embedding specialized agents directly into their platforms and global systems integrator EY is expanding its NVIDIA implementation capabilities around NVIDIA NemoClaw blueprints for LangChain Deep Agents, helping clients customize, evaluate and govern specialized agents across high-value workflows.\",\n   \"- e206 [fact; fool.com (John Bromels); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:79cc3f345545cdd3d37c0472 2026-07-08] Nvidia reported that revenue increased 74.6% in its most recent quarter.\\n    Quote: In the most recent quarter alone, Nvidia increased its revenue by 74.6%\",\n   \"- e210 [fact; Futuriom, relaying Bloomberg; original source Meta ; from gnews:cb05b9f49943ef0ba412cf36 2026-07-08] Bloomberg reported that Meta is setting up a cloud-based business to sell AI compute and models.\\n    Quote: On July 1, the same day NVIDIA announced its new revenue-sharing model, Bloomberg reported that Meta is setting up a cloud-based business selling AI compute and models.\",\n   \"- e214 [fact; CNBC; original source SambaNova 2026-07-08; from gnews:6b89157155648b9ec317d209 2026-07-08] SambaNova raised $1 billion in financing, led by General Atlantic with Seligman Ventures, T. Rowe Price and Capital Group participating; the round valued it at $11 billion.\\n    Quote: An AI chip startup has raised $1 billion in financing as investors continue to pour money into companies looking to challenge Nvidia .\",\n   \"- e215 [fact; CNBC; original source JPMorgan Chase 2026-07-08; from gnews:6b89157155648b9ec317d209 2026-07-08] JPMorgan Chase said it would deploy SambaNova systems for on-prem inference in its enterprise AI workloads.\\n    Quote: On Wednesday, JPMorgan Chase said it would deploy SambaNova's systems for \\\"on-prem inference in our demanding enterprise AI workloads.\\\"\",\n   \"- e216 [party_statement; SambaNova co-founder and CEO Rodrigo Liang, quoted by CNBC; original source Rodrigo Liang ; from gnews:6b89157155648b9ec317d209 2026-07-08] SambaNova CEO Rodrigo Liang said the new capital would let the company accelerate deployments of racks customers want; he gave no deployment amount or date.\\n    Quote: \\\"We're scaling the business really, really fast, and so the capital allows us to really accelerate the deployments of the racks that customers really want,\\\" he said.\",\n   \"- e217 [third_party_view; tradingview.com; original source Bloomberg-tracked analysts ; from gnews:a09988fd9c5c1a739a14f873 2026-07-08] Bloomberg-tracked analysts project NVIDIA FY2027 profit of $228 billion and sales of $393 billion, up 90% and 82%, respectively; the profit estimate rose 13% over the prior three months.\\n    Quote: company is projected to generate $228 billion in profit on $393 billion in sales in fiscal 2027, which ends Jan. 31, representing expected growth of 90% and 82%, respectively, while its profit estimate has risen 13% over the past three months.\",\n   \"- e218 [third_party_view; tradingview.com; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:a09988fd9c5c1a739a14f873 2026-07-08] Bloomberg Intelligence data cited in the source puts NVIDIA's server GPU market share at 97% at the end of 2025, up from 95% at the end of 2024.\\n    Quote: The company is projected to generate $228 billion in profit on $393 billion in sales in fiscal 2027, which ends Jan. 31, representing expected growth of 90% and 82%, respectively, while its profit estimate has risen 13% over the past three months.\",\n   \"- e219 [third_party_view; Bloomberg, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence’s survey; original source Bloomberg Intelligence survey respondents 2026-07-07; from gnews:f3ba15f5e14b15ee61d7fddc 2026-07-08] Chinese executives surveyed by Bloomberg Intelligence said they plan to allocate 46% of their AI-accelerator budgets to domestic products over the next 12 months, up from 30% currently.\\n    Quote: Executives in the country say they’ll allocate 46% of their budget for artificial intelligence accelerators to domestic products over the next 12 months, up from 30% today, according to a Bloomberg Intelligence survey released on Tuesday.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e157; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e220 [third_party_view; Bloomberg, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence’s survey; original source Bloomberg Intelligence 2026-07-07; from gnews:f3ba15f5e14b15ee61d7fddc 2026-07-08] Bloomberg Intelligence survey findings indicate Nvidia’s China market share is expected to shrink as H20 chips become harder to find and domestic suppliers gain ground.\\n    Quote: While Nvidia’s products remain popular, the Santa Clara-based firm’s market share is expected to shrink as its H20 chips, which Beijing has urged its tech firms not to use, become harder to find and local firms take over, according to the survey.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e159; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e221 [third_party_view; Bloomberg, citing Bloomberg News; original source China’s government-led initiative for the data-center buildout; Bloomberg News for the report that at least 80% of core technologies will be supplied domestically ; from gnews:f3ba15f5e14b15ee61d7fddc 2026-07-08] China is allocating roughly 2 trillion yuan ($294 billion) over five years to build data centers, with at least 80% of core technologies, including chips, expected to come from domestic companies, according to Bloomberg News.\\n    Quote: China is allocating roughly 2 trillion yuan ($294 billion) to build data centers across the country in the next five years, a government-led initiative to expand use of AI in sectors from healthcare to city management. At least 80% of core technologies, such as chips, will be supplied by domestic companies, Bloomberg News reported.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e161; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e222 [third_party_view; Bloomberg, citing the report; original source Bloomberg Intelligence 2026-07-07; from gnews:f3ba15f5e14b15ee61d7fddc 2026-07-08] Bloomberg’s report says a global memory-chip shortage, particularly for high-bandwidth memory, is likely to cap Chinese AI firms’ growth, while ChangXin Memory Technologies is poised to benefit.\\n    Quote: But a global memory chip shortage is likely to cap the growth of Chinese AI firms like Semiconductor Manufacturing International Corp. with ChangXin Memory Technologies Inc. poised to reap the benefits. The bottlenecks are shifting from sheer computing power to securing supply of high-bandwidth memory chips that support rapid data transfer, according to the report.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e162; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e224 [third_party_view; uk.finance.yahoo.com; original source Bank of America analyst Vivek Arya 2026-07-08; from gnews:266c882eea8c686ee7aafac7 2026-07-08] Bank of America analyst Vivek Arya reported that NVIDIA's sales to hyperscalers rose 115% year-on-year, nearly twice cloud capital-expenditure growth.\\n    Quote: Sales to hyperscalers rose 115% year-on-year, nearly twice cloud capex growth.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e230; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e225 [fact; qz.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:ee0d6792b6bf98069cfe0cc6 2026-07-08] Nvidia reported FY2027 first-quarter total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: For its fiscal first quarter of 2027, Nvidia posted $81.6 billion in total revenue — an 85% increase from a year earlier\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e102; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e226 [fact; qz.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:ee0d6792b6bf98069cfe0cc6 2026-07-08] Nvidia's data center segment reported record revenue of $75.2 billion in FY2027's first quarter.\\n    Quote: while its data center segment set a record at $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e105; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e227 [party_statement; Tom’s Hardware; original source AMD ; from gnews:9fbd0f954b9cc2281da531d1 2026-07-08] AMD claimed its hardware would deliver 3.3x Vera’s performance for the projected output of a 100 kW rack; the item gives no statement date.\\n    Quote: AMD had some things to say about the Phoronix test, firing back with its own metrics of a 3.3x performance gain over Vera for the projected output of a 100 kW rack of its hardware.\",\n   \"- e228 [third_party_view; aibusiness.com, quoting Lian Jye Su; original source Lian Jye Su, analyst at Omdia ; from gnews:21e9182d07508a6690f10419 2026-07-08] Omdia analyst Lian Jye Su said Nvidia is facing challenges from Chinese vendors as humanoid robotics vendors rise in China.\\n    Quote: “The company is facing some challenges from Chinese vendors due to the rise of humanoid robotics vendors in China ,” Su noted.\",\n   \"- e229 [fact; aibusiness.com; original source Qualcomm and Intel ; from gnews:21e9182d07508a6690f10419 2026-07-08] Qualcomm recently entered robotics with Dragonwing IQ10, and Intel with its OpenVINO robotics offerings, challenging Nvidia’s position.\\n    Quote: In addition, Qualcomm, with its Dragonwing IQ10 and Intel, with its OpenVINO robotics offerings, have recently entered the fold to challenge Nvidia’s position.\",\n   \"- e230 [third_party_view; moomoo.com; original source BofA ; from gnews:1b5a3359dd0644861c0fce42 2026-07-08] BofA reported that Nvidia’s hyperscaler sales rose 115% year over year, nearly twice the growth rate of cloud capital expenditures.\\n    Quote: The report also says Nvidia’s hyperscaler sales rose 115% year over year, nearly twice cloud capex growth, suggesting wallet-share gains rather than share loss.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e224; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e231 [third_party_view; moomoo.com; original source BofA ; from gnews:1b5a3359dd0644861c0fce42 2026-07-08] BofA modeled Nvidia retaining roughly 65%–70% or more of AI capital expenditures over time, with the remainder going to ASICs, AMD and other merchant vendors.\\n    Quote: BofA still models Nvidia holding roughly 65% to 70% plus of AI capex over time, with the rest split across ASICs, AMD and other merchant vendors.\",\n   \"- e232 [rumour; Notebookcheck.net; original source Notebookcheck.net, reporting unnamed sources ; from gnews:134fc6bce6a550f5376d6f27 2026-07-08] Notebookcheck reports that Nvidia is reportedly planning to release RTX 50 Super cards in 2027 instead of launching the next-generation RTX 60 series.\\n    Quote: However, the news has been quite disappointing when it comes to the GeForce RTX 60 series cards. Rather than initiate a full-blown next-gen RTX 60 series launch, Nvidia is reportedly planning to release the RTX 50 Super series cards in 2027.\",\n   \"- e233 [rumour; Notebookcheck.net, relaying Moore’s Law Is Dead; original source An unnamed Nvidia source, as relayed by Moore’s Law Is Dead ; from gnews:134fc6bce6a550f5376d6f27 2026-07-08] An unnamed Nvidia source told leaker Moore’s Law Is Dead that the RTX 60 series GPUs are not expected to come out in 2027.\\n    Quote: One of Moore’s Law Is Dead’s Nvidia source told the leaker that they don’t think the RTX 60 series GPUs are coming out in 2027.\",\n   \"- e234 [third_party_view; Notebookcheck.net; original source Notebookcheck.net 2026-07-08; from gnews:134fc6bce6a550f5376d6f27 2026-07-08] Notebookcheck reports that AMD is expected to release RDNA 5 gaming GPUs in 2027, a potential competitive product launch for Nvidia.\\n    Quote: We have been hearing about the release timeline of the next-gen AMD and Nvidia GPUs for a while now. It is now clear that we approaching the end of the current-gen GPU lifecycle, as AMD is expected to release the RDNA 5 gaming GPUs in 2027.\",\n   \"- e235 [fact; Larsen & Toubro Vyoma; original source L&T Vyoma and Fortanix 2026-07-08; from gnews:79b4840d3de4aa77ec0d0229 2026-07-08] L&T Vyoma and Fortanix announced a partnership to offer sovereign AI infrastructure and secure workloads using NVIDIA Confidential Computing; the announcement gave no amount or timeline.\\n    Quote: Through this partnership, L&T Vyoma will provide sovereign AI infrastructure, including data centres, compute and networking, while Fortanix will secure the data and AI workloads in use by leveraging NVIDIA Confidential Computing.\",\n   \"- e27 [party_statement; fool.com analyst Justin Pope; original source Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang ; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang expects $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\\n    Quote: CEO Jensen Huang has laid out expectations for $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e252; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e252 [party_statement; fool.com (Adam Spatacco); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:931ee0196ca609e637235fad 2026-07-09] NVIDIA management cited roughly $1 trillion of revenue visibility for Blackwell and Vera Rubin processors across 2026 and 2027, anchored by multiyear customer commitments.\\n    Quote: Management has also articulated roughly $1 trillion in revenue visibility for its Blackwell and Vera Rubin processors across 2026 and 2027, anchored by multiyear commitments from hyperscalers and large enterprise customers.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e27; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e258 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Bloomberg Intelligence projects Nvidia will hold 70%–75% of the AI chip market through 2030.\\n    Quote: Bloomberg Intelligence projects the company will hold 70% to 75% of the AI chip market through 2030.\",\n   \"- e259 [party_statement; qz.com; original source Andy Jassy, Amazon CEO ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Amazon CEO Andy Jassy said in late 2025 that Trainium2 had no spare capacity left to sell and was a multibillion-dollar business growing at a 150% quarterly clip.\\n    Quote: Amazon CEO Andy Jassy said in late 2025 that Trainium2, the previous generation, had no spare capacity left to sell. He said it had grown into a multibillion-dollar business at a 150% quarterly clip.\",\n   \"- e263 [party_statement; qz.com; original source Meta ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Meta’s MTIA 300 is in production for ranking and recommendation, and Meta plans to build three further MTIA generations over the next two years for generative AI models.\\n    Quote: The newest version, MTIA 300, is already in production for ranking and recommendation work. Meta is set to build three more generations over the next two years with the purpose of running generative AI models.\",\n   \"- e264 [party_statement; qz.com; original source Meta ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Meta expects its MTIA 450 chip in early 2027 and MTIA 500 later in 2027.\\n    Quote: The next one, MTIA 450, arrives in early 2027, doubling how fast the chip moves data in and out of memory. Its eventual successor, MTIA 500, is expected to come later next year, and pushes memory speed another 50% higher.\",\n   \"- e265 [party_statement; qz.com; original source OpenAI ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] OpenAI’s planned installation of its custom AI chips is set to begin in the second half of 2026 and continue through the end of 2029.\\n    Quote: Installing them is set to begin in the second half of 2026 and run through the end of 2029.\",\n   \"- e266 [fact; qz.com; original source Tesla ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Tesla completed the AI5 inference-chip design in April 2026 and plans production at TSMC’s Arizona plant and Samsung’s Texas plant.\\n    Quote: Tesla finished the design of its AI5 inference chip in April 2026, according to Reuters . Production is planned at both TSMC 's plant in Arizona and Samsung's plant in Texas.\",\n   \"- e267 [party_statement; qz.com; original source Tesla ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Tesla is targeting mid-2027 to begin mass production of its AI5 chip.\\n    Quote: Tesla is targeting mid-2027 for mass production.\",\n   \"- e274 [rumour; au.finance.yahoo.com; original source Cerebras ; from gnews:66cb0387229ac4b1390615cb 2026-07-09] Cerebras plans to build European AI data centres with combined power capacity of 200 MW by the end of 2027, adding competing AI compute capacity.\\n    Quote: The company plans to build a network of AI data centres across Europe by the end of 2027, with a combined power capacity of 200 MW.\",\n   \"- e275 [party_statement; au.finance.yahoo.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:66cb0387229ac4b1390615cb 2026-07-09] Nvidia says its technology powers more than 90% of announced AI factory projects in Europe.\\n    Quote: The expansion comes as AI infrastructure investment accelerates across Europe, where Nvidia says its technology powers more than 90% of the continent's announced AI factory projects.\",\n   \"- e163 [party_statement; NVIDIA Corporation; original source Perplexity ; from nvblog:nvidia-vera-max-single-threaded-cpu-at-scale 2026-07-07] Perplexity is looking to deploy NVIDIA Vera in its upcoming production system; no deployment date or amount is given.\\n    Quote: Perplexity is now looking to deploy Vera in its upcoming production system.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e295; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e169 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source Amazon and Alphabet ; from gnews:ce5daf57bdca5da657e5f677 2026-07-07] Amazon and Alphabet are extending access to their in-house processors, increasing competition for NVIDIA’s AI computing products.\\n    Quote: The move comes as the company faces rising competition from specialized AI chips from cloud providers, including Amazon and Alphabet, which are extending access to in-house processors.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e278; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e218 [third_party_view; tradingview.com; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:a09988fd9c5c1a739a14f873 2026-07-08] Bloomberg Intelligence data cited in the source puts NVIDIA's server GPU market share at 97% at the end of 2025, up from 95% at the end of 2024.\\n    Quote: The company is projected to generate $228 billion in profit on $393 billion in sales in fiscal 2027, which ends Jan. 31, representing expected growth of 90% and 82%, respectively, while its profit estimate has risen 13% over the past three months.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e277; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e277 [third_party_view; Jeran Wittenstein, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence data; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:49f225cd79fb22132f3b9ee4 2026-07-10] Bloomberg Intelligence data put NVIDIA’s server GPU market share at 97% at the end of 2025, up from 95% at the end of 2024.\\n    Quote: Nvidia had 97% of the server GPU market at the end of 2025, up from 95% at the end of 2024, according to data compiled by Bloomberg Intelligence.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e218; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e278 [third_party_view; Jeran Wittenstein; original source Jeran Wittenstein 2026-07-10; from gnews:49f225cd79fb22132f3b9ee4 2026-07-10] Alphabet and Amazon are increasingly deploying their own custom-made chips, adding to competition with NVIDIA.\\n    Quote: For now, that competition — not just from AMD and Intel but also from its biggest customers like Alphabet Inc. and Amazon.com Inc., who are increasingly deploying their own custom-made chips — is a major factor holding back Nvidia’s stock price.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e169, e291; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e280 [third_party_view; Trefis; original source Trefis 2026-07-10; from gnews:6abaf2856736877236d30f6a 2026-07-10] Trefis reports Wall Street consensus expects NVIDIA revenue to grow about 32% annually over the next few years.\\n    Quote: Wall Street consensus sees NVIDIA’s revenue growing about 32% a year for the next few years.\",\n   \"- e291 [rumour; GuruFocus; original source GuruFocus ; from gnews:4c201dc59ba0c7579bfef4db 2026-07-10] GuruFocus reported rumors that major NVIDIA clients were accelerating development of in-house AI chips, potentially increasing competition for NVIDIA.\\n    Quote: rumors of major clients accelerating their development of in-house artificial intelligence (AI) chips\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e278; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e295 [fact; quantumzeitgeist.com; original source Perplexity ; from gnews:b666d35e5247a8ddcc2d7c72 2026-07-10] Perplexity plans to integrate NVIDIA Vera CPUs into its upcoming production systems; no amount or date was given.\\n    Quote: Perplexity is now planning to integrate Vera into its upcoming production systems, demonstrating confidence in its ability to enhance agent performance and overall system efficiency.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e163; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e297 [party_statement; theverge.com; original source Chey Tae-won ; from gnews:3839887e5ca53a0cb0e7c91e 2026-07-10] SK Group chairman Chey Tae-won said in June that SK Hynix plans to ramp up memory-chip capacity over the next five years to address a shortage that could last until 2030.\\n    Quote: SK Group chairman Chey Tae-won said in June that the company plans to ramp up its memory chip capacity over the next five years to address a shortage that could last until 2030, Bloomberg reports .\",\n   \"- e298 [third_party_view; Thomas Richmond, quoting Kristina Partsinevelos; original source Kristina Partsinevelos 2026-07-10; from gnews:9ae96ca750b8e3962c47795f 2026-07-10] Kristina Partsinevelos said no additional HBM supply would arrive before late 2027, keeping the memory shortage and record-high prices in place until then.\\n    Quote: “None of that supply, though, arrives before late 2027, which keeps the memory shortage going and record-high prices intact for now,” Partsinevelos said.\",\n   \"- e194 [third_party_view; mlq.ai; original source Industry surveys ; from gnews:9f430c6ce2e8d551fe1f063a 2026-07-07] Industry surveys indicate Chinese firms plan to allocate 46% of their AI-accelerator budgets to domestic suppliers within 12 months, versus about 30% currently.\\n    Quote: Industry surveys indicate Chinese firms plan to shift 46% of their AI-accelerator budgets to domestic suppliers within 12 months, up from roughly 30% today [5].\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e157, e343; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e327 [party_statement; tech-insider.org; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:8faf69f198e10f14aae67621 2026-07-12] Nvidia said AWS plans to deploy 2 million additional Nvidia GPUs during 2027–2028.\\n    Quote: Nvidia said in August 2026 that AWS plans to deploy 2 million additional Nvidia GPUs in 2027 to 2028 .\",\n   \"- e328 [third_party_view; io-fund.com; original source Yole Research ; from gnews:2dcfaef1a91c2976a4e347da 2026-07-12] Yole Research projected that more than 90% of servers would be CXL-capable by the end of calendar 2026, up from two-thirds in Q1 2025.\\n    Quote: Yole Research estimated that in Q1 2025, two-thirds of servers were CXL-capable , and projects this figure will rise to more than 90% by the end of 2026.\",\n   \"- e329 [party_statement; io-fund.com; original source Marvell ; from gnews:2dcfaef1a91c2976a4e347da 2026-07-12] Marvell plans to begin sampling its Structera S CXL 3.0 switch in calendar Q3 2026.\\n    Quote: Marvell expects to begin sampling its Structera S CXL 3.0 switch in calendar Q3 2026.\",\n   \"- e331 [third_party_view; barchart.com (analyst); original source Wedbush Securities ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Wedbush Securities said Nvidia's Vera CPU could expand its addressable market beyond GPUs and create billions of dollars in additional revenue; no period was specified.\\n    Quote: Wedbush Securities recently argued that Nvidia's new Vera CPU platform could expand the company's total addressable market (TAM) well beyond graphics processors, opening the door to billions of dollars in additional revenue.\",\n   \"- e332 [rumour; barchart.com (analyst); original source barchart.com (unnamed reports) ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Reports said Nvidia had begun offering Vera processors to cloud customers, including some in China where regulations allow; no amount or period was specified.\\n    Quote: Reports also suggest Nvidia has begun offering the new processors to cloud customers, including some in China where regulations allow.\",\n   \"- e343 [third_party_view; barchart.com (analyst); original source Bloomberg survey ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] A Bloomberg survey found Chinese technology companies expect domestic suppliers to receive roughly 46% of their AI-chip spending over the next year, up from about 30% currently.\\n    Quote: A new Bloomberg survey showed Chinese technology companies expect to allocate roughly 46% of their AI chip spending to domestic suppliers over the next year, up from about 30% currently.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e194; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e359 [party_statement; gurufocus.com (analyst); original source Nvidia management ; from gnews:dedacecd6d2ed5192c307199 2026-07-13] Nvidia management expects sovereign AI projects and on-premise deployments to account for a larger share of future growth; no period or amount was specified.\\n    Quote: It expects sovereign AI projects and on-premise deployments to make up a larger share of future growth as AI adoption expands.\",\n   \"- e360 [fact; GuruFocus; original source Google ; from gnews:1c47fd978ef50b1d7f48cbd8 2026-07-13] Google approached neocloud companies about using its TPUs, potentially expanding competition with Nvidia in AI chips.\\n    Quote: Google has approached so-called neocloud companies about using its tensor processing units, or TPUs, according to a report from The Information.\",\n   \"- e361 [third_party_view; GuruFocus; original source Nscale ; from gnews:1c47fd978ef50b1d7f48cbd8 2026-07-13] Nscale reportedly told Google its active projects remain centered on GPU capacity, indicating limited near-term openness to TPU adoption at that provider.\\n    Quote: One provider, Nscale, reportedly told Google that its active projects remain centered on GPU capacity.\",\n   \"- e362 [third_party_view; GuruFocus; original source Google and Blackstone ; from gnews:1c47fd978ef50b1d7f48cbd8 2026-07-13] Google and Blackstone are working on a cloud venture that plans to rent TPU capacity to AI labs and financial firms in 2027.\\n    Quote: Google is also working with Blackstone on a new cloud venture that plans to rent TPU capacity to AI labs and financial firms next year.\",\n   \"- e383 [party_statement; Abhinav Raj, as reported by XDA Developers; original source AMD ; from gnews:6e27fc3ef50f99b180c6646a 2026-07-13] AMD has committed to bringing FSR 4.1 to RDNA 2 GPUs, with the rollout expected to extend into 2027.\\n    Quote: AMD, to its credit, has committed to bringing FSR 4.1 to RDNA 2 cards, but that rollout is expected to stretch into 2027, seven years after those GPUs launched and two full years behind the equivalent Nvidia moment.\",\n   \"- e390 [third_party_view; Rich Duprey; original source Morgan Stanley ; from gnews:e0e5ab6c2aced8d5a6a688a5 2026-07-13] The article reports Morgan Stanley's forecast that Google, Amazon, Microsoft, and Meta will spend over $1 trillion on AI infrastructure and add 19.5 GW of compute capacity in calendar 2027; they added roughly 6.7 GW in 2025, while Google alone is forecast to add 6.8 GW in 2027.\\n    Quote: The analyst says Google, Amazon, Microsoft, and Meta are forecast to spend over $1 trillion on AI infrastructure next year, adding 19.5 gigawatts (GW) of incremental compute capacity. In 2025, they added roughly 6.7 GW. Google alone will add 6.8 GW, or more than the hyperscalers did combined two years ago.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e173; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e391 [third_party_view; Rich Duprey; original source Morgan Stanley ; from gnews:e0e5ab6c2aced8d5a6a688a5 2026-07-13] Morgan Stanley says hyperscalers are continuing to expand investment in proprietary silicon to improve total cost of ownership and reduce dependence on merchant GPU suppliers.\\n    Quote: Morgan Stanley says hyperscalers continue to expand their investments in proprietary silicon to improve total cost of ownership and reduce dependence on merchant GPU suppliers.\",\n   \"- e392 [third_party_view; Rich Duprey; original source Milk Road AI ; from gnews:e0e5ab6c2aced8d5a6a688a5 2026-07-13] Milk Road AI estimates that one GW of AI infrastructure costs $6 billion–$11 billion with Broadcom- or Marvell-designed ASIC racks, versus roughly $19 billion with Nvidia GB300-based racks and $25 billion with Vera Rubin racks.\\n    Quote: Milk Road AI estimates that building one gigawatt of AI infrastructure using Broadcom- or Marvell-designed ASIC racks cost between $6 billion and $11 billion, compared with roughly $19 billion using Nvidia GB300-based racks. Under Vera Rubin, rack costs jump to $25 billion.\",\n   \"- e28 [third_party_view; fool.com analyst Justin Pope; original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] Wall Street analysts estimate Nvidia revenue of $392 billion in FY2027, compared with trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts estimate that Nvidia's business could double over the next couple of years, from trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion to $392 billion this fiscal year, and $554 billion the following year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e401; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e401 [third_party_view; Justin Pope, The Motley Fool; original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:84e90d3da2d3779da0e7bdb0 2026-07-14] Wall Street analysts estimate NVIDIA total revenue of approximately $555 billion in FY2028, ending January 2028.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts estimate that Nvidia will generate approximately $555 billion in revenue for the company's next fiscal year, ending January 2028.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e28; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e404 [party_statement; Nokia, as reported by the outlet; original source Nokia 2026-07-15; from gnews:e153ff10e5adda87a52745a4 2026-07-14] Nokia said it developed the first commercial AI-driven radio access network platform with Nvidia.\\n    Quote: Nokia Oyj says it developed the first commercial artificial intelligence-driven radio access network platform together with Nvidia Corp to radically increase the amount of data operators can transmit using existing infrastructure.\",\n   \"- e425 [third_party_view; sg.finance.yahoo.com; original source Zacks ; from gnews:f10cd8ddb00105698ac294cf 2026-07-14] Zacks reported that consensus analyst estimates for Nvidia increased 13.7% over the three months before 2026-07-14; the estimate measure and fiscal period are not specified.\\n    Quote: Analysts have been steadily raising their estimates for Nvidia. Over the past three months, the Zacks Consensus Estimate for the company has increased 13.7%.\"\n  ],\n  \"points_to_rule\": [\n   \"item i256\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"control\": 7,\n  \"ruler_question\": {\n   \"question\": \"How much will the largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?\",\n   \"unit\": \"USD\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2028-12-31\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Below $700 billion\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is less than $700 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": 700000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"$700 billion to below $800 billion\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $700 billion and less than $800 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 700000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 800000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"$800 billion to below $900 billion\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $800 billion and less than $900 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 800000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 900000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"$900 billion to below $1000 billion\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $900 billion and less than $1000 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 900000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 1000000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"$1000 billion or more\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $1000 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 1000000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": null\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"judged_question\": {\n   \"view_id\": \"v5\",\n   \"question\": \"What will the big four AI hyperscalers' combined data center capital expenditures be in calendar 2027?\",\n   \"looks_at\": \"Combined data center capital expenditures of the big four AI hyperscalers in calendar 2027\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2028-03-31\",\n   \"year\": \"2027\",\n   \"kind\": \"theme\"\n  },\n  \"judged_rungs\": [\n   {\n    \"position\": 1,\n    \"label\": \"Lowest\",\n    \"condition\": \"Below $850 billion\",\n    \"lo\": null,\n    \"hi\": 850000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 2,\n    \"label\": \"Low\",\n    \"condition\": \"At least $850 billion but below $950 billion\",\n    \"lo\": 850000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 950000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 3,\n    \"label\": \"Middle\",\n    \"condition\": \"At least $950 billion but below $1.05 trillion\",\n    \"lo\": 950000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 1050000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 4,\n    \"label\": \"High\",\n    \"condition\": \"At least $1.05 trillion but below $1.15 trillion\",\n    \"lo\": 1050000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 1150000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 5,\n    \"label\": \"Highest\",\n    \"condition\": \"At least $1.15 trillion\",\n    \"lo\": 1150000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": null\n   }\n  ],\n  \"reader_b_decisive_items\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i256\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-07\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Stock Is Down 17% From Its High. Is the Artificial Intelligence (AI) Leader Finally Cheap?\",\n    \"passage\": \"This year, the big four AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures . Next year, Nvidia claims this group will spend more than $1 trillion.\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"big four AI hyperscalers' own plans (2026); NVIDIA's claim (2027)\",\n     \"what\": \"data-center capital expenditure of the big four\",\n     \"how_much\": \"around $650bn (2026); more than $1 trillion (2027)\",\n     \"period\": \"calendar 2026; calendar 2027\",\n     \"status\": \"plan (2026); forecast by NVIDIA (2027)\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i090\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-04\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Stock Is Nearly Flat for 2026. Time to Cash Out, or Load Up on Shares?\",\n    \"passage\": \"Wall Street analysts project 82% revenue growth for this year and 41% next year\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"Wall Street analysts\",\n     \"what\": \"NVIDIA revenue growth forecast\",\n     \"how_much\": \"82% this year; 41% next year\",\n     \"period\": \"this year and next year (fiscal or calendar both accepted, D233)\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i143\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"How Nvidia Became The Black Sheep Of The Chip Stock Rally\",\n    \"passage\": \"Some estimates put half of all data center spend going toward memory in 2027.\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"unnamed estimates\",\n     \"what\": \"memory's share of data center spend\",\n     \"how_much\": \"about half\",\n     \"period\": \"2027\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i161\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"CAPITAL IDEAS: The lag 7 — Is Micron the new Nvidia?\",\n    \"passage\": \"Goldman Sachs estimates annual AI infrastructure capital expenditures could reach $765 billion in 2026 and grow to $1.6 trillion by 2031\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"Goldman Sachs estimate\",\n     \"what\": \"annual AI infrastructure capex (chips, data centers, power, cooling, networking)\",\n     \"how_much\": \"$765B (2026); $1.6T (2031); ~$7.6T cumulative 2026-2031\",\n     \"period\": \"2026; 2031; 2026-2031\",\n     \"condition\": \"could reach\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   }\n  ],\n  \"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\": [\n   \"- e49 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568 2026-07-04] Nvidia projects that the big four AI hyperscalers' combined data center capital expenditures could reach $1 trillion in 2027.\\n    Quote: Next year, Nvidia projects that this figure could reach $1 trillion.\",\n   \"- e49 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568 2026-07-04] Nvidia projects that the big four AI hyperscalers' combined data center capital expenditures could reach $1 trillion in 2027.\\n    Quote: Next year, Nvidia projects that this figure could reach $1 trillion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e96; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e96 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia management ; from gnews:71df54965281684cc500960f 2026-07-06] Nvidia management forecast that hyperscaler spending would exceed $1 trillion in 2027.\\n    Quote: During its last quarterly conference call, management forecast that it expects hyperscaler spending to top $1 trillion in 2027\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e49; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e96 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia management ; from gnews:71df54965281684cc500960f 2026-07-06] Nvidia management forecast that hyperscaler spending would exceed $1 trillion in 2027.\\n    Quote: During its last quarterly conference call, management forecast that it expects hyperscaler spending to top $1 trillion in 2027\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e49, e173; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e173 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:f8191f5bb960d79e47c73d6c 2026-07-07] Nvidia claims the big four AI hyperscalers will spend more than $1 trillion on data center capital expenditures in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: Next year, Nvidia claims this group will spend more than $1 trillion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e96; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e177 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-07-07; from gnews:d0f3f83296df884fae64921e 2026-07-07] The author estimates that AI hyperscalers plan to spend $650 billion on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026 and that their spending could exceed $1 trillion in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: While the AI hyperscalers plan to spend $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year, next year that figure could be over $1 trillion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e48; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e49 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568 2026-07-04] Nvidia projects that the big four AI hyperscalers' combined data center capital expenditures could reach $1 trillion in 2027.\\n    Quote: Next year, Nvidia projects that this figure could reach $1 trillion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e96, e321; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e321 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:07cf5835d106467db5448c13 2026-07-12] Nvidia expects AI hyperaccelerator spending to exceed $1 trillion next year.\\n    Quote: However, Nvidia told investors last quarter that it expects AI hyperaccelerator spending to rise to over $1 trillion next year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e49; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e173 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:f8191f5bb960d79e47c73d6c 2026-07-07] Nvidia claims the big four AI hyperscalers will spend more than $1 trillion on data center capital expenditures in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: Next year, Nvidia claims this group will spend more than $1 trillion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e96, e390; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e390 [third_party_view; Rich Duprey; original source Morgan Stanley ; from gnews:e0e5ab6c2aced8d5a6a688a5 2026-07-13] The article reports Morgan Stanley's forecast that Google, Amazon, Microsoft, and Meta will spend over $1 trillion on AI infrastructure and add 19.5 GW of compute capacity in calendar 2027; they added roughly 6.7 GW in 2025, while Google alone is forecast to add 6.8 GW in 2027.\\n    Quote: The analyst says Google, Amazon, Microsoft, and Meta are forecast to spend over $1 trillion on AI infrastructure next year, adding 19.5 gigawatts (GW) of incremental compute capacity. In 2025, they added roughly 6.7 GW. Google alone will add 6.8 GW, or more than the hyperscalers did combined two years ago.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e173; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e437 [fact; ebc.com; original source Amazon ; from gnews:f83ae0a4f01c18d48f20a629 2026-07-14] Amazon borrowed another $25 billion, a financing move the article connects with a selloff in AI-related debt.\\n    Quote: Amazon recently made headlines by borrowing another $25 billion, causing a minor selloff in AI-related debt .\"\n  ],\n  \"points_to_rule\": [\n   \"same_question\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"control\": 8,\n  \"ruler_question\": {\n   \"question\": \"What will Nvidia's total revenue be in FY2027?\",\n   \"unit\": \"USD\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $500 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 500000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": null\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $400 billion and below $500 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 400000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 500000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $350 billion and below $400 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 350000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 400000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $300 billion and below $350 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 300000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 350000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is below $300 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": 300000000000.0\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"judged_question\": {\n   \"view_id\": \"v9\",\n   \"question\": \"What will NVIDIA's total revenue be in FY2027?\",\n   \"looks_at\": \"NVIDIA total revenue in FY2027\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-02-24\",\n   \"year\": \"FY2027\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\"\n  },\n  \"judged_rungs\": [\n   {\n    \"position\": 1,\n    \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n    \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is below $300 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": null,\n    \"hi\": 300000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 2,\n    \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n    \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $300 billion and below $350 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": 300000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 350000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 3,\n    \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n    \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $350 billion and below $400 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": 350000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 400000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 4,\n    \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n    \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $400 billion and below $450 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": 400000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 450000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 5,\n    \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n    \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $450 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": 450000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": null\n   }\n  ],\n  \"reader_b_decisive_items\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i281\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-09\",\n    \"title\": \"DeepSeek Just Dealt Nvidia Stock a Potentially Major Blow\",\n    \"passage\": \"forecasting revenue of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%, and a non-GAAP gross margin of about 75%\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"NVIDIA\",\n     \"what\": \"Q2 FY2027 revenue and gross-margin guidance\",\n     \"how_much\": \"$91 billion ±2%; non-GAAP gross margin about 75%\",\n     \"period\": \"Q2 FY2027\",\n     \"condition\": \"assumes no China Data Center compute revenue\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i295\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-10\",\n    \"title\": \"Here are Friday's biggest analyst calls: Nvidia, SpaceX, Toll, Shopify, Twilio, Seagate, Chipotle & more\",\n    \"passage\": \"the company describing \\\"accelerating growth rates\\\" even as revenues approach the $100 bn per quarter mark\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"NVIDIA management, relayed by Morgan Stanley\",\n     \"what\": \"revenue growth rates accelerating\",\n     \"how_much\": \"quarterly revenue approaching $100 bn\",\n     \"status\": \"claim\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i106\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-05\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia's next-gen AI rack system delayed to 2028 on manufacturing snags, SemiAnalysis says\",\n    \"passage\": \"SemiAnalysis also projects Nvidia's data-center compute revenue will run 20% above Wall Street consensus in the second half of fiscal 2027\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"SemiAnalysis\",\n     \"what\": \"NVIDIA data-center compute revenue versus Wall Street consensus\",\n     \"how_much\": \"20% above consensus\",\n     \"period\": \"second half of fiscal 2027\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i219\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Vera Rubin rack costs $7.8M — memory is why\",\n    \"passage\": \"First shipments are scheduled for the third quarter of 2026, with volume ramping in the fourth.\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"what\": \"Vera Rubin VR200 NVL72 first shipments and volume ramp\",\n     \"period\": \"first shipments Q3 2026; volume ramp Q4 2026\",\n     \"status\": \"plan\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i037\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-02\",\n    \"title\": \"Microsoft vs. Nvidia: Which Is the Better AI Stock to Own for the Next 3 Years?\",\n    \"passage\": \"from trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion to $392 billion this fiscal year, and $554 billion the following year\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"Wall Street analysts\",\n     \"what\": \"NVIDIA total revenue estimates\",\n     \"how_much\": \"$392 billion this fiscal year, $554 billion next year (from $253 billion trailing twelve months)\",\n     \"period\": \"this fiscal year (FY2027) and the following year (FY2028)\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   }\n  ],\n  \"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\": [\n   \"- e204 [fact; Yahoo Finance; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:b40db2c507df72ec016e99e6 2026-07-08] NVIDIA reported FY2026 revenue above $215.9 billion, up 65% year over year.\\n    Quote: The company's most recent fiscal 2026 revenue topped $215.9 billion, up 65% year over year and well ahead of the $11.7 billion it posted in 2019.\",\n   \"- e205 [third_party_view; Yahoo Finance; original source Analysts ; from gnews:b40db2c507df72ec016e99e6 2026-07-08] Analysts anticipate NVIDIA FY2027 revenue of $392.7 billion.\\n    Quote: And analysts are anticipating further gains of $392.7 billion in its current fiscal year.\",\n   \"- e236 [fact; FEV Group; original source FEV Group and Microsoft 2026-07-09; from gnews:c8324bfbfe7f0c60c826e72f 2026-07-09] FEV is collaborating with Microsoft to integrate in-vehicle generative AI built on NVIDIA GPU-accelerated compute and AI model microservices; no scale or completion date was given.\\n    Quote: FEV is collaborating with Microsoft to integrate powerful, in-vehicle Generative AI capabilities built on NVIDIA GPU-accelerated compute and AI model microservices.\",\n   \"- e237 [third_party_view; TechCrunch author Russell Brandom; original source TechCrunch author Russell Brandom 2026-07-09; from gnews:3ea4e94c707ece2db2d7caec 2026-07-09] The article reports that memory makers have increased high-bandwidth memory chip prices tenfold over the past year as demand outpaced supply.\\n    Quote: For memory companies like Micron, the story is much simpler. They build high-bandwidth memory chips — specialized components designed to move data in and out of processors as fast as possible — which have been getting incrementally better for 20 years. Without the chips or the companies changing too much, the service they provide suddenly became very valuable — and since demand is growing faster t\",\n   \"- e238 [third_party_view; TechCrunch author Russell Brandom; original source TechCrunch author Russell Brandom 2026-07-09; from gnews:3ea4e94c707ece2db2d7caec 2026-07-09] The article reports that the spot price for an hour of Nvidia H100 GPU compute peaked at around $3.20 in May 2026 and then declined steadily.\\n    Quote: Just like Nvidia’s stock price, there’s a peak in May (around $3.20 an hour) and then a steady drop-off.\",\n   \"- e239 [third_party_view; Ornn co-founder and CTO Wayne Nelms, quoted by TechCrunch author Russell Brandom; original source Wayne Nelms ; from gnews:3ea4e94c707ece2db2d7caec 2026-07-09] Ornn co-founder and CTO Wayne Nelms said more GPU and accelerator players are entering the market and predicted that current market conditions would broadly persist absent an HBM breakthrough, a supply-demand shift, or a new memory-market entrant.\\n    Quote: “More GPU and accelerator players are entering the market.\",\n   \"- e241 [third_party_view; barchart.com; original source Experts cited by barchart.com ; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Experts cited by barchart.com say DeepSeek's chip is unlikely to materially affect Nvidia's near-term revenue, partly because China contributes less to Nvidia sales, but custom silicon could gradually erode Nvidia's pricing power and margins.\\n    Quote: Although experts note that DeepSeek's move is unlikely to materially impact Nvidia's near-term revenue, particularly given China's shrinking contribution to Nvidia's sales, it reinforces concerns that custom silicon could gradually erode the company's pricing power and margins.\",\n   \"- e244 [fact; barchart.com; original source Nvidia 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia reported fiscal 2027 first-quarter revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year, and net income of $58.32 billion, up 211% year over year, for the quarter ended April 26.\\n    Quote: For the quarter ended April 26, Nvidia posted record revenue of $81.6 billion, an 85% year-over-year (YOY) increase, while net income jumped 211% YOY to $58.32 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e254; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e245 [fact; barchart.com; original source Nvidia 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia Data Center revenue was $75.2 billion in fiscal 2027 first-quarter, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Moreover, the Data Center segment remained Nvidia's biggest growth driver, with revenue surging 92% YOY to a record $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e250; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e246 [fact; barchart.com; original source Nvidia 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia Data Center networking revenue was $14.8 billion in fiscal 2027 first-quarter, up 199% year over year; Data Center computing revenue was $60.4 billion.\\n    Quote: Data Center networking revenue soared 199% YOY to $14.8 billion, while computing revenue accounted for the remaining $60.4 billion.\",\n   \"- e247 [fact; barchart.com; original source Nvidia 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia Edge Computing revenue was $6.4 billion in fiscal 2027 first-quarter, up 29% year over year.\\n    Quote: Its Edge Computing revenue increased 29% YOY to $6.4 billion, supported by demand across gaming GPUs, autonomous driving, robotics, and AI-enabled edge devices.\",\n   \"- e248 [party_statement; barchart.com; original source Nvidia 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia forecast fiscal 2027 second-quarter revenue of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%, and non-GAAP gross margin of about 75%.\\n    Quote: Additionally, Nvidia issued another optimistic outlook for the second quarter of fiscal 2027, forecasting revenue of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%, and a non-GAAP gross margin of about 75%.\",\n   \"- e249 [party_statement; barchart.com; original source Nvidia 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia's fiscal 2027 second-quarter guidance assumes zero China Data Center compute revenue because of U.S. export restrictions.\\n    Quote: The guidance assumes no contribution from China Data Center compute revenue due to ongoing U.S. export restrictions.\",\n   \"- e250 [fact; fool.com (Adam Spatacco); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:931ee0196ca609e637235fad 2026-07-09] NVIDIA reported record data center segment revenue in Q1 FY2027.\\n    Quote: Revenues from Nvidia's data center segment -- the primary engine of the business -- set a record in the first quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e245; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e251 [party_statement; fool.com (Adam Spatacco); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:931ee0196ca609e637235fad 2026-07-09] NVIDIA management guided to accelerating data center segment revenue growth in Q2 FY2027.\\n    Quote: Moreover, management guided for further revenue growth acceleration for the second quarter.\",\n   \"- e252 [party_statement; fool.com (Adam Spatacco); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:931ee0196ca609e637235fad 2026-07-09] NVIDIA management cited roughly $1 trillion of revenue visibility for Blackwell and Vera Rubin processors across 2026 and 2027, anchored by multiyear customer commitments.\\n    Quote: Management has also articulated roughly $1 trillion in revenue visibility for its Blackwell and Vera Rubin processors across 2026 and 2027, anchored by multiyear commitments from hyperscalers and large enterprise customers.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e27; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e253 [third_party_view; Rick Munarriz; original source Rick Munarriz 2026-07-09; from gnews:b412380d12c5a222545d42f1 2026-07-09] The author says Nvidia's revenue growth accelerated for three consecutive quarters.\\n    Quote: Nvidia's revenue has accelerated for three consecutive quarters.\",\n   \"- e254 [fact; Rick Munarriz; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:b412380d12c5a222545d42f1 2026-07-09] Nvidia reported 85% year-over-year revenue growth in fiscal Q1, its strongest increase in a year and a half.\\n    Quote: The 85% top-line jump it posted in its fiscal first quarter is the strongest increase in a year and a half.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e244; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e259 [party_statement; qz.com; original source Andy Jassy, Amazon CEO ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Amazon CEO Andy Jassy said in late 2025 that Trainium2 had no spare capacity left to sell and was a multibillion-dollar business growing at a 150% quarterly clip.\\n    Quote: Amazon CEO Andy Jassy said in late 2025 that Trainium2, the previous generation, had no spare capacity left to sell. He said it had grown into a multibillion-dollar business at a 150% quarterly clip.\",\n   \"- e260 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source qz.com 2026-07-09; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Amazon’s Trainium4 chip could arrive later in 2026.\\n    Quote: Amazon 's next chip, Trainium4, which packs three times the performance of its predecessor, could arrive later this year.\",\n   \"- e261 [fact; qz.com; original source Microsoft ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Microsoft announced its Maia 200 inference chip in January 2026, and the chip is now reaching a handful of U.S. data centers.\\n    Quote: It announced Maia 200, a chip built for that work, in January 2026, and the chip is already reaching a handful of U.S. data centers.\",\n   \"- e262 [party_statement; qz.com; original source Microsoft ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Microsoft’s Maia 200 chip is planned to power OpenAI’s newest models and Microsoft AI products including Copilot.\\n    Quote: The chip will power OpenAI's newest models, along with Microsoft 's own AI products, such as Copilot.\",\n   \"- e263 [party_statement; qz.com; original source Meta ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Meta’s MTIA 300 is in production for ranking and recommendation, and Meta plans to build three further MTIA generations over the next two years for generative AI models.\\n    Quote: The newest version, MTIA 300, is already in production for ranking and recommendation work. Meta is set to build three more generations over the next two years with the purpose of running generative AI models.\",\n   \"- e265 [party_statement; qz.com; original source OpenAI ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] OpenAI’s planned installation of its custom AI chips is set to begin in the second half of 2026 and continue through the end of 2029.\\n    Quote: Installing them is set to begin in the second half of 2026 and run through the end of 2029.\",\n   \"- e266 [fact; qz.com; original source Tesla ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Tesla completed the AI5 inference-chip design in April 2026 and plans production at TSMC’s Arizona plant and Samsung’s Texas plant.\\n    Quote: Tesla finished the design of its AI5 inference chip in April 2026, according to Reuters . Production is planned at both TSMC 's plant in Arizona and Samsung's plant in Texas.\",\n   \"- e268 [fact; gizmodo.com, as reported by Bruce Gil; original source Micron ; from gnews:fe9210b7b43c51e0939ecbbb 2026-07-09] Micron decided to wind down its Crucial consumer business brand to focus on data center demand; no date or amount was given.\\n    Quote: Micron even decided to wind down its consumer business brand , Crucial, to focus on data center demand.\",\n   \"- e269 [rumour; moomoo.com; original source Meta Platforms 2026-07-09; from gnews:7b39859113d4e2b8ebd8aa86 2026-07-09] Meta reportedly plans to start manufacturing its AI chip in September 2026, according to a Reuters report citing an internal memo.\\n    Quote: Meta Platforms (META.US)$ is reportedly planning to start manufacturing its AI chip in September, Reuters reported Thursday, citing the company’s internal memo.\",\n   \"- e270 [fact; moomoo.com; original source Quanta ; from gnews:7b39859113d4e2b8ebd8aa86 2026-07-09] Quanta's monthly sales rose to NT$385.19 billion in June 2026, more than doubling year over year; Quanta supplies AI servers powered by Nvidia GPUs.\\n    Quote: Quanta, which supplies AI servers powered by Nvidia’s GPUs, saw its monthly sales more than double to 385.19 billion New Taiwanese dollars in June from a year earlier, according to data compiled by Bloomberg.\",\n   \"- e205 [third_party_view; Yahoo Finance; original source Analysts ; from gnews:b40db2c507df72ec016e99e6 2026-07-08] Analysts anticipate NVIDIA FY2027 revenue of $392.7 billion.\\n    Quote: And analysts are anticipating further gains of $392.7 billion in its current fiscal year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e276; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e244 [fact; barchart.com; original source Nvidia 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia reported fiscal 2027 first-quarter revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year, and net income of $58.32 billion, up 211% year over year, for the quarter ended April 26.\\n    Quote: For the quarter ended April 26, Nvidia posted record revenue of $81.6 billion, an 85% year-over-year (YOY) increase, while net income jumped 211% YOY to $58.32 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e254, e281; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e245 [fact; barchart.com; original source Nvidia 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia Data Center revenue was $75.2 billion in fiscal 2027 first-quarter, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Moreover, the Data Center segment remained Nvidia's biggest growth driver, with revenue surging 92% YOY to a record $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e250, e285, e305; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e246 [fact; barchart.com; original source Nvidia 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia Data Center networking revenue was $14.8 billion in fiscal 2027 first-quarter, up 199% year over year; Data Center computing revenue was $60.4 billion.\\n    Quote: Data Center networking revenue soared 199% YOY to $14.8 billion, while computing revenue accounted for the remaining $60.4 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e286; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e248 [party_statement; barchart.com; original source Nvidia 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia forecast fiscal 2027 second-quarter revenue of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%, and non-GAAP gross margin of about 75%.\\n    Quote: Additionally, Nvidia issued another optimistic outlook for the second quarter of fiscal 2027, forecasting revenue of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%, and a non-GAAP gross margin of about 75%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e282; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e249 [party_statement; barchart.com; original source Nvidia 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia's fiscal 2027 second-quarter guidance assumes zero China Data Center compute revenue because of U.S. export restrictions.\\n    Quote: The guidance assumes no contribution from China Data Center compute revenue due to ongoing U.S. export restrictions.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e287; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e254 [fact; Rick Munarriz; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:b412380d12c5a222545d42f1 202