said Meta plans to begin manufacturing its custom AI processor, code-named Iris, in September after completing initial testing.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e269; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e285 [fact; 247wallst.com, summarizing NVIDIA’s results; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Data Center revenue of $75.246 billion, up 92% year over year, in Q1 FY2027.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue hit $75.246 billion, up 92% year over year\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e245, e299; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e286 [fact; 247wallst.com, summarizing NVIDIA’s results; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] NVIDIA networking revenue grew 199% year over year in Q1 FY2027.\\n    Quote: networking alone grew 199%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e246; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e287 [party_statement; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] NVIDIA’s Q2 FY2027 revenue guidance excluded Data Center compute revenue from China, and NVIDIA reported zero H20 shipments in Q1 FY2027.\\n    Quote: Q2 FY27 guidance explicitly excludes Data Center compute revenue from China, and there were zero H20 shipments in the quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e249; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e289 [party_statement; 247wallst.com, summarizing NVIDIA’s guidance; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] NVIDIA guided to Q2 FY2027 revenue of $91 billion.\\n    Quote: Q2 FY27 guidance points to $91 billion in revenue.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e282; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e290 [fact; Vandita Jadeja; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] The article cites NVIDIA revenue growth of 85.23% year over year and a non-GAAP gross margin of 75.0%.\\n    Quote: For a business growing revenue 85.23% year over year at 75.0% non-GAAP gross margins\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e254; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e292 [fact; 247Wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially; Data Center revenue was $75.2 billion.\\n    Quote: The company reported record revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially, with Data Center revenue reaching $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e254; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e293 [party_statement; 247Wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 non-GAAP gross margin of 75% and guided Q2 FY2027 revenue to $91 billion.\\n    Quote: Non-GAAP gross margin came in at 75%, and management guided Q2 FY2027 revenue to $91 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e282; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e296 [third_party_view; theverge.com; original source Counterpoint ; from gnews:3839887e5ca53a0cb0e7c91e 2026-07-10] Counterpoint reported that in June 2026 SK Hynix had 29% of the global DRAM market, versus Samsung at 38% and Micron at 22%.\\n    Quote: As of June 2026, SK Hynix makes up 29 percent of the global DRAM market, with Samsung at 38 percent and Micron at 22 percent, according to data from Counterpoint .\",\n   \"- e298 [third_party_view; Thomas Richmond, quoting Kristina Partsinevelos; original source Kristina Partsinevelos 2026-07-10; from gnews:9ae96ca750b8e3962c47795f 2026-07-10] Kristina Partsinevelos said no additional HBM supply would arrive before late 2027, keeping the memory shortage and record-high prices in place until then.\\n    Quote: “None of that supply, though, arrives before late 2027, which keeps the memory shortage going and record-high prices intact for now,” Partsinevelos said.\",\n   \"- e299 [fact; Thomas Richmond; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:9ae96ca750b8e3962c47795f 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.62 billion, Data Center revenue of $75.25 billion, and total supply-related commitments of $119.0 billion.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.62 billion, up 85.2% year over year, with Data Center revenue of $75.25 billion and total supply-related commitments of $119.0 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e285, e304; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e300 [party_statement; TIKR.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] Nvidia estimates that supporting frontier AI models accounts for about 20% of its business; the item gives no period.\\n    Quote: To put some numbers behind that, Nvidia estimates about 20% of its business comes from supporting frontier AI models built by companies like OpenAI and Anthropic.\",\n   \"- e301 [third_party_view; TIKR.com; original source TD Cowen ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] TD Cowen estimates Nvidia’s revenue from enterprise applications across multiple industries is in the low-to-mid-teens range; the item gives no period or explicit unit for the range.\\n    Quote: Meanwhile, TD Cowen estimates that Nvidia’s revenue from enterprise applications across multiple industries is in the low-to-mid-teens range.\",\n   \"- e302 [third_party_view; TIKR.com; original source TD Cowen ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] TD Cowen reported that rental prices for older GPU models have been climbing; no amount or period was specified.\\n    Quote: Rental prices for older GPU models have been climbing\",\n   \"- e303 [third_party_view; TIKR.com; original source TD Cowen ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] TD Cowen reported that recent cloud computing deals were signed at premium prices; no counterparties, amounts, or dates were specified.\\n    Quote: recent cloud computing deals have been signed at premium prices.\",\n   \"- e304 [fact; TIKR.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] Nvidia reported total revenue of $82 billion, up 85% year over year, in the quarter; this was its third consecutive quarter of accelerating growth.\\n    Quote: The company posted $82 billion in total revenue, up 85% year-over-year, marking its third straight quarter of accelerating growth.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e299; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e305 [fact; TIKR.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] Nvidia reported data center revenue of $75 billion, up 92% year over year, in the quarter; the exact period was not specified.\\n    Quote: Data center revenue alone hit $75 billion, up 92% year over year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e245; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e306 [party_statement; TIKR.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] Nvidia expects its Vera CPU line to generate $20 billion in sales by the end of the fiscal year; the article date places that year in FY2027.\\n    Quote: Nvidia also highlighted a new growth driver: its Vera CPU line, which the company expects to generate $20 billion in sales by the end of this fiscal year, a notable push into a market historically dominated by Intel and AMD.\",\n   \"- e307 [fact; TIKR.com; original source Nvidia and Valar Atomics ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] Nvidia and Valar Atomics have a deal to build a nuclear-powered data center in Utah to support AI computing and reduce water use; no capacity or completion date was specified.\\n    Quote: Beyond the CPU expansion, Nvidia has been striking new partnerships, including a deal with Valar Atomics to build a nuclear-powered data center in Utah aimed at reducing water use for AI computing.\",\n   \"- e308 [fact; TIKR.com; original source Perplexity ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] Perplexity chose to use Nvidia’s new CPUs for AI agent tasks; no deployment date or scale was specified.\\n    Quote: AI startup Perplexity has also chosen to use Nvidia’s new CPUs for AI agent tasks.\",\n   \"- e309 [third_party_view; TIKR.com; original source Mark Zuckerberg ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] Meta CEO Mark Zuckerberg commented that progress in AI agents was slower than expected; the article gives no specific measure or period.\\n    Quote: Comments from Meta’s Mark Zuckerberg about slower-than-expected progress in AI agents have also added caution to the broader AI narrative.\",\n   \"- e310 [third_party_view; TIKR.com; original source Bank of America ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] Bank of America views the recent semiconductor-sector pullback as a temporary adjustment rather than evidence that AI demand is fading.\\n    Quote: Still, firms like Bank of America view the recent semiconductor sector pullback as a temporary adjustment rather than a sign that AI demand is fading, keeping names like Nvidia stock in focus for investors watching this space closely.\",\n   \"- e311 [third_party_view; es.tradingview.com; original source Morgan Stanley ; from gnews:1bfc0e875ab1f26dcf48fb06 2026-07-11] Morgan Stanley estimated that AI laboratories account for roughly 20% of Nvidia’s demand; no period was specified.\\n    Quote: The bank noted that AI laboratories now account for roughly 20% of Nvidia’s demand, highlighting how enterprise AI adoption is expanding beyond hyperscale cloud providers.\",\n   \"- e281 [third_party_view; Trefis; original source Trefis 2026-07-10; from gnews:6abaf2856736877236d30f6a 2026-07-10] Trefis says NVIDIA revenue grew 71% over the last twelve months and 85% in the most recent quarter.\\n    Quote: That figure seems high until you set it against what the company is actually delivering: revenue grew 71% over the last twelve months and 85% in the most recent quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e244, e319; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e285 [fact; 247wallst.com, summarizing NVIDIA’s results; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Data Center revenue of $75.246 billion, up 92% year over year, in Q1 FY2027.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue hit $75.246 billion, up 92% year over year\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e245, e299, e334; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e292 [fact; 247Wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially; Data Center revenue was $75.2 billion.\\n    Quote: The company reported record revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially, with Data Center revenue reaching $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e254, e333; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e293 [party_statement; 247Wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 non-GAAP gross margin of 75% and guided Q2 FY2027 revenue to $91 billion.\\n    Quote: Non-GAAP gross margin came in at 75%, and management guided Q2 FY2027 revenue to $91 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e282, e335; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e314 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source Silicon Analysts ; from gnews:2beadbce40c7f927f33d9fc5 2026-07-12] Silicon Analysts estimated that Nvidia held more than 90% of the AI-chip training market in 2025.\\n    Quote: Nvidia 's share exceeded 90% in training in 2025.\",\n   \"- e315 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source Silicon Analysts ; from gnews:2beadbce40c7f927f33d9fc5 2026-07-12] Silicon Analysts estimated that Nvidia held 60%–75% of the AI-chip inference market in 2025, with custom silicon competition reducing its share.\\n    Quote: Its inference share sat between 60% and 75% over the same period, undercut by growing competition from custom silicon.\",\n   \"- e316 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source TechCrunch ; from gnews:2beadbce40c7f927f33d9fc5 2026-07-12] TechCrunch reported that 1.4 million Amazon Trainium chips across three generations were deployed as of March 2026.\\n    Quote: As of March, 1.4 million Trainium chips were deployed across three generations, according to TechCrunch\",\n   \"- e317 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source TechCrunch ; from gnews:2beadbce40c7f927f33d9fc5 2026-07-12] TechCrunch reported that Anthropic's Claude was running on more than one million Amazon Trainium2 chips as of March 2026.\\n    Quote: with Anthropic's Claude running on more than one million Trainium2 chips alone.\",\n   \"- e318 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source Mizuho Securities and Silicon Analysts ; from gnews:2beadbce40c7f927f33d9fc5 2026-07-12] Mizuho Securities estimated Nvidia's overall AI-chip market share at 70%–95%, depending on segment; Silicon Analysts projected it would settle near 75% as the market grows beyond $200 billion.\\n    Quote: Nvidia 's overall AI chip market share, estimated by Mizuho Securities at between 70% and 95% depending on segment, is projected by Silicon Analysts to settle near 75% as the total market expands past $200 billion.\",\n   \"- e319 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:07cf5835d106467db5448c13 2026-07-12] Nvidia revenue increased 85% in its past quarter.\\n    Quote: During its past quarter, Nvidia's revenue increased at an 85% clip.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e281; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e320 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:07cf5835d106467db5448c13 2026-07-12] Wall Street analysts expect Nvidia revenue to grow 96% in Q2.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts expect 96% growth during Q2.\",\n   \"- e322 [third_party_view; Keithen Drury; original source Broadcom ; from gnews:f8f440b5020fec9773812b6e 2026-07-12] Broadcom plans to ramp production of custom AI chips for Meta Platforms, Anthropic, and OpenAI in late 2026 and into 2027.\\n    Quote: However, Broadcom is also making custom AI chips for Meta Platforms , Anthropic, and OpenAI, and production for those chips is scheduled to ramp up late this year and into next.\",\n   \"- e330 [third_party_view; jpost.com; original source jpost.com 2026-07-12; from gnews:c14249088492921c802c839a 2026-07-12] The article reports that Nvidia’s server GPU market share was about 97% at the end of 2025, up from 95% at the end of 2024.\\n    Quote: Nvidia's firm grip on the server GPU market showed no signs of weakening, with its market share climbing to about 97% at the end of 2025, compared to 95% the previous year.\",\n   \"- e333 [fact; barchart.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Nvidia reported fiscal Q1 2027 total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: For the first quarter of fiscal 2027, revenue jumped 85% year-over-year (YOY) to $81.6 billion, easily beating analyst expectations.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e292, e344; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e334 [fact; barchart.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Nvidia reported fiscal Q1 2027 Data Center revenue of $75.2 billion, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue climbed 92% YOY to $75.2 billion, highlighting that AI infrastructure remains the company's primary growth engine.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e285; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e335 [party_statement; barchart.com (analyst); original source Nvidia management ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Nvidia management forecast approximately $91 billion in total revenue for fiscal Q2 2027, assuming no China Data Center sales.\\n    Quote: Management also issued strong guidance, forecasting approximately $91 billion in Q2 revenue despite assuming no China data-center sales because of export restrictions.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e293, e345; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e336 [third_party_view; barchart.com (analyst); original source Wall Street consensus, as reported by barchart.com ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Wall Street expected Nvidia's fiscal 2027 total revenue to exceed $300 billion.\\n    Quote: Wall Street expects Nvidia to generate well over $300 billion in fiscal 2027 revenue, while consensus earnings estimates have moved to $8.80 per share.\",\n   \"- e337 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source SK Hynix ; from gnews:03c38d2fe2e6e02ba5736307 2026-07-12] SK Hynix reported quarterly revenue of about $35 billion, up 198% year over year and a record.\\n    Quote: In the recent quarter, for example, the company reported revenue growth of 198% to about $35 billion dollars, a record level.\",\n   \"- e338 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst), citing Counterpoint Research; original source Counterpoint Research ; from gnews:03c38d2fe2e6e02ba5736307 2026-07-12] Counterpoint Research estimated SK Hynix held 58% of the global HBM market at the end of the first quarter.\\n    Quote: SK Hynix held 58% share globally of the HBM market as of the end of the first quarter, according to Counterpoint Research.\",\n   \"- e339 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source SK Hynix and NVIDIA ; from gnews:03c38d2fe2e6e02ba5736307 2026-07-12] SK Hynix and NVIDIA signed a multi-year technology partnership under which SK Hynix will supply memory for areas including AI infrastructure, personal AI and robotics.\\n    Quote: The two companies even reinforced their relationship recently, signing a multi-year technology partnership. It involves SK Hynix supplying memory across a broad range of areas, from AI infrastructure to personal AI and robotics .\",\n   \"- e340 [party_statement; Jensen Huang, quoted by fool.com (analyst); original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:03c38d2fe2e6e02ba5736307 2026-07-12] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said SK Hynix had been NVIDIA's largest memory partner and would continue to be its largest memory partner.\\n    Quote: \\\"SK Hynix has been Nvidia's largest memory partner and will continue to be our largest memory partner,\\\" Nvidia chief Jensen Huang said at the time.\",\n   \"- e344 [fact; barchart.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] NVIDIA reported record FY2027 first-quarter revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: During the fiscal first quarter of 2027, Nvidia generated record revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year-over-year (YOY).\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e333; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e345 [party_statement; barchart.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] NVIDIA management guided FY2027 Q2 revenue to approximately $91 billion, assuming zero China data-center revenue because of export restrictions.\\n    Quote: Looking ahead, management guided Q2 revenue to approximately $91 billion, despite assuming zero China data-center revenue because of export restrictions.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e335; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e347 [fact; barchart.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] NVIDIA expanded partnerships with Alphabet and Marvell.\\n    Quote: expanded partnerships with companies such as Alphabet (GOOGL) and Marvell (MRVL)\",\n   \"- e244 [fact; barchart.com; original source Nvidia 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia reported fiscal 2027 first-quarter revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year, and net income of $58.32 billion, up 211% year over year, for the quarter ended April 26.\\n    Quote: For the quarter ended April 26, Nvidia posted record revenue of $81.6 billion, an 85% year-over-year (YOY) increase, while net income jumped 211% YOY to $58.32 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e254, e281, e363; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e246 [fact; barchart.com; original source Nvidia 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia Data Center networking revenue was $14.8 billion in fiscal 2027 first-quarter, up 199% year over year; Data Center computing revenue was $60.4 billion.\\n    Quote: Data Center networking revenue soared 199% YOY to $14.8 billion, while computing revenue accounted for the remaining $60.4 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e286, e376; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e285 [fact; 247wallst.com, summarizing NVIDIA’s results; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Data Center revenue of $75.246 billion, up 92% year over year, in Q1 FY2027.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue hit $75.246 billion, up 92% year over year\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e245, e299, e334, e373, e375; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e287 [party_statement; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] NVIDIA’s Q2 FY2027 revenue guidance excluded Data Center compute revenue from China, and NVIDIA reported zero H20 shipments in Q1 FY2027.\\n    Quote: Q2 FY27 guidance explicitly excludes Data Center compute revenue from China, and there were zero H20 shipments in the quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e249, e368, e380; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e292 [fact; 247Wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially; Data Center revenue was $75.2 billion.\\n    Quote: The company reported record revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially, with Data Center revenue reaching $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e254, e333, e367; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e293 [party_statement; 247Wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 non-GAAP gross margin of 75% and guided Q2 FY2027 revenue to $91 billion.\\n    Quote: Non-GAAP gross margin came in at 75%, and management guided Q2 FY2027 revenue to $91 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e282, e335, e366, e381; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e305 [fact; TIKR.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] Nvidia reported data center revenue of $75 billion, up 92% year over year, in the quarter; the exact period was not specified.\\n    Quote: Data center revenue alone hit $75 billion, up 92% year over year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e245, e365; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e344 [fact; barchart.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] NVIDIA reported record FY2027 first-quarter revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: During the fiscal first quarter of 2027, Nvidia generated record revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year-over-year (YOY).\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e333, e364, e372, e384; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e345 [party_statement; barchart.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] NVIDIA management guided FY2027 Q2 revenue to approximately $91 billion, assuming zero China data-center revenue because of export restrictions.\\n    Quote: Looking ahead, management guided Q2 revenue to approximately $91 billion, despite assuming zero China data-center revenue because of export restrictions.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e335, e388; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e349 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Nvidia automotive chief Xinzhou Wu estimated that autonomous driving accounts for about 0.006% of all miles driven, without specifying a measurement period.\\n    Quote: Right now the percentage of autonomous miles among all the mileage driven is probably negligible. I think it’s 0.006%, or something like that.\",\n   \"- e350 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said Nvidia hopes to earn a share of ecosystem revenue for each autonomously driven mile, which he described as a potential trillion-dollar opportunity; he gave no timing.\\n    Quote: We hope that we can get a percentage of the revenue that the ecosystem can get from every mile that is driven autonomously in the future. This is where the trillion-dollar opportunity can come from.\",\n   \"- e351 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said Tesla is ahead of other companies in L2++ advanced driver-assistance technology and that competitors are trying to catch up.\\n    Quote: For the basic L2++ technology, Elon is probably ahead of everybody. He had a division a long time ago and he has stuck to the vision for a long time to develop and test the technology among a massive fleet. Nobody would argue that Elon is ahead of everybody in the ADAS market and everybody is playing a catch-up game, essentially.\",\n   \"- e352 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu forecast that Level 4 self-driving could become a mainstream experience in less than five years; he did not give a specific date.\\n    Quote: I would say if I need to give a time, I wouldn’t say five years, but less than five years.\",\n   \"- e353 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said Nvidia chip prices would most likely need to rise because demand for chips is intense; he did not specify timing or the size of any increase.\\n    Quote: Actually, most likely even the chip price will need to go up, because of this intense demand for every chip everybody can grab onto.\",\n   \"- e354 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said Nvidia offers two Hyperion 10 sensor configurations: a base version with 10 cameras and three radars and no lidar, and a high-end version with 14 cameras, three lidars, and seven radars for Level 4 driving.\\n    Quote: In Hyperion 10, for example, we really offer two versions. One is a base, which is mostly cameras: 10 cameras, three radars, no lidar. It’s a very cost-effective way to build a L2++ ADAS kind of vehicle. And on the other hand, for the high end, is what we call the Hyperion High: we provide the sensor set required, which has, I think, 14 cameras, three lidars, and seven radars to have enough sensor\",\n   \"- e355 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said Nvidia planned to roll out its ADAS technology in all Mercedes vehicles and in vehicles from some other partners across the United States by the end of 2026.\\n    Quote: First of all, by the end of this year, we are rolling out our technology on the ADAS side in all Mercedes vehicles and some other partners as well, all over the United States.\",\n   \"- e356 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said Nvidia and Uber were working toward rolling out an L4 service in the next few years; he did not give a specific date.\\n    Quote: Meanwhile, we are also working closely with our partners, for example, Uber. We announced that at GTC, we are trying to roll out our L4 service in the next few years.\",\n   \"- e357 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said 80% of mass-production automakers were in Nvidia’s Hyperion ecosystem for Level 4 driving; he did not specify a measurement date.\\n    Quote: Right now, I would say 80% of the mass-production OEMs are in Nvidia’s Hyperion ecosystem for L4.\",\n   \"- e358 [third_party_view; gurufocus.com (analyst); original source Citi ; from gnews:dedacecd6d2ed5192c307199 2026-07-13] Citi said Nvidia has strong access to high-bandwidth DRAM memory, a critical component for AI systems.\\n    Quote: The bank pointed to Nvidia's strong access to high-bandwidth DRAM memory, a critical component for AI systems.\",\n   \"- e363 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:f4eb5206f2995f5dbb86c5e9 2026-07-13] Nvidia reported quarterly revenue of $81.6 billion for the quarter ended April 26, 2026, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: In its most recent quarter (ended April 26), it made $81.6 billion in revenue (up 85% year over year)\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e244; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e364 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:3a9054a950c410e249837c91 2026-07-13] Nvidia reported FY2027 Q1 revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% quarter over quarter.\\n    Quote: For its fiscal 2027 first quarter (ended April 26), Nvidia generated record revenue, up 85% year over year and 20% quarter over quarter to $81.6 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e344; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e365 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:3a9054a950c410e249837c91 2026-07-13] Nvidia reported record data center revenue of $75 billion for FY2027 Q1, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: record data center revenue of $75 billion, up 92%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e305; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e366 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia management ; from gnews:3a9054a950c410e249837c91 2026-07-13] Nvidia management forecast FY2027 Q2 revenue of $91 billion, up 95% year over year.\\n    Quote: Management expects its growth spurt to continue, forecasting year-over-year revenue growth of 95% to $91 billion in Q2.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e293; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e367 [fact; 247Wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:799ec454c15dd