IDIA ; from gnews:184645c8d683d95b684bd6da 2026-07-14] NVIDIA guided Q2 revenue to $91 billion, assuming zero China Data Center compute revenue.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA guided Q2 to $91 billion in revenue, which assumes zero China Data Center compute.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e368; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e424 [fact; Vandita Jadeja; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:386a294bd395bde25e3f4a11 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.61 billion, up 85.2% year over year, and Data Center revenue of $75.25 billion, up 92%.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA’s Q1 FY27 revenue hit $81.61B, up 85.2% YoY, with Data Center at $75.25B (+92%).\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e285; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e425 [third_party_view; sg.finance.yahoo.com; original source Zacks ; from gnews:f10cd8ddb00105698ac294cf 2026-07-14] Zacks reported that consensus analyst estimates for Nvidia increased 13.7% over the three months before 2026-07-14; the estimate measure and fiscal period are not specified.\\n    Quote: Analysts have been steadily raising their estimates for Nvidia. Over the past three months, the Zacks Consensus Estimate for the company has increased 13.7%.\",\n   \"- e426 [third_party_view; sg.finance.yahoo.com; original source Zacks ; from gnews:f10cd8ddb00105698ac294cf 2026-07-14] Zacks reported expected Nvidia earnings of $9.10 per share for the fiscal year ending January 2027, unchanged from the year-ago reported figure.\\n    Quote: For the fiscal year ending January 2027, this maker of graphics chips for gaming and artificial intelligence is expected to earn $9.10 per share, which is unchanged compared with the year-ago reported number.\",\n   \"- e427 [fact; Reuters; original source U.S. authorities, as reported from documents and sources familiar with the matter 2026-07-14; from gnews:24268bfaab6ef1d7876b188c 2026-07-14] U.S. authorities permitted ZTE Kangxun Telecom and server maker Maginfra to purchase Nvidia H200 chips; a Kingsoft subsidiary was cleared to use some AMD chips.\\n    Quote: ZTE Kangxun Telecom and server maker Maginfra have been permitted to purchase Nvidia's H200 chips, while Zhuhai Hengqin Yunxiang Zhisheng Network Technology, a subsidiary of cloud computing company Kingsoft, has ‌been cleared to use some ⁠AMD chips that rival the H200, according to the documents and the sources.\",\n   \"- e428 [rumour; Reuters; original source Unnamed sources familiar with the matter 2026-07-14; from gnews:24268bfaab6ef1d7876b188c 2026-07-14] Unnamed sources said some Chinese cloud firms recently told partners and clients they may soon be able to obtain Nvidia H200 chips, indicating progress in Chinese authorities' import reviews.\\n    Quote: However, some Chinese cloud firms have recently told partners and clients they may soon be able to obtain H200 chips, the sources said, indicating some progress in import reviews by Chinese authorities.\",\n   \"- e429 [fact; Rest of World; original source Saudi Arabia 2026-06-01; from gnews:01a49ffd41f6abe24538da65 2026-07-14] Saudi Arabia agreed on June 1, 2026, to use self-driving taxis that run on Nvidia technology.\\n    Quote: Saudi Arabia agreed on June 1 to use self-driving taxis that run on Nvidia technology — from the computer inside each car to the software that steers it.\",\n   \"- e430 [fact; Rest of World; original source Humain ; from gnews:01a49ffd41f6abe24538da65 2026-07-14] Humain is building data centers in Riyadh and Dammam, planned to be powered by several hundred thousand Nvidia chips.\\n    Quote: Humain is also building data centers in Riyadh and Dammam, powered by several hundred thousand Nvidia chips.\",\n   \"- e431 [fact; Rest of World; original source G42 ; from gnews:01a49ffd41f6abe24538da65 2026-07-14] G42’s first stage of its Stargate data center in Abu Dhabi is planned to run on 400,000 Nvidia chips.\\n    Quote: Its first stage will run on 400,000 Nvidia chips .\",\n   \"- e432 [party_statement; Rest of World; original source Peng Xiao, G42 CEO ; from gnews:01a49ffd41f6abe24538da65 2026-07-14] G42 CEO Peng Xiao said Stargate’s machines would be mostly Nvidia despite G42’s efforts to spread orders among suppliers.\\n    Quote: G42 has spent months trying to spread its orders among several suppliers, yet the machines inside Stargate would be “mostly” Nvidia, CEO Peng Xiao said in an interview in January.\",\n   \"- e434 [third_party_view; Tom's Hardware; original source Reuters ; from gnews:3221eba2826b001b12b82770 2026-07-14] Reuters said Chinese technology firms had more than 2 million Nvidia H200 chips on order about six months before 2026-07-14, exceeding Nvidia's available inventory at the time.\\n    Quote: But even with those domestic production initiatives, the Chinese hunger for AI silicon is so deep that six months ago, Reuters said the nation's tech firms had more than two million H200 chips on order, far more than what Nvidia had on hand at the time.\",\n   \"- e438 [fact; mlq.ai; original source FBI ; from gnews:ca7564a0dc63b215f5d49402 2026-07-14] The FBI published an RFI seeking market input on AI supercomputer hardware for its CJIS Division, including Nvidia Blackwell Ultra GPUs and Google TPUs; the RFI does not commit the FBI to a procurement.\\n    Quote: The FBI has published a Request for Information on SAM.gov seeking market input on AI supercomputer hardware for its Criminal Justice Information Services (CJIS) Division in Clarksburg, West Virginia. The RFI outlines four distinct categories of accelerator systems spanning training, inference, and analytics workloads — including both Nvidia Blackwell Ultra GPUs and Google TPUs [1].\",\n   \"- e439 [third_party_view; mlq.ai; original source mlq.ai 2026-07-14; from gnews:ca7564a0dc63b215f5d49402 2026-07-14] Federal AI spending obligations reached $7.2 billion in 2026, up from $675 million in 2024, while potential contract awards reached $91.8 billion, up from $4.6 billion in 2024.\\n    Quote: Federal AI spending obligations reached $7.2 billion in 2026, up from $675 million in 2024 — a 966% increase. Potential contract awards ballooned to $91.8 billion, up 1,912% from 2024's $4.6 billion [2].\",\n   \"- e440 [party_statement; Jakarta Globe; original source Airlangga Hartarto ; from gnews:e001119c6342373f6b1f3cf4 2026-07-14] Indonesia’s Chief Economic Affairs Minister Airlangga Hartarto said investors are planning data center projects with a combined capacity of about 1.3 GW, in addition to roughly 580 MW already operating; no project period was specified.\\n    Quote: Chief Economic Affairs Minister Airlangga Hartarto said investors are planning data center projects with a combined capacity of about 1.3 gigawatts (GW), on top of the roughly 580 megawatts (MW) currently in operation.\",\n   \"- e444 [rumour; Reuters; original source Unnamed sources cited by the Financial Times 2026-07-14; from gnews:dc642adc9738cb72e71bf4cd 2026-07-14] The Financial Times reported on July 14 that NVIDIA had more than halved its authorised Asian AI-chip customer list after creating a new whitelist to prevent chips reaching China.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA has more than halved the number of Asian customers authorised to buy its AI chips after creating a new “white list” of companies that have passed tougher compliance checks aimed at preventing the products from reaching China, the Financial Times reported on Monday (Jul 14).\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e415; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e445 [rumour; Reuters; original source Three unnamed people familiar with the matter, cited by the Financial Times 2026-07-14; from gnews:dc642adc9738cb72e71bf4cd 2026-07-14] Three people familiar with the matter told the Financial Times that NVIDIA intensified customer due diligence in Singapore, Malaysia and Japan over the past few months.\\n    Quote: Over the past few months, the chipmaker has intensified due diligence in Singapore, Malaysia and Japan, the report added, citing three people familiar with the matter.\",\n   \"- e446 [fact; Reuters; original source US Commerce Department ; from gnews:dc642adc9738cb72e71bf4cd 2026-07-14] The US Commerce Department issued guidance in May to curb advanced AI-chip transfers to overseas subsidiaries of Chinese companies, citing concern that Blackwell processors may have reached Chinese-linked entities in countries including Malaysia despite US restrictions.\\n    Quote: The US Commerce Department issued guidance in May aimed at curbing advanced AI chips from reaching overseas subsidiaries of Chinese companies, highlighting concerns that Nvidia’s cutting-edge Blackwell processors may have been exported to Chinese-linked entities in countries such as Malaysia despite US restrictions.\",\n   \"- e447 [rumour; Reuters; original source Unnamed sources cited by the Financial Times 2026-07-14; from gnews:dc642adc9738cb72e71bf4cd 2026-07-14] The Financial Times reported that NVIDIA tightened compliance procedures after pressure from Washington, with staff now visiting customers’ data centres, verifying contracts and interviewing end users.\\n    Quote: Nvidia has tightened compliance procedures following pressure from Washington, the FT said, adding that staff now visit customers’ data centres, verify contracts and interview end users as part of the checks.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e415; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e448 [rumour; Reuters; original source Unnamed sources cited by the Financial Times 2026-07-14; from gnews:dc642adc9738cb72e71bf4cd 2026-07-14] The Financial Times reported that the US Department of Commerce is providing oversight and political backing for the compliance checks.\\n    Quote: The US Department of Commerce is also involved, providing oversight and political backing, the report said.\"\n  ],\n  \"points_to_rule\": [\n   \"item i295\",\n   \"item i037\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"control\": 9,\n  \"ruler_question\": {\n   \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA sign a guarantee of OpenAI's Ohio data-center lease by 2027-06-30?\",\n   \"unit\": \"yes/no\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-06-30\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Yes\",\n     \"condition\": \"NVIDIA has signed the guarantee by the due day.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"No\",\n     \"condition\": \"It has not.\"\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"judged_question\": {\n   \"view_id\": \"v2\",\n   \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA sign a financial guarantee for OpenAI’s Ohio data-center lease by 2027-07-01?\",\n   \"looks_at\": \"NVIDIA guarantee for OpenAI’s Ohio data-center lease\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-07-01\",\n   \"year\": \"2027\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\"\n  },\n  \"judged_rungs\": [\n   {\n    \"position\": 1,\n    \"label\": \"No\",\n    \"condition\": \"NVIDIA has not signed the guarantee by 2027-07-01.\",\n    \"lo\": null,\n    \"hi\": null\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 2,\n    \"label\": \"Yes\",\n    \"condition\": \"NVIDIA has signed the guarantee by 2027-07-01.\",\n    \"lo\": null,\n    \"hi\": null\n   }\n  ],\n  \"reader_b_decisive_items\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i005\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-01\",\n    \"title\": \"NVIDIA is about to start taking a share of cloud providers' revenue.\",\n    \"passage\": \"NVIDIA has also recently been negotiating to provide financial guarantees for OpenAI’s lease of a large data center in Ohio\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"NVIDIA (per The Information)\",\n     \"what\": \"negotiating to guarantee OpenAI's lease of a large Ohio data center\",\n     \"how_much\": \"the data center could cost as much as $500 billion if fully built (asset cost, not the guarantee amount)\",\n     \"condition\": \"in negotiation; nothing signed\",\n     \"status\": \"rumour\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i006\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-01\",\n    \"title\": \"NVIDIA is about to start taking a share of cloud providers' revenue.\",\n    \"passage\": \"NVIDIA subsequently added another $3.5 billion to guarantee customer data center leases in exchange for rights to purchase their shares\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"NVIDIA\",\n     \"what\": \"guarantees of customer data center leases, in exchange for rights to buy their shares\",\n     \"how_much\": \"an additional $3.5 billion\",\n     \"period\": \"quarter ended April 2026 (filed May)\",\n     \"status\": \"happened\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i116\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia GPU Debt Backstop Unleashes the AI Project Trinity: Capital, Offtake and Datacenters\",\n    \"passage\": \"Nvidia is diving even deeper, as it has started backstopping datacenter leases\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"SemiAnalysis\",\n     \"what\": \"NVIDIA backstops datacenter leases for neoclouds (a second kind of obligation)\",\n     \"status\": \"happened\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i119\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia GPU Debt Backstop Unleashes the AI Project Trinity: Capital, Offtake and Datacenters\",\n    \"passage\": \"Nvidia’s backstop program is only getting started, and we see announcements coming faster every quarter. Many Neoclouds are already deep in negotiations with Nvidia\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"SemiAnalysis\",\n     \"what\": \"more NVIDIA backstops exist but are not public; many neoclouds in negotiation; announcements accelerating\",\n     \"status\": \"claim\",\n     \"status_note\": \"existing undisclosed backstops; more deals are a forecast\"\n    }\n   }\n  ],\n  \"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\": [\n   \"- e8 [rumour; moomoo.com, citing The Information; original source The Information ; from gnews:4d1677af37befd53ca3e7b45 2026-07-01] The Information previously reported that NVIDIA was negotiating to guarantee OpenAI’s lease of a large Ohio data center, whose fully built-out cost could reach $500 billion.\\n    Quote: According to prior reporting by The Information, NVIDIA has also recently been negotiating to provide financial guarantees for OpenAI’s lease of a large data center in Ohio—an asset that, if fully built out at current prices for chips, labor, power, and other materials, could cost as much as $500 billion.\",\n   \"- e15 [fact; CNBC; original source NVIDIA 2026-07-02; from gnews:d1364ee37c17c361ae74f563 2026-07-02] Nvidia announced a partnership program using AI cloud providers to give AI startups access to computing infrastructure.\\n    Quote: Chipmaker Nvidia is expanding its support for fast-growing AI startups by introducing a partnership program that leverages its network of AI cloud service providers to offer these firms access to critical computing infrastructure, the company said Thursday.\",\n   \"- e16 [fact; CNBC; original source NVIDIA 2026-07-02; from gnews:d1364ee37c17c361ae74f563 2026-07-02] Under Nvidia’s announced partnership program, cloud-based AI firms, model builders and other enterprises will share product and cloud revenue with Nvidia.\\n    Quote: Cloud-based AI firms, model builders and other enterprises will share both product and cloud revenue with Nvidia, which is positioning itself as an intermediary helping startups gain direct access to full-stack computing powered by Nvidia chips.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e10, e24, e25; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e17 [fact; CNBC; original source Sharon AI 2026-07-02; from gnews:d1364ee37c17c361ae74f563 2026-07-02] Sharon AI plans to deploy up to 40,000 Nvidia GPUs through the program.\\n    Quote: Sharon AI will deploy up to 40,000 Nvidia GPUs\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e23; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e18 [party_statement; CNBC; original source Firmus Technologies 2026-07-02; from gnews:d1364ee37c17c361ae74f563 2026-07-02] Firmus Technologies says it is building a data center in Batam, Indonesia, expected to reach 360 megawatts and house up to 170,000 Nvidia GPUs.\\n    Quote: AI infrastructure company Firmus Technologies says it is building a data center in Batam, Indonesia, which is expected to scale to 360 megawatts and house up to 170,000 Nvidia GPUs.\",\n   \"- e19 [fact; datacenterdynamics.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:c3e020d179ab025bf3ba56b0 2026-07-02] NVIDIA is acting as a financial backstop for AI-cloud customers in exchange for a share of their revenue.\\n    Quote: The chip designer is acting as a financial backstop for companies in exchange for a share in their revenue.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e1; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e20 [fact; datacenterdynamics.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:c3e020d179ab025bf3ba56b0 2026-07-02] Under the backstop, NVIDIA agrees to rent back unused GPUs from AI-cloud customers at a fixed rate.\\n    Quote: The backstop sees Nvidia agreeing to rent back unused GPUs at a fixed rate.\",\n   \"- e21 [fact; datacenterdynamics.com; original source Firmus and Sharon AI ; from gnews:c3e020d179ab025bf3ba56b0 2026-07-02] Firmus and Sharon AI are among the first companies to adopt NVIDIA's AI-cloud backstop offer.\\n    Quote: Firmus and Sharon AI are among the first companies to have adopted the offer.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e5; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e22 [fact; datacenterdynamics.com; original source Firmus ; from gnews:c3e020d179ab025bf3ba56b0 2026-07-02] Firmus is deploying 170,000 GPUs in Batam, Indonesia.\\n    Quote: Firmus is deploying 170,000 GPUs in Batam, Indonesia,\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e13; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e23 [fact; datacenterdynamics.com; original source Sharon AI ; from gnews:c3e020d179ab025bf3ba56b0 2026-07-02] Sharon AI is deploying 40,000 GB300 GPUs.\\n    Quote: Sharon AI is deploying 40,000 GB300 GPUs.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e17, e27; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e24 [party_statement; NVIDIA, in a post quoted by datacenterdynamics.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-07-02; from gnews:c3e020d179ab025bf3ba56b0 2026-07-02] NVIDIA said its new model lets AI clouds procure NVIDIA infrastructure through a revenue-sharing and credit-support model serving AI-native, enterprise, and ISV customers.\\n    Quote: This new model enables AI clouds to procure Nvidia infrastructure for AI-native, enterprise, and ISV customers through economic alignment with a revenue-sharing and credit-support model.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e16; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e25 [party_statement; NVIDIA, in a post quoted by datacenterdynamics.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-07-02; from gnews:c3e020d179ab025bf3ba56b0 2026-07-02] NVIDIA said the partnerships will generate product revenue plus a share of cloud revenue on supported capacity, creating a recurring, usage-linked earnings stream.\\n    Quote: Through the partnership, AI clouds will sell Nvidia-powered cloud services, with Nvidia earning both standard product revenue and a share of the cloud revenue on the supported capacity. This structure accelerates adoption of Nvidia platforms among the high-growth, high-conviction AI native sector, and provides Nvidia with a recurring, usage-linked earnings stream.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e16, e26; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e19 [fact; datacenterdynamics.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:c3e020d179ab025bf3ba56b0 2026-07-02] NVIDIA is acting as a financial backstop for AI-cloud customers in exchange for a share of their revenue.\\n    Quote: The chip designer is acting as a financial backstop for companies in exchange for a share in their revenue.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e1, e61; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e178 [party_statement; Futuriom, quoting NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress and VP of Global AI Clouds and Infrastructure Ecosystem Raj Mirpuri; original source NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress and VP of Global AI Clouds and Infrastructure Ecosystem Raj Mirpuri ; from gnews:cb05b9f49943ef0ba412cf36 2026-07-08] NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress and VP of Global AI Clouds and Infrastructure Ecosystem Raj Mirpuri said the new AI-cloud partnership model combines credit support and revenue sharing, with NVIDIA earning product revenue and a share of cloud revenue on supported capacity.\\n    Quote: “This new model enables AI clouds to procure NVIDIA infrastructure for AI-native, enterprise and ISV customers through economic alignment with a revenue-sharing and credit-support model. Through the partnership, AI clouds will sell NVIDIA-powered cloud services, with NVIDIA earning both standard product revenue and a share of the cloud revenue on the supported capacity. This structure accelerates \\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e44; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e179 [party_statement; Futuriom; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cb05b9f49943ef0ba412cf36 2026-07-08] NVIDIA said Sharon AI signed onto its AI-cloud plan and will buy up to 40,000 Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA states that two AI cloud providers have already signed on for the new deal: Sharon AI, based in Australia, will buy up to 40,000 NVIDIA Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs under the plan.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e37; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e180 [fact; Futuriom; original source Firmus ; from gnews:cb05b9f49943ef0ba412cf36 2026-07-08] Firmus is building a DSX AI factory in Indonesia expected to scale to 360 megawatts and contain up to 170,000 NVIDIA GPUs.\\n    Quote: Firmus, based in Indoesia, is building a DSX AI factory there that’s expected to scale to 360 megawatts and contain up to 170,000 NVIDIA GPUs.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e38; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e451 [fact; Jakarta Globe; original source Firmus Technologies and DayOne ; from gnews:e001119c6342373f6b1f3cf4 2026-07-14] Firmus Technologies and DayOne are developing NVIDIA's DSX AI Factory Campus in Batam, a planned 360 MW AI data-center complex.\\n    Quote: The Batam development marks Firmus Technologies' first data center investment in Indonesia. The Australian AI infrastructure company is partnering with Singapore-based data center operator DayOne to develop the Nvidia DSX AI Factory Campus, a 360-megawatt AI data center complex that is expected to become one of Southeast Asia's largest AI computing hubs.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e46; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e452 [third_party_view; Jakarta Globe, citing The Straits Times; original source The Straits Times ; from gnews:e001119c6342373f6b1f3cf4 2026-07-14] The Straits Times projected that the Batam campus could generate up to $30 billion in off-take agreements during its first six years of operation.\\n    Quote: According to The Straits Times , the project is projected to generate as much as $30 billion in off-take agreements during its first six years of operation.\",\n   \"- e453 [party_statement; Jakarta Globe; original source Firmus Technologies ; from gnews:e001119c6342373f6b1f3cf4 2026-07-14] Firmus plans to deploy about 170,000 NVIDIA GPUs in phases from Q1 2027 through early 2028 to provide AI computing capacity for startups and fast-growing AI companies.\\n    Quote: Under the partnership, Firmus plans to deploy about 170,000 of Nvidia's latest-generation graphics processing units (GPUs) in phases from the first quarter of 2027 through early 2028, providing AI computing capacity for startups and fast-growing AI companies.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e99; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\"\n  ],\n  \"points_to_rule\": [\n   \"same_question\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"control\": 10,\n  \"ruler_question\": {\n   \"question\": \"Will Nvidia begin shipping its Rubin generation by December 31, 2026?\",\n   \"unit\": \"yes/no\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2026-12-31\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Yes\",\n     \"condition\": \"Nvidia has begun shipping Rubin by December 31, 2026.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": null\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"No\",\n     \"condition\": \"Nvidia has not begun shipping Rubin by December 31, 2026.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": null\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"judged_question\": {\n   \"view_id\": \"v3\",\n   \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA begin shipping Rubin by 2026-12-31?\",\n   \"looks_at\": \"Whether NVIDIA begins shipping its Rubin-generation platform by the end of 2026.\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2026-12-31\",\n   \"year\": \"2026\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\"\n  },\n  \"judged_rungs\": [\n   {\n    \"position\": 1,\n    \"label\": \"Yes\",\n    \"condition\": \"NVIDIA begins shipping Rubin on or before 2026-12-31.\",\n    \"lo\": null,\n    \"hi\": null\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 2,\n    \"label\": \"No\",\n    \"condition\": \"NVIDIA has not begun shipping Rubin by 2026-12-31.\",\n    \"lo\": null,\n    \"hi\": null\n   }\n  ],\n  \"reader_b_decisive_items\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i105\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-05\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia's next-gen AI rack system delayed to 2028 on manufacturing snags, SemiAnalysis says\",\n    \"passage\": \"Nvidia's current-generation Rubin systems are in full production and begin shipping this fall to eight cloud partners\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"NVIDIA\",\n     \"what\": \"Vera Rubin systems in full production; shipping to eight cloud partners including AWS, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud\",\n     \"period\": \"this fall (2026)\",\n     \"status\": \"happened (full production); plan (shipping this fall)\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i219\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Vera Rubin rack costs $7.8M — memory is why\",\n    \"passage\": \"First shipments are scheduled for the third quarter of 2026, with volume ramping in the fourth.\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"what\": \"Vera Rubin VR200 NVL72 first shipments and volume ramp\",\n     \"period\": \"first shipments Q3 2026; volume ramp Q4 2026\",\n     \"status\": \"plan\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i202\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia's Kyber rack for Rubin Ultra reportedly delayed to 2028, stopgap solution also axed due to customer pushback — Analyst firm SemiAnalysis says PCB midplane problems led to the delay [Updated]\",\n    \"passage\": \"Nvidia's 2026 Rubin GPUs, which reuse the current Oberon rack, aren't part of the reported delay.\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"Tom's Hardware\",\n     \"what\": \"scope of the reported delay: Rubin Ultra/Kyber only; 2026 Rubin on Oberon unaffected\",\n     \"period\": \"2026\",\n     \"status\": \"claim\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i207\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Delays Next-Generation Kyber Server Architecture as Manufacturing Hurdles Give Rivals a Rare Opening\",\n    \"passage\": \"the company’s current-generation Rubin systems are already in full production and set to start shipping this fall to eight major cloud partners, including Amazon Web Services, Microsoft Azure, and Google Cloud\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"NVIDIA (as restated)\",\n     \"what\": \"Rubin systems in full production; first shipments to eight cloud partners incl. AWS, Azure, Google Cloud\",\n     \"period\": \"this fall\",\n     \"status\": \"happened\",\n     \"status_note\": \"in full production; shipping this fall is a plan\"\n    }\n   }\n  ],\n  \"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\": [\n   \"- e29 [third_party_view; fool.com; original source fool.com 2026-07-02; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] The article says NVIDIA’s Vera Rubin platform is in full production and could begin shipping in 2026.\\n    Quote: Vera Rubin, Nvidia's next-generation AI chip platform, is in full production and could begin shipping later this year.\",\n   \"- e30 [party_statement; fool.com; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang expects $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\\n    Quote: CEO Jensen Huang has laid out expectations for $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\",\n   \"- e30 [party_statement; fool.com; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang expects $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\\n    Quote: CEO Jensen Huang has laid out expectations for $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e34; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e34 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst), quoting Jensen Huang; original source Jensen Huang, NVIDIA CEO ; from gnews:e4e5f1b5c0c68381e4c486e1 2026-07-03] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang forecast $1 trillion in combined Blackwell and Vera Rubin chip sales from March through the end of 2027.\\n    Quote: In March, CEO Jensen Huang said he expects the company's Blackwell and Vera Rubin chips to generate $1 trillion in sales between that time and the end of 2027.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e30; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e39 [fact; BGR.com, reporting on NVIDIA's blog post by Josh Parker; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:a8fab49de53d125314a6688a 2026-07-04] NVIDIA announced that its DSX AI factories are hosting Rubin AI infrastructure, using a design with no fans or cold aisles.\\n    Quote: In Nvidia's blog post by Josh Parker, head of corporate sustainability at Nvidia, it was announced that Nvidia DSX AI factories are hosting Nvidia's Rubin AI infrastructure with no fans or cold aisles.\",\n   \"- e47 [rumour; CNBC; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA’s Kyber rack-scale architecture, designed for Rubin Ultra, had been delayed by more than 12 months to 2028.\\n    Quote: Nvidia 's next marquee product — the Kyber rack-scale architecture designed to house its 2027 Rubin Ultra chips — has been delayed by more than 12 months to 2028, according to research firm SemiAnalysis\",\n   \"- e48 [party_statement; CNBC, quoting NVIDIA; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] NVIDIA rejected SemiAnalysis’s report and said its product roadmap remained intact.\\n    Quote: Nvidia rejected the SemiAnalysis report and said, \\\"Our roadmap is intact.\\\"\",\n   \"- e49 [rumour; CNBC, quoting SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis said the Kyber NVL144 rack architecture was delayed to 2028 because its PCB midplane remained difficult to manufacture.\\n    Quote: \\\"Kyber NVL144 rack architecture has been delayed to 2028 as the PCB midplane remains challenging from a manufacturability standpoint,\\\" the firm said\",\n   \"- e50 [rumour; CNBC; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis said NVIDIA’s NVL576 system, which links eight racks, was likely to be delayed or produced in only small volumes.\\n    Quote: NVL576 — a larger system linking eight racks via optical connections — is also likely delayed or limited to small volumes, the research firm said.\",\n   \"- e51 [rumour; CNBC, quoting SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis said NVIDIA scrapped its backup plan to bolt two current-generation racks together after cloud providers and hyperscalers objected to the design and operating burden.\\n    Quote: A backup plan — bolting two of Nvidia's current-generation racks together for similar power — has also been scrapped after cloud customers rejected the design as awkward and costly to operate. \\\"It has since been cancelled due to heavy pushback from CSPs [cloud service providers] and hyperscalers over its odd design and heavy operational burden,\\\" SemiAnalysis said.\",\n   \"- e52 [third_party_view; CNBC, quoting SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis said NVIDIA had no proven solution to expand Rubin Ultra’s scale-up system size and that this could give AMD and Google a technical opening in the high-end market.\\n    Quote: That leaves Nvidia with \\\"no proven solution to expand the scale-up world size for Rubin Ultra,\\\" SemiAnalysis said, predicting that could give rivals Advanced Micro Devices and Google , whose in-house chips are already winning business from top AI labs, a rare technical opening at the high end of the market.\",\n   \"- e53 [fact; CNBC; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] NVIDIA’s current-generation Rubin systems were in full production and were scheduled to begin shipping in fall 2026 to eight cloud partners, including AWS, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud.\\n    Quote: Nvidia's current-generation Rubin systems are in full production and begin shipping this fall to eight cloud partners, including Amazon Web Services, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud.\",\n   \"- e55 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:2f953a56cd06571ab0afc348 2026-07-05] NVIDIA plans to launch its first stand-alone CPU this fall as part of the Vera Rubin platform.\\n    Quote: In fact, it's launching its first-ever stand-alone CPU this fall as part of the Vera Rubin platform.\",\n   \"- e51 [rumour; CNBC, quoting SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis said NVIDIA scrapped its backup plan to bolt two current-generation racks together after cloud providers and hyperscalers objected to the design and operating burden.\\n    Quote: A backup plan — bolting two of Nvidia's current-generation racks together for similar power — has also been scrapped after cloud customers rejected the design as awkward and costly to operate. \\\"It has since been cancelled due to heavy pushback from CSPs [cloud service providers] and hyperscalers over its odd design and heavy operational burden,\\\" SemiAnalysis said.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e125; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e52 [third_party_view; CNBC, quoting SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis said NVIDIA had no proven solution to expand Rubin Ultra’s scale-up system size and that this could give AMD and Google a technical opening in the high-end market.\\n    Quote: That leaves Nvidia with \\\"no proven solution to expand the scale-up world size for Rubin Ultra,\\\" SemiAnalysis said, predicting that could give rivals Advanced Micro Devices and Google , whose in-house chips are already winning business from top AI labs, a rare technical opening at the high end of the market.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e119, e120; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"