the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA had canceled the four-compute-die version of its upcoming Rubin Ultra chip.\\n    Quote: The more powerful version of the upcoming Rubin Ultra chip with four compute dies has also been canceled.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e79, e126; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e117 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis said only the two-die Rubin Ultra version remained, with roughly half the real-world compute performance of the canceled four-die version.\\n    Quote: Only the smaller two-die version remains, delivering roughly half the real-world compute performance.\",\n   \"- e118 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA's CPO-NVSwitch interconnect technology would not arrive until the Feynman generation, the generation after next.\\n    Quote: A key interconnect technology called CPO-NVSwitch, which links many chips into a single large system, won't arrive until the generation after next, called Feynman.\",\n   \"- e119 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis said NVIDIA currently lacked a proven way to scale Rubin Ultra to very large systems.\\n    Quote: That means Nvidia lacks a proven way to scale Rubin Ultra to very large systems for now.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e52; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e120 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis said the gap in NVIDIA's ability to scale Rubin Ultra could give AMD's MI500X and Google's TPUv8i Broadfly room to compete.\\n    Quote: The gap could give competitors like AMD's MI500X or Google's TPUv8i Broadfly room to move in.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e52; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e121 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA planned to offset the shortfall by selling more Oberon-Rubin racks in the existing form factor.\\n    Quote: Nvidia plans to make up for the shortfall by selling more Oberon-Rubin racks in the existing form factor.\",\n   \"- e125 [rumour; Investing.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:d5c48abb470f394f86549b6b 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis alleged that NVIDIA cancelled an alternative back-to-back rack design after operational pushback from hyperscale cloud clients.\\n    Quote: The research firm further alleged that Nvidia cancelled an alternative back-to-back rack design following heavy operational pushback from hyperscale cloud clients.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e51; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e126 [rumour; Investing.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:d5c48abb470f394f86549b6b 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis claimed NVIDIA scrapped a four-die configuration of its upcoming Rubin Ultra platform in favor of a downsized version.\\n    Quote: Additionally, the report pointed to a downsized version of the upcoming Rubin Ultra platform, claiming a crucial four-die configuration had been scrapped.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e116; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e129 [third_party_view; tikr.com (analyst); original source tikr.com (analyst) 2026-07-06; from gnews:d4c5dc540392f8df39aee250 2026-07-06] NVIDIA’s current-generation Rubin systems are in full production and are scheduled to begin shipping in fall 2026 to eight major cloud partners, including AWS, Microsoft Azure, and Google Cloud.\\n    Quote: That’s likely because the company’s current-generation Rubin systems are already in full production and set to start shipping this fall to eight major cloud partners, including Amazon Web Services, Microsoft Azure, and Google Cloud.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e53; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e278 [third_party_view; Vandita Jadeja; original source Vandita Jadeja 2026-07-10; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] The author said the $300 NVIDIA share-price case depended on Blackwell Ultra and Vera Rubin shipping on schedule, gross margins remaining at 75%, and a sovereign or hyperscaler deal being upsized.\\n    Quote: Three things need to go right: Blackwell Ultra and Vera Rubin ship on schedule, gross margins hold the 75% line, and one sovereign or hyperscaler deal gets upsized in a headline print.\",\n   \"- e350 [fact; barchart.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] NVIDIA recently launched its Vera Rubin AI platform.\\n    Quote: Nvidia recently launched its Vera Rubin AI platform, released the AI PC platform RTX Spark, expanded partnerships with companies such as Alphabet (GOOGL) and Marvell (MRVL), and further invested in networking, CPUs, and AI infrastructure.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e90 (); both are in force: Reports said NVIDIA's upcoming Vera Rubin server systems were delayed; the item does not specify the extent or timing.\",\n   \"- e351 [fact; en.sedaily.com; original source LG Electronics ; from gnews:bf96def37a9c3a5f19f5d43c 2026-07-12] LG Electronics completed a Vera Rubin-specification AI server rack prototype in the first half of 2026 and plans to seek orders after second-half reliability evaluations, with mass production planned for 2027.\\n    Quote: According to the semiconductor industry on the 12th, LG Electronics' Production Research Institute (PRI) completed development of an AI server rack prototype matching the compute tray specifications of Nvidia's \\\"Vera Rubin\\\" in the first half of the year. LG plans to secure orders from global big tech companies after reliability evaluations in the second half and begin mass production next year.\",\n   \"- e359 [party_statement; gurufocus.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:dedacecd6d2ed5192c307199 2026-07-13] NVIDIA said development of its next-generation Rubin Ultra platform remains on schedule.\\n    Quote: The company said development of its next-generation Rubin Ultra platform remains on schedule\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e90 (); both are in force: Reports said NVIDIA's upcoming Vera Rubin server systems were delayed; the item does not specify the extent or timing.\",\n   \"- e427 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com; original source 247wallst.com 2026-07-14; from gnews:ac8a489e54fbb1b85a1c7a2c 2026-07-14] NVIDIA’s Blackwell 300 was ramping, with the Vera Rubin platform queued behind it.\\n    Quote: Blackwell 300 is ramping, and the Vera Rubin platform is queued behind it.\",\n   \"- e445 [party_statement; ebc.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f83ae0a4f01c18d48f20a629 2026-07-14] NVIDIA’s Vera Rubin architecture remains on track for late-2026 delivery, according to the article.\\n    Quote: the Vera Rubin architecture remains officially on track for late 2026\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e90 (); both are in force: Reports said NVIDIA's upcoming Vera Rubin server systems were delayed; the item does not specify the extent or timing.\"\n  ],\n  \"points_to_rule\": [\n   \"item i202\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"control\": 12,\n  \"ruler_question\": {\n   \"question\": \"How much will the largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?\",\n   \"unit\": \"USD\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2028-12-31\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Below $700 billion\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is less than $700 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": 700000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"$700 billion to below $800 billion\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $700 billion and less than $800 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 700000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 800000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"$800 billion to below $900 billion\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $800 billion and less than $900 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 800000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 900000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"$900 billion to below $1000 billion\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $900 billion and less than $1000 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 900000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 1000000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"$1000 billion or more\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $1000 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 1000000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": null\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"judged_question\": {\n   \"view_id\": \"v5\",\n   \"question\": \"How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?\",\n   \"looks_at\": \"Calendar 2027 data-center capital expenditures by the four largest AI hyperscalers\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2028-03-31\",\n   \"year\": \"2027\",\n   \"kind\": \"theme\"\n  },\n  \"judged_rungs\": [\n   {\n    \"position\": 1,\n    \"label\": \"Lowest range\",\n    \"condition\": \"Combined spending is below $800 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": null,\n    \"hi\": 800000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 2,\n    \"label\": \"Lower-middle range\",\n    \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $800 billion but below $900 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": 800000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 900000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 3,\n    \"label\": \"Neutral comparison: around NVIDIA's reported $1 trillion projection\",\n    \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $900 billion but below $1.1 trillion.\",\n    \"lo\": 900000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 1100000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 4,\n    \"label\": \"Upper-middle range\",\n    \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $1.1 trillion but below $1.2 trillion.\",\n    \"lo\": 1100000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 1200000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 5,\n    \"label\": \"Highest range\",\n    \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $1.2 trillion.\",\n    \"lo\": 1200000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": null\n   }\n  ],\n  \"reader_b_decisive_items\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i256\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-07\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Stock Is Down 17% From Its High. Is the Artificial Intelligence (AI) Leader Finally Cheap?\",\n    \"passage\": \"This year, the big four AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures . Next year, Nvidia claims this group will spend more than $1 trillion.\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"big four AI hyperscalers' own plans (2026); NVIDIA's claim (2027)\",\n     \"what\": \"data-center capital expenditure of the big four\",\n     \"how_much\": \"around $650bn (2026); more than $1 trillion (2027)\",\n     \"period\": \"calendar 2026; calendar 2027\",\n     \"status\": \"plan (2026); forecast by NVIDIA (2027)\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i090\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-04\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Stock Is Nearly Flat for 2026. Time to Cash Out, or Load Up on Shares?\",\n    \"passage\": \"Wall Street analysts project 82% revenue growth for this year and 41% next year\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"Wall Street analysts\",\n     \"what\": \"NVIDIA revenue growth forecast\",\n     \"how_much\": \"82% this year; 41% next year\",\n     \"period\": \"this year and next year (fiscal or calendar both accepted, D233)\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i143\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"How Nvidia Became The Black Sheep Of The Chip Stock Rally\",\n    \"passage\": \"Some estimates put half of all data center spend going toward memory in 2027.\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"unnamed estimates\",\n     \"what\": \"memory's share of data center spend\",\n     \"how_much\": \"about half\",\n     \"period\": \"2027\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i161\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"CAPITAL IDEAS: The lag 7 — Is Micron the new Nvidia?\",\n    \"passage\": \"Goldman Sachs estimates annual AI infrastructure capital expenditures could reach $765 billion in 2026 and grow to $1.6 trillion by 2031\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"Goldman Sachs estimate\",\n     \"what\": \"annual AI infrastructure capex (chips, data centers, power, cooling, networking)\",\n     \"how_much\": \"$765B (2026); $1.6T (2031); ~$7.6T cumulative 2026-2031\",\n     \"period\": \"2026; 2031; 2026-2031\",\n     \"condition\": \"could reach\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   }\n  ],\n  \"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\": [\n   \"- e41 [party_statement; fool.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568 2026-07-04] NVIDIA projects that the four largest AI hyperscalers' data-center capital expenditures could reach $1 trillion in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: Next year, Nvidia projects that this figure could reach $1 trillion.\",\n   \"- e41 [party_statement; fool.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568 2026-07-04] NVIDIA projects that the four largest AI hyperscalers' data-center capital expenditures could reach $1 trillion in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: Next year, Nvidia projects that this figure could reach $1 trillion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e80; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e80 [party_statement; fool.com analyst; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:71df54965281684cc500960f 2026-07-06] NVIDIA management forecast that hyperscaler spending would exceed $1 trillion in 2027, after reaching a projected $650 billion in 2026.\\n    Quote: During its last quarterly conference call, management forecast that it expects hyperscaler spending to top $1 trillion in 2027 after reaching a projected $650 billion in 2026 .\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e41; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e80 [party_statement; fool.com analyst; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:71df54965281684cc500960f 2026-07-06] NVIDIA management forecast that hyperscaler spending would exceed $1 trillion in 2027, after reaching a projected $650 billion in 2026.\\n    Quote: During its last quarterly conference call, management forecast that it expects hyperscaler spending to top $1 trillion in 2027 after reaching a projected $650 billion in 2026 .\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e41, e149; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e149 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f8191f5bb960d79e47c73d6c 2026-07-07] NVIDIA says the four largest AI hyperscalers will spend more than $1 trillion on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: Next year, Nvidia claims this group will spend more than $1 trillion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e80; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e152 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-07-07; from gnews:d0f3f83296df884fae64921e 2026-07-07] The author estimates that AI hyperscalers plan to spend $650 billion on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026.\\n    Quote: While the AI hyperscalers plan to spend $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year, next year that figure could be over $1 trillion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e40; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e280 [third_party_view; gurufocus.com; original source gurufocus.com 2026-07-10; from gnews:4c201dc59ba0c7579bfef4db 2026-07-10] GuruFocus reports analysts expect NVIDIA’s share within Meta to decline while major cloud providers’ overall AI capital expenditures rise significantly.\\n    Quote: However, analysts remain optimistic about NVIDIA's future, suggesting that while its share within Meta may decline, overall AI capital expenditures from major cloud service providers are expected to rise significantly.\",\n   \"- e152 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-07-07; from gnews:d0f3f83296df884fae64921e 2026-07-07] The author estimates that AI hyperscalers plan to spend $650 billion on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026.\\n    Quote: While the AI hyperscalers plan to spend $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year, next year that figure could be over $1 trillion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e40, e315; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e315 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:07cf5835d106467db5448c13 2026-07-12] NVIDIA told investors last quarter that it expects AI hyperaccelerator spending to exceed $1 trillion next year.\\n    Quote: Nvidia told investors last quarter that it expects AI hyperaccelerator spending to rise to over $1 trillion next year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e152; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e316 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-07-12; from gnews:07cf5835d106467db5448c13 2026-07-12] The author estimates that NVIDIA likely already has orders on the books for next year, giving it visibility into demand.\\n    Quote: I'm more inclined to believe Nvidia over the market's skepticism, as it likely has orders on the books for next year, so it can easily see the demand already.\",\n   \"- e149 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f8191f5bb960d79e47c73d6c 2026-07-07] NVIDIA says the four largest AI hyperscalers will spend more than $1 trillion on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: Next year, Nvidia claims this group will spend more than $1 trillion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e80, e390; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e390 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com, reporting Morgan Stanley’s forecast; original source Morgan Stanley ; from gnews:e0e5ab6c2aced8d5a6a688a5 2026-07-13] Morgan Stanley forecasts that Google, Amazon, Microsoft, and Meta will spend over $1 trillion on AI infrastructure in calendar 2027 and add 19.5 GW of incremental compute capacity that year.\\n    Quote: The analyst says Google, Amazon, Microsoft, and Meta are forecast to spend over $1 trillion on AI infrastructure next year, adding 19.5 gigawatts (GW) of incremental compute capacity.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e149; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\"\n  ],\n  \"points_to_rule\": [\n   \"same_question\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"control\": 14,\n  \"ruler_question\": {\n   \"question\": \"Will Nvidia begin shipping its Rubin generation by December 31, 2026?\",\n   \"unit\": \"yes/no\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2026-12-31\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Yes\",\n     \"condition\": \"Nvidia has begun shipping Rubin by December 31, 2026.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": null\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"No\",\n     \"condition\": \"Nvidia has not begun shipping Rubin by December 31, 2026.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": null\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"judged_question\": {\n   \"view_id\": \"v3\",\n   \"question\": \"Will Nvidia's Rubin platform begin shipping by December 31, 2026?\",\n   \"looks_at\": \"Whether Nvidia's Rubin platform begins shipping by the end of 2026.\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2026-12-31\",\n   \"year\": \"2026\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\"\n  },\n  \"judged_rungs\": [\n   {\n    \"position\": 1,\n    \"label\": \"Yes\",\n    \"condition\": \"Nvidia begins shipping the Rubin platform on or before December 31, 2026.\",\n    \"lo\": null,\n    \"hi\": null\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 2,\n    \"label\": \"No\",\n    \"condition\": \"Nvidia has not begun shipping the Rubin platform by December 31, 2026.\",\n    \"lo\": null,\n    \"hi\": null\n   }\n  ],\n  \"reader_b_decisive_items\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i105\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-05\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia's next-gen AI rack system delayed to 2028 on manufacturing snags, SemiAnalysis says\",\n    \"passage\": \"Nvidia's current-generation Rubin systems are in full production and begin shipping this fall to eight cloud partners\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"NVIDIA\",\n     \"what\": \"Vera Rubin systems in full production; shipping to eight cloud partners including AWS, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud\",\n     \"period\": \"this fall (2026)\",\n     \"status\": \"happened (full production); plan (shipping this fall)\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i219\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Vera Rubin rack costs $7.8M — memory is why\",\n    \"passage\": \"First shipments are scheduled for the third quarter of 2026, with volume ramping in the fourth.\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"what\": \"Vera Rubin VR200 NVL72 first shipments and volume ramp\",\n     \"period\": \"first shipments Q3 2026; volume ramp Q4 2026\",\n     \"status\": \"plan\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i202\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia's Kyber rack for Rubin Ultra reportedly delayed to 2028, stopgap solution also axed due to customer pushback — Analyst firm SemiAnalysis says PCB midplane problems led to the delay [Updated]\",\n    \"passage\": \"Nvidia's 2026 Rubin GPUs, which reuse the current Oberon rack, aren't part of the reported delay.\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"Tom's Hardware\",\n     \"what\": \"scope of the reported delay: Rubin Ultra/Kyber only; 2026 Rubin on Oberon unaffected\",\n     \"period\": \"2026\",\n     \"status\": \"claim\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i207\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Delays Next-Generation Kyber Server Architecture as Manufacturing Hurdles Give Rivals a Rare Opening\",\n    \"passage\": \"the company’s current-generation Rubin systems are already in full production and set to start shipping this fall to eight major cloud partners, including Amazon Web Services, Microsoft Azure, and Google Cloud\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"NVIDIA (as restated)\",\n     \"what\": \"Rubin systems in full production; first shipments to eight cloud partners incl. AWS, Azure, Google Cloud\",\n     \"period\": \"this fall\",\n     \"status\": \"happened\",\n     \"status_note\": \"in full production; shipping this fall is a plan\"\n    }\n   }\n  ],\n  \"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\": [\n   \"- e24 [third_party_view; fool.com (Justin Pope); original source fool.com (Justin Pope) 2026-07-02; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] The author says Vera Rubin is in full production and could begin shipping later in 2026.\\n    Quote: Vera Rubin, Nvidia's next-generation AI chip platform, is in full production and could begin shipping later this year.\",\n   \"- e57 [fact; CNBC; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] Nvidia’s current-generation Rubin systems are in full production and are scheduled to begin shipping in fall 2026 to eight cloud partners, including AWS, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud.\\n    Quote: Nvidia's current-generation Rubin systems are in full production and begin shipping this fall to eight cloud partners, including Amazon Web Services, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud.\",\n   \"- e59 [party_statement; fool.com analyst; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:2f953a56cd06571ab0afc348 2026-07-05] Nvidia plans to launch its first stand-alone CPU as part of the Vera Rubin platform in fall 2026.\\n    Quote: In fact, it's launching its first-ever stand-alone CPU this fall as part of the Vera Rubin platform.\",\n   \"- e60 [party_statement; fool.com analyst; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:2f953a56cd06571ab0afc348 2026-07-05] Nvidia plans to release a personal-computing superchip that combines a GPU and a CPU in fall 2026.\\n    Quote: And at the same time, Nvidia is targeting the personal computing market with a superchip -- also set for fall release -- that includes a GPU and a CPU.\",\n   \"- e64 [rumour; finance.yahoo.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:68a3ed21f77b935d9fa7ec5e 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis claimed the Rubin Ultra high-density rack design was delayed by more than 12 months because of persistent manufacturing problems with its PCB midplane.\\n    Quote: SemiAnalysis claims the high-density rack design built for Rubin Ultra GPUs has slipped by more than 12 months. The firm blamed persistent manufacturing problems with the system's complex PCB midplane.\",\n   \"- e65 [rumour; finance.yahoo.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:68a3ed21f77b935d9fa7ec5e 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis claimed Nvidia scrapped its NVL72x2 back-to-back rack after hyperscaler customers pushed back.\\n    Quote: The firm also claimed Nvidia scrapped its NVL72x2 back-to-back rack after pushback from hyperscaler customers.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e54, e130, e145, e146; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e66 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:68a3ed21f77b935d9fa7ec5e 2026-07-06] Nvidia told media outlets that its roadmap remains intact, rejecting claims of delays to its next-generation AI rack systems.\\n    Quote: Nvidia rejected the claims, telling media outlets that its roadmap remains intact.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e56, e90, e134; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e80 [third_party_view; MarketScale; original source Morgan Stanley Research ; from gnews:f66e1689ec2e27e7eab2a2dd 2026-07-06] Morgan Stanley estimated the Vera Rubin VR200 NVL72 rack would cost hyperscale cloud providers about $7.8 million per unit, versus about $4 million for the GB300 NVL72.\\n    Quote: Morgan Stanley Research estimates that Nvidia 's Vera Rubin VR200 NVL72 rack will cost hyperscale cloud providers around $7.8 million per unit, up from roughly $4 million for the current GB300 NVL72 generation.\",\n   \"- e81 [third_party_view; MarketScale; original source Morgan Stanley Research ; from gnews:f66e1689ec2e27e7eab2a2dd 2026-07-06] Morgan Stanley estimated Nvidia would charge about $55,000 per Rubin GPU and $5,000 per Vera CPU at volume.\\n    Quote: The bank estimates Nvidia will charge about $55,000 per Rubin GPU and $5,000 per Vera CPU when sold in volume.\",\n   \"- e82 [third_party_view; MarketScale; original source Morgan Stanley Research ; from gnews:f66e1689ec2e27e7eab2a2dd 2026-07-06] Morgan Stanley estimated memory content in a Vera Rubin rack at about $2 million, up 435% from the prior generation, including roughly $1 million or more of 3D NAND storage.\\n    Quote: Morgan Stanley puts memory content per rack at about $2 million, a 435% jump from the prior generation, driven by a threefold increase in LPDDR5X capacity to 54 terabytes per rack plus roughly $1 million or more in 3D NAND storage that was virtually absent from earlier systems.\",\n   \"- e83 [third_party_view; MarketScale; original source Morgan Stanley Research ; from gnews:f66e1689ec2e27e7eab2a2dd 2026-07-06] The article reported Morgan Stanley's estimate that memory's share of the bill of materials rose from 5–10% on GB200 to 25–30% on VR200, while the GPU share fell from about 63% to 51%.\\n    Quote: As a share of the bill of materials, memory rose from 5 to 10 percent on the GB200 to 25 to 30 percent on the VR200, while the GPU's share fell from roughly 63 percent to 51 percent.\",\n   \"- e84 [third_party_view; MarketScale; original source MarketScale 2026-07-06; from gnews:f66e1689ec2e27e7eab2a2dd 2026-07-06] First shipments of Nvidia's Vera Rubin VR200 NVL72 rack were scheduled for Q3 2026, with volume ramping in Q4 2026.\\n    Quote: First shipments are scheduled for the third quarter of 2026, with volume ramping in the fourth.\",\n   \"- e85 [third_party_view; MarketScale; original source Morgan Stanley Research ; from gnews:f66e1689ec2e27e7eab2a2dd 2026-07-06] Morgan Stanley estimated that hyperscalers self-sourcing certain memory modules could reduce the Vera Rubin rack price to around $6.7 million.\\n    Quote: Morgan Stanley notes that a hyperscaler self-sourcing certain memory modules could bring the rack price down to around $6.7 million, a reminder that procurement structure now materially moves the number.\",\n   \"- e86 [rumour; datacenterdynamics.com, reporting SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:98a4e8ff0c0260d8dc9e531d 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia delayed production of its Kyber rack-scale architecture by more than 12 months, pushing its release to 2028.\\n    Quote: Nvidia has delayed production of its Kyber rack-scale architecture by more than 12 months, pushing its release date to 2028, SemiAnalysis has reported.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e144; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e87 [rumour; datacenterdynamics.com, quoting SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:98a4e8ff0c0260d8dc9e531d 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis said Kyber NVL144 was delayed to 2028 because of PCB midplane manufacturing challenges, and Nvidia scrapped its alternative two-Oberon-rack design after cloud companies and hyperscalers objected to it.\\n    Quote: “Kyber NVL144 rack architecture has been delayed to 2028 as the PCB midplane remains challenging from a manufacturability standpoint,” SemiAnalysis said, adding that Nvidia’s alternative plan, which involved placing two Oberon racks back-to-back in order to achieve a similar power output, has also been scrapped after cloud companies and hyperscalers pushed back against its “odd design and heavy op\",\n   \"- e88 [rumour; datacenterdynamics.com, reporting SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:98a4e8ff0c0260d8dc9e531d 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis said manufacturing issues would likely delay Nvidia’s planned NVL576 system or limit it to small volumes.\\n    Quote: The manufacturing issues will also impact the planned NVL576 system, which connects 8x Oberon racks over CPO between the NVSwitches, meaning that the system will also likely be delayed or limited to small volumes, the firm noted.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e147; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e89 [rumour; datacenterdynamics.com, reporting SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:98a4e8ff0c0260d8dc9e531d 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia canceled the four-die Rubin Ultra design in favor of a two-chiplet design because of manufacturing execution concerns.\\n    Quote: The news comes a week after SemiAnalysis separately reported that Nvidia had canceled the four-die Rubin Ultra design in favor of the two-chiplet design, also due to “manufacturing execution concerns.”\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e131, e148; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e90 [party_statement; Nvidia spokesperson, quoted by datacenterdynamics.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:98a4e8ff0c0260d8dc9e531d 2026-07-06] An Nvidia spokesperson said the company’s roadmap was intact in response to questions about the Kyber claims.\\n    Quote: In response to a request for comment from DCD regarding the Kyber claims, a spokesperson for Nvidia said: \\\"Our roadmap is intact.\\\"\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e66; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e97 [rumour; Danielle Liverance; original source Danielle Liverance 2026-07-06; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] The author reported that NVIDIA’s upcoming Vera Rubin server systems were reportedly delayed; no timing or scale was specified.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA shares are under pressure on reports of delays across their upcoming lineup of Vera Rubin server systems.\",\n   \"- e131 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia canceled the four-die Rubin Ultra version, leaving only the two-die version, which it said delivers roughly half the real-world compute performance.\\n    Quote: The more powerful version of the upcoming Rubin Ultra chip with four compute dies has also been canceled. Only the smaller two-die version remains, delivering roughly half the real-world compute performance.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e89, e135; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e134 [party_statement; NVIDIA spokesperson, in a statement emailed to Investing.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-07-06; from gnews:d5c48abb470f394f86549b6b 2026-07-06] An NVIDIA spokesperson said the company's product roadmap remained intact.\\n    Quote: Our roadmap is intact.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e66, e149; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e135 [rumour; Investing.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:d5c48abb470f394f86549b6b 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis claimed that NVIDIA had scrapped a four-die configuration for the upcoming Rubin Ultra platform and would use a downsized version instead.\\n    Quote: Additionally, the report pointed to a downsized version of the upcoming Rubin Ultra platform, claiming a crucial four-die configuration had been scrapped.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e131; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e138 [party_statement; Investing.com, reporting Mizuho analyst Jordan Klein's note; original source Hon Hai Precision Industry management 2026-07-03; from gnews:d5c48abb470f394f86549b6b 2026-07-06] Hon Hai management forecast continued acceleration in AI demand; Mizuho analyst Jordan Klein said this was a positive sign ahead of NVIDIA's Vera Rubin rack launch.\\n    Quote: Klein noted that Hon Hai management forecasted a continued acceleration in AI demand, which the analyst said was \\\"a very good sign into the NVDA launch of their new Vera Rubin rack.\\\"\",\n   \"- e144 [rumour; Tom's Hardware, reporting SemiAnalysis's X thread; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:c75f16a6d64cc27fc28fb571 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia’s Kyber NVL144 rack for Rubin Ultra would not ship until 2028, more than 12 months later than planned.\\n    Quote: Nvidia reportedly won't ship its Kyber NVL144 rack until 2028, a delay of more than 12 months that pushes the cabinet meant for 2027's Rubin Ultra GPUs into the following year, according to a SemiAnalysis thread on X.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e86; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e145 [rumour; Tom's Hardware; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:c75f16a6d64cc27fc28fb571 2026-07-06] Nvidia reportedly abandoned the NVL72x2 stopgap rack intended to provide Rubin Ultra scale-up in 2027; the report says no proven alternative is available.\\n    Quote: Nvidia is also understood to have killed NVL72x2, a stopgap rack designed to tide customers over, and that no proven alternative is now available to widen Rubin Ultra's scale-up in 2027.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e65; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e146 [rumour; Tom's Hardware, reporting SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:c75f16a6d64cc27fc28fb571 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis said Nvidia’s largest customers objected to operating two linked Oberon racks as one unit, prompting Nvidia to abandon the NVL72x2 stopgap for Rubin Ultra scale-up.\\n    Quote: NVL72x2 would have bolted two Oberon racks back-to-back to reach Kyber-class density over copper NVLink, per SemiAnalysis, which said Nvidia abandoned the stopgap after its largest customers balked at running two linked cabinets as a single unit.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e65; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e147 [third_party_view; Tom's Hardware; original source Tom's Hardware 2026-07-06; from gnews:c75f16a6d64cc27fc28fb571 2026-07-06] Tom's Hardware reported that the NVL576 configuration for Rubin Ultra may be delayed or ship in low volumes until co-packaged optics matures.\\n    Quote: NVL576, a separate configuration tying eight racks together through co-packaged optics, is likely to slip too or ship in low volume until that optical technology matures.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e88; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e148 [rumour; Tom's Hardware; original source Tom's Hardware ; from gnews:c75f16a6d64cc27fc28fb571 2026-07-06] Nvidia reportedly changed Rubin Ultra from a quad-chiplet GPU to a dual-chiplet part the week before publication, halving per-package compute because of manufacturing execution concerns.\\n    Quote: Nvidia dropped the quad-chiplet Rubin Ultra GPU for a dual-chiplet part last week over manufacturing execution concerns, halving the accelerator's per-package compute.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e89; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e149 [party_statement; Nvidia representative, quoted by Tom's Hardware; original source NVIDIA 2026-07-06; from gnews:c75f16a6d64cc27fc28fb571 2026-07-06] An Nvidia representative said the company’s roadmap was intact in response to Tom's Hardware; the company gave no further details.\\n    Quote: An Nvidia representative responded with a short statement to Tom's Hardware : \\\"Our roadmap is intact.\\\"\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e134; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e202 [rumour; The Straits Times; original source The Straits Times 2026-07-08; from gnews:c8c39f971721fd820aab5c1c 2026-07-08] Nvidia is reported to be working toward releasing its Rubin lineup in the second half of 2026.\\n    Quote: Nvidia is now working to release an even more powerful line-up called Rubin in the second half of 2026 .\",\n   \"- e223 [third_party_view; Investing.com, reporting Vivek Arya's note; original source Vivek Arya, Bank of America 2026-07-08; from gnews:266c882eea8c686ee7aafac7 2026-07-08] Bank of America analyst Vivek Arya estimated that HBM content per rack may increase by $0.2–0.3 million from Blackwell to Rubin, while rack pricing could increase by $2–3 million because of compute, networking, and software upgrades.\\n    Quote: While HBM content per rack may rise by approximately $0.2-0.3 million from Blackwell to Rubin, Arya noted that rack pricing could increase by $2-3 million, driven by upgrades across compute, networking and software.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e230; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e230 [third_party_view; moomoo.com; original source BofA ; from gnews:1b5a3359dd0644861c0fce42 2026-07-08] BofA estimated HBM content per rack could increase by $0.2 million to $0.3 million from Blackwell to Rubin, while total rack pricing could rise from about $3 million–$4 million to $6 million–$7 million.\\n    Quote: The report estimates HBM content per rack could rise by about $0.2 million to $0.3 million from Blackwell to Rubin, while total rack pricing could increase by $2 million to $3 million, from roughly $3 million to $4 million for Blackwell to $6 million to $7 million for Vera Rubin.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e223; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e66 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:68a3ed21f77b935d9fa7ec5e 2026-07-06] Nvidia told media outlets that its roadmap remains intact, rejecting claims of delays to its next-generation AI rack systems.\\n    Quote: Nvidia rejected the claims, telling media outlets that its roadmap remains intact.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e56, e90, e134, e270; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e270 [party_statement; moomoo.com, reporting NVIDIA’s statement to Bloomberg; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:7b39859113d4e2b8ebd8aa86 2026-07-09] NVIDIA told Bloomberg that it had no technical delay and that its product roadmap remained intact.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA recently issued a statement to Bloomberg denying claims of a technical delay, confirming that its product roadmap remains intact.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e66; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e353 [fact; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] Nvidia recently launched its Vera Rubin AI platform.\\n    Quote: Nvidia recently launched its Vera Rubin AI platform, released the AI PC platform RTX Spark, expanded partnerships with companies such as Alphabet (GOOGL) and Marvell (MRVL), and further invested in networking, CPUs, and AI infrastructure.\",\n   \"- e354 [rumour; en.sedaily.com; original source Unnamed semiconductor-industry sources, as reported by en.sedaily.com 2026-07-12; from gnews:bf96def37a9c3a5f19f5d43c 2026-07-12] LG Electronics completed a Vera Rubin-specification AI server rack prototype in the first half of 2026 and plans to seek orders after second-half reliability evaluations and begin mass production in 2027.\\n    Quote: According to the semiconductor industry on the 12th, LG Electronics' Production Research Institute (PRI) completed development of an AI server rack prototype matching the compute tray specifications of Nvidia's \\\"Vera Rubin\\\" in the first half of the year. LG plans to secure orders from global big tech companies after reliability evaluations in the second half and begin mass production next year.\",\n   \"- e66 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:68a3ed21f77b935d9fa7ec5e 2026-07-06] Nvidia told media outlets that its roadmap remains intact, rejecting claims of delays to its next-generation AI rack systems.\\n    Quote: Nvidia rejected the claims, telling media outlets that its roadmap remains intact.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e56, e90, e134, e270, e364; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e364 [party_statement; gurufocus.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:dedacecd6d2ed5192c307199 2026-07-13] Nvidia said development of its Rubin Ultra platform remains on schedule.\\n    Quote: The company said development of its next-generation Rubin Ultra platform remains on schedule\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e66; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e24 [third_party_view; fool.com (Justin Pope); original source fool.com (Justin Pope) 2026-07-02; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] The author says Vera Rubin is in full production and could begin shipping later in 2026.\\n    Quote: Vera Rubin, Nvidia's next-generation AI chip platform, is in full production and could begin shipping later this year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e456; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e456 [third_party_view; ebc.com; original source ebc.com 2026-07-14; from gnews:f83ae0a4f01c18d48f20a629 2026-07-14] Nvidia’s Vera Rubin architecture remains on track for shipment in late 2026, according to the article.\\n    Quote: the Vera Rubin architecture remains officially on track for late 2026\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e24; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\"\n  ],\n  \"points_to_rule\": [\n   \"item i202\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"control\": 15,\n  \"ruler_question\": {\n   \"question\": \"What will Nvidia's total revenue be in FY2027?\",\n   \"unit\": \"USD\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $500 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 500000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": null\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $400 billion and below $500 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 400000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 500000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $350 billion and below $400 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 350000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 400000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $300 billion and below $350 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 300000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 350000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is below $300 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": 300000000000.0\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"judged_question\": {\n   \"view_id\": \"v4\",\n   \"question\": \"What will Nvidia's total revenue be in FY2027?\",\n   \"looks_at\": \"Nvidia total revenue in FY2027.\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\",\n   \"year\": \"FY2027\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\"\n  },\n  \"judged_rungs\": [\n   {\n    \"position\": 1,\n    \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n    \"condition\": \"Total revenue is above $430 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": 430000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": null\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 2,\n    \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n    \"condition\": \"Total revenue is above $392 billion and at or below $430 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": 392000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 430000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 3,\n    \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n    \"condition\": \"Total revenue is at or below $392 billion and at or above $350 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": 350000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 392000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 4,\n    \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n    \"condition\": \"Total revenue is below $350 billion and at or above $300 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": 300000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 350000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 5,\n    \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n    \"condition\": \"Total revenue is below $300 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": null,\n    \"hi\": 300000000000.0\n   }\n  ],\n  \"reader_b_decisive_items\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i281\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-09\",\n    \"title\": \"DeepSeek Just Dealt Nvidia Stock a Potentially Major Blow\",\n    \"passage\": \"forecasting revenue of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%, and a non-GAAP gross margin of about 75%\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"NVIDIA\",\n     \"what\": \"Q2 FY2027 revenue and gross-margin guidance\",\n     \"how_much\": \"$91 billion ±2%; non-GAAP gross margin about 75%\",\n     \"period\": \"Q2 FY2027\",\n     \"condition\": \"assumes no China Data Center compute revenue\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i295\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-10\",\n    \"title\": \"Here are Friday's biggest analyst calls: Nvidia, SpaceX, Toll, Shopify, Twilio, Seagate, Chipotle & more\",\n    \"passage\": \"the company describing \\\"accelerating growth rates\\\" even as revenues approach the $100 bn per quarter mark\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"NVIDIA management, relayed by Morgan Stanley\",\n     \"what\": \"revenue growth rates accelerating\",\n     \"how_much\": \"quarterly revenue approaching $100 bn\",\n     \"status\": \"claim\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i106\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-05\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia's next-gen AI rack system delayed to 2028 on manufacturing snags, SemiAnalysis says\",\n    \"passage\": \"SemiAnalysis also projects Nvidia's data-center compute revenue will run 20% above Wall Street consensus in the second half of fiscal 2027\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"SemiAnalysis\",\n     \"what\": \"NVIDIA data-center compute revenue versus Wall Street consensus\",\n     \"how_much\": \"20% above consensus\",\n     \"period\": \"second half of fiscal 2027\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i219\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Vera Rubin rack costs $7.8M — memory is why\",\n    \"passage\": \"First shipments are scheduled for the third quarter of 2026, with volume ramping in the fourth.\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"what\": \"Vera Rubin VR200 NVL72 first shipments and volume ramp\",\n     \"period\": \"first shipments Q3 2026; volume ramp Q4 2026\",\n     \"status\": \"plan\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i037\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-02\",\n    \"title\": \"Microsoft vs. Nvidia: Which Is the Better AI Stock to Own for the Next 3 Years?\",\n    \"passage\": \"from trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion to $392 billion this fiscal year, and $554 billion the following year\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"Wall Street analysts\",\n     \"what\": \"NVIDIA total revenue estimates\",\n     \"how_much\": \"$392 billion this fiscal year, $554 billion next year (from $253 billion trailing twelve months)\",\n     \"period\": \"this fiscal year (FY2027) and the following year (FY2028)\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   }\n  ],\n  \"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\": [\n   \"- e25 [party_statement; fool.com (Justin Pope); original source Jensen Huang, Nvidia CEO ; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] The author reports that Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang expects $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\\n    Quote: CEO Jensen Huang has laid out expectations for $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\",\n   \"- e26 [third_party_view; fool.com (Justin Pope); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] Wall Street analysts estimate Nvidia revenue of $392 billion in FY2027.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts estimate that Nvidia's business could double over the next couple of years, from trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion to $392 billion this fiscal year, and $554 billion the following year.\",\n   \"- e25 [party_statement; fool.com (Justin Pope); original source Jensen Huang, Nvidia CEO ; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] The author reports that Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang expects $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\\n    Quote: CEO Jensen Huang has laid out expectations for $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e35; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e30 [fact; storagereview.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-07-01; from gnews:8c9d215416b714064de3b095 2026-07-03] NVIDIA removed the AI Enterprise subscription requirement for Omniverse production use and redistribution; the change was announced July 1, 2026, and the licensing documentation says it took effect in May 2026.\\n    Quote: The new terms remove that requirement entirely; anything built with Omniverse can also be redistributed under the same free terms, which is a substantive impact for ISVs and integrators who embed Omniverse applications inside their own products.\",\n   \"- e31 [third_party_view; storagereview.com; original source storagereview.com 2026-07-03; from gnews:8c9d215416b714064de3b095 2026-07-03] The Mercedes-Benz CLA with NVIDIA's DRIVE platform reached the US market in 2026, described as the platform's first production deployment.\\n    Quote: The first production deployment, the Mercedes-Benz CLA on the DRIVE platform, reached the US market this year.\",\n   \"- e33 [party_statement; Ben Wodecki, SDxCentral, recounting Aldo Kamper's remarks to investors; original source Aldo Kamper, AMS-Osram CEO ; from gnews:1740f3733eedc34d8bac9b65 2026-07-03] AMS-Osram CEO Aldo Kamper said the company was working toward developing microLED optical interconnects for inside racks and for chip-to-chip communication between GPUs and high-bandwidth memory.\\n    Quote: AMS-Osram’s efforts, meanwhile, will see work toward developing microLED optical interconnects for inside the rack as well as chip-to-chip communication between graphic processing units (GPUs) and high-bandwidth memory, CEO Aldo Kamper told investors during its Q1 2026 earnings call back in May.\",\n   \"- e34 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:e4e5f1b5c0c68381e4c486e1 2026-07-03] Nvidia’s revenue grew 85% year over year in fiscal Q1 2027.\\n    Quote: In the first quarter of Nvidia's fiscal year 2027, ending April 26, the company grew revenue 85% year over year\",\n   \"- e35 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Jensen Huang, Nvidia CEO ; from gnews:e4e5f1b5c0c68381e4c486e1 2026-07-03] In March, CEO Jensen Huang expected Nvidia’s Blackwell and Vera Rubin chips to generate $1 trillion in sales from then through the end of 2027.\\n    Quote: In March, CEO Jensen Huang said he expects the company's Blackwell and Vera Rubin chips to generate $1 trillion in sales between that time and the end of 2027.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e25; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e36 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia management ; from gnews:e4e5f1b5c0c68381e4c486e1 2026-07-03] Nvidia management said it thinks the company can generate nearly $20 billion in CPU sales; no period was specified.\\n    Quote: Management said they think they can generate nearly $20 billion of CPU sales, making it an instant industry leader.\",\n   \"- e37 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source Palantir and NVIDIA ; from gnews:bdcb0ed0921c2e9ae241083c 2026-07-03] Palantir is making a deal to use NVIDIA's Nemotron to build government AI models; no amount or timing is specified.\\n    Quote: With Palantir now inking a deal to use Nvidia's Nemotron to build models for the government\",\n   \"- e38 [third_party_view; Jim Cramer, as quoted by finance.yahoo.com; original source Google and Amazon, as reported by Jim Cramer ; from gnews:a96a4cbf6aae35d01d0d285b 2026-07-03] Jim Cramer said Google and Amazon claim their chips are better than NVIDIA’s, despite using NVIDIA products.\\n    Quote: The first two claim that they have better chips than NVIDIA, even as they use NVIDIA.\",\n   \"- e39 [party_statement; Jim Cramer, as quoted by finance.yahoo.com; original source Hock Tan, Broadcom CEO ; from gnews:a96a4cbf6aae35d01d0d285b 2026-07-03] Broadcom CEO Hock Tan said Broadcom can compete with NVIDIA and take share from it.\\n    Quote: Plus, there's Broadcom, vicious competitor, and CEO Hock Tan's out there saying it can compete; it can take share from NVIDIA.\",\n   \"- e43 [fact; mlq.ai; original source Sharon AI ; from gnews:9e0d5b0d6b3e603c60340128 2026-07-03] Sharon AI plans to deploy up to 40,000 NVIDIA Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs under a six-year agreement with NVIDIA.\\n    Quote: Sharon AI, which listed on the Nasdaq in February 2026 via a $125 million IPO, is deploying up to 40,000 Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs under a six-year agreement with Nvidia [2] [6] .\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e28; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e44 [fact; mlq.ai; original source Firmus Technologies ; from gnews:9e0d5b0d6b3e603c60340128 2026-07-03] Firmus Technologies is constructing a DSX-aligned campus in Batam, Indonesia, expected to scale to 360 MW and house up to 170,000 NVIDIA GPUs.\\n    Quote: Firmus Technologies, a private company, is constructing a campus in Batam, Indonesia, built to Nvidia's DGX SuperPOD (DSX) reference architecture specifications. The facility is expected to scale to 360MW and house up to 170,000 Nvidia GPUs [1] [3] .\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e5; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e44 [fact; mlq.ai; original source Firmus Technologies ; from gnews:9e0d5b0d6b3e603c60340128 2026-07-03] Firmus Technologies is constructing a DSX-aligned campus in Batam, Indonesia, expected to scale to 360 MW and house up to 170,000 NVIDIA GPUs.\\n    Quote: Firmus Technologies, a private company, is constructing a campus in Batam, Indonesia, built to Nvidia's DGX SuperPOD (DSX) reference architecture specifications. The facility is expected to scale to 360MW and house up to 170,000 Nvidia GPUs [1] [3] .\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e5, e51; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e47 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568 2026-07-04] Wall Street analysts project Nvidia revenue growth of 82% in FY2027 and 41% in FY2028.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts project 82% revenue growth for this year and 41% next year, so there's another external source that's projecting even more growth for Nvidia.\",\n   \"- e48 [third_party_view; fool.com analyst; original source fool.com analyst 2026-07-04; from gnews:068a24e2743bab750f43f048 2026-07-04] The author calculated that NVIDIA revenue increased 1,033% from Q1 2024 through Q1 FY2027, which ended April 26.\\n    Quote: Just in the last three years, from Q1 2024 to the first quarter of fiscal 2027 (ended April 26), Nvidia's revenue soared 1,033%.\",\n   \"- e50 [fact; datacenters.economictimes.indiatimes.com; original source Sharon AI ; from gnews:1e7a9c953f3ad70093b67ae4 2026-07-04] Sharon AI plans to deploy up to 40,000 NVIDIA Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs under the financing model.\\n    Quote: Sharon AI plans to deploy up to 40,000 Nvidia Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs,\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e28; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e51 [fact; datacenters.economictimes.indiatimes.com; original source Firmus ; from gnews:1e7a9c953f3ad70093b67ae4 2026-07-04] Firmus is developing a DSX AI factory campus in Batam, Indonesia, expected to reach 360 MW and accommodate up to 170,000 NVIDIA GPUs.\\n    Quote: Firmus is developing a DSX AI factory campus in Batam, Indonesia, which is expected to scale to 360 megawatts and accommodate up to 170,000 Nvidia GPUs.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e44; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e58 [third_party_view; CNBC, reporting SemiAnalysis’s projection; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis projected Nvidia data-center compute revenue in the second half of FY2027 to be 20% above Wall Street consensus.\\n    Quote: SemiAnalysis also projects Nvidia's data-center compute revenue will run 20% above Wall Street consensus in the second half of fiscal 2027.\",\n   \"- e61 [third_party_view; fool.com analyst; original source fool.com analyst 2026-07-05; from gnews:2f953a56cd06571ab0afc348 2026-07-05] The author describes Nvidia's goal as dominating a CPU market estimated at $200 billion, without specifying a period.\\n    Quote: I'll start with the goal, and this is to dominate the $200 billion CPU market -- a market where Nvidia has not been greatly present in the past.\",\n   \"- e62 [party_statement; fool.com analyst; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:2f953a56cd06571ab0afc348 2026-07-05] Nvidia forecasts $20 billion in stand-alone CPU sales in 2026.\\n    Quote: Nvidia already forecasts $20 billion in stand-alone CPU sales this year.\",\n   \"- e34 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:e4e5f1b5c0c68381e4c486e1 2026-07-03] Nvidia’s revenue grew 85% year over year in fiscal Q1 2027.\\n    Quote: In the first quarter of Nvidia's fiscal year 2027, ending April 26, the company grew revenue 85% year over year\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e95, e122; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e43 [fact; mlq.ai; original source Sharon AI ; from gnews:9e0d5b0d6b3e603c60340128 2026-07-03] Sharon AI plans to deploy up to 40,000 NVIDIA Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs under a six-year agreement with NVIDIA.\\n    Quote: Sharon AI, which listed on the Nasdaq in February 2026 via a $125 million IPO, is deploying up to 40,000 Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs under a six-year agreement with Nvidia [2] [6] .\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e28, e74; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e58 [third_party_view; CNBC, reporting SemiAnalysis’s projection; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis projected Nvidia data-center compute revenue in the second half of FY2027 to be 20% above Wall Street consensus.\\n    Quote: SemiAnalysis also projects Nvidia's data-center compute revenue will run 20% above Wall Street consensus in the second half of fiscal 2027.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e142; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e67 [third_party_view; SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis 2026-07-06; from gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis says market estimates for Nvidia shipment volumes and revenue in the second half of 2026 are materially below its supply-chain-tracking estimates.\\n    Quote: Nvidia revenue is skyrocketing, and even 3 years into the build out, the general market is still materially lower on shipment volumes and revenue estimates for Nvidia in the 2nd half of this year versus our through supply chain tracking in the Accelerator Model .\",\n   \"- e69 [third_party_view; SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis 2026-07-06; from gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis says data-center supply improved by early 2026, chip production became the limiting constraint, and financing was a significant obstacle to expanding compute by mid-2026.\\n    Quote: In 2025, we wrote extensively about how datacenter capacity was the bottleneck for AI compute growth. By early 2026, the datacenter supply situation improved considerably, but it became clear that chip production was now the limiting constraint. Now – mid-way through the year – it is clear that financing will now be one of the most significant obstacles to ramping large scale compute broadly avail\",\n   \"- e74 [fact; SemiAnalysis; original source SharonAI ; from gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6 2026-07-06] SharonAI’s June 2026 Australia AI-factory deal includes a six-year backstop for up to 40,000 GB300 GPUs valued at $4.88 billion; SharonAI plans a 132 MW footprint, 102 MW contracted, and more than 55,000 Nvidia GPUs by mid-2027.\\n    Quote: The first is SharonAI’s 72MW AI factory in Australia. Announced in June 2026, the deal has SharonAI scaling up to as many as 40,000 GB300s under a six-year backstop. Sharon disclosed a total backstop value of $4.88B, which works out to an implied floor of about $2.33/hr/GPU on average over the six year period. Sharon AI’s footprint is now set to grow to 132MW with 102MW contracted, and the company\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e43; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e92 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:71df54965281684cc500960f 2026-07-06] Wall Street analysts expect Nvidia revenue growth of 82% for the rest of 2026 and 41% in 2027.\\n    Quote: For the rest of this year, they expect 82% growth. For 2027, that figure rises to 41%.\",\n   \"- e93 [fact; fool.com; original source Nvidia and Palantir Technologies ; from gnews:0e3cbf453958ce83fabf7a65 2026-07-06] Nvidia and Palantir announced a collaboration to bring open AI models into classified environments.\\n    Quote: Nvidia ( NVDA +2.48% ) and Palantir Technologies ( PLTR +1.34% ) announced a collaboration designed to bring powerful open AI models into highly sensitive, classified environments.\",\n   \"- e94 [fact; tradingview.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] NVIDIA's Data Center segment generated $75.25 billion in revenue in FY2027 Q1, 92% of total sales, up 92% year over year and 21% sequentially.\\n    Quote: During the first quarter of fiscal 2027, the Data Center segment generated $75.25 billion in revenues, accounting for 92% of total sales. Revenues from the segment surged 92% year over year and grew 21% sequentially, driven by the rapid ramp-up of Blackwell 300 systems and robust networking demand.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e98, e115; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e95 [fact; tradingview.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reported FY2027 Q1 revenue of $81.62 billion, up 85% year over year, and non-GAAP EPS of $1.87, up 140%.\\n    Quote: First-quarter fiscal 2027 revenues climbed 85% year over year to $81.62 billion, while non-GAAP earnings per share jumped 140% to $1.87.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e34; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e96 [party_statement; tradingview.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] NVIDIA guided FY2027 Q2 revenue to approximately $91 billion, nearly 95% above the year-earlier quarter.\\n    Quote: For the second quarter of fiscal 2027, NVIDIA projects revenues of approximately $91 billion, representing nearly 95% year-over-year growth.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e117; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e97 [rumour; Danielle Liverance; original source Danielle Liverance 2026-07-06; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] The author reported that NVIDIA’s upcoming Vera Rubin server systems were reportedly delayed; no timing or scale was specified.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA shares are under pressure on reports of delays across their upcoming lineup of Vera Rubin server systems.\",\n   \"- e98 [fact; Danielle Liverance; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] NVIDIA revenue was $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year; data-center revenue was $75.2 billion, up 92%.\\n    Quote: Revenue rose 85% year over year to $81.6 billion, with data center up 92% to $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e94, e114; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e99 [third_party_view; Danielle Liverance; original source Danielle Liverance 2026-07-06; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] NVIDIA had roughly 81% of the AI chip market, according to the author.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA still owns roughly 81% of the AI chip market\",\n   \"- e100 [party_statement; Danielle Liverance; original source Broadcom ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] Broadcom guided to Q3 AI semiconductor revenue of $16.0 billion, more than 200% higher year over year.\\n    Quote: Broadcom guided Q3 AI semiconductor revenue to $16.0 billion, more than 200% year over year.\",\n   \"- e101 [third_party_view; Danielle Liverance; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] Bloomberg Intelligence forecast custom ASICs to grow at a 27% CAGR through 2033, compared with 16% for AI accelerators.\\n    Quote: Bloomberg Intelligence forecasting a 27% CAGR for custom ASICs through 2033 versus 16% for AI accelerators.\",\n   \"- e102 [party_statement; Danielle Liverance; original source Lisa Su ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] AMD CEO Lisa Su said leading-customer forecasts for MI450 exceeded AMD’s initial expectations.\\n    Quote: Lisa Su noted “leading customer forecasts exceeding our initial expectations” on MI450.\",\n   \"- e103 [fact; Danielle Liverance; original source Micron ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] Micron Q3 revenue was $41.46 billion, up 345.7% year over year.\\n    Quote: Q3 revenue exploded 345.7% year over year to $41.46 billion,\",\n   \"- e104 [party_statement; Danielle Liverance; original source Micron ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] Micron forecast an adjusted gross margin of 86% next quarter.\\n    Quote: Micron is now forecasting adjusted gross margins of 86% next quarter, above the peak gross margins NVIDIA ever achieved.\",\n   \"- e105 [third_party_view; Danielle Liverance; original source Danielle Liverance 2026-07-06; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] Some estimates put memory at half of total data-center spending in 2027.\\n    Quote: Some estimates put half of all data center spend going toward memory in 2027.\",\n   \"- e106 [third_party_view; Danielle Liverance; original source Danielle Liverance 2026-07-06; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] The author said NVIDIA had $119 billion in supply commitments, whose value depends on AI delivering measurable economic value beyond productivity tools.\\n    Quote: Nvidia's $119B in supply commitments hinge on AI delivering measurable economic value beyond productivity tools, which is a question the market appears to already be pricing in.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e121; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e107 [third_party_view; Danielle Liverance; original source Danielle Liverance 2026-07-06; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] The author calculated that NVIDIA traded at a forward price-to-earnings ratio below 20.\\n    Quote: trades at a forward P/E of less than 20 now, and\",\n   \"- e114 [fact; 247wallst.com (Omor Ibne Ehsan); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.61 billion, up 85.2% year over year.\\n    Quote: Q1 FY27 revenue came in at $81.61 billion, up 85.2% year over year\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e98; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e115 [fact; 247wallst.com (Omor Ibne Ehsan); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 data center revenue of $75.25 billion.\\n    Quote: with data center revenue of $75.25 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e94; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e116 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com (Omor Ibne Ehsan); original source 247wallst.com (Omor Ibne Ehsan) 2026-07-06; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] The author estimates hyperscalers account for about 50% of NVIDIA's data center revenue.\\n    Quote: About 50% of that data center number comes from hyperscalers\",\n   \"- e117 [party_statement; 247wallst.com (Omor Ibne Ehsan); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] NVIDIA management guided Q2 FY2027 revenue to $91.0 billion and non-GAAP gross margin to 75%.\\n    Quote: Management guided Q2 FY27 revenue to $91.0 billion with non-GAAP gross margin holding at 75%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e96; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e118 [fact; 247wallst.com (Omor Ibne Ehsan); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] NVIDIA networking revenue was $14.8 billion in Q1 FY2027, up 199% year over year.\\n    Quote: Networking revenue grew 199% year over year to $14.8 billion\",\n   \"- e119 [fact; 247wallst.com (Omor Ibne Ehsan); original source Amazon ; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] Amazon disclosed that its Trainium business has reached multi-billion-dollar scale.\\n    Quote: Amazon has disclosed Trainium is now a multi-billion-dollar business\",\n   \"- e120 [party_statement; 247wallst.com (Omor Ibne Ehsan); original source Colette Kress, NVIDIA CFO ; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress said the future China data center compute market could be close to $50 billion and that losing it would be material; the author says NVIDIA's China data center compute revenue is effectively zero.\\n    Quote: China data center compute revenue is effectively zero, and Colette Kress (Nvidia’s CFO) said losing that market, which NVIDIA sizes at “close to about $50 billion in the future,” would be material.\",\n   \"- e121 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com (Omor Ibne Ehsan); original source 247wallst.com (Omor Ibne Ehsan) 2026-07-06; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] The author cites $119 billion of NVIDIA supply commitments as a risk if hyperscaler orders slow.\\n    Quote: Supply commitments of $119 billion compound demand risk if hyperscaler orders slow\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e106; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e122 [third_party_view; Allen Harris, the author; original source Allen Harris ; from gnews:54aa9ce326115cedf8857512 2026-07-06] The author reported Nvidia revenue growth of 85 percent, compared with Micron’s 346 percent; the period was not specified.\\n    Quote: Micron’s latest revenue growth was about 346 percent, compared with Nvidia’s 85 percent.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e34; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e123 [third_party_view; Allen Harris, the author; original source Allen Harris ; from gnews:54aa9ce326115cedf8857512 2026-07-06] The author reported Nvidia GAAP gross margin of 74.9 percent, compared with Micron’s 84.6 percent; the period was not specified.\\n    Quote: Micron’s GAAP gross margin was 84.6 percent, compared with Nvidia’s 74.9 percent.\",\n   \"- e124 [third_party_view; Allen Harris, the author; original source Allen Harris ; from gnews:54aa9ce326115cedf8857512 2026-07-06] The author reported Nvidia operating margin of roughly 66 percent, compared with Micron’s 80.4 percent; the period was not specified.\\n    Quote: Micron’s operating margin was 80.4 percent, compared with Nvidia’s roughly 66 percent.\",\n   \"- e125 [third_party_view; Allen Harris, the author, reporting Goldman Sachs’ estimate; original source Goldman Sachs ; from gnews:54aa9ce326115cedf8857512 2026-07-06] Goldman Sachs estimated annual AI infrastructure capital expenditures could reach $765 billion in 2026 and $1.6 trillion by 2031, with cumulative spending of about $7.6 trillion over 2026–2031.\\n    Quote: Goldman Sachs estimates annual AI infrastructure capital expenditures could reach $765 billion in 2026 and grow to $1.6 trillion by 2031, with cumulative spending of about $7.6 trillion from 2026 through 2031.\",\n   \"- e126 [fact; DCD; original source Bleeding Edge ; from gnews:c2924b0380602940d68de7ff 2026-07-06] Bleeding Edge launched its Querétaro AI Factory and neocloud offering using Nvidia Blackwell B300 systems.\\n    Quote: Bleeding Edge has launched an AI Factory in Querétaro, Mexico, bringing online its neocloud offering.\",\n   \"- e127 [party_statement; DCD; original source Bleeding Edge ; from gnews:c2924b0380602940d68de7ff 2026-07-06] Bleeding Edge said AI companies had contracted the entire initial capacity of its neocloud platform.\\n    Quote: According to Bleeding Edge, the platform’s entire initial capacity has already been contracted by companies dedicated to developing AI solutions.\",\n   \"- e128 [party_statement; DCD; original source Bleeding Edge ; from gnews:c2924b0380602940d68de7ff 2026-07-06] Bleeding Edge plans to expand neocloud and AI Factory capacity in the coming months, adding Nvidia systems and deploying infrastructure in other markets.\\n    Quote: Bleeding Edge plans to expand both the capacity of its neocloud and its AI Factories in the coming months by incorporating new Nvidia systems and deploying infrastructure in other strategic markets.\",\n   \"- e130 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia scrapped its planned NVL72x2 design, which would have placed two Oberon racks back to back, after cloud providers and large data center operators objected to its form factor and operational overhead.\\n    Quote: A planned alternative design called NVL72x2, which would have placed two Oberon racks back to back, has been scrapped entirely. Cloud providers and large data center operators pushed back against the unusual form factor and the high operational overhead.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e65; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e131 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia canceled the four-die Rubin Ultra version, leaving only the two-die version, which it said delivers roughly half the real-world compute performance.\\n    Quote: The more powerful version of the upcoming Rubin Ultra chip with four compute dies has also been canceled. Only the smaller two-die version remains, delivering roughly half the real-world compute performance.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e89, e135; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e132 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia’s CPO-NVSwitch interconnect technology will not arrive until the Feynman generation, two generations from the current one.\\n    Quote: A key interconnect technology called CPO-NVSwitch, which links many chips into a single large system, won't arrive until the generation after next, called Feynman.\",\n   \"- e133 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia plans to offset the product shortfall by selling more Oberon-Rubin racks in the existing form factor.\\n    Quote: Nvidia plans to make up for the shortfall by selling more Oberon-Rubin racks in the existing form factor.\",\n   \"- e135 [rumour; Investing.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:d5c48abb470f394f86549b6b 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis claimed that NVIDIA had scrapped a four-die configuration for the upcoming Rubin Ultra platform and would use a downsized version instead.\\n    Quote: Additionally, the report pointed to a downsized version of the upcoming Rubin Ultra platform, claiming a crucial four-die configuration had been scrapped.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e131; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e136 [third_party_view; Investing.com, citing analysts quoted by Bloomberg; original source Analysts cited by Bloomberg ; from gnews:d5c48abb470f394f86549b6b 2026-07-06] Analysts cited by Bloomberg said the rumored technical setbacks could severely limit the scale-up capacity of NVIDIA's future hardware.\\n    Quote: According to analysts cited by Bloomberg, these rumored technical setbacks could severely cap the scale-up capacity of Nvidia's future hardware.\",\n   \"- e137 [third_party_view; Investing.com, citing analysts quoted by Bloomberg; original source Analysts cited by Bloomberg ; from gnews:d5c48abb470f394f86549b6b 2026-07-06] Analysts cited by Bloomberg said perceived weaknesses in NVIDIA's future hardware could give AMD's MI500X and Broadcom-backed custom TPUs a wider competitive opportunity.\\n    Quote: This perceived vulnerability may create a wider competitive window for alternative AI platforms, specifically AMD's MI500X and Broadcom-backed custom TPUs.\",\n   \"- e138 [party_statement; Investing.com, reporting Mizuho analyst Jordan Klein's note; original source Hon Hai Precision Industry management 2026-07-03; from gnews:d5c48abb470f394f86549b6b 2026-07-06] Hon Hai management forecast continued acceleration in AI demand; Mizuho analyst Jordan Klein said this was a positive sign ahead of NVIDIA's Vera Rubin rack launch.\\n    Quote: Klein noted that Hon Hai management forecasted a continued acceleration in AI demand, which the analyst said was \\\"a very good sign into the NVDA launch of their new Vera Rubin rack.\\\"\",\n   \"- e142 [third_party_view; tikr.com (analyst); original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:d4c5dc540392f8df39aee250 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis expects Nvidia data-center compute revenue in the second half of FY2027 to be 20% above Wall Street’s current expectations.\\n    Quote: SemiAnalysis actually expects Nvidia’s data-center compute revenue in the second half of fiscal 2027 to come in 20% above Wall Street’s current expectations.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e58; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e150 [third_party_view; Business Times, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence’s survey; original source Bloomberg Intelligence survey respondents 2026-07-07; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] Chinese executives surveyed by Bloomberg Intelligence said domestic products would receive 46% of their AI-accelerator budgets over the next 12 months, up from 30% currently.\\n    Quote: Executives in the country say they will allocate 46 per cent of their budget for AI accelerators to domestic products over the next 12 months.\",\n   \"- e151 [third_party_view; Business Times, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence’s survey; original source Bloomberg Intelligence survey respondents 2026-07-07; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] 80% of surveyed Chinese executives said their total infrastructure spending was running over budget in 2026, mostly because of AI-project costs.\\n    Quote: In addition, 80 per cent of executives said their total infrastructure spending is running over-budget this year, mostly because of the high cost of AI-related projects.\",\n   \"- e152 [third_party_view; Business Times, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence’s survey; original source Bloomberg Intelligence survey respondents 2026-07-07; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] A large pool of surveyed Chinese executives was evaluating AI accelerators from Hygon Information Technology and Cambricon Technologies.\\n    Quote: AI accelerators produced by Hygon Information Technology and Cambricon Technologies were also being evaluated by a large pool of respondents to the survey.\",\n   \"- e153 [third_party_view; Business Times, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence’s survey; original source Bloomberg Intelligence survey respondents 2026-07-07; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] Bloomberg Intelligence survey respondents expected Nvidia’s market share in China to shrink as H20 chips became harder to find and local suppliers took over.\\n    Quote: While Nvidia’s products remain popular, the Santa Clara-based firm’s market share is expected to shrink as its H20 chips, which Beijing has urged its tech firms not to use , become harder to find and local firms take over, according to the survey.\",\n   \"- e154 [fact; Business Times; original source China ; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] China is allocating about 2 trillion yuan (US$294 billion) over five years to build data centres and expand AI use across sectors.\\n    Quote: China is allocating roughly two trillion yuan (US$294 billion) to build data centres across the country in the next five years, a government-led initiative to expand the use of AI in sectors from healthcare to city management.\",\n   \"- e155 [third_party_view; Business Times, citing Bloomberg News; original source Bloomberg News ; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] Bloomberg News reported that domestic companies would supply at least 80% of core technologies, including chips, for China’s data-centre initiative.\\n    Quote: At least 80 per cent of core technologies, such as chips, will be supplied by domestic companies, Bloomberg News reported.\",\n   \"- e156 [third_party_view; Business Times, reporting the survey report; original source Bloomberg Intelligence survey report ; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] The report said a global memory-chip shortage was likely to cap growth at Chinese AI firms such as SMIC, with high-bandwidth memory supply becoming the bottleneck.\\n    Quote: But a global memory chip shortage is likely to cap the growth of Chinese AI firms like Semiconductor Manufacturing International Corporation, with ChangXin Memory Technologies poised to reap the benefits.\",\n   \"- e37 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source Palantir and NVIDIA ; from gnews:bdcb0ed0921c2e9ae241083c 2026-07-03] Palantir is making a deal to use NVIDIA's Nemotron to build government AI models; no amount or timing is specified.\\n    Quote: With Palantir now inking a deal to use Nvidia's Nemotron to build models for the government\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e157; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e100 [party_statement; Danielle Liverance; original source Broadcom ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] Broadcom guided to Q3 AI semiconductor revenue of $16.0 billion, more than 200% higher year over year.\\n    Quote: Broadcom guided Q3 AI semiconductor revenue to $16.0 billion, more than 200% year over year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e175; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e115 [fact; 247wallst.com (Omor Ibne Ehsan); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 data center revenue of $75.25 billion.\\n    Quote: with data center revenue of $75.25 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e94, e173; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e157 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source Palantir ; from gnews:1a116fecd5de1747cc5a06b1 2026-07-07] Palantir announced it is combining its intelligence engine with Nvidia Nemotron models to deliver AI for U.S. government agencies and major infrastructure operators.\\n    Quote: Earlier this week, Palantir announced that it is combining its new intelligence engine and Nvidia's Nemotron open AI models to deliver mission-focused AI for government agencies and major infrastructure operators in the U.S.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e37; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e164 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-07-07; from gnews:f8191f5bb960d79e47c73d6c 2026-07-07] The author forecasts that Nvidia will report another blowout quarter in late August 2026, citing no shift in its core clients' actual spending habits.\\n    Quote: Even if it doesn't, Nvidia reports earnings in late August and will likely report another blowout quarter, as there hasn't been any shift in actual spending habits from Nvidia's core clients yet.\",\n   \"- e165 [fact; CNBC; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:784c556d2e58ed09dd8aa7fc 2026-07-07] NVIDIA reported automotive revenue grew 39% year over year in FY2026, driven by adoption of its self-driving platforms.\\n    Quote: In its latest annual filing, Nvidia reported automotive revenue for fiscal year 2026 was up 39% from a year prior, driven by the adoption of its self-driving platforms.\",\n   \"- e166 [party_statement; fool.com (Keithen Drury); original source Micron Technology ; from gnews:d0f3f83296df884fae64921e 2026-07-07] Micron said tight memory-market conditions could last until 2028.\\n    Quote: Micron recently announced another jaw-dropping quarter with huge growth and incredible expectations for the following quarter, dropping huge news that tight market conditions could last until 2028.\",\n   \"- e167 [third_party_view; fool.com (Keithen Drury); original source fool.com (Keithen Drury) 2026-07-07; from gnews:d0f3f83296df884fae64921e 2026-07-07] The author says new capacity across the memory-chip industry will not be online until 2027 or later, leaving inventory supply low for at least the next year and a half.\\n    Quote: As mentioned, new capacity for many in this industry won't be online until 2027 or later, creating a low supply of inventory for at least the next year and a half.\",\n   \"- e169 [third_party_view; fool.com (Keithen Drury); original source fool.com (Keithen Drury) 2026-07-07; from gnews:d0f3f83296df884fae64921e 2026-07-07] The author estimates Nvidia will generate about $100 billion in revenue next quarter, based on Micron's expected $50 billion being about half that amount.\\n    Quote: Next quarter, it expects $50 billion in revenue, or about half of what Nvidia is expected to generate.\",\n   \"- e173 [fact; 24/7 Wall St.; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] NVIDIA Data Center revenue was $75.246 billion in Q1 FY2027, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue reached $75.246 billion (+92% YoY) in Q1 FY27\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e115; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e175 [fact; 24/7 Wall St.; original source Broadcom ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] Broadcom AI semiconductor revenue was $10.8 billion in Q2, up 143% year over year, and the company guided to $16.0 billion for Q3.\\n    Quote: Q2 AI semiconductor revenue was $10.8 billion, +143% YoY, with Q3 guided to $16.0 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e100; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e176 [party_statement; 24/7 Wall St.; original source Google ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] Google Cloud revenue rose 63%, its backlog nearly doubled to more than $460 billion, and Google guided 2026 capital expenditures to $190 billion.\\n    Quote: Google Cloud revenue rose 63% with backlog nearly doubling to over $460 billion, and 2026 capex is guided up tp $190 billion.\",\n   \"- e177 [fact; NVIDIA; original source id Software and Bethesda Softworks 2026-07-07; from gnews:2f1cb54b7a3da28d093523b6 2026-07-07] id Software and Bethesda Softworks launched the DOOM: The Dark Ages | Revelations expansion on July 7, 2026, with support for NVIDIA DLSS Multi Frame Generation, Super Resolution, and path tracing with Ray Reconstruction on supported GeForce RTX GPUs.\\n    Quote: DOOM: The Dark Ages | Revelations launches today with native support for DLSS Multi Frame Generation (up to 6X mode), Super Resolution, and path tracing enhanced with Ray Reconstruction on supported GeForce RTX GPUs, which was used to great effect in the base game .\",\n   \"- e178 [party_statement; NVIDIA; original source Ubisoft 2026-07-07; from gnews:2f1cb54b7a3da28d093523b6 2026-07-07] Ubisoft planned to launch the PC release of Assassin’s Creed Black Flag Resynced on July 9, 2026, with ray tracing and support for NVIDIA DLSS Multi Frame Generation, Frame Generation, and Super Resolution on GeForce RTX GPUs.\\n    Quote: Launching July 9th, the PC release of Assassin’s Creed Black Flag Resynced includes support for ray-traced reflections and ray-traced lighting for realistic reflections, shadows, and water/lighting interactions across the Caribbean, which can be accelerated by DLSS Multi Frame Generation, Frame Generation and Super Resolution on GeForce RTX GPUs.\",\n   \"- e179 [fact; NVIDIA; original source MADFINGER Games 2026-07-07; from gnews:2f1cb54b7a3da28d093523b6 2026-07-07] MADFINGER Games added NVIDIA’s latest DLSS Dynamic Multi Frame Generation and Super Resolution models to Gray Zone Warfare, for use on GeForce RTX GPUs.\\n    Quote: Now, the latest DLSS Dynamic Multi Frame Generation and Super Resolution models have been added to further enhance frame rates and image quality on GeForce RTX GPUs.\",\n   \"- e180 [rumour; mlq.ai, relaying Reuters; original source Three unnamed sources cited by Reuters 2026-07-06; from gnews:9f430c6ce2e8d551fe1f063a 2026-07-07] Reuters, citing three unnamed sources, reported that DeepSeek is developing a custom AI inference chip rather than a training chip.\\n    Quote: DeepSeek, the Hangzhou-based AI startup behind some of China's most advanced large language models, is developing its own custom AI chip, Reuters reported on Monday, citing three people with knowledge of the matter [1] . The chip is designed for inference — the phase where trained models generate responses to user queries — rather than for training new models.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e186; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e181 [rumour; mlq.ai, relaying Reuters; original source Three unnamed sources cited by Reuters 2026-07-06; from gnews:9f430c6ce2e8d551fe1f063a 2026-07-07] DeepSeek has reportedly been working on its inference-chip project for about a year, expanding its chip engineering team and discussing the project with chip design firms, foundries and memory suppliers.\\n    Quote: The project has been underway for roughly a year and remains in early stages, with DeepSeek quietly expanding its chip engineering team without public job postings [2] . The company is in discussions with chip design firms, semiconductor foundries, and memory suppliers, though no specific partners have been named.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e189; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e182 [fact; mlq.ai; original source DeepSeek ; from gnews:9f430c6ce2e8d551fe1f063a 2026-07-07] DeepSeek cut prices for its V4-Pro API by 75% in May 2026, intensifying price competition among Chinese AI providers.\\n    Quote: In May 2026, the company cut prices on its V4-Pro API by 75%, intensifying a price war among Chinese AI providers [5] .\",\n   \"- e183 [third_party_view; mlq.ai, quoting Richard Windey; original source Richard Windey ; from gnews:9f430c6ce2e8d551fe1f063a 2026-07-07] Analyst Richard Windey said U.S. export rules had effectively reduced Nvidia's China revenue to zero and also constrained DeepSeek's ability to manufacture or sell advanced chips outside China.\\n    Quote: Analyst Richard Windey highlighted the constraint: the same export rules that have effectively zeroed out Nvidia's China revenue also limit DeepSeek's ability to manufacture or sell advanced silicon outside China [3] .\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e187; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e184 [third_party_view; mlq.ai; original source Industry surveys ; from gnews:9f430c6ce2e8d551fe1f063a 2026-07-07] Industry surveys indicate Chinese firms plan to allocate 46% of their AI-accelerator budgets to domestic suppliers within 12 months, up from about 30% currently.\\n    Quote: Industry surveys indicate Chinese firms plan to shift 46% of their AI-accelerator budgets to domestic suppliers within 12 months, up from roughly 30% today [5] .\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e150; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e185 [fact; mlq.ai; original source The United States government ; from gnews:9f430c6ce2e8d551fe1f063a 2026-07-07] U.S. export controls bar Chinese chip designers from accessing the most advanced overseas foundries and high-bandwidth memory, constraining their ability to manufacture advanced chips.\\n    Quote: U.S. export controls bar Chinese designers from accessing the most advanced overseas foundries and high-bandwidth memory, posing a major manufacturing hurdle\",\n   \"- e186 [rumour; idnfinancials.com; original source Three unnamed sources cited by Reuters ; from gnews:2957e5c79a365952140c8cce 2026-07-07] Three unnamed sources told Reuters that DeepSeek is designing inference chips, a project that could reduce demand for Nvidia chips.\\n    Quote: According to Reuters , citing three sources familiar with the plans, DeepSeek's chips are being designed specifically for inference, the stage where trained AI models generate responses for users.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e180; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e187 [third_party_view; idnfinancials.com, quoting Richard Windsor; original source Richard Windsor, Radio Free Mobile ; from gnews:2957e5c79a365952140c8cce 2026-07-07] Richard Windsor of Radio Free Mobile said Nvidia's position in China is effectively zero and will remain so, and that DeepSeek is unlikely to sell chips outside China without access to advanced manufacturing technology.\\n    Quote: \\\"Nvidia's position in China is effectively at zero and will remain that way. DeepSeek has almost no chance of selling chips outside China unless it gains access to advanced manufacturing technology,\\\" said analyst Richard Windsor of Radio Free Mobile, adding that the development would not affect the chipmaker.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e183; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e188 [third_party_view; idnfinancials.com; original source idnfinancials.com 2026-07-07; from gnews:2957e5c79a365952140c8cce 2026-07-07] Huawei now controls around half of China's AI chip market, which is valued at approximately US$50 billion.\\n    Quote: Huawei has expanded its domestic market share and now controls around half of China's AI chip market, which is valued at approximately US$50 billion.\",\n   \"- e189 [rumour; idnfinancials.com; original source Unnamed sources cited by Reuters ; from gnews:2957e5c79a365952140c8cce 2026-07-07] Reuters sources said DeepSeek's chip project remains at an early stage and that the company has been communicating with chip-design firms, foundries and memory suppliers over the past year.\\n    Quote: According to Reuters sources, DeepSeek's chip development project remains at an early stage. Over the past year, the company has been communicating with chip design firms, foundries and memory suppliers to support the development of the semiconductors.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e181; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e190 [rumour; idnfinancials.com; original source idnfinancials.com ; from gnews:2957e5c79a365952140c8cce 2026-07-07] DeepSeek has increased recruitment of chip-design engineers in recent months to support its chip-development effort.\\n    Quote: DeepSeek has also increased recruitment of chip design engineers in recent months.\",\n   \"- e191 [fact; idnfinancials.com; original source OpenAI; and, for the reported consideration, unnamed sources cited by idnfinancials.com ; from gnews:2957e5c79a365952140c8cce 2026-07-07] OpenAI introduced its first inference chip, Jalapeno, in collaboration with Broadcom in June 2026; Anthropic is reportedly considering developing AI chips of its own.\\n    Quote: OpenAI introduced its first inference chip, called Jalapeno, last month in collaboration with Broadcom, while Anthropic is also reportedly considering developing its own AI chips.\",\n   \"- e192 [fact; idnfinancials.com; original source DeepSeek, for the V4 launch and optimization; Huawei, for its statement about V4-Flash training ; from gnews:2957e5c79a365952140c8cce 2026-07-07] DeepSeek launched its V4 model in April 2026, optimized for Huawei Ascend chips; Huawei also revealed that V4-Flash training used Ascend processors.\\n    Quote: In April, DeepSeek launched its V4 model, which had been optimised for Huawei Ascend chips, while Huawei revealed that training for the V4-Flash model also used Ascend processors.\",\n   \"- e193 [third_party_view; idnfinancials.com; original source idnfinancials.com 2026-07-07; from gnews:2957e5c79a365952140c8cce 2026-07-07] The DeepSeek V4 launch drove a surge in demand for Huawei Ascend 950 chips among Chinese technology companies.\\n    Quote: The launch also drove a surge in demand for Huawei's Ascend 950 chips among Chinese technology companies.\",\n   \"- e26 [third_party_view; fool.com (Justin Pope); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] Wall Street analysts estimate Nvidia revenue of $392 billion in FY2027.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts estimate that Nvidia's business could double over the next couple of years, from trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion to $392 billion this fiscal year, and $554 billion the following year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e204; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e47 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568 2026-07-04] Wall Street analysts project Nvidia revenue growth of 82% in FY2027 and 41% in FY2028.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts project 82% revenue growth for this year and 41% next year, so there's another external source that's projecting even more growth for Nvidia.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e216; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e98 [fact; Danielle Liverance; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] NVIDIA revenue was $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year; data-center revenue was $75.2 billion, up 92%.\\n    Quote: Revenue rose 85% year over year to $81.6 billion, with data center up 92% to $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e94, e114, e226; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e151 [third_party_view; Business Times, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence’s survey; original source Bloomberg Intelligence survey respondents 2026-07-07; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] 80% of surveyed Chinese executives said their total infrastructure spending was running over budget in 2026, mostly because of AI-project costs.\\n    Quote: In addition, 80 per cent of executives said their total infrastructure spending is running over-budget this year, mostly because of the high cost of AI-related projects.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e218; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e153 [third_party_view; Business Times, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence’s survey; original source Bloomberg Intelligence survey respondents 2026-07-07; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] Bloomberg Intelligence survey respondents expected Nvidia’s market share in China to shrink as H20 chips became harder to find and local suppliers took over.\\n    Quote: While Nvidia’s products remain popular, the Santa Clara-based firm’s market share is expected to shrink as its H20 chips, which Beijing has urged its tech firms not to use , become harder to find and local firms take over, according to the survey.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e219; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e154 [fact; Business Times; original source China ; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] China is allocating about 2 trillion yuan (US$294 billion) over five years to build data centres and expand AI use across sectors.\\n    Quote: China is allocating roughly two trillion yuan (US$294 billion) to build data centres across the country in the next five years, a government-led initiative to expand the use of AI in sectors from healthcare to city management.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e220; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e155 [third_party_view; Business Times, citing Bloomberg News; original source Bloomberg News ; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] Bloomberg News reported that domestic companies would supply at least 80% of core technologies, including chips, for China’s data-centre initiative.\\n    Quote: At least 80 per cent of core technologies, such as chips, will be supplied by domestic companies, Bloomberg News reported.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e221; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e194 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source LangChain ; from nvblog:nemotron-langchain-agents-open-stack 2026-07-08] LangChain tuned its Deep Agents harness for NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Ultra; the company reported the integration and benchmark results.\\n    Quote: LangChain tuned its Deep Agents harness for NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Ultra, achieving the highest accuracy among open models, while completing more tasks at higher throughput and running at 10x lower inference cost per run than leading closed models.\",\n   \"- e195 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source Abridge, Amdocs, Box and EY ; from nvblog:nemotron-langchain-agents-open-stack 2026-07-08] Abridge, Amdocs and Box are embedding specialized agents in their platforms, while EY is expanding its NVIDIA implementation capabilities around NemoClaw blueprints for LangChain Deep Agents.\\n    Quote: Abridge, Amdocs and Box are embedding specialized agents directly into their platforms and global systems integrator EY is expanding its NVIDIA implementation capabilities around NVIDIA NemoClaw blueprints for LangChain Deep Agents, helping clients customize, evaluate and govern specialized agents across high-value workflows.\",\n   \"- e196 [party_statement; NVIDIA Corporation; original source NVIDIA 2026-07-08; from nvblog:nemotron-langchain-agents-open-stack 2026-07-08] NVIDIA announced that NemoClaw for LangChain Deep Agents and the tuned Nemotron 3 Ultra profile are available, with developers able to access the harness through LangChain or use the blueprint to build agents.\\n    Quote: NemoClaw for LangChain Deep Agents and the tuned Nemotron 3 Ultra model profile are available now . Developers can pull the tuned Deep Agents harness directly from LangChain, or use the NemoClaw for LangChain Deep Agents blueprint as a starting point for building specialized agents from scratch.\",\n   \"- e197 [party_statement; NVIDIA Corporation; original source NVIDIA 2026-07-08; from nvblog:nemotron-langchain-agents-open-stack 2026-07-08] LangChain developers can access Nemotron 3 Ultra and the tuned harness through six hosted platforms: Baseten, Crusoe Cloud, DeepInfra, Fireworks, Nebius and Together AI.\\n    Quote: LangChain developers can access Nemotron 3 Ultra on Baseten , Crusoe Cloud , DeepInfra, Fireworks , Nebius and Together AI platforms, giving them a direct, hosted path to the tuned harness in production.\",\n   \"- e201 [party_statement; The Straits Times; original source Nvidia CFO Colette Kress ; from gnews:c8c39f971721fd820aab5c1c 2026-07-08] In May 2026, Nvidia CFO Colette Kress said H200 chips had generated no revenue for Nvidia in China as of then.\\n    Quote: In May, Nvidia chief financial officer Colette Kress said the H200 chips had yet to generate any revenue for the company in China.\",\n   \"- e204 [third_party_view; finance.yahoo.com; original source Analysts ; from gnews:b40db2c507df72ec016e99e6 2026-07-08] Analysts expect NVIDIA total revenue of $392.7 billion in FY2027.\\n    Quote: And analysts are anticipating further gains of $392.7 billion in its current fiscal year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e26; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e205 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:79cc3f345545cdd3d37c0472 2026-07-08] Nvidia's revenue increased 74.6% in its most recent quarter.\\n    Quote: In the most recent quarter alone, Nvidia increased its revenue by 74.6%\",\n   \"- e206 [third_party_view; gurufocus.com; original source Analysts ; from gnews:bbb38537c01d8be774edc057 2026-07-08] Analysts forecast Nvidia to have one of the strongest revenue growth rates among large-cap companies in 2026.\\n    Quote: Nvidia remains among the fastest-growing large-cap companies, with analysts forecasting one of the strongest revenue expansion rates in the index this year.\",\n   \"- e208 [party_statement; futuriom.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cb05b9f49943ef0ba412cf36 2026-07-08] NVIDIA said Sharon AI signed onto its AI-cloud program and will buy up to 40,000 Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA states that two AI cloud providers have already signed on for the new deal: Sharon AI, based in Australia, will buy up to 40,000 NVIDIA Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs under the plan.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e111; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e209 [fact; futuriom.com; original source Firmus ; from gnews:cb05b9f49943ef0ba412cf36 2026-07-08] Firmus is building a DSX AI factory in Indonesia expected to scale to 360 megawatts and contain up to 170,000 NVIDIA GPUs.\\n    Quote: Firmus, based in Indoesia, is building a DSX AI factory there that’s expected to scale to 360 megawatts and contain up to 170,000 NVIDIA GPUs.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e111; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e213 [fact; CNBC; original source SambaNova 2026-07-08; from gnews:6b89157155648b9ec317d209 2026-07-08] SambaNova raised $1 billion in financing, valuing the Nvidia chip challenger at $11 billion; the round was led by General Atlantic with participation from Seligman Ventures, T. Rowe Price and Capital Group.\\n    Quote: SambaNova is now valued at $11 billion thanks to the financing, which was led by General Atlantic along with participation from Seligman Ventures, T. Rowe Price and Capital Group.\",\n   \"- e214 [fact; CNBC; original source JPMorgan Chase 2026-07-08; from gnews:6b89157155648b9ec317d209 2026-07-08] JPMorgan Chase said it would deploy SambaNova systems for on-prem inference in enterprise AI workloads.\\n    Quote: On Wednesday, JPMorgan Chase said it would deploy SambaNova's systems for \\\"on-prem inference in our demanding enterprise AI workloads.\\\"\",\n   \"- e215 [party_statement; Rodrigo Liang, quoted by CNBC; original source SambaNova CEO Rodrigo Liang 2026-07-08; from gnews:6b89157155648b9ec317d209 2026-07-08] SambaNova CEO Rodrigo Liang said the new capital would accelerate deployments of its racks, which he said customers wanted.\\n    Quote: We're scaling the business really, really fast, and so the capital allows us to really accelerate the deployments of the racks that customers really want,\",\n   \"- e216 [third_party_view; tradingview.com; original source Bloomberg-cited analysts ; from gnews:a09988fd9c5c1a739a14f873 2026-07-08] Bloomberg-cited projections put Nvidia FY2027 sales at $393 billion, up 82%; the article reports no separate date for the original estimate.\\n    Quote: The company is projected to generate $228 billion in profit on $393 billion in sales in fiscal 2027, which ends Jan. 31, representing expected growth of 90% and 82%, respectively, while its profit estimate has risen 13% over the past three months.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e47; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e217 [third_party_view; Bloomberg, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence’s survey; original source Bloomberg Intelligence 2026-07-07; from gnews:f3ba15f5e14b15ee61d7fddc 2026-07-08] Chinese executives surveyed by Bloomberg Intelligence said domestic products would receive 46% of their AI-accelerator budgets over the next 12 months, up from 30% currently.\\n    Quote: Executives in the country say they’ll allocate 46% of their budget for artificial intelligence accelerators to domestic products over the next 12 months, up from 30% today, according to a Bloomberg Intelligence survey released on Tuesday.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e150; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e218 [third_party_view; Bloomberg, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence’s survey; original source Bloomberg Intelligence 2026-07-07; from gnews:f3ba15f5e14b15ee61d7fddc 2026-07-08] In Bloomberg Intelligence’s survey, 80% of executives said their total infrastructure spending was running over budget in 2026, mostly because of the high cost of AI-related projects.\\n    Quote: In addition, 80% of executives said their total infrastructure spending is running over-budget this year, mostly because of the high cost of AI-related projects.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e151; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e219 [third_party_view; Bloomberg, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence’s survey; original source Bloomberg Intelligence 2026-07-07; from gnews:f3ba15f5e14b15ee61d7fddc 2026-07-08] Bloomberg Intelligence’s survey said Nvidia’s market share was expected to shrink as H20 chips became harder to find and local firms took over; it cited Beijing’s urging that Chinese technology firms not use H20 chips.\\n    Quote: While Nvidia’s products remain popular, the Santa Clara-based firm’s market share is expected to shrink as its H20 chips, which Beijing has urged its tech firms not to use, become harder to find and local firms take over, according to the survey.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e153; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e220 [third_party_view; Bloomberg; original source Bloomberg ; from gnews:f3ba15f5e14b15ee61d7fddc 2026-07-08] China is allocating roughly 2 trillion yuan ($294 billion) to build data centers over the next five years as part of a government-led AI expansion initiative.\\n    Quote: China is allocating roughly 2 trillion yuan ($294 billion) to build data centers across the country in the next five years, a government-led initiative to expand use of AI in sectors from healthcare to city management.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e154; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e221 [third_party_view; Bloomberg; original source Bloomberg News ; from gnews:f3ba15f5e14b15ee61d7fddc 2026-07-08] Bloomberg News reported that domestic companies will supply at least 80% of core technologies, including chips, for China’s data-center initiative.\\n    Quote: At least 80% of core technologies, such as chips, will be supplied by domestic companies, Bloomberg News reported.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e155; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e222 [third_party_view; Bloomberg, reporting the survey report; original source Bloomberg Intelligence 2026-07-07; from gnews:f3ba15f5e14b15ee61d7fddc 2026-07-08] The report said a global memory-chip shortage was likely to cap growth at Chinese AI firms such as SMIC, with ChangXin Memory Technologies poised to benefit, as bottlenecks shifted toward securing high-bandwidth memory supply.\\n    Quote: But a global memory chip shortage is likely to cap the growth of Chinese AI firms like Semiconductor Manufacturing International Corp. with ChangXin Memory Technologies Inc. poised to reap the benefits. The bottlenecks are shifting from sheer computing power to securing supply of high-bandwidth memory chips that support rapid data transfer, according to the report.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e156; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e223 [third_party_view; Investing.com, reporting Vivek Arya's note; original source Vivek Arya, Bank of America 2026-07-08; from gnews:266c882eea8c686ee7aafac7 2026-07-08] Bank of America analyst Vivek Arya estimated that HBM content per rack may increase by $0.2–0.3 million from Blackwell to Rubin, while rack pricing could increase by $2–3 million because of compute, networking, and software upgrades.\\n    Quote: While HBM content per rack may rise by approximately $0.2-0.3 million from Blackwell to Rubin, Arya noted that rack pricing could increase by $2-3 million, driven by upgrades across compute, networking and software.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e230; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e224 [third_party_view; Investing.com, reporting Vivek Arya's note; original source Vivek Arya, Bank of America 2026-07-08; from gnews:266c882eea8c686ee7aafac7 2026-07-08] Bank of America analyst Vivek Arya said NVIDIA GPU revenue had grown approximately 700 times since 2015, despite Google's TPU, Amazon's Trainium, and Meta's MTIA having existed for years.\\n    Quote: On ASIC competition, Arya pointed out that Google's TPU, Amazon's Trainium and Meta's MTIA have all existed for years, \\\"yet NVDA GPU revenue has grown approximately 700 times since 2015.\\\"\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e233; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e225 [third_party_view; Investing.com, reporting Bank of America's note; original source Bank of America 2026-07-08; from gnews:266c882eea8c686ee7aafac7 2026-07-08] NVIDIA sales to hyperscalers rose 115% year-on-year, nearly twice the growth in cloud capital expenditures; the period is not specified.\\n    Quote: Sales to hyperscalers rose 115% year-on-year, nearly twice cloud capex growth.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e231; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e226 [fact; qz.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:ee0d6792b6bf98069cfe0cc6 2026-07-08] Nvidia reported FY2027 first-quarter total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: For its fiscal first quarter of 2027, Nvidia posted $81.6 billion in total revenue — an 85% increase from a year earlier\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e98; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e228 [fact; aibusiness.com; original source Nvidia and Hugging Face 2026-07-06; from gnews:21e9182d07508a6690f10419 2026-07-08] Nvidia and Hugging Face announced a collaboration unveiled July 6, integrating Nvidia’s Isaac GR00T 1.7 models and Isaac Teleop framework into LeRobot, with Cosmos 3 planned for future integration.\\n    Quote: Nvidia and Hugging Face entered into a new collaboration for open source robotics, integrating the chipmaker’s models onto LeRobot, Hugging Face’s open source library for physical AI developers. Under the deal, unveiled on July 6, the companies added Nvidia's Isaac GR00T 1.7 open reasoning vision-language-action (VLA) models for humanoid robotics and the Isaac Teleop framework for robotics data co\",\n   \"- e229 [fact; aibusiness.com; original source Qualcomm and Intel ; from gnews:21e9182d07508a6690f10419 2026-07-08] Qualcomm recently entered robotics with its Dragonwing IQ10 and Intel with its OpenVINO offerings, adding named competitors to Nvidia in robotics.\\n    Quote: In addition, Qualcomm, with its Dragonwing IQ10 and Intel, with its OpenVINO robotics offerings, have recently entered the fold to challenge Nvidia’s position.\",\n   \"- e230 [third_party_view; moomoo.com; original source BofA ; from gnews:1b5a3359dd0644861c0fce42 2026-07-08] BofA estimated HBM content per rack could increase by $0.2 million to $0.3 million from Blackwell to Rubin, while total rack pricing could rise from about $3 million–$4 million to $6 million–$7 million.\\n    Quote: The report estimates HBM content per rack could rise by about $0.2 million to $0.3 million from Blackwell to Rubin, while total rack pricing could increase by $2 million to $3 million, from roughly $3 million to $4 million for Blackwell to $6 million to $7 million for Vera Rubin.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e223; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e231 [third_party_view; moomoo.com; original source BofA ; from gnews:1b5a3359dd0644861c0fce42 2026-07-08] BofA reported that Nvidia’s hyperscaler sales rose 115% year over year, nearly twice the growth in cloud capital expenditures.\\n    Quote: The report also says Nvidia’s hyperscaler sales rose 115% year over year, nearly twice cloud capex growth, suggesting wallet-share gains rather than share loss.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e225; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e232 [third_party_view; moomoo.com; original source BofA ; from gnews:1b5a3359dd0644861c0fce42 2026-07-08] BofA modeled Nvidia holding roughly 65% to 70% or more of AI capital expenditures over time, with the remainder going to ASICs, AMD and other merchant vendors.\\n    Quote: BofA still models Nvidia holding roughly 65% to 70% plus of AI capex over time, with the rest split across ASICs, AMD and other merchant vendors.\",\n   \"- e233 [third_party_view; moomoo.com; original source BofA ; from gnews:1b5a3359dd0644861c0fce42 2026-07-08] BofA said Nvidia GPU accelerator sales had grown about 700 times since 2015, despite the launches of Google TPU, Amazon Trainium and Meta MTIA.\\n    Quote: BofA’s counterpoint is historical: Google TPU launched in 2015, Amazon Trainium in 2020 and Meta MTIA in 2023, yet Nvidia GPU accelerator sales have grown about 700 times since 2015.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e224; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e237 [fact; PR Newswire (company release); original source Parasail and d-Matrix 2026-07-08; from gnews:040c256543fc8106ffecabae 2026-07-08] Parasail announced it is deploying d-Matrix Corsair accelerators alongside its NVIDIA Hopper and Blackwell infrastructure for inference services.\\n    Quote: Parasail, the inference cloud for AI-native startups, and d-Matrix, a pioneer in low-latency AI inference compute platforms for data centers, today announced Parasail is deploying d-Matrix Corsair inference accelerators alongside the NVIDIA Hopper and NVIDIA Blackwell architectures to deliver up to 10x faster, more cost-efficient inference services to its customers.\",\n   \"- e238 [party_statement; PR Newswire (company release); original source Parasail and d-Matrix 2026-07-08; from gnews:040c256543fc8106ffecabae 2026-07-08] Parasail and d-Matrix plan to publish performance results after initial deployments and explore expanding the integration across Parasail's fleet of more than 40 data centers in 15 countries.\\n    Quote: The companies plan to share detailed performance results and case studies following the first series of deployments and explore expanded integration across Parasail's global fleet of over 40 data centers in 15 countries.\",\n   \"- e239 [fact; larsentoubro.com; original source L&T Vyoma and Fortanix 2026-07-08; from gnews:79b4840d3de4aa77ec0d0229 2026-07-08] L&T Vyoma and Fortanix announced a strategic partnership to jointly deliver sovereign AI and security offerings, with Fortanix leveraging NVIDIA Confidential Computing; they plan to develop solutions, co-sell and support customer engagements in India.\\n    Quote: Larsen & Toubro Vyoma (L&T Vyoma), L&T’s next-generation sovereign AI cloud and digital infrastructure business, has entered a strategic partnership with Fortanix Inc, a US-headquartered global leader in data and AI security and a pioneer in Confidential Computing. They will jointly deliver sovereign, secure software-as-a-service offerings for enterprises and government organisations in India.\",\n   \"- e25 [party_statement; fool.com (Justin Pope); original source Jensen Huang, Nvidia CEO ; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] The author reports that Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang expects $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\\n    Quote: CEO Jensen Huang has laid out expectations for $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e35, e253; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e95 [fact; tradingview.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reported FY2027 Q1 revenue of $81.62 billion, up 85% year over year, and non-GAAP EPS of $1.87, up 140%.\\n    Quote: First-quarter fiscal 2027 revenues climbed 85% year over year to $81.62 billion, while non-GAAP earnings per share jumped 140% to $1.87.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e34, e255; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e240 [party_statement; NVIDIA Corporation; original source NVIDIA Corporation 2026-07-09; from nvblog:geforce-now-thursday-toronto-expansion 2026-07-09] NVIDIA said it plans to roll out a new RTX 5080-powered GeForce NOW server in Toronto within days, expanding cloud gaming service in the region.\\n    Quote: A new GeForce RTX 5080-powered GeForce NOW server is coming to Toronto, expanding service in the region and bringing dedicated cloud gaming performance closer to local members. The new server will roll out within days, giving more players access to top-tier cloud gaming across Canada.\",\n   \"- e246 [third_party_view; Citi analyst Atif Malik; original source Citi analyst Atif Malik ; from gnews:86c243945145ed901feb26cf 2026-07-09] Citi analyst Atif Malik said Nvidia had strong access to DRAM memory amid constrained industry supply.\\n    Quote: We maintain Nvidia as our top buy-rated mega-cap data center semis pick on strong access to DRAM memory amidst constrained industry supply,\",\n   \"- e253 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia management ; from gnews:931ee0196ca609e637235fad 2026-07-09] Nvidia management cited roughly $1 trillion in revenue visibility for Blackwell and Vera Rubin processors across 2026 and 2027, supported by multiyear commitments from hyperscalers and large enterprise customers.\\n    Quote: Management has also articulated roughly $1 trillion in revenue visibility for its Blackwell and Vera Rubin processors across 2026 and 2027, anchored by multiyear commitments from hyperscalers and large enterprise customers.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e25; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e254 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:b412380d12c5a222545d42f1 2026-07-09] Nvidia's revenue growth accelerated for three consecutive quarters.\\n    Quote: Nvidia's revenue has accelerated for three consecutive quarters.\",\n   \"- e255 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:b412380d12c5a222545d42f1 2026-07-09] Nvidia's revenue increased 85% year over year in its fiscal first quarter, its strongest increase in a year and a half.\\n    Quote: The 85% top-line jump it posted in its fiscal first quarter is the strongest increase in a year and a half.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e95; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e257 [fact; South China Morning Post; original source The US government ; from gnews:91684b863d274b10246d0c13 2026-07-09] The US government approved exports of Nvidia H200 GPUs to China in early 2026.\\n    Quote: In early 2026, Washington took the rare step of approving Nvidia’s H200 graphics processing unit for export to China\",\n   \"- e259 [fact; IEEE Spectrum; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:a4eb2bdfabca94f5887881c6 2026-07-09] Nvidia added photonics companies Ayar Labs, Marvell Technologies, and Lightmatter to the NVLink Fusion partner list this summer.\\n    Quote: This summer, the company’s list of partners has grown to include several photonics players such as Ayar Labs , Marvell Technologies, and Lightmatter.\",\n   \"- e261 [party_statement; IEEE Spectrum; original source Nvidia principal product marketing manager Jesse Clayton ; from gnews:a4eb2bdfabca94f5887881c6 2026-07-09] Nvidia expects to adopt optical interconnects in scale-up networking eventually as AI bandwidth requirements grow.\\n    Quote: Clayton says the company expects optics to move into scale-up networking eventually, as AI’s bandwidth requirements continue to grow.\",\n   \"- e267 [rumour; moomoo.com, citing Reuters and Meta’s internal memo; original source Meta ; from gnews:7b39859113d4e2b8ebd8aa86 2026-07-09] Meta reportedly plans to start manufacturing its AI chip in September, potentially adding competition in AI chips; the year was not specified.\\n    Quote: Meta Platforms (META.US)$ is reportedly planning to start manufacturing its AI chip in September, Reuters reported Thursday, citing the company’s internal memo.\",\n   \"- e268 [fact; moomoo.com, citing data compiled by Bloomberg; original source Quanta ; from gnews:7b39859113d4e2b8ebd8aa86 2026-07-09] Quanta’s June sales more than doubled year over year to NT$385.19 billion; the company supplies AI servers powered by Nvidia GPUs.\\n    Quote: Quanta, which supplies AI servers powered by Nvidia’s GPUs, saw its monthly sales more than double to 385.19 billion New Taiwanese dollars in June from a year earlier, according to data compiled by Bloomberg.\",\n   \"- e269 [fact; moomoo.com, citing Bloomberg; original source Hon Hai Precision Industry ; from gnews:7b39859113d4e2b8ebd8aa86 2026-07-09] Nvidia server-assembly partner Hon Hai reported June sales up 52% year over year to NT$821.8 billion and quarterly sales up 40%, according to Bloomberg.\\n    Quote: $HON HAI PRECISION INDUSTRY SPON GDS EACH REP 2 SHS TWD10 REG'S' (HNHPF.US)$ , Nvidia’s server assembly partner, saw a 52% surge in monthly sales in June to NT$ 821.8 billion, allowing the Taiwanese company to post a bigger-than-expected 40% surge in quarterly sales, according to Bloomberg.\",\n   \"- e270 [party_statement; moomoo.com, reporting NVIDIA’s statement to Bloomberg; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:7b39859113d4e2b8ebd8aa86 2026-07-09] NVIDIA told Bloomberg that it had no technical delay and that its product roadmap remained intact.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA recently issued a statement to Bloomberg denying claims of a technical delay, confirming that its product roadmap remains intact.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e66; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e273 [party_statement; au.finance.yahoo.com; original source Cerebras 2026-07-09; from gnews:66cb0387229ac4b1390615cb 2026-07-09] Cerebras said it plans to bring its first European data centre capacity online by the end of 2026, then expand across France and the Nordics; it gave no capacity figure for the first centre.\\n    Quote: US-based artificial intelligence chip maker Cerebras said on Thursday that it plans to bring its first European data centre capacity online by the end of 2026, followed by a rapid expansion across France and the Nordics, boosting its AI computing capacity in Europe.\",\n   \"- e275 [party_statement; au.finance.yahoo.com; original source Cerebras 2026-07-09; from gnews:66cb0387229ac4b1390615cb 2026-07-09] Cerebras said part of its planned European data centre capacity is expected to support OpenAI workloads; it did not specify the amount of capacity.\\n    Quote: Cerebras said that part of its planned data centre capacity is expected to support OpenAI workloads under the companies' existing partnership.\",\n   \"- e276 [party_statement; Andrew Feldman, quoted by au.finance.yahoo.com, attributing the statement to AFP; original source Andrew Feldman, Cerebras CEO ; from gnews:66cb0387229ac4b1390615cb 2026-07-09] Cerebras CEO Andrew Feldman said the planned expansions are worth several billion dollars; he did not specify a period or exact amount.\\n    Quote: \\\"These are massive expansions\\\" worth several billion dollars, chief executive Andrew Feldman told AFP on the sidelines of the RAISE Summit in Paris.\",\n   \"- e277 [party_statement; au.finance.yahoo.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:66cb0387229ac4b1390615cb 2026-07-09] Nvidia says its technology powers more than 90% of Europe's announced AI factory projects; the item gives no measurement date.\\n    Quote: The expansion comes as AI infrastructure investment accelerates across Europe, where Nvidia says its technology powers more than 90% of the continent's announced AI factory projects.\",\n   \"- e278 [third_party_view; Andrew Feldman, quoted by au.finance.yahoo.com, attributing the statement to AFP; original source Andrew Feldman, Cerebras CEO ; from gnews:66cb0387229ac4b1390615cb 2026-07-09] Cerebras CEO Andrew Feldman told AFP that European demand for generative-AI computing power is growing very quickly, faster than Cerebras can keep up.\\n    Quote: In Europe, demand for computing power to run generative AI is \\\"extraordinary... growing very, very quickly\\\", Feldman told AFP, adding that the sector's growth is \\\"faster than we can keep up\\\".\",\n   \"- e34 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:e4e5f1b5c0c68381e4c486e1 2026-07-03] Nvidia’s revenue grew 85% year over year in fiscal Q1 2027.\\n    Quote: In the first quarter of Nvidia's fiscal year 2027, ending April 26, the company grew revenue 85% year over year\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e95, e122, e302; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e95 [fact; tradingview.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reported FY2027 Q1 revenue of $81.62 billion, up 85% year over year, and non-GAAP EPS of $1.87, up 140%.\\n    Quote: First-quarter fiscal 2027 revenues climbed 85% year over year to $81.62 billion, while non-GAAP earnings per share jumped 140% to $1.87.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e34, e255, e283; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e96 [party_statement; tradingview.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] NVIDIA guided FY2027 Q2 revenue to approximately $91 billion, nearly 95% above the year-earlier quarter.\\n    Quote: For the second quarter of fiscal 2027, NVIDIA projects revenues of approximately $91 billion, representing nearly 95% year-over-year growth.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e117, e291; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e117 [party_statement; 247wallst.com (Omor Ibne Ehsan); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] NVIDIA management guided Q2 FY2027 revenue to $91.0 billion and non-GAAP gross margin to 75%.\\n    Quote: Management guided Q2 FY27 revenue to $91.0 billion with non-GAAP gross margin holding at 75%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e96, e284; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e121 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com (Omor Ibne Ehsan); original source 247wallst.com (Omor Ibne Ehsan) 2026-07-06; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] The author cites $119 billion of NVIDIA supply commitments as a risk if hyperscaler orders slow.\\n    Quote: Supply commitments of $119 billion compound demand risk if hyperscaler orders slow\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e106, e290; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e167 [third_party_view; fool.com (Keithen Drury); original source fool.com (Keithen Drury) 2026-07-07; from gnews:d0f3f83296df884fae64921e 2026-07-07] The author says new capacity across the memory-chip industry will not be online until 2027 or later, leaving inventory supply low for at least the next year and a half.\\n    Quote: As mentioned, new capacity for many in this industry won't be online until 2027 or later, creating a low supply of inventory for at least the next year and a half.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e300; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e216 [third_party_view; tradingview.com; original source Bloomberg-cited analysts ; from gnews:a09988fd9c5c1a739a14f873 2026-07-08] Bloomberg-cited projections put Nvidia FY2027 sales at $393 billion, up 82%; the article reports no separate date for the original estimate.\\n    Quote: The company is projected to generate $228 billion in profit on $393 billion in sales in fiscal 2027, which ends Jan. 31, representing expected growth of 90% and 82%, respectively, while its profit estimate has risen 13% over the past three months.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e47, e280, e281; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e226 [fact; qz.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:ee0d6792b6bf98069cfe0cc6 2026-07-08] Nvidia reported FY2027 first-quarter total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: For its fiscal first quarter of 2027, Nvidia posted $81.6 billion in total revenue — an 85% increase from a year earlier\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e98, e293, e301; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e267 [rumour; moomoo.com, citing Reuters and Meta’s internal memo; original source Meta ; from gnews:7b39859113d4e2b8ebd8aa86 2026-07-09] Meta reportedly plans to start manufacturing its AI chip in September, potentially adding competition in AI chips; the year was not specified.\\n    Quote: Meta Platforms (META.US)$ is reportedly planning to start manufacturing its AI chip in September, Reuters reported Thursday, citing the company’s internal memo.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e286; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e280 [third_party_view; Jeran Wittenstein, citing Bloomberg data; original source Bloomberg ; from gnews:49f225cd79fb22132f3b9ee4 2026-07-10] Bloomberg data projected Nvidia FY2027 profit of $228 billion, up 90%, and sales of $393 billion, up 82%.\\n    Quote: The chipmaker is projected to deliver $228 billion in profits on sales of $393 billion in fiscal 2027, which ends Jan. 31. That would represent an expansion of 90% and 82%, respectively, according to data compiled by Bloomberg.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e216; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e282 [third_party_view; Trefis; original source Trefis, reporting Wall Street consensus ; from gnews:6abaf2856736877236d30f6a 2026-07-10] Trefis reports Wall Street consensus expects NVIDIA revenue to grow about 32% annually over the next few years.\\n    Quote: Wall Street consensus sees NVIDIA’s revenue growing about 32% a year for the next few years.\",\n   \"- e283 [fact; Trefis; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:6abaf2856736877236d30f6a 2026-07-10] NVIDIA revenue grew 71% over the last twelve months and 85% in the most recent quarter, according to figures cited by Trefis.\\n    Quote: revenue grew 71% over the last twelve months and 85% in the most recent quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e95; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e284 [party_statement; Trefis; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:6abaf2856736877236d30f6a 2026-07-10] NVIDIA guided upcoming-quarter revenue to a midpoint of $91 billion.\\n    Quote: For the upcoming quarter, the company guided revenue to a midpoint of $91.00 billion, signaling continued strong demand.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e117; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e285 [party_statement; Trefis; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:6abaf2856736877236d30f6a 2026-07-10] NVIDIA management said its Vera CPU opens a new addressable market of $200 billion.\\n    Quote: Management sees its new Vera CPU opening a “brand new $200 billion TAM for NVIDIA,” a market it has never addressed before.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e61; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e288 [party_statement; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] NVIDIA’s Q2 FY2027 guidance excluded Data Center compute revenue from China, and NVIDIA reported zero H20 shipments in Q1 FY2027.\\n    Quote: Q2 FY27 guidance explicitly excludes Data Center compute revenue from China, and there were zero H20 shipments in the quarter.\",\n   \"- e290 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com; original source 247wallst.com 2026-07-10; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] The article cited $119 billion in NVIDIA total supply commitments and named OpenAI, Anthropic, and Meta as multi-gigawatt customers.\\n    Quote: backed by $119 billion in total supply commitments and OpenAI, Anthropic, and Meta all named as multi-gigawatt customers.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e121; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e291 [party_statement; 247wallst.com, citing NVIDIA’s guidance; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] NVIDIA guided to Q2 FY2027 revenue of $91 billion.\\n    Quote: Q2 FY27 guidance points to $91 billion in revenue.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e96; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e293 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially, and Data Center revenue of $75.2 billion.\\n    Quote: The company reported record revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially, with Data Center revenue reaching $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e226; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e298 [fact; theverge.com; original source Counterpoint ; from gnews:3839887e5ca53a0cb0e7c91e 2026-07-10] Counterpoint data cited in the article put SK Hynix’s global DRAM market share at 29% as of June 2026, versus Samsung at 38% and Micron at 22%.\\n    Quote: As of June 2026, SK Hynix makes up 29 percent of the global DRAM market, with Samsung at 38 percent and Micron at 22 percent, according to data from Counterpoint.\",\n   \"- e299 [party_statement; theverge.com; original source SK Group chairman Chey Tae-won ; from gnews:3839887e5ca53a0cb0e7c91e 2026-07-10] SK Group chairman Chey Tae-won said in June that SK Hynix plans to ramp up memory-chip capacity over the next five years to address a shortage that could last until 2030.\\n    Quote: SK Group chairman Chey Tae-won said in June that the company plans to ramp up its memory chip capacity over the next five years to address a shortage that could last until 2030, Bloomberg reports .\",\n   \"- e300 [third_party_view; Thomas Richmond, recounting Kristina Partsinevelos’s July 10 CNBC segment; original source Kristina Partsinevelos 2026-07-10; from gnews:9ae96ca750b8e3962c47795f 2026-07-10] CNBC’s Kristina Partsinevelos forecast that new memory supply would not arrive before late 2027, extending the shortage and keeping prices at record highs in the near term.\\n    Quote: “None of that supply, though, arrives before late 2027, which keeps the memory shortage going and record-high prices intact for now,” Partsinevelos said.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e167; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e301 [fact; Thomas Richmond, citing NVIDIA’s report; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:9ae96ca750b8e3962c47795f 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.62 billion, up 85.2% year over year.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.62 billion, up 85.2% year over year, with Data Center revenue of $75.25 billion and total supply-related commitments of $119.0 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e226; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e302 [fact; TIKR; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] Nvidia reported $82 billion in total revenue in its recent quarter, up 85% year over year, its third consecutive quarter of accelerating growth.\\n    Quote: The company posted $82 billion in total revenue, up 85% year-over-year, marking its third straight quarter of accelerating growth.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e34; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e175 [fact; 24/7 Wall St.; original source Broadcom ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] Broadcom AI semiconductor revenue was $10.8 billion in Q2, up 143% year over year, and the company guided to $16.0 billion for Q3.\\n    Quote: Q2 AI semiconductor revenue was $10.8 billion, +143% YoY, with Q3 guided to $16.0 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e100, e342, e343; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e226 [fact; qz.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:ee0d6792b6bf98069cfe0cc6 2026-07-08] Nvidia reported FY2027 first-quarter total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: For its fiscal first quarter of 2027, Nvidia posted $81.6 billion in total revenue — an 85% increase from a year earlier\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e98, e293, e301, e330, e351; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e283 [fact; Trefis; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:6abaf2856736877236d30f6a 2026-07-10] NVIDIA revenue grew 71% over the last twelve months and 85% in the most recent quarter, according to figures cited by Trefis.\\n    Quote: revenue grew 71% over the last twelve months and 85% in the most recent quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e95, e307; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e291 [party_statement; 247wallst.com, citing NVIDIA’s guidance; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] NVIDIA guided to Q2 FY2027 revenue of $91 billion.\\n    Quote: Q2 FY27 guidance points to $91 billion in revenue.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e96, e333; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e293 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially, and Data Center revenue of $75.2 billion.\\n    Quote: The company reported record revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially, with Data Center revenue reaching $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e226, e340; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e307 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:07cf5835d106467db5448c13 2026-07-12] Nvidia's revenue grew 85% in its past quarter.\\n    Quote: During its past quarter, Nvidia's revenue increased at an 85% clip.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e283; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e308 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:07cf5835d106467db5448c13 2026-07-12] Wall Street analysts expect Nvidia's revenue to grow 96% in Q2.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts expect 96% growth during Q2.\",\n   \"- e311 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Broadcom ; from gnews:f8f440b5020fec9773812b6e 2026-07-12] The author says Broadcom plans to ramp production of custom AI chips for Meta, Anthropic, and OpenAI in late 2026 and into 2027, a competitive development for Nvidia.\\n    Quote: Broadcom is also making custom AI chips for Meta Platforms , Anthropic, and OpenAI, and production for those chips is scheduled to ramp up late this year and into next.\",\n   \"- e312 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source the market ; from gnews:f8f440b5020fec9773812b6e 2026-07-12] The author reports that the market expects Nvidia to retain its growth lead for the full fiscal year, while Broadcom is closing the gap.\\n    Quote: Looking ahead, the market still expects Nvidia to maintain its lead for the full fiscal year, though Broadcom is starting to close the gap.\",\n   \"- e313 [third_party_view; Keithen Drury; original source Keithen Drury 2026-07-12; from gnews:f8f440b5020fec9773812b6e 2026-07-12] The author expects Nvidia to remain the fastest-growing of AMD, Nvidia, and Broadcom for some time.\\n    Quote: AMD is still well behind Nvidia, and while I think Broadcom is still a strong pick, Nvidia will likely retain its rapid-growth title for some time.\",\n   \"- e314 [rumour; tech-insider.org; original source The Information ; from gnews:8faf69f198e10f14aae67621 2026-07-12] The Information reported that Nvidia shelved the RTX 50 Super refresh in December 2025, including a completed-design 24GB RTX 5080 Super, and that the RTX 60-series is pushed back to 2028.\\n    Quote: According to The Information, Nvidia quietly shelved its planned RTX 50 “Super” refresh back in December 2025 — including a 24GB RTX 5080 Super that had reportedly reached completed-design stage — and reporting corroborated through September 2026 confirms the company’s next-generation RTX 60-series remains pushed back to 2028.\",\n   \"- e315 [rumour; tech-insider.org; original source CNBC ; from gnews:8faf69f198e10f14aae67621 2026-07-12] CNBC reported in January 2026 that Samsung, SK Hynix, and Micron had sold out their entire 2026 HBM output under long-term contracts to customers including hyperscalers.\\n    Quote: The root cause sits one layer below Nvidia entirely. Hyperscalers including Microsoft, Google, Meta, and Amazon are buying up high-bandwidth memory as fast as Samsung, SK Hynix, and Micron can produce it, and all three manufacturers have reportedly sold out their entire 2026 HBM output under long-term contracts, according to CNBC’s reporting from January 2026.\",\n   \"- e316 [rumour; tech-insider.org; original source Unnamed supply-chain sources ; from gnews:8faf69f198e10f14aae67621 2026-07-12] Nvidia is reportedly cutting RTX 50-series production by an estimated 15% to 20% through at least Q3 2026.\\n    Quote: Nvidia is reportedly cutting production of existing RTX 50-series cards already on shelves by an estimated 15% to 20% through at least Q3 2026 , which helps explain why street prices on cards like the RTX 5070 Ti and RTX 5080 have stayed stubbornly above MSRP for most of 2026\",\n   \"- e317 [rumour; tech-insider.org; original source Unnamed supply-chain sources ; from gnews:8faf69f198e10f14aae67621 2026-07-12] The RTX 5060 has reportedly been pulled from retail for at least six months.\\n    Quote: The entry-level RTX 5060 has taken the hardest hit, reportedly pulled from retail entirely for at least six months .\",\n   \"- e318 [third_party_view; tech-insider.org; original source PCWorld-cited reporting ; from gnews:8faf69f198e10f14aae67621 2026-07-12] PCWorld-cited reporting estimated Nvidia AI-accelerator profit margins at about 65%, versus roughly 40% for consumer gaming GPUs.\\n    Quote: According to reporting cited by PCWorld, Nvidia’s AI accelerators carry profit margins near 65% , compared with roughly 40% for consumer gaming GPUs.\",\n   \"- e319 [party_statement; tech-insider.org; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:8faf69f198e10f14aae67621 2026-07-12] Nvidia told Tom’s Hardware that it faced memory supply constraints, without confirming the reported 2026 gaming GPU skip.\\n    Quote: Nvidia has still not issued a full on-the-record confirmation of the 2026 gaming GPU gap, and the company continues to sell existing RTX 50-series inventory. Its only public acknowledgment to date remains the statement it gave to Tom’s Hardware confirming memory supply constraints, without confirming the broader skip outright.\",\n   \"- e320 [third_party_view; I/O Fund / io-fund.com; original source Yole Research ; from gnews:2dcfaef1a91c2976a4e347da 2026-07-12] Yole Research estimated that CXL-capable servers will exceed 90% of servers by the end of calendar 2026, up from two-thirds in Q1 2025.\\n    Quote: Yole Research estimated that in Q1 2025, two-thirds of servers were CXL-capable , and projects this figure will rise to more than 90% by the end of 2026.\",\n   \"- e321 [party_statement; I/O Fund / io-fund.com; original source Marvell ; from gnews:2dcfaef1a91c2976a4e347da 2026-07-12] Marvell plans to begin sampling its Structera S CXL 3.0 switch in calendar Q3 2026.\\n    Quote: Marvell expects to begin sampling its Structera S CXL 3.0 switch in calendar Q3 2026.\",\n   \"- e324 [third_party_view; I/O Fund / io-fund.com; original source I/O Fund 2026-07-12; from gnews:2dcfaef1a91c2976a4e347da 2026-07-12] I/O Fund analysts said Nvidia’s modular STX architecture could make CMX a new revenue driver.\\n    Quote: STX is modular, which is key to CMX being a new revenue driver for Nvidia.\",\n   \"- e325 [third_party_view; I/O Fund / io-fund.com; original source I/O Fund 2026-07-12; from gnews:2dcfaef1a91c2976a4e347da 2026-07-12] I/O Fund analysts said Nvidia’s CMX could gain significant traction but was unlikely to be a stock catalyst given Nvidia’s market capitalization.\\n    Quote: Nvidia’s CMX could gain significant traction, but is unlikely to be a stock catalyst at such a high market cap.\",\n   \"- e328 [third_party_view; barchart.com (author); original source Wedbush Securities ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Wedbush Securities said Nvidia’s Vera CPU platform could expand its addressable market beyond graphics processors and create billions of dollars in additional revenue; no period was specified.\\n    Quote: Wedbush Securities recently argued that Nvidia's new Vera CPU platform could expand the company's total addressable market (TAM) well beyond graphics processors, opening the door to billions of dollars in additional revenue.\",\n   \"- e329 [rumour; barchart.com (author); original source Unnamed reports ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Reports suggest Nvidia has begun offering Vera processors to cloud customers, including some in China where regulations allow; no date or amount was specified.\\n    Quote: Reports also suggest Nvidia has begun offering the new processors to cloud customers, including some in China where regulations allow.\",\n   \"- e330 [fact; barchart.com (author); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Nvidia reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: For the first quarter of fiscal 2027, revenue jumped 85% year-over-year (YOY) to $81.6 billion, easily beating analyst expectations.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e226; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e333 [party_statement; barchart.com (author); original source Nvidia management ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Nvidia guided to approximately $91 billion in Q2 FY2027 revenue, assuming no China data-center sales because of export restrictions.\\n    Quote: Management also issued strong guidance, forecasting approximately $91 billion in Q2 revenue despite assuming no China data-center sales because of export restrictions.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e291; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e334 [third_party_view; barchart.com (author); original source Wall Street consensus ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Wall Street’s consensus expects Nvidia FY2027 total revenue to exceed $300 billion and EPS to be $8.80.\\n    Quote: Wall Street expects Nvidia to generate well over $300 billion in fiscal 2027 revenue, while consensus earnings estimates have moved to $8.80 per share.\",\n   \"- e335 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source SK Hynix ; from gnews:03c38d2fe2e6e02ba5736307 2026-07-12] SK Hynix reported that quarterly revenue grew 198% to about $35 billion, a record, indicating strong demand in the memory market relevant to Nvidia’s supply.\\n    Quote: In the recent quarter, for example, the company reported revenue growth of 198% to about $35 billion dollars, a record level.\",\n   \"- e336 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source SK Hynix ; from gnews:03c38d2fe2e6e02ba5736307 2026-07-12] SK Hynix reported quarterly net income growth of 398% and an operating margin of 72%.\\n    Quote: Net income soared 398%, and operating margin came in at 72%.\",\n   \"- e337 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Counterpoint Research ; from gnews:03c38d2fe2e6e02ba5736307 2026-07-12] Counterpoint Research reported that SK Hynix held 58% of the global HBM market at the end of the first quarter, indicating the scale of Nvidia’s key memory supplier.\\n    Quote: SK Hynix held 58% share globally of the HBM market as of the end of the first quarter, according to Counterpoint Research.\",\n   \"- e338 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia and SK Hynix ; from gnews:03c38d2fe2e6e02ba5736307 2026-07-12] Nvidia and SK Hynix recently signed a multi-year technology partnership under which SK Hynix will supply memory for AI infrastructure, personal AI and robotics.\\n    Quote: The two companies even reinforced their relationship recently, signing a multi-year technology partnership. It involves SK Hynix supplying memory across a broad range of areas, from AI infrastructure to personal AI and robotics .\",\n   \"- e339 [party_statement; Jensen Huang; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:03c38d2fe2e6e02ba5736307 2026-07-12] Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang said SK Hynix has been Nvidia’s largest memory partner and will continue to be its largest memory partner.\\n    Quote: \\\"SK Hynix has been Nvidia's largest memory partner and will continue to be our largest memory partner,\\\" Nvidia chief Jensen Huang said at the time.\",\n   \"- e340 [fact; fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:635f19578778394086009f6f 2026-07-12] NVIDIA reported record total revenue of $81.6 billion in its fiscal quarter ended in late April, up 85% year over year and 20% quarter over quarter.\\n    Quote: In its most recent fiscal quarter (ended in late April), revenue hit a record $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% from the prior quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e293; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e342 [fact; fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source Broadcom ; from gnews:635f19578778394086009f6f 2026-07-12] Broadcom reported AI chip revenue of $10.8 billion last quarter, up 143% year over year.\\n    Quote: Its AI chip revenue jumped 143% year over year last quarter to $10.8 billion\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e175; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e343 [party_statement; fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source Broadcom management ; from gnews:635f19578778394086009f6f 2026-07-12] Broadcom management forecast roughly $16 billion in AI chip revenue for this quarter.\\n    Quote: management sees roughly $16 billion this quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e175; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e351 [fact; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] Nvidia reported record revenue of $81.6 billion in fiscal Q1 2027, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: During the fiscal first quarter of 2027, Nvidia generated record revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year-over-year (YOY).\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e226; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e353 [fact; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] Nvidia recently launched its Vera Rubin AI platform.\\n    Quote: Nvidia recently launched its Vera Rubin AI platform, released the AI PC platform RTX Spark, expanded partnerships with companies such as Alphabet (GOOGL) and Marvell (MRVL), and further invested in networking, CPUs, and AI infrastructure.\",\n   \"- e96 [party_statement; tradingview.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] NVIDIA guided FY2027 Q2 revenue to approximately $91 billion, nearly 95% above the year-earlier quarter.\\n    Quote: For the second quarter of fiscal 2027, NVIDIA projects revenues of approximately $91 billion, representing nearly 95% year-over-year growth.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e117, e291, e376; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e117 [party_statement; 247wallst.com (Omor Ibne Ehsan); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] NVIDIA management guided Q2 FY2027 revenue to $91.0 billion and non-GAAP gross margin to 75%.\\n    Quote: Management guided Q2 FY27 revenue to $91.0 billion with non-GAAP gross margin holding at 75%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e96, e284, e388; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e226 [fact; qz.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:ee0d6792b6bf98069cfe0cc6 2026-07-08] Nvidia reported FY2027 first-quarter total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: For its fiscal first quarter of 2027, Nvidia posted $81.6 billion in total revenue — an 85% increase from a year earlier\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e98, e293, e301, e330, e351, e392; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e293 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially, and Data Center revenue of $75.2 billion.\\n    Quote: The company reported record revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially, with Data Center revenue reaching $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e226, e340, e383; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e330 [fact; barchart.com (author); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Nvidia reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: For the first quarter of fiscal 2027, revenue jumped 85% year-over-year (YOY) to $81.6 billion, easily beating analyst expectations.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e226, e371, e386; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e333 [party_statement; barchart.com (author); original source Nvidia management ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Nvidia guided to approximately $91 billion in Q2 FY2027 revenue, assuming no China data-center sales because of export restrictions.\\n    Quote: Management also issued strong guidance, forecasting approximately $91 billion in Q2 revenue despite assuming no China data-center sales because of export restrictions.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e291, e380, e396; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e340 [fact; fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:635f19578778394086009f6f 2026-07-12] NVIDIA reported record total revenue of $81.6 billion in its fiscal quarter ended in late April, up 85% year over year and 20% quarter over quarter.\\n    Quote: In its most recent fiscal quarter (ended in late April), revenue hit a record $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% from the prior quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e293, e373; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e355 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu, quoted by The Verge; original source Xinzhou Wu, Nvidia head of automotive ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Nvidia automotive head Xinzhou Wu said the company has limited internal GPU compute and reviews its allocation across teams almost weekly, sometimes with CEO Jensen Huang’s help.\\n    Quote: Even Nvidia has a limited supply of GPU for compute. We have an internal priority, and I’m working with my colleagues basically almost on a weekly basis to decide how to set aside the different compute, sometimes for training, sometimes for testing, or resources for a different thread of work in the company. And sometimes we need Jensen [Huang, Nvidia CEO] to help, but yeah.\",\n   \"- e356 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu, quoted by The Verge; original source Xinzhou Wu, Nvidia head of automotive ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said Nvidia’s Hyperion 10 platform offers a base L2++ configuration with 10 cameras, three radars and no lidar, and a high-end configuration with 14 cameras, three lidars and seven radars for L4.\\n    Quote: We are looking at what we call the sufficient necessary sensor set to achieve a high level of autonomy.\",\n   \"- e357 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu, quoted by The Verge; original source Xinzhou Wu, Nvidia head of automotive ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu estimated that compute requirements for autonomous driving are growing roughly tenfold every two years.\\n    Quote: As you know, the computer’s growing at such a rapid pace. We talked about Moore’s Law in the semiconductor industry some time ago, but in the autonomous driving segment, the computer need has been growing at a really astonishing pace. Roughly we are talking about 10 times every two years. It’s insane. And right now, with the success of AI and obviously Nvidia, we will be able to provide this kind \",\n   \"- e358 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu, quoted by The Verge; original source Xinzhou Wu, Nvidia head of automotive ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said chip prices would most likely need to rise because demand is intense for available chips.\\n    Quote: Actually, most likely even the chip price will need to go up, because of this intense demand for every chip everybody can grab onto.\",\n   \"- e359 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu, quoted by The Verge; original source Xinzhou Wu, Nvidia head of automotive ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said Nvidia continues investing in autonomous-vehicle technology by allocating internal compute and is looking into allocating fabrication capacity for the business.\\n    Quote: We keep investing in this technology and in this future, not only by allocating internal compute, but with fab capacity as well. That’s definitely one of the things we are looking into.\",\n   \"- e360 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu, quoted by The Verge; original source Xinzhou Wu, Nvidia head of automotive ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu predicted that Level 4 autonomy will become a mainstream experience in cars in less than five years.\\n    Quote: That’s exactly my mission, trying to help the industry to get there. I would say if I need to give a time, I wouldn’t say five years, but less than five years.\",\n   \"- e361 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu, quoted by The Verge; original source Xinzhou Wu, Nvidia head of automotive ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said Nvidia plans to roll out its ADAS technology in all Mercedes vehicles and with some other partners across the United States by the end of 2026, then try to expand it to the rest of the world in the following years.\\n    Quote: First of all, by the end of this year, we are rolling out our technology on the ADAS side in all Mercedes vehicles and some other partners as well, all over the United States. Starting in the next few years, we’ll try to roll out this technology to the rest of the world.\",\n   \"- e362 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu, quoted by The Verge; original source Xinzhou Wu, Nvidia head of automotive ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said Nvidia is working with Uber and is trying to roll out an L4 service in the next few years.\\n    Quote: Meanwhile, we are also working closely with our partners, for example, Uber. We announced that at GTC, we are trying to roll out our L4 service in the next few years.\",\n   \"- e363 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu, quoted by The Verge; original source Xinzhou Wu, Nvidia head of automotive ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said 80% of mass-production automakers are currently in Nvidia’s Hyperion ecosystem for L4.\\n    Quote: Right now, I would say 80% of the mass-production OEMs are in Nvidia’s Hyperion ecosystem for L4.\",\n   \"- e366 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Sean Williams 2026-07-13; from gnews:e7e8cbf33738ceb5865837f0 2026-07-13] The author argues that customer-developed chips could occupy data-center capacity and erode Nvidia’s pricing-power and gross-margin tailwind from GPU supply shortages.\\n    Quote: For starters, some of Nvidia's pricing power and otherworldly gross margin originates from persistent GPU supply shortages. If the company's top customers are developing chips that take up valuable data center real estate, Nvidia can quickly lose its biggest tailwind .\",\n   \"- e367 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Sean Williams 2026-07-13; from gnews:e7e8cbf33738ceb5865837f0 2026-07-13] The author identifies competition from customers’ internally developed chips as the greatest threat to Nvidia’s ongoing success.\\n    Quote: There's no question that internal competition is the greatest threat to Nvidia's ongoing success .\",\n   \"- e368 [rumour; GuruFocus; original source The Information ; from gnews:1c47fd978ef50b1d7f48cbd8 2026-07-13] Google reportedly approached neocloud companies about using its TPUs, with no amount or timeline specified.\\n    Quote: Google has approached so-called neocloud companies about using its tensor processing units, or TPUs, according to a report from The Information.\",\n   \"- e369 [rumour; GuruFocus; original source Nscale ; from gnews:1c47fd978ef50b1d7f48cbd8 2026-07-13] Nscale reportedly told Google that its active projects remain centered on GPU capacity; no amount or timeline was specified.\\n    Quote: One provider, Nscale, reportedly told Google that its active projects remain centered on GPU capacity.\",\n   \"- e370 [fact; GuruFocus; original source Google and Blackstone ; from gnews:1c47fd978ef50b1d7f48cbd8 2026-07-13] Google and Blackstone are working on a cloud venture that plans to rent TPU capacity to AI labs and financial firms in 2027; no capacity amount was given.\\n    Quote: Google is also working with Blackstone on a new cloud venture that plans to rent TPU capacity to AI labs and financial firms next year.\",\n   \"- e371 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f4eb5206f2995f5dbb86c5e9 2026-07-13] Nvidia reported revenue of $81.6 billion in its quarter ended April 26, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: In its most recent quarter (ended April 26), it made $81.6 billion in revenue (up 85% year over year)\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e330; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e373 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3a9054a950c410e249837c91 2026-07-13] Nvidia reported record total revenue of $81.6 billion in FY2027 Q1, up 85% year over year and 20% quarter over quarter.\\n    Quote: For its fiscal 2027 first quarter (ended April 26), Nvidia generated record revenue, up 85% year over year and 20% quarter over quarter to $81.6 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e340; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e376 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:3a9054a950c410e249837c91 2026-07-13] NVIDIA management forecast Q2 revenue of $91 billion, up 95% year over year.\\n    Quote: Management expects its growth spurt to continue, forecasting year-over-year revenue growth of 95% to $91 billion in Q2.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e96; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e379 [fact; Alex Sirois; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:799ec454c15ddf61f08d042f 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.615 billion, up 85.23%, and Data Center revenue of $75.246 billion; networking revenue was up 199%.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA’s Q1 FY2027 revenue reached $81.615 billion, up 85.23%, with Data Center at $75.246 billion and networking alone up 199%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e115; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e382 [third_party_view; Alex Sirois; original source Analyst consensus, as reported by Alex Sirois ; from gnews:799ec454c15ddf61f08d042f 2026-07-13] The article reported analyst consensus price targets of $301.62 for NVIDIA and $523.73 for Broadcom; Broadcom had 44 buy ratings and no sell ratings.\\n    Quote: Analyst consensus targets tell the same story: $523.73 for AVGO against $301.62 for NVDA, with 44 buys and zero sells on Broadcom.\",\n   \"- e383 [fact; Vandita Jadeja, 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:301b0738dab6ca32e88b019a 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.61 billion, up 85.2% year over year, including Data Center revenue of $75.25 billion.\\n    Quote: Q1 FY27 revenue hit $81.61 billion, +85.2% YoY, with Data Center at $75.25 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e293; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e386 [fact; 247wallst.com, citing NVIDIA’s reported results; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:b68c019528300c6a1fcd3515 2026-07-13] NVIDIA total revenue was $81.615 billion in Q1 FY2027, up 85.2% year over year.\\n    Quote: Total revenue was $81.615 billion, growing 85.2%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e330; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e388 [party_statement; 247wallst.com, citing NVIDIA’s guidance; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:b68c019528300c6a1fcd3515 2026-07-13] NVIDIA guided to $91 billion in total revenue and a 75% non-GAAP gross margin for Q2 FY2027.\\n    Quote: But NVIDIA guided $91 billion for Q2 FY27 anyway, with a 75% non-GAAP gross margin.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e117; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e390 [fact; Abhinav Raj, XDA Developers; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:6e27fc3ef50f99b180c6646a 2026-07-13] Nvidia rolled out its second-generation transformer-based upscaler as a driver update at CES 2026, with support for RTX generations dating back to 2018.\\n    Quote: When Nvidia rolled out its second-gen transformer-based upscaler at CES 2026, it arrived as a driver update, in week one, for every RTX generation going all the way back to 2018.\",\n   \"- e391 [third_party_view; Samarveer Singh, XDA Developers; original source AMD ; from gnews:6e27fc3ef50f99b180c6646a 2026-07-13] AMD has committed to bringing FSR 4.1 to RDNA 2 cards, with the rollout expected to extend into 2027.\\n    Quote: AMD, to its credit, has committed to bringing FSR 4.1 to RDNA 2 cards, but that rollout is expected to stretch into 2027, seven years after those GPUs launched and two full years behind the equivalent Nvidia moment.\",\n   \"- e392 [fact; 247wallst.com (Alex Sirois); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:221f52333c8f5e936e515c4d 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported revenue of $81.615 billion, up 85.23%, for the quarter discussed.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA ( NASDAQ: NVDA ) followed with $81.615 billion and 85.23% growth.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e226; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e394 [fact; 247wallst.com (Alex Sirois); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:221f52333c8f5e936e515c4d 2026-07-13] NVIDIA shipped zero H20 chips to China in the quarter, compared with $4.6 billion of H20 shipments a year earlier.\\n    Quote: Yet zero H20 chips shipped to China this quarter, versus $4.6 billion a year ago.\",\n   \"- e396 [party_statement; 247wallst.com (Alex Sirois); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:221f52333c8f5e936e515c4d 2026-07-13] NVIDIA guided to quarterly revenue of $91.0 billion, plus or minus 2%, excluding China.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA guided to $91.0 billion, plus or minus 2%, explicitly excluding China.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e333; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e397 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com (Alex Sirois); original source 247wallst.com (Alex Sirois) 2026-07-13; from gnews:221f52333c8f5e936e515c4d 2026-07-13] The author said NVIDIA carries $119 billion in supply commitments tied to hyperscaler order books.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA, by contrast, carries $119 billion in supply commitments, tying its fortunes to hyperscaler order books .\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e121; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e26 [third_party_view; fool.com (Justin Pope); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] Wall Street analysts estimate Nvidia revenue of $392 billion in FY2027.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts estimate that Nvidia's business could double over the next couple of years, from trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion to $392 billion this fiscal year, and $554 billion the following year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e204, e406; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e51 [fact; datacenters.economictimes.indiatimes.com; original source Firmus ; from gnews:1e7a9c953f3ad70093b67ae4 2026-07-04] Firmus is developing a DSX AI factory campus in Batam, Indonesia, expected to reach 360 MW and accommodate up to 170,000 NVIDIA GPUs.\\n    Quote: Firmus is developing a DSX AI factory campus in Batam, Indonesia, which is expected to scale to 360 megawatts and accommodate up to 170,000 Nvidia GPUs.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e44, e463; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e253 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia management ; from gnews:931ee0196ca609e637235fad 2026-07-09] Nvidia management cited roughly $1 trillion in revenue visibility for Blackwell and Vera Rubin processors across 2026 and 2027, supported by multiyear commitments from hyperscalers and large enterprise customers.\\n    Quote: Management has also articulated roughly $1 trillion in revenue visibility for its Blackwell and Vera Rubin processors across 2026 and 2027, anchored by multiyear commitments from hyperscalers and large enterprise customers.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e25, e405; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e255 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:b412380d12c5a222545d42f1 2026-07-09] Nvidia's revenue increased 85% year over year in its fiscal first quarter, its strongest increase in a year and a half.\\n    Quote: The 85% top-line jump it posted in its fiscal first quarter is the strongest increase in a year and a half.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e95, e431; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e291 [party_statement; 247wallst.com, citing NVIDIA’s guidance; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] NVIDIA guided to Q2 FY2027 revenue of $91 billion.\\n    Quote: Q2 FY27 guidance points to $91 billion in revenue.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e96, e333, e420; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e301 [fact; Thomas Richmond, citing NVIDIA’s report; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:9ae96ca750b8e3962c47795f 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.62 billion, up 85.2% year over year.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.62 billion, up 85.2% year over year, with Data Center revenue of $75.25 billion and total supply-related commitments of $119.0 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e226, e418; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e333 [party_statement; barchart.com (author); original source Nvidia management ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Nvidia guided to approximately $91 billion in Q2 FY2027 revenue, assuming no China data-center sales because of export restrictions.\\n    Quote: Management also issued strong guidance, forecasting approximately $91 billion in Q2 revenue despite assuming no China data-center sales because of export restrictions.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e291, e380, e396, e437; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e342 [fact; fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source Broadcom ; from gnews:635f19578778394086009f6f 2026-07-12] Broadcom reported AI chip revenue of $10.8 billion last quarter, up 143% year over year.\\n    Quote: Its AI chip revenue jumped 143% year over year last quarter to $10.8 billion\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e175, e441; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e351 [fact; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] Nvidia reported record revenue of $81.6 billion in fiscal Q1 2027, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: During the fiscal first quarter of 2027, Nvidia generated record revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year-over-year (YOY).\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e226, e427; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e376 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:3a9054a950c410e249837c91 2026-07-13] NVIDIA management forecast Q2 revenue of $91 billion, up 95% year over year.\\n    Quote: Management expects its growth spurt to continue, forecasting year-over-year revenue growth of 95% to $91 billion in Q2.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e96, e430; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e404 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Goldman Sachs ; from gnews:84e90d3da2d3779da0e7bdb0 2026-07-14] Goldman Sachs estimates AI compute spending at approximately $494 billion in 2026, growing to $1.13 trillion by 2031.\\n    Quote: Goldman Sachs estimates that AI compute spending will grow from approximately $494 billion this year to $1.13 trillion by 2031.\",\n   \"- e405 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:84e90d3da2d3779da0e7bdb0 2026-07-14] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang sees at least $1 trillion in revenue from the Blackwell and Rubin platforms through the end of 2027.\\n    Quote: CEO Jensen Huang has said that he sees at least $1 trillion in revenue from Nvidia's Blackwell and Rubin platforms through the end of 2027.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e253; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e418 [fact; 247wallst.com, reporting NVIDIA’s results; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:1e1fa5a194198eaf05d90c9e 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.615 billion, up 85.23% year over year.\\n    Quote: It delivered $81.615 billion in Q1 FY27 revenue, up 85.23% year over year\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e301, e432; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e420 [party_statement; 247wallst.com, reporting NVIDIA’s guidance; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:1e1fa5a194198eaf05d90c9e 2026-07-14] NVIDIA guided to Q2 FY2027 revenue of $91 billion.\\n    Quote: Q2 FY27 revenue guided to $91 billion\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e291; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e426 [rumour; Tom's Hardware, relaying the Financial Times; original source Unnamed sources cited by the Financial Times ; from gnews:2a41a34c16f5280b624481fb 2026-07-14] Unnamed sources cited by the Financial Times said Nvidia cut its roster of authorized clients in Asia by more than half and subjected the remaining clients to tougher compliance inspections to deter shipments of Nvidia GPUs and servers into China.\\n    Quote: According to the Financial Times , this roster cuts the number of authorized clients by more than half, with those remaining having passed tougher compliance inspections to ensure that they are genuine businesses, not shell companies designed to forward Nvidia GPUs and servers into China.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e467; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e427 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ac8a489e54fbb1b85a1c7a2c 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85.2% year over year.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA’s Q1 FY27 revenue hit $81.6 billion, up 85.2% YoY\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e351; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e429 [party_statement; Jensen Huang, quoted by 247wallst.com; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:ac8a489e54fbb1b85a1c7a2c 2026-07-14] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said the AI-factory buildout was accelerating at extraordinary speed.\\n    Quote: The buildout of AI factories, the largest infrastructure expansion in human history, is accelerating at extraordinary speed.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e389; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e430 [party_statement; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ac8a489e54fbb1b85a1c7a2c 2026-07-14] NVIDIA guided to Q2 revenue of $91 billion.\\n    Quote: unusual for a company guiding to $91 billion in Q2 revenue.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e376; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e431 [third_party_view; Alex Sirois; original source Alex Sirois 2026-07-14; from gnews:ac8a489e54fbb1b85a1c7a2c 2026-07-14] The author characterized NVIDIA as growing revenue 85% and having 75% gross margins, and judged its shares compelling at 22 times forward earnings.\\n    Quote: Paying 22x forward earnings for 85% revenue growth and 75% gross margins makes Nvidia the more compelling twelve-month setup.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e255; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e432 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:184645c8d683d95b684bd6da 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.615 billion, up 85.23% year over year.\\n    Quote: Revenue hit $81.615 billion, up 85.23% YoY\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e418; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e436 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com; original source 247wallst.com 2026-07-14; from gnews:184645c8d683d95b684bd6da 2026-07-14] The author cited $119 billion in NVIDIA supply commitments; the item gives no period for the commitments.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA is spending like a company that already won , with $119 billion in supply commitments\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e121; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e437 [party_statement; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:184645c8d683d95b684bd6da 2026-07-14] NVIDIA guided Q2 revenue to $91 billion, assuming no China Data Center compute revenue.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA guided Q2 to $91 billion in revenue, which assumes zero China Data Center compute.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e333; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e438 [fact; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:386a294bd395bde25e3f4a11 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.61 billion, up 85.2% year over year.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA’s Q1 FY27 revenue hit $81.61B, up 85.2% YoY\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e114; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e440 [party_statement; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source Broadcom management ; from gnews:386a294bd395bde25e3f4a11 2026-07-14] Broadcom guided to Q3 revenue of $29.4 billion, up 84% year over year, and stated a goal of exceeding $100 billion in AI sales by 2027.\\n    Quote: Broadcom guided Q3 revenue to $29.4B (+84% YoY), and management’s stated goal is to exceed $100B in AI sales by 2027.\",\n   \"- e441 [fact; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source Broadcom ; from gnews:386a294bd395bde25e3f4a11 2026-07-14] Broadcom reported AI semiconductor revenue of $10.8 billion last quarter, up 143% year over year.\\n    Quote: AI semi revenue grew 143% YoY to $10.8B last quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e342; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e446 [fact; rdworldonline.com; original source Tecan 2026-06-24; from gnews:b46d410f1a3e3ad1888d51de 2026-07-14] Tecan integrated NVIDIA’s BioNeMo Agent Toolkit into its Introspect analytics platform and opened early access to the agentic AI features to pharmaceutical, biotech and clinical labs on June 24, 2026.\\n    Quote: Tecan’s latest bet is on agents. The Swiss lab automation company has built agentic AI into Introspect, its cloud analytics platform, using NVIDIA’s BioNeMo Agent Toolkit, in an announcement on June 24 that opened early access to pharmaceutical, biotech and clinical labs.\",\n   \"- e447 [fact; Rest of World; original source Humain 2026-06-01; from gnews:01a49ffd41f6abe24538da65 2026-07-14] Humain agreed on June 1 for Saudi Arabia to use Nvidia technology in self-driving taxis.\\n    Quote: Saudi Arabia agreed on June 1 to use self-driving taxis that run on Nvidia technology — from the computer inside each car to the software that steers it. The deal with the U.S. chipmaker was struck by Humain, the venture set up by Saudi Arabia’s Public Investment Fund last year to make the kingdom a global AI power.\",\n   \"- e448 [fact; Rest of World; original source Humain ; from gnews:01a49ffd41f6abe24538da65 2026-07-14] Humain is building data centers in Riyadh and Dammam that are planned to use several hundred thousand Nvidia chips.\\n    Quote: Humain is also building data centers in Riyadh and Dammam, powered by several hundred thousand Nvidia chips.\",\n   \"- e449 [fact; Rest of World; original source G42 ; from gnews:01a49ffd41f6abe24538da65 2026-07-14] G42’s first stage of its Abu Dhabi Stargate data center is planned to run on 400,000 Nvidia chips.\\n    Quote: Its first stage will run on 400,000 Nvidia chips .\",\n   \"- e450 [third_party_view; Rest of World, quoting Kamil Dimmich; original source Kamil Dimmich ; from gnews:01a49ffd41f6abe24538da65 2026-07-14] Humain’s first order from Nvidia was 18,000 Blackwell chips, according to Kamil Dimmich.\\n    Quote: Humain's first order from Nvidia was 18,000 of its newest Blackwell chips — the hardware that does that heavy lifting, which no rival can yet match, he said.\",\n   \"- e451 [fact; Tom's Hardware, reporting Reuters; original source U.S. government 2026-07-14; from gnews:3221eba2826b001b12b82770 2026-07-14] The U.S. approved ZTE and Maginfra to buy Nvidia H200 chips on July 14, 2026.\\n    Quote: Today, Reuters reports that Chinese telecoms giant ZTE and server firm Maginfra have received U.S. approval to buy Nvidia's last-gen H200 \\\"Hopper\\\" chips.\",\n   \"- e452 [third_party_view; Tom's Hardware; original source Tom's Hardware 2026-07-14; from gnews:3221eba2826b001b12b82770 2026-07-14] U.S. policy allows case-by-case sales of Nvidia Hopper-family chips, but not Blackwell chips, to Chinese firms and imposes a 25% export tariff.\\n    Quote: The current status of the AI chip trade situation is roughly that the U.S. allows Chinese firms to buy AI chips up to and including the Hopper family (meaning no Blackwell chips), with a 25% export tariff, though final decisions are made on a case-by-case basis.\",\n   \"- e453 [party_statement; Tom's Hardware, citing CNBC; original source U.S. trade official 2026-07-14; from gnews:3221eba2826b001b12b82770 2026-07-14] A U.S. trade official said very few shipments had taken place against licenses for H200 chips and equivalents as of July 14, 2026.\\n    Quote: CNBC cites a U.S. trade official who today stated that \\\"very few shipments against licenses for H200s and equivalents have taken place. It’s a very small quantity of chips\\\" during a congressional hearing.\",\n   \"- e456 [third_party_view; ebc.com; original source ebc.com 2026-07-14; from gnews:f83ae0a4f01c18d48f20a629 2026-07-14] Nvidia’s Vera Rubin architecture remains on track for shipment in late 2026, according to the article.\\n    Quote: the Vera Rubin architecture remains officially on track for late 2026\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e24; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e467 [rumour; Business Times, reporting the Financial Times; original source Financial Times, citing unnamed people familiar with the matter 2026-07-14; from gnews:dc642adc9738cb72e71bf4cd 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reportedly more than halved the number of Asian customers authorised to buy its AI chips after creating a whitelist of companies that passed tougher checks to prevent chips reaching China; the report was dated July 14, 2026.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA has more than halved the number of Asian customers authorised to buy its AI chips after creating a new “white list” of companies that have passed tougher compliance checks aimed at preventing the products from reaching China, the Financial Times reported on Monday (Jul 14).\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e426; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e468 [rumour; Business Times, reporting the Financial Times; original source Financial Times, citing three unnamed people familiar with the matter 2026-07-14; from gnews:dc642adc9738cb72e71bf4cd 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reportedly intensified customer due diligence in Singapore, Malaysia and Japan over the past few months, according to three unnamed people cited by the Financial Times.\\n    Quote: Over the past few months, the chipmaker has intensified due diligence in Singapore, Malaysia and Japan, the report added, citing three people familiar with the matter.\",\n   \"- e469 [fact; Business Times, reporting Reuters; original source US Commerce Department ; from gnews:dc642adc9738cb72e71bf4cd 2026-07-14] The US Commerce Department issued guidance in May 2026 aimed at curbing advanced AI chips reaching overseas subsidiaries of Chinese companies, citing concerns that Nvidia Blackwell processors may have reached Chinese-linked entities in countries including Malaysia.\\n    Quote: The US Commerce Department issued guidance in May aimed at curbing advanced AI chips from reaching overseas subsidiaries of Chinese companies, highlighting concerns that Nvidia’s cutting-edge Blackwell processors may have been exported to Chinese-linked entities in countries such as Malaysia despite US restrictions.\",\n   \"- e470 [rumour; Business Times, reporting the Financial Times; original source Financial Times, citing unnamed sources 2026-07-14; from gnews:dc642adc9738cb72e71bf4cd 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reportedly tightened compliance procedures under pressure from Washington, with staff visiting customers’ data centres, verifying contracts and interviewing end users.\\n    Quote: Nvidia has tightened compliance procedures following pressure from Washington, the FT said, adding that staff now visit customers’ data centres, verify contracts and interview end users as part of the checks.\",\n   \"- e471 [rumour; Business Times, reporting the Financial Times; original source Financial Times, citing unnamed sources 2026-07-14; from gnews:dc642adc9738cb72e71bf4cd 2026-07-14] The Financial Times reported that the US Department of Commerce was providing oversight and political backing for the compliance checks.\\n    Quote: The US Department of Commerce is also involved, providing oversight and political backing, the report said.\"\n  ],\n  \"points_to_rule\": [\n   \"item i295\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"control\": 16,\n  \"ruler_question\": {\n   \"question\": \"What will Nvidia's total revenue be in FY2028?\",\n   \"unit\": \"USD\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2028-02-28\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2028 total revenue is at least $650 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 650000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": null\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2028 total revenue is at least $550 billion and below $650 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 550000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 650000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2028 total revenue is at least $480 billion and below $550 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 480000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 550000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2028 total revenue is at least $420 billion and below $480 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 420000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 480000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2028 total revenue is below $420 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": 420000000000.0\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"judged_question\": {\n   \"view_id\": \"v5\",\n   \"question\": \"What will Nvidia's total revenue be in FY2028?\",\n   \"looks_at\": \"Nvidia total revenue in FY2028.\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2028-02-28\",\n   \"year\": \"FY2028\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\"\n  },\n  \"judged_rungs\": [\n   {\n    \"position\": 1,\n    \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n    \"condition\": \"Total revenue is above $610 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": 610000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": null\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 2,\n    \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n    \"condition\": \"Total revenue is above $554 billion and at or below $610 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": 554000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 610000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 3,\n    \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n    \"condition\": \"Total revenue is at or below $554 billion and at or above $500 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": 500000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 554000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 4,\n    \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n    \"condition\": \"Total revenue is below $500 billion and at or above $450 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": 450000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 500000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 5,\n    \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n    \"condition\": \"Total revenue is below $450 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": null,\n    \"hi\": 450000000000.0\n   }\n  ],\n  \"reader_b_decisive_items\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i037\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-02\",\n    \"title\": \"Microsoft vs. Nvidia: Which Is the Better AI Stock to Own for the Next 3 Years?\",\n    \"passage\": \"from trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion to $392 billion this fiscal year, and $554 billion the following year\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"Wall Street analysts\",\n     \"what\": \"NVIDIA total revenue estimates\",\n     \"how_much\": \"$392 billion this fiscal year, $554 billion next year (from $253 billion trailing twelve months)\",\n     \"period\": \"this fiscal year (FY2027) and the following year (FY2028)\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i256\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-07\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Stock Is Down 17% From Its High. Is the Artificial Intelligence (AI) Leader Finally Cheap?\",\n    \"passage\": \"This year, the big four AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures . Next year, Nvidia claims this group will spend more than $1 trillion.\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"big four AI hyperscalers' own plans (2026); NVIDIA's claim (2027)\",\n     \"what\": \"data-center capital expenditure of the big four\",\n     \"how_much\": \"around $650bn (2026); more than $1 trillion (2027)\",\n     \"period\": \"calendar 2026; calendar 2027\",\n     \"status\": \"plan (2026); forecast by NVIDIA (2027)\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i079\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-03\",\n    \"title\": \"Here's What a $25,000 Investment in Nvidia Could Be Worth if History Repeats Itself\",\n    \"passage\": \"In March, CEO Jensen Huang said he expects the company's Blackwell and Vera Rubin chips to generate $1 trillion in sales between that time and the end of 2027\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"Jensen Huang\",\n     \"what\": \"Blackwell and Vera Rubin sales\",\n     \"how_much\": \"$1 trillion\",\n     \"period\": \"March 2026 to end-2027\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i100\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-05\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia's next-gen AI rack system delayed to 2028 on manufacturing snags, SemiAnalysis says\",\n    \"passage\": \"Kyber NVL144 rack architecture has been delayed to 2028 as the PCB midplane remains challenging from a manufacturability standpoint\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"SemiAnalysis (a research firm's report, not NVIDIA)\",\n     \"what\": \"Kyber NVL144 rack for Vera Rubin Ultra delayed; cause: PCB midplane manufacturability\",\n     \"how_much\": \"more than 12 months\",\n     \"period\": \"from 2027 to 2028\",\n     \"status\": \"claim\"\n    }\n   }\n  ],\n  \"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\": [\n   \"- e25 [party_statement; fool.com (Justin Pope); original source Jensen Huang, Nvidia CEO ; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] The author reports that Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang expects $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\\n    Quote: CEO Jensen Huang has laid out expectations for $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\",\n   \"- e26 [third_party_view; fool.com (Justin Pope); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] Wall Street analysts estimate Nvidia revenue of $392 billion in FY2027.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts estimate that Nvidia's business could double over the next couple of years, from trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion to $392 billion this fiscal year, and $554 billion the following year.\",\n   \"- e25 [party_statement; fool.com (Justin Pope); original source Jensen Huang, Nvidia CEO ; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] The author reports that Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang expects $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\\n    Quote: CEO Jensen Huang has laid out expectations for $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e35; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e30 [fact; storagereview.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-07-01; from gnews:8c9d215416b714064de3b095 2026-07-03] NVIDIA removed the AI Enterprise subscription requirement for Omniverse production use and redistribution; the change was announced July 1, 2026, and the licensing documentation says it took effect in May 2026.\\n    Quote: The new terms remove that requirement entirely; anything built with Omniverse can also be redistributed under the same free terms, which is a substantive impact for ISVs and integrators who embed Omniverse applications inside their own products.\",\n   \"- e32 [fact; Ben Wodecki, SDxCentral; original source Microsoft and MediaTek ; from gnews:1740f3733eedc34d8bac9b65 2026-07-03] Microsoft and MediaTek plan to launch microLED-based data center networking interconnects for partners by late 2027.\\n    Quote: The pair plans to launch microLED-based data center networking interconnects for partners by late 2027 .\",\n   \"- e33 [party_statement; Ben Wodecki, SDxCentral, recounting Aldo Kamper's remarks to investors; original source Aldo Kamper, AMS-Osram CEO ; from gnews:1740f3733eedc34d8bac9b65 2026-07-03] AMS-Osram CEO Aldo Kamper said the company was working toward developing microLED optical interconnects for inside racks and for chip-to-chip communication between GPUs and high-bandwidth memory.\\n    Quote: AMS-Osram’s efforts, meanwhile, will see work toward developing microLED optical interconnects for inside the rack as well as chip-to-chip communication between graphic processing units (GPUs) and high-bandwidth memory, CEO Aldo Kamper told investors during its Q1 2026 earnings call back in May.\",\n   \"- e35 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Jensen Huang, Nvidia CEO ; from gnews:e4e5f1b5c0c68381e4c486e1 2026-07-03] In March, CEO Jensen Huang expected Nvidia’s Blackwell and Vera Rubin chips to generate $1 trillion in sales from then through the end of 2027.\\n    Quote: In March, CEO Jensen Huang said he expects the company's Blackwell and Vera Rubin chips to generate $1 trillion in sales between that time and the end of 2027.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e25; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e36 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia management ; from gnews:e4e5f1b5c0c68381e4c486e1 2026-07-03] Nvidia management said it thinks the company can generate nearly $20 billion in CPU sales; no period was specified.\\n    Quote: Management said they think they can generate nearly $20 billion of CPU sales, making it an instant industry leader.\",\n   \"- e47 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568 2026-07-04] Wall Street analysts project Nvidia revenue growth of 82% in FY2027 and 41% in FY2028.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts project 82% revenue growth for this year and 41% next year, so there's another external source that's projecting even more growth for Nvidia.\",\n   \"- e52 [rumour; SemiAnalysis, as quoted by CNBC; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis said Nvidia’s Kyber NVL144 rack architecture is delayed to 2028 because of midplane manufacturability challenges.\\n    Quote: Kyber NVL144 rack architecture has been delayed to 2028 as the PCB midplane remains challenging from a manufacturability standpoint,\",\n   \"- e53 [rumour; CNBC, reporting SemiAnalysis’s assessment; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis said Nvidia’s NVL576 system is likely to be delayed or limited to small volumes.\\n    Quote: NVL576 — a larger system linking eight racks via optical connections — is also likely delayed or limited to small volumes, the research firm said.\",\n   \"- e54 [rumour; SemiAnalysis, as quoted by CNBC; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis said Nvidia scrapped a backup plan to bolt two current-generation racks together after cloud service providers and hyperscalers objected to its design and operating burden.\\n    Quote: A backup plan — bolting two of Nvidia's current-generation racks together for similar power — has also been scrapped after cloud customers rejected the design as awkward and costly to operate. \\\"It has since been cancelled due to heavy pushback from CSPs [cloud service providers] and hyperscalers over its odd design and heavy operational burden,\\\" SemiAnalysis said.\",\n   \"- e55 [third_party_view; SemiAnalysis, as quoted by CNBC; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis said Nvidia has no proven solution to expand Rubin Ultra’s scale-up system size, potentially giving AMD and Google a technical opening in the high-end market.\\n    Quote: That leaves Nvidia with \\\"no proven solution to expand the scale-up world size for Rubin Ultra,\\\" SemiAnalysis said, predicting that could give rivals Advanced Micro Devices and Google , whose in-house chips are already winning business from top AI labs, a rare technical opening at the high end of the market.\",\n   \"- e56 [party_statement; Nvidia, as quoted by CNBC; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] Nvidia said its product roadmap remains intact, rejecting SemiAnalysis’s report of a Kyber delay.\\n    Quote: Nvidia rejected the SemiAnalysis report and said, \\\"Our roadmap is intact.\\\"\",\n   \"- e52 [rumour; SemiAnalysis, as quoted by CNBC; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis said Nvidia’s Kyber NVL144 rack architecture is delayed to 2028 because of midplane manufacturability challenges.\\n    Quote: Kyber NVL144 rack architecture has been delayed to 2028 as the PCB midplane remains challenging from a manufacturability standpoint,\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e143; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e54 [rumour; SemiAnalysis, as quoted by CNBC; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis said Nvidia scrapped a backup plan to bolt two current-generation racks together after cloud service providers and hyperscalers objected to its design and operating burden.\\n    Quote: A backup plan — bolting two of Nvidia's current-generation racks together for similar power — has also been scrapped after cloud customers rejected the design as awkward and costly to operate. \\\"It has since been cancelled due to heavy pushback from CSPs [cloud service providers] and hyperscalers over its odd design and heavy operational burden,\\\" SemiAnalysis said.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e65; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e56 [party_statement; Nvidia, as quoted by CNBC; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] Nvidia said its product roadmap remains intact, rejecting SemiAnalysis’s report of a Kyber delay.\\n    Quote: Nvidia rejected the SemiAnalysis report and said, \\\"Our roadmap is intact.\\\"\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e66; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e64 [rumour; finance.yahoo.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:68a3ed21f77b935d9fa7ec5e 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis claimed the Rubin Ultra high-density rack design was delayed by more than 12 months because of persistent manufacturing problems with its PCB midplane.\\n    Quote: SemiAnalysis claims the high-density rack design built for Rubin Ultra GPUs has slipped by more than 12 months. The firm blamed persistent manufacturing problems with the system's complex PCB midplane.\",\n   \"- e65 [rumour; finance.yahoo.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:68a3ed21f77b935d9fa7ec5e 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis claimed Nvidia scrapped its NVL72x2 back-to-back rack after hyperscaler customers pushed back.\\n    Quote: The firm also claimed Nvidia scrapped its NVL72x2 back-to-back rack after pushback from hyperscaler customers.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e54, e130, e145, e146; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e66 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:68a3ed21f77b935d9fa7ec5e 2026-07-06] Nvidia told media outlets that its roadmap remains intact, rejecting claims of delays to its next-generation AI rack systems.\\n    Quote: Nvidia rejected the claims, telling media outlets that its roadmap remains intact.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e56, e90, e134; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e68 [third_party_view; SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis 2026-07-06; from gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis forecasts annual AI capital spending will exceed $2 trillion in calendar 2028 and cumulative spending will reach about $11.1 trillion over 2024–2029, with credit markets the main funding source.\\n    Quote: Annual AI Capex – including GPUs, networking, storage and attached CPU compute as well as for the Datacenters to house AI compute – will be well north of $2T in 2028. Cumulative AI Capex from 2024 to 2029 will reach ~$11.1T, and credit markets will be the main funding source for this buildout.\",\n   \"- e69 [third_party_view; SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis 2026-07-06; from gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis says data-center supply improved by early 2026, chip production became the limiting constraint, and financing was a significant obstacle to expanding compute by mid-2026.\\n    Quote: In 2025, we wrote extensively about how datacenter capacity was the bottleneck for AI compute growth. By early 2026, the datacenter supply situation improved considerably, but it became clear that chip production was now the limiting constraint. Now – mid-way through the year – it is clear that financing will now be one of the most significant obstacles to ramping large scale compute broadly avail\",\n   \"- e92 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:71df54965281684cc500960f 2026-07-06] Wall Street analysts expect Nvidia revenue growth of 82% for the rest of 2026 and 41% in 2027.\\n    Quote: For the rest of this year, they expect 82% growth. For 2027, that figure rises to 41%.\",\n   \"- e97 [rumour; Danielle Liverance; original source Danielle Liverance 2026-07-06; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] The author reported that NVIDIA’s upcoming Vera Rubin server systems were reportedly delayed; no timing or scale was specified.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA shares are under pressure on reports of delays across their upcoming lineup of Vera Rubin server systems.\",\n   \"- e99 [third_party_view; Danielle Liverance; original source Danielle Liverance 2026-07-06; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] NVIDIA had roughly 81% of the AI chip market, according to the author.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA still owns roughly 81% of the AI chip market\",\n   \"- e100 [party_statement; Danielle Liverance; original source Broadcom ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] Broadcom guided to Q3 AI semiconductor revenue of $16.0 billion, more than 200% higher year over year.\\n    Quote: Broadcom guided Q3 AI semiconductor revenue to $16.0 billion, more than 200% year over year.\",\n   \"- e101 [third_party_view; Danielle Liverance; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] Bloomberg Intelligence forecast custom ASICs to grow at a 27% CAGR through 2033, compared with 16% for AI accelerators.\\n    Quote: Bloomberg Intelligence forecasting a 27% CAGR for custom ASICs through 2033 versus 16% for AI accelerators.\",\n   \"- e102 [party_statement; Danielle Liverance; original source Lisa Su ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] AMD CEO Lisa Su said leading-customer forecasts for MI450 exceeded AMD’s initial expectations.\\n    Quote: Lisa Su noted “leading customer forecasts exceeding our initial expectations” on MI450.\",\n   \"- e103 [fact; Danielle Liverance; original source Micron ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] Micron Q3 revenue was $41.46 billion, up 345.7% year over year.\\n    Quote: Q3 revenue exploded 345.7% year over year to $41.46 billion,\",\n   \"- e104 [party_statement; Danielle Liverance; original source Micron ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] Micron forecast an adjusted gross margin of 86% next quarter.\\n    Quote: Micron is now forecasting adjusted gross margins of 86% next quarter, above the peak gross margins NVIDIA ever achieved.\",\n   \"- e105 [third_party_view; Danielle Liverance; original source Danielle Liverance 2026-07-06; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] Some estimates put memory at half of total data-center spending in 2027.\\n    Quote: Some estimates put half of all data center spend going toward memory in 2027.\",\n   \"- e106 [third_party_view; Danielle Liverance; original source Danielle Liverance 2026-07-06; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] The author said NVIDIA had $119 billion in supply commitments, whose value depends on AI delivering measurable economic value beyond productivity tools.\\n    Quote: Nvidia's $119B in supply commitments hinge on AI delivering measurable economic value beyond productivity tools, which is a question the market appears to already be pricing in.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e121; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e107 [third_party_view; Danielle Liverance; original source Danielle Liverance 2026-07-06; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] The author calculated that NVIDIA traded at a forward price-to-earnings ratio below 20.\\n    Quote: trades at a forward P/E of less than 20 now, and\",\n   \"- e108 [third_party_view; Danielle Liverance; original source Danielle Liverance 2026-07-06; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] The author said NVIDIA traded at 12 times its forecast 2028 earnings.\\n    Quote: The ‘good’ news for NVIDIA investors is the company now trades for just 12X its forecasted 2028 earnings.\",\n   \"- e130 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia scrapped its planned NVL72x2 design, which would have placed two Oberon racks back to back, after cloud providers and large data center operators objected to its form factor and operational overhead.\\n    Quote: A planned alternative design called NVL72x2, which would have placed two Oberon racks back to back, has been scrapped entirely. Cloud providers and large data center operators pushed back against the unusual form factor and the high operational overhead.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e65; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e131 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia canceled the four-die Rubin Ultra version, leaving only the two-die version, which it said delivers roughly half the real-world compute performance.\\n    Quote: The more powerful version of the upcoming Rubin Ultra chip with four compute dies has also been canceled. Only the smaller two-die version remains, delivering roughly half the real-world compute performance.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e89, e135; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e132 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia’s CPO-NVSwitch interconnect technology will not arrive until the Feynman generation, two generations from the current one.\\n    Quote: A key interconnect technology called CPO-NVSwitch, which links many chips into a single large system, won't arrive until the generation after next, called Feynman.\",\n   \"- e133 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia plans to offset the product shortfall by selling more Oberon-Rubin racks in the existing form factor.\\n    Quote: Nvidia plans to make up for the shortfall by selling more Oberon-Rubin racks in the existing form factor.\",\n   \"- e135 [rumour; Investing.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:d5c48abb470f394f86549b6b 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis claimed that NVIDIA had scrapped a four-die configuration for the upcoming Rubin Ultra platform and would use a downsized version instead.\\n    Quote: Additionally, the report pointed to a downsized version of the upcoming Rubin Ultra platform, claiming a crucial four-die configuration had been scrapped.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e131; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e136 [third_party_view; Investing.com, citing analysts quoted by Bloomberg; original source Analysts cited by Bloomberg ; from gnews:d5c48abb470f394f86549b6b 2026-07-06] Analysts cited by Bloomberg said the rumored technical setbacks could severely limit the scale-up capacity of NVIDIA's future hardware.\\n    Quote: According to analysts cited by Bloomberg, these rumored technical setbacks could severely cap the scale-up capacity of Nvidia's future hardware.\",\n   \"- e137 [third_party_view; Investing.com, citing analysts quoted by Bloomberg; original source Analysts cited by Bloomberg ; from gnews:d5c48abb470f394f86549b6b 2026-07-06] Analysts cited by Bloomberg said perceived weaknesses in NVIDIA's future hardware could give AMD's MI500X and Broadcom-backed custom TPUs a wider competitive opportunity.\\n    Quote: This perceived vulnerability may create a wider competitive window for alternative AI platforms, specifically AMD's MI500X and Broadcom-backed custom TPUs.\",\n   \"- e138 [party_statement; Investing.com, reporting Mizuho analyst Jordan Klein's note; original source Hon Hai Precision Industry management 2026-07-03; from gnews:d5c48abb470f394f86549b6b 2026-07-06] Hon Hai management forecast continued acceleration in AI demand; Mizuho analyst Jordan Klein said this was a positive sign ahead of NVIDIA's Vera Rubin rack launch.\\n    Quote: Klein noted that Hon Hai management forecasted a continued acceleration in AI demand, which the analyst said was \\\"a very good sign into the NVDA launch of their new Vera Rubin rack.\\\"\",\n   \"- e143 [rumour; businesstimes.com.sg; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:c0432377817a1c00a1bbadf0 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia’s Kyber NVL144 faced printed-circuit-board construction setbacks, delaying the AI server rack system by more than a year.\\n    Quote: Research firm SemiAnalysis said in an X post that Nvidia’s Kyber NVL144 hit setbacks in the construction of printed circuit boards for the platform.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e52; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e100 [party_statement; Danielle Liverance; original source Broadcom ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] Broadcom guided to Q3 AI semiconductor revenue of $16.0 billion, more than 200% higher year over year.\\n    Quote: Broadcom guided Q3 AI semiconductor revenue to $16.0 billion, more than 200% year over year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e175; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e166 [party_statement; fool.com (Keithen Drury); original source Micron Technology ; from gnews:d0f3f83296df884fae64921e 2026-07-07] Micron said tight memory-market conditions could last until 2028.\\n    Quote: Micron recently announced another jaw-dropping quarter with huge growth and incredible expectations for the following quarter, dropping huge news that tight market conditions could last until 2028.\",\n   \"- e167 [third_party_view; fool.com (Keithen Drury); original source fool.com (Keithen Drury) 2026-07-07; from gnews:d0f3f83296df884fae64921e 2026-07-07] The author says new capacity across the memory-chip industry will not be online until 2027 or later, leaving inventory supply low for at least the next year and a half.\\n    Quote: As mentioned, new capacity for many in this industry won't be online until 2027 or later, creating a low supply of inventory for at least the next year and a half.\",\n   \"- e176 [party_statement; 24/7 Wall St.; original source Google ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] Google Cloud revenue rose 63%, its backlog nearly doubled to more than $460 billion, and Google guided 2026 capital expenditures to $190 billion.\\n    Quote: Google Cloud revenue rose 63% with backlog nearly doubling to over $460 billion, and 2026 capex is guided up tp $190 billion.\",\n   \"- e180 [rumour; mlq.ai, relaying Reuters; original source Three unnamed sources cited by Reuters 2026-07-06; from gnews:9f430c6ce2e8d551fe1f063a 2026-07-07] Reuters, citing three unnamed sources, reported that DeepSeek is developing a custom AI inference chip rather than a training chip.\\n    Quote: DeepSeek, the Hangzhou-based AI startup behind some of China's most advanced large language models, is developing its own custom AI chip, Reuters reported on Monday, citing three people with knowledge of the matter [1] . The chip is designed for inference — the phase where trained models generate responses to user queries — rather than for training new models.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e186; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e181 [rumour; mlq.ai, relaying Reuters; original source Three unnamed sources cited by Reuters 2026-07-06; from gnews:9f430c6ce2e8d551fe1f063a 2026-07-07] DeepSeek has reportedly been working on its inference-chip project for about a year, expanding its chip engineering team and discussing the project with chip design firms, foundries and memory suppliers.\\n    Quote: The project has been underway for roughly a year and remains in early stages, with DeepSeek quietly expanding its chip engineering team without public job postings [2] . The company is in discussions with chip design firms, semiconductor foundries, and memory suppliers, though no specific partners have been named.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e189; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e182 [fact; mlq.ai; original source DeepSeek ; from gnews:9f430c6ce2e8d551fe1f063a 2026-07-07] DeepSeek cut prices for its V4-Pro API by 75% in May 2026, intensifying price competition among Chinese AI providers.\\n    Quote: In May 2026, the company cut prices on its V4-Pro API by 75%, intensifying a price war among Chinese AI providers [5] .\",\n   \"- e183 [third_party_view; mlq.ai, quoting Richard Windey; original source Richard Windey ; from gnews:9f430c6ce2e8d551fe1f063a 2026-07-07] Analyst Richard Windey said U.S. export rules had effectively reduced Nvidia's China revenue to zero and also constrained DeepSeek's ability to manufacture or sell advanced chips outside China.\\n    Quote: Analyst Richard Windey highlighted the constraint: the same export rules that have effectively zeroed out Nvidia's China revenue also limit DeepSeek's ability to manufacture or sell advanced silicon outside China [3] .\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e187; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e184 [third_party_view; mlq.ai; original source Industry surveys ; from gnews:9f430c6ce2e8d551fe1f063a 2026-07-07] Industry surveys indicate Chinese firms plan to allocate 46% of their AI-accelerator budgets to domestic suppliers within 12 months, up from about 30% currently.\\n    Quote: Industry surveys indicate Chinese firms plan to shift 46% of their AI-accelerator budgets to domestic suppliers within 12 months, up from roughly 30% today [5] .\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e150; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e185 [fact; mlq.ai; original source The United States government ; from gnews:9f430c6ce2e8d551fe1f063a 2026-07-07] U.S. export controls bar Chinese chip designers from accessing the most advanced overseas foundries and high-bandwidth memory, constraining their ability to manufacture advanced chips.\\n    Quote: U.S. export controls bar Chinese designers from accessing the most advanced overseas foundries and high-bandwidth memory, posing a major manufacturing hurdle\",\n   \"- e186 [rumour; idnfinancials.com; original source Three unnamed sources cited by Reuters ; from gnews:2957e5c79a365952140c8cce 2026-07-07] Three unnamed sources told Reuters that DeepSeek is designing inference chips, a project that could reduce demand for Nvidia chips.\\n    Quote: According to Reuters , citing three sources familiar with the plans, DeepSeek's chips are being designed specifically for inference, the stage where trained AI models generate responses for users.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e180; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e187 [third_party_view; idnfinancials.com, quoting Richard Windsor; original source Richard Windsor, Radio Free Mobile ; from gnews:2957e5c79a365952140c8cce 2026-07-07] Richard Windsor of Radio Free Mobile said Nvidia's position in China is effectively zero and will remain so, and that DeepSeek is unlikely to sell chips outside China without access to advanced manufacturing technology.\\n    Quote: \\\"Nvidia's position in China is effectively at zero and will remain that way. DeepSeek has almost no chance of selling chips outside China unless it gains access to advanced manufacturing technology,\\\" said analyst Richard Windsor of Radio Free Mobile, adding that the development would not affect the chipmaker.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e183; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e188 [third_party_view; idnfinancials.com; original source idnfinancials.com 2026-07-07; from gnews:2957e5c79a365952140c8cce 2026-07-07] Huawei now controls around half of China's AI chip market, which is valued at approximately US$50 billion.\\n    Quote: Huawei has expanded its domestic market share and now controls around half of China's AI chip market, which is valued at approximately US$50 billion.\",\n   \"- e189 [rumour; idnfinancials.com; original source Unnamed sources cited by Reuters ; from gnews:2957e5c79a365952140c8cce 2026-07-07] Reuters sources said DeepSeek's chip project remains at an early stage and that the company has been communicating with chip-design firms, foundries and memory suppliers over the past year.\\n    Quote: According to Reuters sources, DeepSeek's chip development project remains at an early stage. Over the past year, the company has been communicating with chip design firms, foundries and memory suppliers to support the development of the semiconductors.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e181; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e190 [rumour; idnfinancials.com; original source idnfinancials.com ; from gnews:2957e5c79a365952140c8cce 2026-07-07] DeepSeek has increased recruitment of chip-design engineers in recent months to support its chip-development effort.\\n    Quote: DeepSeek has also increased recruitment of chip design engineers in recent months.\",\n   \"- e191 [fact; idnfinancials.com; original source OpenAI; and, for the reported consideration, unnamed sources cited by idnfinancials.com ; from gnews:2957e5c79a365952140c8cce 2026-07-07] OpenAI introduced its first inference chip, Jalapeno, in collaboration with Broadcom in June 2026; Anthropic is reportedly considering developing AI chips of its own.\\n    Quote: OpenAI introduced its first inference chip, called Jalapeno, last month in collaboration with Broadcom, while Anthropic is also reportedly considering developing its own AI chips.\",\n   \"- e192 [fact; idnfinancials.com; original source DeepSeek, for the V4 launch and optimization; Huawei, for its statement about V4-Flash training ; from gnews:2957e5c79a365952140c8cce 2026-07-07] DeepSeek launched its V4 model in April 2026, optimized for Huawei Ascend chips; Huawei also revealed that V4-Flash training used Ascend processors.\\n    Quote: In April, DeepSeek launched its V4 model, which had been optimised for Huawei Ascend chips, while Huawei revealed that training for the V4-Flash model also used Ascend processors.\",\n   \"- e193 [third_party_view; idnfinancials.com; original source idnfinancials.com 2026-07-07; from gnews:2957e5c79a365952140c8cce 2026-07-07] The DeepSeek V4 launch drove a surge in demand for Huawei Ascend 950 chips among Chinese technology companies.\\n    Quote: The launch also drove a surge in demand for Huawei's Ascend 950 chips among Chinese technology companies.\",\n   \"- e26 [third_party_view; fool.com (Justin Pope); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] Wall Street analysts estimate Nvidia revenue of $392 billion in FY2027.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts estimate that Nvidia's business could double over the next couple of years, from trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion to $392 billion this fiscal year, and $554 billion the following year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e204; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e47 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568 2026-07-04] Wall Street analysts project Nvidia revenue growth of 82% in FY2027 and 41% in FY2028.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts project 82% revenue growth for this year and 41% next year, so there's another external source that's projecting even more growth for Nvidia.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e216; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e217 [third_party_view; Bloomberg, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence’s survey; original source Bloomberg Intelligence 2026-07-07; from gnews:f3ba15f5e14b15ee61d7fddc 2026-07-08] Chinese executives surveyed by Bloomberg Intelligence said domestic products would receive 46% of their AI-accelerator budgets over the next 12 months, up from 30% currently.\\n    Quote: Executives in the country say they’ll allocate 46% of their budget for artificial intelligence accelerators to domestic products over the next 12 months, up from 30% today, according to a Bloomberg Intelligence survey released on Tuesday.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e150; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e219 [third_party_view; Bloomberg, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence’s survey; original source Bloomberg Intelligence 2026-07-07; from gnews:f3ba15f5e14b15ee61d7fddc 2026-07-08] Bloomberg Intelligence’s survey said Nvidia’s market share was expected to shrink as H20 chips became harder to find and local firms took over; it cited Beijing’s urging that Chinese technology firms not use H20 chips.\\n    Quote: While Nvidia’s products remain popular, the Santa Clara-based firm’s market share is expected to shrink as its H20 chips, which Beijing has urged its tech firms not to use, become harder to find and local firms take over, according to the survey.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e153; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e220 [third_party_view; Bloomberg; original source Bloomberg ; from gnews:f3ba15f5e14b15ee61d7fddc 2026-07-08] China is allocating roughly 2 trillion yuan ($294 billion) to build data centers over the next five years as part of a government-led AI expansion initiative.\\n    Quote: China is allocating roughly 2 trillion yuan ($294 billion) to build data centers across the country in the next five years, a government-led initiative to expand use of AI in sectors from healthcare to city management.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e154; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e221 [third_party_view; Bloomberg; original source Bloomberg News ; from gnews:f3ba15f5e14b15ee61d7fddc 2026-07-08] Bloomberg News reported that domestic companies will supply at least 80% of core technologies, including chips, for China’s data-center initiative.\\n    Quote: At least 80% of core technologies, such as chips, will be supplied by domestic companies, Bloomberg News reported.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e155; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e222 [third_party_view; Bloomberg, reporting the survey report; original source Bloomberg Intelligence 2026-07-07; from gnews:f3ba15f5e14b15ee61d7fddc 2026-07-08] The report said a global memory-chip shortage was likely to cap growth at Chinese AI firms such as SMIC, with ChangXin Memory Technologies poised to benefit, as bottlenecks shifted toward securing high-bandwidth memory supply.\\n    Quote: But a global memory chip shortage is likely to cap the growth of Chinese AI firms like Semiconductor Manufacturing International Corp. with ChangXin Memory Technologies Inc. poised to reap the benefits. The bottlenecks are shifting from sheer computing power to securing supply of high-bandwidth memory chips that support rapid data transfer, according to the report.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e156; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e223 [third_party_view; Investing.com, reporting Vivek Arya's note; original source Vivek Arya, Bank of America 2026-07-08; from gnews:266c882eea8c686ee7aafac7 2026-07-08] Bank of America analyst Vivek Arya estimated that HBM content per rack may increase by $0.2–0.3 million from Blackwell to Rubin, while rack pricing could increase by $2–3 million because of compute, networking, and software upgrades.\\n    Quote: While HBM content per rack may rise by approximately $0.2-0.3 million from Blackwell to Rubin, Arya noted that rack pricing could increase by $2-3 million, driven by upgrades across compute, networking and software.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e230; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e230 [third_party_view; moomoo.com; original source BofA ; from gnews:1b5a3359dd0644861c0fce42 2026-07-08] BofA estimated HBM content per rack could increase by $0.2 million to $0.3 million from Blackwell to Rubin, while total rack pricing could rise from about $3 million–$4 million to $6 million–$7 million.\\n    Quote: The report estimates HBM content per rack could rise by about $0.2 million to $0.3 million from Blackwell to Rubin, while total rack pricing could increase by $2 million to $3 million, from roughly $3 million to $4 million for Blackwell to $6 million to $7 million for Vera Rubin.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e223; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e231 [third_party_view; moomoo.com; original source BofA ; from gnews:1b5a3359dd0644861c0fce42 2026-07-08] BofA reported that Nvidia’s hyperscaler sales rose 115% year over year, nearly twice the growth in cloud capital expenditures.\\n    Quote: The report also says Nvidia’s hyperscaler sales rose 115% year over year, nearly twice cloud capex growth, suggesting wallet-share gains rather than share loss.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e225; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e232 [third_party_view; moomoo.com; original source BofA ; from gnews:1b5a3359dd0644861c0fce42 2026-07-08] BofA modeled Nvidia holding roughly 65% to 70% or more of AI capital expenditures over time, with the remainder going to ASICs, AMD and other merchant vendors.\\n    Quote: BofA still models Nvidia holding roughly 65% to 70% plus of AI capex over time, with the rest split across ASICs, AMD and other merchant vendors.\",\n   \"- e233 [third_party_view; moomoo.com; original source BofA ; from gnews:1b5a3359dd0644861c0fce42 2026-07-08] BofA said Nvidia GPU accelerator sales had grown about 700 times since 2015, despite the launches of Google TPU, Amazon Trainium and Meta MTIA.\\n    Quote: BofA’s counterpoint is historical: Google TPU launched in 2015, Amazon Trainium in 2020 and Meta MTIA in 2023, yet Nvidia GPU accelerator sales have grown about 700 times since 2015.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e224; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e234 [rumour; Notebookcheck; original source Notebookcheck ; from gnews:134fc6bce6a550f5376d6f27 2026-07-08] Nvidia is reportedly planning to release RTX 50 Super graphics cards in 2027.\\n    Quote: Rather than initiate a full-blown next-gen RTX 60 series launch, Nvidia is reportedly planning to release the RTX 50 Super series cards in 2027.\",\n   \"- e235 [rumour; Notebookcheck; original source Unnamed Nvidia source ; from gnews:134fc6bce6a550f5376d6f27 2026-07-08] An unnamed Nvidia source told leaker Moore’s Law Is Dead that RTX 60 GPUs would not launch in 2027, consistent with reports of a delay to 2028.\\n    Quote: One of Moore’s Law Is Dead’s Nvidia source told the leaker that they don’t think the RTX 60 series GPUs are coming out in 2027. This lines up with previous reports about Nvidia delaying the next-gen GeForce GPUs to 2028.\",\n   \"- e236 [third_party_view; Notebookcheck; original source Notebookcheck ; from gnews:134fc6bce6a550f5376d6f27 2026-07-08] AMD is expected to release RDNA 5 gaming GPUs in 2027.\\n    Quote: It is now clear that we approaching the end of the current-gen GPU lifecycle, as AMD is expected to release the RDNA 5 gaming GPUs in 2027.\",\n   \"- e25 [party_statement; fool.com (Justin Pope); original source Jensen Huang, Nvidia CEO ; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] The author reports that Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang expects $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\\n    Quote: CEO Jensen Huang has laid out expectations for $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e35, e253; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e66 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:68a3ed21f77b935d9fa7ec5e 2026-07-06] Nvidia told media outlets that its roadmap remains intact, rejecting claims of delays to its next-generation AI rack systems.\\n    Quote: Nvidia rejected the claims, telling media outlets that its roadmap remains intact.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e56, e90, e134, e270; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e253 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia management ; from gnews:931ee0196ca609e637235fad 2026-07-09] Nvidia management cited roughly $1 trillion in revenue visibility for Blackwell and Vera Rubin processors across 2026 and 2027, supported by multiyear commitments from hyperscalers and large enterprise customers.\\n    Quote: Management has also articulated roughly $1 trillion in revenue visibility for its Blackwell and Vera Rubin processors across 2026 and 2027, anchored by multiyear commitments from hyperscalers and large enterprise customers.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e25; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e270 [party_statement; moomoo.com, reporting NVIDIA’s statement to Bloomberg; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:7b39859113d4e2b8ebd8aa86 2026-07-09] NVIDIA told Bloomberg that it had no technical delay and that its product roadmap remained intact.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA recently issued a statement to Bloomberg denying claims of a technical delay, confirming that its product roadmap remains intact.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e66; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e274 [party_statement; au.finance.yahoo.com; original source Cerebras 2026-07-09; from gnews:66cb0387229ac4b1390615cb 2026-07-09] Cerebras plans a European network of AI data centres with combined power capacity of 200 MW by the end of 2027.\\n    Quote: The company plans to build a network of AI data centres across Europe by the end of 2027, with a combined power capacity of 200 MW.\",\n   \"- e275 [party_statement; au.finance.yahoo.com; original source Cerebras 2026-07-09; from gnews:66cb0387229ac4b1390615cb 2026-07-09] Cerebras said part of its planned European data centre capacity is expected to support OpenAI workloads; it did not specify the amount of capacity.\\n    Quote: Cerebras said that part of its planned data centre capacity is expected to support OpenAI workloads under the companies' existing partnership.\",\n   \"- e276 [party_statement; Andrew Feldman, quoted by au.finance.yahoo.com, attributing the statement to AFP; original source Andrew Feldman, Cerebras CEO ; from gnews:66cb0387229ac4b1390615cb 2026-07-09] Cerebras CEO Andrew Feldman said the planned expansions are worth several billion dollars; he did not specify a period or exact amount.\\n    Quote: \\\"These are massive expansions\\\" worth several billion dollars, chief executive Andrew Feldman told AFP on the sidelines of the RAISE Summit in Paris.\",\n   \"- e167 [third_party_view; fool.com (Keithen Drury); original source fool.com (Keithen Drury) 2026-07-07; from gnews:d0f3f83296df884fae64921e 2026-07-07] The author says new capacity across the memory-chip industry will not be online until 2027 or later, leaving inventory supply low for at least the next year and a half.\\n    Quote: As mentioned, new capacity for many in this industry won't be online until 2027 or later, creating a low supply of inventory for at least the next year and a half.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e300; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e234 [rumour; Notebookcheck; original source Notebookcheck ; from gnews:134fc6bce6a550f5376d6f27 2026-07-08] Nvidia is reportedly planning to release RTX 50 Super graphics cards in 2027.\\n    Quote: Rather than initiate a full-blown next-gen RTX 60 series launch, Nvidia is reportedly planning to release the RTX 50 Super series cards in 2027.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e297; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e282 [third_party_view; Trefis; original source Trefis, reporting Wall Street consensus ; from gnews:6abaf2856736877236d30f6a 2026-07-10] Trefis reports Wall Street consensus expects NVIDIA revenue to grow about 32% annually over the next few years.\\n    Quote: Wall Street consensus sees NVIDIA’s revenue growing about 32% a year for the next few years.\",\n   \"- e297 [rumour; Engadget; original source Unnamed reports, as retold by Engadget ; from gnews:1e2532e32b5227ae9622524b 2026-07-10] Unnamed reports say NVIDIA is not expected to launch its next set of consumer-facing gaming GPUs until 2027.\\n    Quote: According to reports , NVIDIA isn't expected to launch its next set of consumer-facing GPUs for gamers until 2027.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e234; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e298 [fact; theverge.com; original source Counterpoint ; from gnews:3839887e5ca53a0cb0e7c91e 2026-07-10] Counterpoint data cited in the article put SK Hynix’s global DRAM market share at 29% as of June 2026, versus Samsung at 38% and Micron at 22%.\\n    Quote: As of June 2026, SK Hynix makes up 29 percent of the global DRAM market, with Samsung at 38 percent and Micron at 22 percent, according to data from Counterpoint.\",\n   \"- e299 [party_statement; theverge.com; original source SK Group chairman Chey Tae-won ; from gnews:3839887e5ca53a0cb0e7c91e 2026-07-10] SK Group chairman Chey Tae-won said in June that SK Hynix plans to ramp up memory-chip capacity over the next five years to address a shortage that could last until 2030.\\n    Quote: SK Group chairman Chey Tae-won said in June that the company plans to ramp up its memory chip capacity over the next five years to address a shortage that could last until 2030, Bloomberg reports .\",\n   \"- e300 [third_party_view; Thomas Richmond, recounting Kristina Partsinevelos’s July 10 CNBC segment; original source Kristina Partsinevelos 2026-07-10; from gnews:9ae96ca750b8e3962c47795f 2026-07-10] CNBC’s Kristina Partsinevelos forecast that new memory supply would not arrive before late 2027, extending the shortage and keeping prices at record highs in the near term.\\n    Quote: “None of that supply, though, arrives before late 2027, which keeps the memory shortage going and record-high prices intact for now,” Partsinevelos said.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e167; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e309 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:07cf5835d106467db5448c13 2026-07-12] Nvidia expects AI hyperaccelerator spending to exceed $1 trillion next year.\\n    Quote: However, Nvidia told investors last quarter that it expects AI hyperaccelerator spending to rise to over $1 trillion next year.\",\n   \"- e310 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-07-12; from gnews:07cf5835d106467db5448c13 2026-07-12] The author believes Nvidia likely already has orders on the books for next year, giving it visibility into demand.\\n    Quote: I'm more inclined to believe Nvidia over the market's skepticism, as it likely has orders on the books for next year, so it can easily see the demand already.\",\n   \"- e311 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Broadcom ; from gnews:f8f440b5020fec9773812b6e 2026-07-12] The author says Broadcom plans to ramp production of custom AI chips for Meta, Anthropic, and OpenAI in late 2026 and into 2027, a competitive development for Nvidia.\\n    Quote: Broadcom is also making custom AI chips for Meta Platforms , Anthropic, and OpenAI, and production for those chips is scheduled to ramp up late this year and into next.\",\n   \"- e312 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source the market ; from gnews:f8f440b5020fec9773812b6e 2026-07-12] The author reports that the market expects Nvidia to retain its growth lead for the full fiscal year, while Broadcom is closing the gap.\\n    Quote: Looking ahead, the market still expects Nvidia to maintain its lead for the full fiscal year, though Broadcom is starting to close the gap.\",\n   \"- e313 [third_party_view; Keithen Drury; original source Keithen Drury 2026-07-12; from gnews:f8f440b5020fec9773812b6e 2026-07-12] The author expects Nvidia to remain the fastest-growing of AMD, Nvidia, and Broadcom for some time.\\n    Quote: AMD is still well behind Nvidia, and while I think Broadcom is still a strong pick, Nvidia will likely retain its rapid-growth title for some time.\",\n   \"- e314 [rumour; tech-insider.org; original source The Information ; from gnews:8faf69f198e10f14aae67621 2026-07-12] The Information reported that Nvidia shelved the RTX 50 Super refresh in December 2025, including a completed-design 24GB RTX 5080 Super, and that the RTX 60-series is pushed back to 2028.\\n    Quote: According to The Information, Nvidia quietly shelved its planned RTX 50 “Super” refresh back in December 2025 — including a 24GB RTX 5080 Super that had reportedly reached completed-design stage — and reporting corroborated through September 2026 confirms the company’s next-generation RTX 60-series remains pushed back to 2028.\",\n   \"- e315 [rumour; tech-insider.org; original source CNBC ; from gnews:8faf69f198e10f14aae67621 2026-07-12] CNBC reported in January 2026 that Samsung, SK Hynix, and Micron had sold out their entire 2026 HBM output under long-term contracts to customers including hyperscalers.\\n    Quote: The root cause sits one layer below Nvidia entirely. Hyperscalers including Microsoft, Google, Meta, and Amazon are buying up high-bandwidth memory as fast as Samsung, SK Hynix, and Micron can produce it, and all three manufacturers have reportedly sold out their entire 2026 HBM output under long-term contracts, according to CNBC’s reporting from January 2026.\",\n   \"- e322 [party_statement; I/O Fund / io-fund.com; original source Marvell ; from gnews:2dcfaef1a91c2976a4e347da 2026-07-12] Marvell said its CXL business is expected to exceed $1 billion in calendar 2028.\\n    Quote: Marvell says consumes CXL business to exceed $1 billion by calendar 2028\",\n   \"- e323 [third_party_view; I/O Fund / io-fund.com; original source UBS ; from gnews:2dcfaef1a91c2976a4e347da 2026-07-12] UBS estimated Marvell CXL revenue at $1 billion in calendar 2027 and $2 billion in calendar 2028.\\n    Quote: UBS seeing Marvell’s CXL revenue hitting $1 billion in calendar 2027 and doubling to $2 billion in calendar 2028.\",\n   \"- e328 [third_party_view; barchart.com (author); original source Wedbush Securities ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Wedbush Securities said Nvidia’s Vera CPU platform could expand its addressable market beyond graphics processors and create billions of dollars in additional revenue; no period was specified.\\n    Quote: Wedbush Securities recently argued that Nvidia's new Vera CPU platform could expand the company's total addressable market (TAM) well beyond graphics processors, opening the door to billions of dollars in additional revenue.\",\n   \"- e329 [rumour; barchart.com (author); original source Unnamed reports ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Reports suggest Nvidia has begun offering Vera processors to cloud customers, including some in China where regulations allow; no date or amount was specified.\\n    Quote: Reports also suggest Nvidia has begun offering the new processors to cloud customers, including some in China where regulations allow.\",\n   \"- e353 [fact; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] Nvidia recently launched its Vera Rubin AI platform.\\n    Quote: Nvidia recently launched its Vera Rubin AI platform, released the AI PC platform RTX Spark, expanded partnerships with companies such as Alphabet (GOOGL) and Marvell (MRVL), and further invested in networking, CPUs, and AI infrastructure.\",\n   \"- e66 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:68a3ed21f77b935d9fa7ec5e 2026-07-06] Nvidia told media outlets that its roadmap remains intact, rejecting claims of delays to its next-generation AI rack systems.\\n    Quote: Nvidia rejected the claims, telling media outlets that its roadmap remains intact.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e56, e90, e134, e270, e364; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e355 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu, quoted by The Verge; original source Xinzhou Wu, Nvidia head of automotive ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Nvidia automotive head Xinzhou Wu said the company has limited internal GPU compute and reviews its allocation across teams almost weekly, sometimes with CEO Jensen Huang’s help.\\n    Quote: Even Nvidia has a limited supply of GPU for compute. We have an internal priority, and I’m working with my colleagues basically almost on a weekly basis to decide how to set aside the different compute, sometimes for training, sometimes for testing, or resources for a different thread of work in the company. And sometimes we need Jensen [Huang, Nvidia CEO] to help, but yeah.\",\n   \"- e356 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu, quoted by The Verge; original source Xinzhou Wu, Nvidia head of automotive ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said Nvidia’s Hyperion 10 platform offers a base L2++ configuration with 10 cameras, three radars and no lidar, and a high-end configuration with 14 cameras, three lidars and seven radars for L4.\\n    Quote: We are looking at what we call the sufficient necessary sensor set to achieve a high level of autonomy.\",\n   \"- e357 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu, quoted by The Verge; original source Xinzhou Wu, Nvidia head of automotive ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu estimated that compute requirements for autonomous driving are growing roughly tenfold every two years.\\n    Quote: As you know, the computer’s growing at such a rapid pace. We talked about Moore’s Law in the semiconductor industry some time ago, but in the autonomous driving segment, the computer need has been growing at a really astonishing pace. Roughly we are talking about 10 times every two years. It’s insane. And right now, with the success of AI and obviously Nvidia, we will be able to provide this kind \",\n   \"- e358 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu, quoted by The Verge; original source Xinzhou Wu, Nvidia head of automotive ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said chip prices would most likely need to rise because demand is intense for available chips.\\n    Quote: Actually, most likely even the chip price will need to go up, because of this intense demand for every chip everybody can grab onto.\",\n   \"- e359 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu, quoted by The Verge; original source Xinzhou Wu, Nvidia head of automotive ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said Nvidia continues investing in autonomous-vehicle technology by allocating internal compute and is looking into allocating fabrication capacity for the business.\\n    Quote: We keep investing in this technology and in this future, not only by allocating internal compute, but with fab capacity as well. That’s definitely one of the things we are looking into.\",\n   \"- e360 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu, quoted by The Verge; original source Xinzhou Wu, Nvidia head of automotive ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu predicted that Level 4 autonomy will become a mainstream experience in cars in less than five years.\\n    Quote: That’s exactly my mission, trying to help the industry to get there. I would say if I need to give a time, I wouldn’t say five years, but less than five years.\",\n   \"- e361 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu, quoted by The Verge; original source Xinzhou Wu, Nvidia head of automotive ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said Nvidia plans to roll out its ADAS technology in all Mercedes vehicles and with some other partners across the United States by the end of 2026, then try to expand it to the rest of the world in the following years.\\n    Quote: First of all, by the end of this year, we are rolling out our technology on the ADAS side in all Mercedes vehicles and some other partners as well, all over the United States. Starting in the next few years, we’ll try to roll out this technology to the rest of the world.\",\n   \"- e362 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu, quoted by The Verge; original source Xinzhou Wu, Nvidia head of automotive ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said Nvidia is working with Uber and is trying to roll out an L4 service in the next few years.\\n    Quote: Meanwhile, we are also working closely with our partners, for example, Uber. We announced that at GTC, we are trying to roll out our L4 service in the next few years.\",\n   \"- e363 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu, quoted by The Verge; original source Xinzhou Wu, Nvidia head of automotive ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said 80% of mass-production automakers are currently in Nvidia’s Hyperion ecosystem for L4.\\n    Quote: Right now, I would say 80% of the mass-production OEMs are in Nvidia’s Hyperion ecosystem for L4.\",\n   \"- e366 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Sean Williams 2026-07-13; from gnews:e7e8cbf33738ceb5865837f0 2026-07-13] The author argues that customer-developed chips could occupy data-center capacity and erode Nvidia’s pricing-power and gross-margin tailwind from GPU supply shortages.\\n    Quote: For starters, some of Nvidia's pricing power and otherworldly gross margin originates from persistent GPU supply shortages. If the company's top customers are developing chips that take up valuable data center real estate, Nvidia can quickly lose its biggest tailwind .\",\n   \"- e367 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Sean Williams 2026-07-13; from gnews:e7e8cbf33738ceb5865837f0 2026-07-13] The author identifies competition from customers’ internally developed chips as the greatest threat to Nvidia’s ongoing success.\\n    Quote: There's no question that internal competition is the greatest threat to Nvidia's ongoing success .\",\n   \"- e368 [rumour; GuruFocus; original source The Information ; from gnews:1c47fd978ef50b1d7f48cbd8 2026-07-13] Google reportedly approached neocloud companies about using its TPUs, with no amount or timeline specified.\\n    Quote: Google has approached so-called neocloud companies about using its tensor processing units, or TPUs, according to a report from The Information.\",\n   \"- e369 [rumour; GuruFocus; original source Nscale ; from gnews:1c47fd978ef50b1d7f48cbd8 2026-07-13] Nscale reportedly told Google that its active projects remain centered on GPU capacity; no amount or timeline was specified.\\n    Quote: One provider, Nscale, reportedly told Google that its active projects remain centered on GPU capacity.\",\n   \"- e370 [fact; GuruFocus; original source Google and Blackstone ; from gnews:1c47fd978ef50b1d7f48cbd8 2026-07-13] Google and Blackstone are working on a cloud venture that plans to rent TPU capacity to AI labs and financial firms in 2027; no capacity amount was given.\\n    Quote: Google is also working with Blackstone on a new cloud venture that plans to rent TPU capacity to AI labs and financial firms next year.\",\n   \"- e26 [third_party_view; fool.com (Justin Pope); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] Wall Street analysts estimate Nvidia revenue of $392 billion in FY2027.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts estimate that Nvidia's business could double over the next couple of years, from trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion to $392 billion this fiscal year, and $554 billion the following year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e204, e406; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e253 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia management ; from gnews:931ee0196ca609e637235fad 2026-07-09] Nvidia management cited roughly $1 trillion in revenue visibility for Blackwell and Vera Rubin processors across 2026 and 2027, supported by multiyear commitments from hyperscalers and large enterprise customers.\\n    Quote: Management has also articulated roughly $1 trillion in revenue visibility for its Blackwell and Vera Rubin processors across 2026 and 2027, anchored by multiyear commitments from hyperscalers and large enterprise customers.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e25, e405; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e405 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:84e90d3da2d3779da0e7bdb0 2026-07-14] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang sees at least $1 trillion in revenue from the Blackwell and Rubin platforms through the end of 2027.\\n    Quote: CEO Jensen Huang has said that he sees at least $1 trillion in revenue from Nvidia's Blackwell and Rubin platforms through the end of 2027.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e253; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e406 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:84e90d3da2d3779da0e7bdb0 2026-07-14] Wall Street analysts estimate NVIDIA will generate approximately $555 billion in total revenue in FY2028, ending January 2028.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts estimate that Nvidia will generate approximately $555 billion in revenue for the company's next fiscal year, ending January 2028.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e26; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e415 [party_statement; sg.finance.yahoo.com; original source Nokia 2026-07-15; from gnews:e153ff10e5adda87a52745a4 2026-07-14] Nokia said it developed a commercial AI-driven radio access network platform with Nvidia; the platform is intended to increase data transmission over existing infrastructure.\\n    Quote: Nokia Oyj says it developed the first commercial artificial intelligence-driven radio access network platform together with Nvidia Corp to radically increase the amount of data operators can transmit using existing infrastructure.\",\n   \"- e416 [party_statement; sg.finance.yahoo.com; original source Jensen Huang, Nvidia CEO 2026-07-15; from gnews:e153ff10e5adda87a52745a4 2026-07-14] Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang said Nvidia CUDA and AI are being brought into Nokia’s radio-access-network baseband, describing the collaboration as a foundation for AI services and 6G.\\n    Quote: “Together with Nokia, we are bringing Nvidia Cuda and AI into the baseband, transforming RAN into a planet-scale AI computer. This is a generational shift for operators - unlocking more capacity and efficiency from today's spectrum while creating the foundation for new AI services and the 6G era,” Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang said in the statement.\",\n   \"- e417 [party_statement; sg.finance.yahoo.com; original source Nokia 2026-07-15; from gnews:e153ff10e5adda87a52745a4 2026-07-14] Nokia said its new network hardware is expected to become available to operators in 2027, with spectrum-efficiency gains expected to reach 50%, compared with 20% currently achieved.\\n    Quote: Next year, when the hardware will become available to operators, spectrum efficiency gains are expected to reach 50%, while currently 20% have been achieved.\",\n   \"- e429 [party_statement; Jensen Huang, quoted by 247wallst.com; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:ac8a489e54fbb1b85a1c7a2c 2026-07-14] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said the AI-factory buildout was accelerating at extraordinary speed.\\n    Quote: The buildout of AI factories, the largest infrastructure expansion in human history, is accelerating at extraordinary speed.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e389; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e447 [fact; Rest of World; original source Humain 2026-06-01; from gnews:01a49ffd41f6abe24538da65 2026-07-14] Humain agreed on June 1 for Saudi Arabia to use Nvidia technology in self-driving taxis.\\n    Quote: Saudi Arabia agreed on June 1 to use self-driving taxis that run on Nvidia technology — from the computer inside each car to the software that steers it. The deal with the U.S. chipmaker was struck by Humain, the venture set up by Saudi Arabia’s Public Investment Fund last year to make the kingdom a global AI power.\",\n   \"- e448 [fact; Rest of World; original source Humain ; from gnews:01a49ffd41f6abe24538da65 2026-07-14] Humain is building data centers in Riyadh and Dammam that are planned to use several hundred thousand Nvidia chips.\\n    Quote: Humain is also building data centers in Riyadh and Dammam, powered by several hundred thousand Nvidia chips.\",\n   \"- e449 [fact; Rest of World; original source G42 ; from gnews:01a49ffd41f6abe24538da65 2026-07-14] G42’s first stage of its Abu Dhabi Stargate data center is planned to run on 400,000 Nvidia chips.\\n    Quote: Its first stage will run on 400,000 Nvidia chips .\",\n   \"- e450 [third_party_view; Rest of World, quoting Kamil Dimmich; original source Kamil Dimmich ; from gnews:01a49ffd41f6abe24538da65 2026-07-14] Humain’s first order from Nvidia was 18,000 Blackwell chips, according to Kamil Dimmich.\\n    Quote: Humain's first order from Nvidia was 18,000 of its newest Blackwell chips — the hardware that does that heavy lifting, which no rival can yet match, he said.\",\n   \"- e456 [third_party_view; ebc.com; original source ebc.com 2026-07-14; from gnews:f83ae0a4f01c18d48f20a629 2026-07-14] Nvidia’s Vera Rubin architecture remains on track for shipment in late 2026, according to the article.\\n    Quote: the Vera Rubin architecture remains officially on track for late 2026\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e24; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\"\n  ],\n  \"points_to_rule\": [\n   \"item i256\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"control\": 18,\n  \"ruler_question\": {\n   \"question\": \"How much will the largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?\",\n   \"unit\": \"USD\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2028-12-31\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Below $700 billion\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is less than $700 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": 700000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"$700 billion to below $800 billion\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $700 billion and less than $800 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 700000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 800000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"$800 billion to below $900 billion\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $800 billion and less than $900 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 800000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 900000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"$900 billion to below $1000 billion\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $900 billion and less than $1000 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 900000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 1000000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"$1000 billion or more\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $1000 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 1000000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": null\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"judged_question\": {\n   \"view_id\": \"v7\",\n   \"question\": \"How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?\",\n   \"looks_at\": \"Combined data center capital expenditures by the four largest AI hyperscalers\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2028-02-28\",\n   \"year\": \"2027\",\n   \"kind\": \"theme\"\n  },\n  \"judged_rungs\": [\n   {\n    \"position\": 1,\n    \"label\": \"Below $800 billion\",\n    \"condition\": \"Combined spending is less than $800 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": null,\n    \"hi\": 800000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 2,\n    \"label\": \"$800 billion to below $900 billion\",\n    \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $800 billion and less than $900 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": 800000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 900000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 3,\n    \"label\": \"$900 billion to below $1.1 trillion\",\n    \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $900 billion and less than $1.1 trillion.\",\n    \"lo\": 900000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 1100000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 4,\n    \"label\": \"$1.1 trillion to below $1.2 trillion\",\n    \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $1.1 trillion and less than $1.2 trillion.\",\n    \"lo\": 1100000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 1200000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 5,\n    \"label\": \"$1.2 trillion or more\",\n    \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $1.2 trillion.\",\n    \"lo\": 1200000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": null\n   }\n  ],\n  \"reader_b_decisive_items\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i256\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-07\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Stock Is Down 17% From Its High. Is the Artificial Intelligence (AI) Leader Finally Cheap?\",\n    \"passage\": \"This year, the big four AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures . Next year, Nvidia claims this group will spend more than $1 trillion.\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"big four AI hyperscalers' own plans (2026); NVIDIA's claim (2027)\",\n     \"what\": \"data-center capital expenditure of the big four\",\n     \"how_much\": \"around $650bn (2026); more than $1 trillion (2027)\",\n     \"period\": \"calendar 2026; calendar 2027\",\n     \"status\": \"plan (2026); forecast by NVIDIA (2027)\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i090\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-04\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Stock Is Nearly Flat for 2026. Time to Cash Out, or Load Up on Shares?\",\n    \"passage\": \"Wall Street analysts project 82% revenue growth for this year and 41% next year\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"Wall Street analysts\",\n     \"what\": \"NVIDIA revenue growth forecast\",\n     \"how_much\": \"82% this year; 41% next year\",\n     \"period\": \"this year and next year (fiscal or calendar both accepted, D233)\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i143\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"How Nvidia Became The Black Sheep Of The Chip Stock Rally\",\n    \"passage\": \"Some estimates put half of all data center spend going toward memory in 2027.\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"unnamed estimates\",\n     \"what\": \"memory's share of data center spend\",\n     \"how_much\": \"about half\",\n     \"period\": \"2027\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i161\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"CAPITAL IDEAS: The lag 7 — Is Micron the new Nvidia?\",\n    \"passage\": \"Goldman Sachs estimates annual AI infrastructure capital expenditures could reach $765 billion in 2026 and grow to $1.6 trillion by 2031\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"Goldman Sachs estimate\",\n     \"what\": \"annual AI infrastructure capex (chips, data centers, power, cooling, networking)\",\n     \"how_much\": \"$765B (2026); $1.6T (2031); ~$7.6T cumulative 2026-2031\",\n     \"period\": \"2026; 2031; 2026-2031\",\n     \"condition\": \"could reach\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   }\n  ],\n  \"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\": [\n   \"- e46 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568 2026-07-04] Nvidia projects that the four largest AI hyperscalers’ combined data center capital expenditures could reach $1 trillion in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: Next year, Nvidia projects that this figure could reach $1 trillion.\",\n   \"- e46 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568 2026-07-04] Nvidia projects that the four largest AI hyperscalers’ combined data center capital expenditures could reach $1 trillion in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: Next year, Nvidia projects that this figure could reach $1 trillion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e91; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e91 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia management ; from gnews:71df54965281684cc500960f 2026-07-06] Nvidia management forecast hyperscaler spending of $650 billion in calendar 2026 and more than $1 trillion in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: During its last quarterly conference call, management forecast that it expects hyperscaler spending to top $1 trillion in 2027 after reaching a projected $650 billion in 2026 .\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e46; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e91 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia management ; from gnews:71df54965281684cc500960f 2026-07-06] Nvidia management forecast hyperscaler spending of $650 billion in calendar 2026 and more than $1 trillion in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: During its last quarterly conference call, management forecast that it expects hyperscaler spending to top $1 trillion in 2027 after reaching a projected $650 billion in 2026 .\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e46, e163, e168; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e163 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:f8191f5bb960d79e47c73d6c 2026-07-07] The author reports that Nvidia claims the four largest AI hyperscalers will spend more than $1 trillion on data center capital expenditures in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: Next year, Nvidia claims this group will spend more than $1 trillion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e91; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e168 [third_party_view; fool.com (Keithen Drury); original source fool.com (Keithen Drury) 2026-07-07; from gnews:d0f3f83296df884fae64921e 2026-07-07] The author estimates AI hyperscalers plan $650 billion of data-center capex in calendar 2026 and could spend more than $1 trillion in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: While the AI hyperscalers plan to spend $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year, next year that figure could be over $1 trillion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e91; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e389 [party_statement; 247wallst.com, quoting Jensen Huang; original source Jensen Huang, NVIDIA CEO ; from gnews:b68c019528300c6a1fcd3515 2026-07-13] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said the buildout of AI factories was accelerating at extraordinary speed.\\n    Quote: Jensen Huang put it plainly: “The buildout of AI factories, the largest infrastructure expansion in human history, is accelerating at extraordinary speed.”\",\n   \"- e389 [party_statement; 247wallst.com, quoting Jensen Huang; original source Jensen Huang, NVIDIA CEO ; from gnews:b68c019528300c6a1fcd3515 2026-07-13] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said the buildout of AI factories was accelerating at extraordinary speed.\\n    Quote: Jensen Huang put it plainly: “The buildout of AI factories, the largest infrastructure expansion in human history, is accelerating at extraordinary speed.”\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e429; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e429 [party_statement; Jensen Huang, quoted by 247wallst.com; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:ac8a489e54fbb1b85a1c7a2c 2026-07-14] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said the AI-factory buildout was accelerating at extraordinary speed.\\n    Quote: The buildout of AI factories, the largest infrastructure expansion in human history, is accelerating at extraordinary speed.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e389; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e457 [fact; ebc.com; original source Amazon ; from gnews:f83ae0a4f01c18d48f20a629 2026-07-14] Amazon recently borrowed another $25 billion, which the article says caused a minor selloff in AI-related debt.\\n    Quote: Amazon recently made headlines by borrowing another $25 billion, causing a minor selloff in AI-related debt .\"\n  ],\n  \"points_to_rule\": [\n   \"same_question\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"control\": 19,\n  \"ruler_question\": {\n   \"question\": \"What Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\",\n   \"unit\": \"USD\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 Data Center revenue is at least $440 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 440000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": null\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"at least $360 billion and below $440 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 360000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 440000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n     \"condition\": \"at least $310 billion and below $360 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 310000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 360000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"at least $260 billion and below $310 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 260000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 310000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"below $260 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": 260000000000.0\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"judged_question\": {\n   \"view_id\": \"v12\",\n   \"question\": \"How much revenue will Nvidia's data center segment generate in FY2027?\",\n   \"looks_at\": \"Nvidia FY2027 data center segment revenue\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\",\n   \"year\": \"FY2027\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\"\n  },\n  \"judged_rungs\": [\n   {\n    \"position\": 1,\n    \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n    \"condition\": \"FY2027 data center segment revenue is at least $340 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": 340000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": null\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 2,\n    \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n    \"condition\": \"FY2027 data center segment revenue is at least $310 billion and less than $340 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": 310000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 340000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 3,\n    \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n    \"condition\": \"FY2027 data center segment revenue is at least $280 billion and less than $310 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": 280000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 310000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 4,\n    \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n    \"condition\": \"FY2027 data center segment revenue is at least $250 billion and less than $280 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": 250000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 280000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 5,\n    \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n    \"condition\": \"FY2027 data center segment revenue is less than $250 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": null,\n    \"hi\": 250000000000.0\n   }\n  ],\n  \"reader_b_decisive_items\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i129\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"NVIDIA Falls 7% in a Month: Should You Still Hold NVDA Stock or Exit?\",\n    \"passage\": \"During the first quarter of fiscal 2027, the Data Center segment generated $75.25 billion in revenues, accounting for 92% of total sales.\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"NVIDIA reported\",\n     \"what\": \"Q1 FY2027 revenue, data center revenue, non-GAAP EPS\",\n     \"how_much\": \"revenue $81.62B (+85% y/y); data center $75.25B (+92% y/y, +21% q/q, 92% of sales); EPS $1.87\",\n     \"period\": \"Q1 FY2027\",\n     \"status\": \"happened\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i281\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-09\",\n    \"title\": \"DeepSeek Just Dealt Nvidia Stock a Potentially Major Blow\",\n    \"passage\": \"forecasting revenue of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%, and a non-GAAP gross margin of about 75%\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"NVIDIA\",\n     \"what\": \"Q2 FY2027 revenue and gross-margin guidance\",\n     \"how_much\": \"$91 billion ±2%; non-GAAP gross margin about 75%\",\n     \"period\": \"Q2 FY2027\",\n     \"condition\": \"assumes no China Data Center compute revenue\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i106\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-05\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia's next-gen AI rack system delayed to 2028 on manufacturing snags, SemiAnalysis says\",\n    \"passage\": \"SemiAnalysis also projects Nvidia's data-center compute revenue will run 20% above Wall Street consensus in the second half of fiscal 2027\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"SemiAnalysis\",\n     \"what\": \"NVIDIA data-center compute revenue versus Wall Street consensus\",\n     \"how_much\": \"20% above consensus\",\n     \"period\": \"second half of fiscal 2027\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i208\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Delays Next-Generation Kyber Server Architecture as Manufacturing Hurdles Give Rivals a Rare Opening\",\n    \"passage\": \"SemiAnalysis actually expects Nvidia’s data-center compute revenue in the second half of fiscal 2027 to come in 20% above Wall Street’s current expectations.\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"SemiAnalysis estimate\",\n     \"what\": \"NVIDIA data-center compute revenue vs consensus\",\n     \"how_much\": \"20% above consensus\",\n     \"period\": \"second half of FY2027\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i295\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-10\",\n    \"title\": \"Here are Friday's biggest analyst calls: Nvidia, SpaceX, Toll, Shopify, Twilio, Seagate, Chipotle & more\",\n    \"passage\": \"the company describing \\\"accelerating growth rates\\\" even as revenues approach the $100 bn per quarter mark\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"NVIDIA management, relayed by Morgan Stanley\",\n     \"what\": \"revenue growth rates accelerating\",\n     \"how_much\": \"quarterly revenue approaching $100 bn\",\n     \"status\": \"claim\"\n    }\n   }\n  ],\n  \"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\": [\n   \"- e227 [fact; qz.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:ee0d6792b6bf98069cfe0cc6 2026-07-08] Nvidia's data center segment generated a record $75.2 billion in revenue in FY2027's first quarter.\\n    Quote: its data center segment set a record at $75.2 billion\",\n   \"- e227 [fact; qz.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:ee0d6792b6bf98069cfe0cc6 2026-07-08] Nvidia's data center segment generated a record $75.2 billion in revenue in FY2027's first quarter.\\n    Quote: its data center segment set a record at $75.2 billion\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e251; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e241 [third_party_view; TechCrunch, Russell Brandom; original source Russell Brandom 2026-07-09; from gnews:3ea4e94c707ece2db2d7caec 2026-07-09] TechCrunch reported that the GPU shortage had eased somewhat by July 2026.\\n    Quote: The GPU shortage that looked so alarming last year has eased off a bit.\",\n   \"- e242 [third_party_view; TechCrunch, Russell Brandom; original source Russell Brandom 2026-07-09; from gnews:3ea4e94c707ece2db2d7caec 2026-07-09] Russell Brandom said memory-chip makers had increased prices tenfold over the past year as demand outpaced supply growth.\\n    Quote: since demand is growing faster than anyone can scale up supply, they have been able to increase prices tenfold over the past year.\",\n   \"- e243 [third_party_view; TechCrunch, Russell Brandom; original source Russell Brandom 2026-07-09; from gnews:3ea4e94c707ece2db2d7caec 2026-07-09] Russell Brandom reported that the spot price for an hour of Nvidia H100 GPU time peaked at about $3.20 in May 2026 and then steadily declined.\\n    Quote: Just like Nvidia’s stock price, there’s a peak in May (around $3.20 an hour) and then a steady drop-off.\",\n   \"- e244 [third_party_view; TechCrunch, Russell Brandom; original source Russell Brandom 2026-07-09; from gnews:3ea4e94c707ece2db2d7caec 2026-07-09] Russell Brandom said Google, Amazon, Microsoft and OpenAI had launched custom processors to reduce reliance on Nvidia, and that these chips were good enough to drive down compute prices.\\n    Quote: Google , Amazon , Microsoft , and even OpenAI have launched their own custom processors to lessen their dependence on Nvidia; even if those chips aren’t as good as the latest model from Nvidia, they’re good enough to drive down the price of compute.\",\n   \"- e245 [third_party_view; Wayne Nelms, quoted by TechCrunch’s Russell Brandom; original source Wayne Nelms ; from gnews:3ea4e94c707ece2db2d7caec 2026-07-09] Ornn co-founder and CTO Wayne Nelms said more GPU and accelerator competitors were entering the market, while he expected current market conditions to persist absent a major HBM breakthrough, a supply-demand shift, or a new memory entrant.\\n    Quote: “More GPU and accelerator players are entering the market. Everyone wants to make their own silicon, but no one is making their own DRAM,” Nelms told me. “Until there’s a major technological breakthrough on HBM [high-bandwidth memory], a shift in supply and demand, or someone new [enters the market in memory], I think things will more or less persist as we see today.”\",\n   \"- e246 [third_party_view; Citi analyst Atif Malik; original source Citi analyst Atif Malik ; from gnews:86c243945145ed901feb26cf 2026-07-09] Citi analyst Atif Malik said Nvidia had strong access to DRAM memory amid constrained industry supply.\\n    Quote: We maintain Nvidia as our top buy-rated mega-cap data center semis pick on strong access to DRAM memory amidst constrained industry supply,\",\n   \"- e247 [third_party_view; Bank of America analyst Vivek Arya, in a note this week; original source Bank of America analyst Vivek Arya ; from gnews:86c243945145ed901feb26cf 2026-07-09] Bank of America analyst Vivek Arya said Nvidia faced gross-margin pressure from higher memory costs, custom-ASIC competition, crowded investor ownership, and unproductive use of cash in vendor financing.\\n    Quote: Several concerns are fueling the sell-off, Bank of America analyst Vivek Arya wrote in a note this week. They include gross margin pressure from higher memory costs, competition from custom ASIC chips, crowded investor ownership, and unproductive use of cash in vendor financing rather than stronger buybacks/dividends.\",\n   \"- e248 [rumour; barchart.com; original source Unnamed sources cited in reports about DeepSeek ; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] DeepSeek is reportedly developing an inference-focused chip and engaging chip-design, foundry, and memory partners while expanding its chip engineering team, potentially reducing reliance on Nvidia GPUs.\\n    Quote: Reports that DeepSeek is developing its own inference-focused AI chip could reduce its reliance on Nvidia's GPUs, highlighting a broader industry trend in which leading AI developers are increasingly designing custom silicon to lower costs, improve efficiency, and gain greater control over their AI infrastructure. The project is still in its early stages, with the company engaging chip design, fou\",\n   \"- e249 [third_party_view; barchart.com; original source barchart.com 2026-07-09; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] The article says experts see DeepSeek's chip effort as unlikely to materially affect Nvidia's near-term revenue, given China's shrinking contribution to sales, but says custom silicon could gradually weaken Nvidia's pricing power and margins.\\n    Quote: Although experts note that DeepSeek's move is unlikely to materially impact Nvidia's near-term revenue, particularly given China's shrinking contribution to Nvidia's sales, it reinforces concerns that custom silicon could gradually erode the company's pricing power and margins.\",\n   \"- e251 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:931ee0196ca609e637235fad 2026-07-09] Nvidia's data center segment revenue set a record in the first quarter; the item gives no amount.\\n    Quote: Revenues from Nvidia's data center segment -- the primary engine of the business -- set a record in the first quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e227; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e252 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia management ; from gnews:931ee0196ca609e637235fad 2026-07-09] Nvidia management guided to accelerating data center segment revenue growth in the second quarter.\\n    Quote: management guided for further revenue growth acceleration for the second quarter.\",\n   \"- e262 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Bloomberg Intelligence projects Nvidia will hold 70% to 75% of the AI chip market through 2030.\\n    Quote: Bloomberg Intelligence projects the company will hold 70% to 75% of the AI chip market through 2030.\",\n   \"- e263 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source qz.com 2026-07-09; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] QZ says Amazon's Trainium4 chip could arrive later in 2026.\\n    Quote: Amazon 's next chip, Trainium4, which packs three times the performance of its predecessor, could arrive later this year.\",\n   \"- e264 [party_statement; qz.com; original source Meta ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Meta plans three more MTIA generations for generative AI over two years; MTIA 450 is due in early 2027 and MTIA 500 is expected later in 2027.\\n    Quote: Meta is set to build three more generations over the next two years with the purpose of running generative AI models. The next one, MTIA 450, arrives in early 2027, doubling how fast the chip moves data in and out of memory. Its eventual successor, MTIA 500, is expected to come later next year, and pushes memory speed another 50% higher.\",\n   \"- e265 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source Reuters ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Tesla completed the AI5 inference chip design in April 2026 and plans production at TSMC's Arizona plant and Samsung's Texas plant.\\n    Quote: Tesla finished the design of its AI5 inference chip in April 2026, according to Reuters . Production is planned at both TSMC 's plant in Arizona and Samsung's plant in Texas.\",\n   \"- e266 [party_statement; qz.com; original source Tesla ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Tesla is targeting mid-2027 to begin mass production of its AI5 inference chip.\\n    Quote: Tesla is targeting mid-2027 for mass production.\",\n   \"- e267 [rumour; moomoo.com, citing Reuters and Meta’s internal memo; original source Meta ; from gnews:7b39859113d4e2b8ebd8aa86 2026-07-09] Meta reportedly plans to start manufacturing its AI chip in September, potentially adding competition in AI chips; the year was not specified.\\n    Quote: Meta Platforms (META.US)$ is reportedly planning to start manufacturing its AI chip in September, Reuters reported Thursday, citing the company’s internal memo.\",\n   \"- e268 [fact; moomoo.com, citing data compiled by Bloomberg; original source Quanta ; from gnews:7b39859113d4e2b8ebd8aa86 2026-07-09] Quanta’s June sales more than doubled year over year to NT$385.19 billion; the company supplies AI servers powered by Nvidia GPUs.\\n    Quote: Quanta, which supplies AI servers powered by Nvidia’s GPUs, saw its monthly sales more than double to 385.19 billion New Taiwanese dollars in June from a year earlier, according to data compiled by Bloomberg.\",\n   \"- e269 [fact; moomoo.com, citing Bloomberg; original source Hon Hai Precision Industry ; from gnews:7b39859113d4e2b8ebd8aa86 2026-07-09] Nvidia server-assembly partner Hon Hai reported June sales up 52% year over year to NT$821.8 billion and quarterly sales up 40%, according to Bloomberg.\\n    Quote: $HON HAI PRECISION INDUSTRY SPON GDS EACH REP 2 SHS TWD10 REG'S' (HNHPF.US)$ , Nvidia’s server assembly partner, saw a 52% surge in monthly sales in June to NT$ 821.8 billion, allowing the Taiwanese company to post a bigger-than-expected 40% surge in quarterly sales, according to Bloomberg.\",\n   \"- e227 [fact; qz.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:ee0d6792b6bf98069cfe0cc6 2026-07-08] Nvidia's data center segment generated a record $75.2 billion in revenue in FY2027's first quarter.\\n    Quote: its data center segment set a record at $75.2 billion\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e251, e287; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e267 [rumour; moomoo.com, citing Reuters and Meta’s internal memo; original source Meta ; from gnews:7b39859113d4e2b8ebd8aa86 2026-07-09] Meta reportedly plans to start manufacturing its AI chip in September, potentially adding competition in AI chips; the year was not specified.\\n    Quote: Meta Platforms (META.US)$ is reportedly planning to start manufacturing its AI chip in September, Reuters reported Thursday, citing the company’s internal memo.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e286; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e279 [third_party_view; Jeran Wittenstein, citing Bloomberg Intelligence; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:49f225cd79fb22132f3b9ee4 2026-07-10] Bloomberg Intelligence data showed Nvidia held 97% of the server GPU market at the end of 2025, up from 95% at the end of 2024.\\n    Quote: the company’s market share has hardly been dented as demand for equipment going into new data centers remains strong. Nvidia had 97% of the server GPU market at the end of 2025, up from 95% at the end of 2024, according to data compiled by Bloomberg Intelligence.\",\n   \"- e286 [fact; Gurufocus, retelling Reuters; original source Meta Platforms ; from gnews:09b9d76297a57f198651c5e7 2026-07-10] Meta plans to begin manufacturing its Iris custom AI processor in September, after initial testing; the chip is designed with Broadcom and made by TSMC, and is intended to complement rather than replace Meta's GPU purchases from Nvidia and AMD.\\n    Quote: Reuters said Meta plans to begin manufacturing its custom AI processor, code-named Iris, in September after completing initial testing. The chip is being designed with Broadcom (AVGO) and manufactured by Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing (TSM). The report said the processor is intended to support Meta's AI infrastructure while complementing, rather than replacing, the large number of graphics pro\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e267; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e287 [fact; 247wallst.com, citing NVIDIA’s Q1 FY2027 results; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Data Center revenue of $75.246 billion, up 92% year over year, and networking revenue growth of 199% year over year in Q1 FY2027.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue hit $75.246 billion, up 92% year over year, and networking alone grew 199%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e227, e294, e303; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e292 [rumour; gurufocus.com; original source gurufocus.com ; from gnews:4c201dc59ba0c7579bfef4db 2026-07-10] Unnamed reports say major NVIDIA clients, including Meta, are shifting toward developing their own AI chips, raising a potential competitive risk to NVIDIA's Data Center revenue.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA's stock surge comes amidst growing concerns that major clients, such as Meta, are shifting towards developing their own AI chips.\",\n   \"- e293 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially, and Data Center revenue of $75.2 billion.\\n    Quote: The company reported record revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially, with Data Center revenue reaching $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e226; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e294 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 Data Center Networking revenue of $14.8 billion, up 199% year over year.\\n    Quote: Within that segment, Data Center Networking alone hit $14.8 billion, up 199% from a year earlier, reflecting surging demand for the Spectrum-X Ethernet and NVLink interconnect systems that travel with every rack-scale Blackwell deployment.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e287; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e296 [rumour; quantumzeitgeist.com; original source Perplexity 2026-07-07; from gnews:b666d35e5247a8ddcc2d7c72 2026-07-10] Perplexity plans to integrate NVIDIA Vera CPUs into its upcoming production systems; no timing or quantity was stated.\\n    Quote: Perplexity is now planning to integrate Vera into its upcoming production systems\",\n   \"- e301 [fact; Thomas Richmond, citing NVIDIA’s report; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:9ae96ca750b8e3962c47795f 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.62 billion, up 85.2% year over year.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.62 billion, up 85.2% year over year, with Data Center revenue of $75.25 billion and total supply-related commitments of $119.0 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e226; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e303 [fact; TIKR; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] Nvidia reported $75 billion in Data Center revenue in its recent quarter, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data center revenue alone hit $75 billion, up 92% year over year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e287; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e304 [third_party_view; es.tradingview.com; original source Morgan Stanley ; from gnews:1bfc0e875ab1f26dcf48fb06 2026-07-11] Morgan Stanley said AI laboratories account for roughly 20% of Nvidia’s demand, indicating demand beyond hyperscale cloud providers.\\n    Quote: The bank noted that AI laboratories now account for roughly 20% of Nvidia’s demand, highlighting how enterprise AI adoption is expanding beyond hyperscale cloud providers.\",\n   \"- e279 [third_party_view; Jeran Wittenstein, citing Bloomberg Intelligence; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:49f225cd79fb22132f3b9ee4 2026-07-10] Bloomberg Intelligence data showed Nvidia held 97% of the server GPU market at the end of 2025, up from 95% at the end of 2024.\\n    Quote: the company’s market share has hardly been dented as demand for equipment going into new data centers remains strong. Nvidia had 97% of the server GPU market at the end of 2025, up from 95% at the end of 2024, according to data compiled by Bloomberg Intelligence.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e326; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e293 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially, and Data Center revenue of $75.2 billion.\\n    Quote: The company reported record revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially, with Data Center revenue reaching $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e226, e340; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e303 [fact; TIKR; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] Nvidia reported $75 billion in Data Center revenue in its recent quarter, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data center revenue alone hit $75 billion, up 92% year over year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e287, e331; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e326 [third_party_view; jpost.com; original source jpost.com ; from gnews:c14249088492921c802c839a 2026-07-12] Nvidia's server GPU market share was about 97% at the end of 2025, up from 95% at the end of 2024.\\n    Quote: Nvidia's firm grip on the server GPU market showed no signs of weakening, with its market share climbing to about 97% at the end of 2025, compared to 95% the previous year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e279; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e331 [fact; barchart.com (author); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Nvidia reported Q1 FY2027 Data Center revenue of $75.2 billion, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue climbed 92% YOY to $75.2 billion, highlighting that AI infrastructure remains the company's primary growth engine.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e303, e341; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e333 [party_statement; barchart.com (author); original source Nvidia management ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Nvidia guided to approximately $91 billion in Q2 FY2027 revenue, assuming no China data-center sales because of export restrictions.\\n    Quote: Management also issued strong guidance, forecasting approximately $91 billion in Q2 revenue despite assuming no China data-center sales because of export restrictions.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e291; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e341 [fact; fool.com (Daniel Sp