e market.\",\n   \"- e301 [rumour; barchart.com; original source  ; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Reports (unnamed sources) suggested that NVIDIA's next-generation Kyber rack-scale AI infrastructure, designed for the Rubin Ultra platform, could be delayed until 2028.\\n    Quote: Recently, Nvidia faced reports that suggested its next-generation Kyber rack-scale AI infrastructure could be delayed until 2028.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e91; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e302 [party_statement; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] NVIDIA denied reports that Kyber could be delayed, maintaining that its roadmap remains on track. It said Kyber, designed for the Rubin Ultra platform, is expected to launch in 2027 as an integrated AI infrastructure system and a key part of its long-term AI infrastructure strategy.\\n    Quote: However, the company denied the speculation, maintaining that its roadmap remains on track. Designed for the Rubin Ultra platform, Kyber is expected to launch in 2027 as an integrated AI infrastructure system and a key component of Nvidia's long-term AI infrastructure strategy.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e92; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e256 (); both are in force: Research firm SemiAnalysis stated in an X post that NVIDIA's Kyber NVL144 rack system has hit manufacturing setbacks; the item says this could push NVIDIA to lean further on its new credit and revenue-sharing model to sustain demand.\",\n   \"- e316 [party_statement; IEEE Spectrum; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:a4eb2bdfabca94f5887881c6 2026-07-09] NVIDIA is planning to add more processors to its single interconnected systems, scaling from 72 GPUs today to as many as 576 GPUs by 2027, according to IEEE Spectrum.\\n    Quote: At the same time, Nvidia is planning to add even more processors to single interconnected systems, going from 72 GPUs today to as many as 576 by 2027.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e257; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e334 [party_statement; moomoo; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:7b39859113d4e2b8ebd8aa86 2026-07-09] NVIDIA issued a statement to Bloomberg denying claims of a technical delay and confirming that its product roadmap remains intact.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA recently issued a statement to Bloomberg denying claims of a technical delay, confirming that its product roadmap remains intact. This clarification serves as a counterweight to concerns that infrastructure bottlenecks could disrupt the company’s competitive lead in the artificial intelligence sector.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e92; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e92 [party_statement; CNBC; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] NVIDIA rejected SemiAnalysis's report that its next-generation Kyber rack system is delayed, stating that 'Our roadmap is intact.'\\n    Quote: Nvidia rejected the SemiAnalysis report and said, \\\"Our roadmap is intact.\\\"\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e109, e129, e173, e189, e204, e220, e302, e334, e385; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e256 [third_party_view; futuriom.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:cb05b9f49943ef0ba412cf36 2026-07-08] Research firm SemiAnalysis stated in an X post that NVIDIA's Kyber NVL144 rack system has hit manufacturing setbacks; the item says this could push NVIDIA to lean further on its new credit and revenue-sharing model to sustain demand.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA’s stock also suffered this week because research firm SemiAnalysis stated in an X post that NVIDIA’s Kyber NVL144 rack system has hit manufacturing setbacks—a situation that could be further impetus for NVIDIA to deploy its new credit and revenue-sharing model, creating a continuing flow of demand for its products.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e384; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e384 [rumour; Jim Cramer (via finance.yahoo.com); original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:1c3c0c58ed5ec3da43292f9b 2026-07-11] Reports circulated that NVIDIA's next-generation AI chips face delays; per Jim Cramer, SemiAnalysis reported that \\\"everything could be late for NVIDIA because one particular part of their business is late,\\\" in the context of what the article calls the Kyber delay. The reports are contested (see NVIDIA's denial in a separate item).\\n    Quote: AI giant NVIDIA Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA) is currently in the news these days due to reports of a delay to its next generation AI chips. … You know Semi Analysis does pretty good work, saying that everything could be late for NVIDIA because one particular part of their business is late.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e256; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e385 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com; original source NVIDIA Corp. ; from gnews:1c3c0c58ed5ec3da43292f9b 2026-07-11] NVIDIA Corp. denied reports that its Kyber platform is being delayed, asserting that its product plan/schedule stands.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA) has denied reports that the Kyber platform is being delayed.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e92; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e91 [third_party_view; CNBC; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] Research firm SemiAnalysis reported in a post published Monday that NVIDIA's Kyber NVL144 rack-scale architecture, which is designed to house its 2027 Rubin Ultra chips, has been delayed by more than 12 months to 2028 because the specialized multi-layer PCB midplane remains difficult to manufacture; the larger NVL576 system linking eight racks via optical connections is also likely delayed or limited to small volumes.\\n    Quote: Nvidia 's next marquee product — the Kyber rack-scale architecture designed to house its 2027 Rubin Ultra chips — has been delayed by more than 12 months to 2028, according to research firm SemiAnalysis, the latest in a string of reported setbacks raising questions about the AI giant's product roadmap. … The setback stems from difficulties manufacturing a key circuit board at the heart of the syst\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e107, e125, e126, e167, e172, e176, e182, e184, e203, e219, e301, e419; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e92 [party_statement; CNBC; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] NVIDIA rejected SemiAnalysis's report that its next-generation Kyber rack system is delayed, stating that 'Our roadmap is intact.'\\n    Quote: Nvidia rejected the SemiAnalysis report and said, \\\"Our roadmap is intact.\\\"\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e109, e129, e173, e189, e204, e220, e302, e334, e385, e420; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e419 [third_party_view; Geoffrey Seiler (fool.com); original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:3cd991655d4cdeaa4a578b84 2026-07-12] Technology research outfit SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA's Kyber NVL144 next-generation AI rack system could be delayed until 2028 because of difficulties in manufacturing a crucial circuit board, as recounted by fool.com's Geoffrey Seiler, who notes NVIDIA's rack-scale strategy is central to CEO Jensen Huang's plan.\\n    Quote: This has been a key part of CEO Jensen Huang's strategy; however, it could have hit a snag when technology research outfit SemiAnalysis reported that its Kyber NVL144 next-gen AI rack system could be delayed until 2028 due to troubles with manufacturing a crucial circuit board.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e91; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e420 [party_statement; Geoffrey Seiler (fool.com); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3cd991655d4cdeaa4a578b84 2026-07-12] NVIDIA responded to SemiAnalysis's report that its Kyber NVL144 rack could slip to 2028 by saying its roadmap remains intact, though the article says questions linger; no schedule or shipment date was given.\\n    Quote: Nvidia has come out and said its roadmap remains intact, although questions linger.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e92; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e430 [party_statement; gurufocus.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:dedacecd6d2ed5192c307199 2026-07-13] NVIDIA said, in investor-relations discussions reported by gurufocus.com on 2026-07-13, that development of its next-generation Rubin Ultra platform remains on schedule and confirmed there have been no changes to its NVLink architecture.\\n    Quote: The company said development of its next-generation Rubin Ultra platform remains on schedule and confirmed there have been no changes to its NVLink architecture.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e128 (); both are in force: A week before the Kyber report, SemiAnalysis separately reported that Nvidia had canceled the four-die Rubin Ultra design in favor of a two-chiplet design, also due to 'manufacturing execution concerns.' The two-die offering will deliver around half the performance of the four-die Rubin Ultra.\",\n   \"- e91 [third_party_view; CNBC; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] Research firm SemiAnalysis reported in a post published Monday that NVIDIA's Kyber NVL144 rack-scale architecture, which is designed to house its 2027 Rubin Ultra chips, has been delayed by more than 12 months to 2028 because the specialized multi-layer PCB midplane remains difficult to manufacture; the larger NVL576 system linking eight racks via optical connections is also likely delayed or limited to small volumes.\\n    Quote: Nvidia 's next marquee product — the Kyber rack-scale architecture designed to house its 2027 Rubin Ultra chips — has been delayed by more than 12 months to 2028, according to research firm SemiAnalysis, the latest in a string of reported setbacks raising questions about the AI giant's product roadmap. … The setback stems from difficulties manufacturing a key circuit board at the heart of the syst\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e107, e125, e126, e167, e172, e176, e182, e184, e203, e219, e301, e419, e540; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e92 [party_statement; CNBC; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] NVIDIA rejected SemiAnalysis's report that its next-generation Kyber rack system is delayed, stating that 'Our roadmap is intact.'\\n    Quote: Nvidia rejected the SemiAnalysis report and said, \\\"Our roadmap is intact.\\\"\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e109, e129, e173, e189, e204, e220, e302, e334, e385, e420, e541; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e540 [third_party_view; EBC (ebc.com); original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:f83ae0a4f01c18d48f20a629 2026-07-14] Industry research firm SemiAnalysis reported over the weekend that Nvidia's upcoming Kyber NVL144 rack architecture could face delays extending into 2028, according to reports the article describes as unverified rumors.\\n    Quote: Over the weekend, reports circulated from industry research firm SemiAnalysis suggesting that Nvidia’s upcoming Kyber NVL144 architecture could face delays extending into 2028.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e91; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e541 [party_statement; Nvidia spokesperson, reported by EBC (ebc.com); original source NVIDIA Corp. ; from gnews:f83ae0a4f01c18d48f20a629 2026-07-14] An Nvidia spokesperson countered the SemiAnalysis delay report, telling reporters that the company's \\\"roadmap is intact\\\".\\n    Quote: Although an Nvidia spokesperson quickly countered the reports, telling that the company's \\\"roadmap is intact,\\\" the seeds of doubt were already sown.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e92; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e393 (); both are in force: Multiple reports, led by The Information and corroborated through September 2026, say NVIDIA has shipped no new gaming GPU architecture in calendar 2026 — the first blank year since the GeForce 256 debut in October 1999. NVIDIA reportedly shelved its entire planned RTX 50 'Super' refresh in December 2025, including a 24GB RTX 5080 Super that had reached completed-design stage, and its next-generation RTX 60-series (Rubin-based) has slipped from a rumored late-2027 launch to 2028. NVIDIA has not confirmed the skip on the record, only acknowledging memory supply constraints in a statement to Tom's Hardware.\"\n  ],\n  \"points_to_rule\": [\n   \"same_question\"\n  ]\n }\n]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; p=json.load(open(\\\"/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/full-eligibility/third-reader-packet.json\\\"));\nfor x in p:\n print(json.dumps({k:x[k] for k in (\\\"control\\\",\\\"points_to_rule\\\",\\\"ruler_question\\\",\\\"judged_question\\\",\\\"judged_rungs\\\")},ensure_ascii=False));\n for pt in x[\\\"points_to_rule\\\"]:\n  if pt.startswith(\\\"item \\\"):\n   print(\\\"ITEM\\\",json.dumps([i for i in x[\\\"reader_b_decisive_items\\\"] if i[\\\"id\\\"]==pt[5:]],ensure_ascii=False)); print(\\\"EVIDENCE\\\",json.dumps(x[\\\"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\\\"],ensure_ascii=False))'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; p=json.load(open(\\\"/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/full-eligibility/third-reader-packet.json\\\"));\nfor x in p:\n print(json.dumps({k:x[k] for k in (\\\"control\\\",\\\"points_to_rule\\\",\\\"ruler_question\\\",\\\"judged_question\\\",\\\"judged_rungs\\\")},ensure_ascii=False));\n for pt in x[\\\"points_to_rule\\\"]:\n  if pt.startswith(\\\"item \\\"):\n   print(\\\"ITEM\\\",json.dumps([i for i in x[\\\"reader_b_decisive_items\\\"] if i[\\\"id\\\"]==pt[5:]],ensure_ascii=False)); print(\\\"EVIDENCE\\\",json.dumps(x[\\\"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\\\"],ensure_ascii=False))'\"","aggregated_output":"{\"control\": 1, \"points_to_rule\": [\"same_question\"], \"ruler_question\": {\"question\": \"Will Nvidia begin shipping its Rubin generation by December 31, 2026?\", \"unit\": \"yes/no\", \"due_day\": \"2026-12-31\", \"rungs\": [{\"label\": \"Yes\", \"condition\": \"Nvidia has begun shipping Rubin by December 31, 2026.\", \"lo\": null, \"hi\": null}, {\"label\": \"No\", \"condition\": \"Nvidia has not begun shipping Rubin by December 31, 2026.\", \"lo\": null, \"hi\": null}]}, \"judged_question\": {\"view_id\": \"v4\", \"question\": \"Will Nvidia make first customer shipments of its Vera Rubin platform by December 31, 2026, as confirmed in Nvidia's quarterly reports, filings, or management commentary?\", \"looks_at\": \"First customer shipments / initial revenue from Nvidia's Vera Rubin platform, confirmed by the company.\", \"due_day\": \"2026-12-31\", \"year\": \"2026\", \"kind\": \"asset\"}, \"judged_rungs\": [{\"position\": 1, \"label\": \"Yes\", \"condition\": \"Nvidia confirms that it made first customer shipments of its Vera Rubin platform by December 31, 2026.\", \"lo\": null, \"hi\": null}, {\"position\": 2, \"label\": \"Ruled out\", \"condition\": \"After July 2, 2026, Nvidia formally cancels or abandons the Vera Rubin platform before making any first customer shipments. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-02 and stands on 2026-12-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\", \"lo\": null, \"hi\": null}, {\"position\": 3, \"label\": \"Still open\", \"condition\": \"Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2026-12-31.\", \"lo\": null, \"hi\": null}]}\n{\"control\": 2, \"points_to_rule\": [\"same_question\"], \"ruler_question\": {\"question\": \"How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026?\", \"unit\": \"USD\", \"due_day\": \"2027-12-31\", \"rungs\": [{\"label\": \"Below $550 billion\", \"condition\": \"Combined spending is less than $550 billion.\", \"lo\": null, \"hi\": 550000000000.0}, {\"label\": \"$550 billion to below $600 billion\", \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $550 billion and less than $600 billion.\", \"lo\": 550000000000.0, \"hi\": 600000000000.0}, {\"label\": \"$600 billion to below $700 billion\", \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $600 billion and less than $700 billion.\", \"lo\": 600000000000.0, \"hi\": 700000000000.0}, {\"label\": \"$700 billion to below $800 billion\", \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $700 billion and less than $800 billion.\", \"lo\": 700000000000.0, \"hi\": 800000000000.0}, {\"label\": \"$800 billion or more\", \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $800 billion.\", \"lo\": 800000000000.0, \"hi\": null}]}, \"judged_question\": {\"view_id\": \"v5\", \"question\": \"What will the big four AI hyperscalers' combined data-center capital expenditure be for calendar 2026, as measured by summing the capex lines in their Q4 2026 earnings reports?\", \"looks_at\": \"The big four AI hyperscalers' aggregated calendar-2026 data center capital expenditure versus the ~$650 billion plan reported in the item, with Nvidia's own projection of ~$1 trillion for 2027 as the forward reference.\", \"due_day\": \"2027-03-31\", \"year\": \"2026\", \"kind\": \"theme\"}, \"judged_rungs\": [{\"position\": 1, \"label\": \"below 500,000,000,000 USD\", \"condition\": \"below 500,000,000,000 USD\", \"lo\": null, \"hi\": 500000000000.0}, {\"position\": 2, \"label\": \"from 500,000,000,000 USD to below 600,000,000,000 USD\", \"condition\": \"from 500,000,000,000 USD to below 600,000,000,000 USD\", \"lo\": 500000000000.0, \"hi\": 600000000000.0}, {\"position\": 3, \"label\": \"from 600,000,000,000 USD to below 700,000,000,000 USD\", \"condition\": \"from 600,000,000,000 USD to below 700,000,000,000 USD (the reference when the question opened: \\\"plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year\\\")\", \"lo\": 600000000000.0, \"hi\": 700000000000.0}, {\"position\": 4, \"label\": \"from 700,000,000,000 USD to below 800,000,000,000 USD\", \"condition\": \"from 700,000,000,000 USD to below 800,000,000,000 USD\", \"lo\": 700000000000.0, \"hi\": 800000000000.0}, {\"position\": 5, \"label\": \"800,000,000,000 USD or more\", \"condition\": \"800,000,000,000 USD or more\", \"lo\": 800000000000.0, \"hi\": null}]}\n{\"control\": 5, \"points_to_rule\": [\"item i256\"], \"ruler_question\": {\"question\": \"What will Nvidia's total revenue be in FY2028?\", \"unit\": \"USD\", \"due_day\": \"2028-02-28\", \"rungs\": [{\"label\": \"Strongly bullish\", \"condition\": \"FY2028 total revenue is at least $650 billion.\", \"lo\": 650000000000.0, \"hi\": null}, {\"label\": \"Bullish\", \"condition\": \"FY2028 total revenue is at least $550 billion and below $650 billion.\", \"lo\": 550000000000.0, \"hi\": 650000000000.0}, {\"label\": \"Neutral\", \"condition\": \"FY2028 total revenue is at least $480 billion and below $550 billion.\", \"lo\": 480000000000.0, \"hi\": 550000000000.0}, {\"label\": \"Bearish\", \"condition\": \"FY2028 total revenue is at least $420 billion and below $480 billion.\", \"lo\": 420000000000.0, \"hi\": 480000000000.0}, {\"label\": \"Strongly bearish\", \"condition\": \"FY2028 total revenue is below $420 billion.\", \"lo\": null, \"hi\": 420000000000.0}]}, \"judged_question\": {\"view_id\": \"v3\", \"question\": \"What will Nvidia's total revenue be in FY2028?\", \"looks_at\": \"Nvidia's total revenue in FY2028.\", \"due_day\": \"2028-02-24\", \"year\": \"FY2028\", \"kind\": \"asset\"}, \"judged_rungs\": [{\"position\": 1, \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\", \"condition\": \"FY2028 total revenue is at least $650 billion.\", \"lo\": 650000000000.0, \"hi\": null}, {\"position\": 2, \"label\": \"Bullish\", \"condition\": \"FY2028 total revenue is at least $600 billion and below $650 billion.\", \"lo\": 600000000000.0, \"hi\": 650000000000.0}, {\"position\": 3, \"label\": \"Neutral\", \"condition\": \"FY2028 total revenue is at least $500 billion and below $600 billion, bracketing the cited $554 billion analyst estimate.\", \"lo\": 500000000000.0, \"hi\": 600000000000.0}, {\"position\": 4, \"label\": \"Bearish\", \"condition\": \"FY2028 total revenue is at least $450 billion and below $500 billion.\", \"lo\": 450000000000.0, \"hi\": 500000000000.0}, {\"position\": 5, \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\", \"condition\": \"FY2028 total revenue is below $450 billion.\", \"lo\": null, \"hi\": 450000000000.0}]}\nITEM [{\"id\": \"i256\", \"day\": \"2026-07-07\", \"title\": \"Nvidia Stock Is Down 17% From Its High. Is the Artificial Intelligence (AI) Leader Finally Cheap?\", \"passage\": \"This year, the big four AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures . Next year, Nvidia claims this group will spend more than $1 trillion.\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"big four AI hyperscalers' own plans (2026); NVIDIA's claim (2027)\", \"what\": \"data-center capital expenditure of the big four\", \"how_much\": \"around $650bn (2026); more than $1 trillion (2027)\", \"period\": \"calendar 2026; calendar 2027\", \"status\": \"plan (2026); forecast by NVIDIA (2027)\"}}]\nEVIDENCE [\"- e27 [party_statement; fool.com analyst Justin Pope; original source Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang ; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang expects $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\\n    Quote: CEO Jensen Huang has laid out expectations for $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\", \"- e28 [third_party_view; fool.com analyst Justin Pope; original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] Wall Street analysts estimate Nvidia revenue of $392 billion in FY2027, compared with trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts estimate that Nvidia's business could double over the next couple of years, from trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion to $392 billion this fiscal year, and $554 billion the following year.\", \"- e32 [fact; storagereview.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:8c9d215416b714064de3b095 2026-07-03] NVIDIA removed the AI Enterprise subscription requirement for Omniverse production use and allowed Omniverse-based products to be redistributed for free; the change was effective as of May 2026.\\n    Quote: The new terms remove that requirement entirely; anything built with Omniverse can also be redistributed under the same free terms, which is a substantive impact for ISVs and integrators who embed Omniverse applications inside their own products.\", \"- e33 [fact; storagereview.com; original source Mercedes-Benz ; from gnews:8c9d215416b714064de3b095 2026-07-03] The Mercedes-Benz CLA, the first production deployment on NVIDIA's DRIVE platform, reached the US market in 2026.\\n    Quote: The first production deployment, the Mercedes-Benz CLA on the DRIVE platform, reached the US market this year.\", \"- e34 [fact; SDxCentral, reporting the companies’ plan; original source Microsoft and MediaTek ; from gnews:1740f3733eedc34d8bac9b65 2026-07-03] Microsoft and MediaTek plan to launch microLED-based data center networking interconnects for partners by late 2027.\\n    Quote: The pair plans to launch microLED-based data center networking interconnects for partners by late 2027 .\", \"- e35 [third_party_view; Jim Cramer, as quoted by finance.yahoo.com; original source Google and Amazon, as reported by Jim Cramer ; from gnews:a96a4cbf6aae35d01d0d285b 2026-07-03] Jim Cramer said Google and Amazon claim their chips are better than NVIDIA's, although they use NVIDIA's products.\\n    Quote: The first two claim that they have better chips than NVIDIA, even as they use NVIDIA.\", \"- e36 [third_party_view; Jim Cramer, as quoted by finance.yahoo.com; original source Hock Tan ; from gnews:a96a4cbf6aae35d01d0d285b 2026-07-03] Jim Cramer said Broadcom CEO Hock Tan says Broadcom can compete with NVIDIA and take share from it.\\n    Quote: Plus, there's Broadcom, vicious competitor, and CEO Hock Tan's out there saying it can compete; it can take share from NVIDIA.\", \"- e45 [party_statement; Valve engineer Pierre-Loup Griffais, as quoted by the outlet; original source Valve ; from gnews:c1658c3cc3b216fa2b0eaa54 2026-07-04] Valve engineer Pierre-Loup Griffais said Valve is working with Nvidia, AMD and Intel to expand SteamOS support across hardware.\\n    Quote: the company is working with AMD, Intel, and Nvidia to make the SteamOS experience better on a wider range of hardware.\", \"- e46 [third_party_view; xda-developers.com; original source Pierre-Loup Griffais ; from gnews:c1658c3cc3b216fa2b0eaa54 2026-07-04] The outlet reported that Griffais did not expect official SteamOS support for Nvidia GPUs before 2027.\\n    Quote: He doesn't expect anything before 2027, so Nvidia users have to wait, relying on Bazzite in the meantime.\", \"- e47 [party_statement; BGR.com, reporting a statement by Josh Parker in an NVIDIA blog post; original source Josh Parker, head of corporate sustainability at NVIDIA ; from gnews:a8fab49de53d125314a6688a 2026-07-04] NVIDIA head of corporate sustainability Josh Parker said AI compute demand driving data center construction was growing faster than almost any other infrastructure-investment category; no period was specified.\\n    Quote: AI workloads are not getting lighter. The compute demand driving data center construction is growing faster than almost any other category of infrastructure investment.\", \"- e50 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568 2026-07-04] Wall Street analysts project Nvidia revenue growth of 82% in 2026 and 41% in 2027.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts project 82% revenue growth for this year and 41% next year, so there's another external source that's projecting even more growth for Nvidia.\", \"- e51 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:068a24e2743bab750f43f048 2026-07-04] Nvidia's revenue increased 1,033% from Q1 2024 through Q1 FY2027, which ended April 26.\\n    Quote: Just in the last three years, from Q1 2024 to the first quarter of fiscal 2027 (ended April 26), Nvidia's revenue soared 1,033%.\", \"- e62 [fact; wccftech.com; original source US and European retailers ; from gnews:3faf8050f6d3b8ddee1d18c2 2026-07-05] US and European retailers are restocking NVIDIA’s GeForce RTX 3060 12 GB at prices starting at $329 and €333, respectively; the item gives no date for the retailers’ action.\\n    Quote: So as of right now, both US and European retailers are restocking the NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 12 GB with prices starting at $329 and €333, respectively.\", \"- e63 [third_party_view; wccftech.com; original source wccftech.com 2026-07-05; from gnews:3faf8050f6d3b8ddee1d18c2 2026-07-05] wccftech.com reported that graphics card prices were continuing to rise as the DRAM crisis intensified in 2026; no price amount or comparison was given.\\n    Quote: As the DRAM crisis intensifies in 2026, graphics card prices continue to go up.\", \"- e50 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568 2026-07-04] Wall Street analysts project Nvidia revenue growth of 82% in 2026 and 41% in 2027.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts project 82% revenue growth for this year and 41% next year, so there's another external source that's projecting even more growth for Nvidia.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e98, e99; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e71 [third_party_view; SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis 2026-07-06; from gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis says its supply-chain tracking indicates Nvidia’s second-half 2026 shipment-volume and revenue estimates are materially higher than the general market’s estimates.\\n    Quote: Nvidia revenue is skyrocketing, and even 3 years into the build out, the general market is still materially lower on shipment volumes and revenue estimates for Nvidia in the 2nd half of this year versus our through supply chain tracking in the Accelerator Model .\", \"- e72 [third_party_view; SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis 2026-07-06; from gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis forecasts AI debt financing will exceed $7 trillion outstanding by 2029, driven by AI IT and data-center capital needs.\\n    Quote: AI Debt Financing will become a multi-trillion-dollar credit market, with over $7T of debt outstanding by 2029 driven both by AI IT Capex and AI Datacenter Capex needs for Neoclouds, datacenter builders, and even hyperscalers.\", \"- e73 [third_party_view; SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis 2026-07-06; from gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis forecasts annual AI capital expenditure, including AI IT equipment and the data centers that house it, will exceed $2 trillion in calendar 2028.\\n    Quote: Annual AI Capex – including GPUs, networking, storage and attached CPU compute as well as for the Datacenters to house AI compute – will be well north of $2T in 2028.\", \"- e74 [third_party_view; SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis 2026-07-06; from gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis forecasts cumulative AI capital expenditure from 2024 through 2029 will reach about $11.1 trillion and says credit markets will be its main funding source.\\n    Quote: Cumulative AI Capex from 2024 to 2029 will reach ~$11.1T, and credit markets will be the main funding source for this buildout.\", \"- e88 [fact; fool.com author; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:4a892d75e355bee00aa3c572 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reported calendar Q1 2026 total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: During the first quarter of calendar 2026, Nvidia generated record revenue of $81.6 billion -- up 85% year over year.\", \"- e89 [fact; fool.com author; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:4a892d75e355bee00aa3c572 2026-07-06] NVIDIA's data center segment revenue was $75.2 billion in calendar Q1 2026, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: The company's core data center segment grew even faster, at 92% year over year, to $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e105; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e98 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:71df54965281684cc500960f 2026-07-06] Wall Street analysts expect Nvidia revenue to grow 82% for the rest of 2026.\\n    Quote: For the rest of this year, they expect 82% growth.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e50; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e99 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:71df54965281684cc500960f 2026-07-06] Wall Street analysts expect Nvidia revenue to grow 41% in 2027.\\n    Quote: For 2027, that figure rises to 41%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e50; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e100 [fact; TradingView; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reported Data Center revenue of $75.25 billion in fiscal 2027 Q1, 92% of total sales.\\n    Quote: During the first quarter of fiscal 2027, the Data Center segment generated $75.25 billion in revenues, accounting for 92% of total sales.\", \"- e101 [fact; TradingView; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] NVIDIA Data Center revenue grew 92% year over year and 21% sequentially in fiscal 2027 Q1.\\n    Quote: Revenues from the segment surged 92% year over year and grew 21% sequentially, driven by the rapid ramp-up of Blackwell 300 systems and robust networking demand.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e124; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e102 [fact; TradingView; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reported total revenue of $81.62 billion in fiscal 2027 Q1, up 85% year over year; non-GAAP EPS was $1.87, up 140%.\\n    Quote: First-quarter fiscal 2027 revenues climbed 85% year over year to $81.62 billion, while non-GAAP earnings per share jumped 140% to $1.87.\", \"- e103 [party_statement; TradingView; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] NVIDIA guided to approximately $91 billion of total revenue in fiscal 2027 Q2, nearly 95% growth year over year.\\n    Quote: For the second quarter of fiscal 2027, NVIDIA projects revenues of approximately $91 billion, representing nearly 95% year-over-year growth.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e118; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e105 [fact; Danielle Liverance; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reported revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year, and data-center revenue of $75.2 billion, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Revenue rose 85% year over year to $81.6 billion, with data center up 92% to $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e89, e116; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e106 [party_statement; Jensen Huang, quoted by Danielle Liverance; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said agentic AI is generating value and scaling rapidly across companies and industries.\\n    Quote: “Agentic AI has arrived, doing productive work, generating real value and scaling rapidly across companies and industries.”\", \"- e108 [third_party_view; Danielle Liverance; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] Bloomberg Intelligence forecast a 27% compound annual growth rate for custom ASICs through 2033, compared with 16% for AI accelerators.\\n    Quote: Broadcom’s custom ASICs for Alphabet and Meta are eating the story, with Bloomberg Intelligence forecasting a 27% CAGR for custom ASICs through 2033 versus 16% for AI accelerators.\", \"- e109 [party_statement; Danielle Liverance; original source Broadcom ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] Broadcom guided Q3 AI semiconductor revenue to $16.0 billion, more than 200% higher year over year.\\n    Quote: Broadcom guided Q3 AI semiconductor revenue to $16.0 billion, more than 200% year over year.\", \"- e110 [party_statement; Danielle Liverance; original source Micron ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] Micron forecast an adjusted gross margin of 86% for next quarter.\\n    Quote: Micron is now forecasting adjusted gross margins of 86% next quarter, above the peak gross margins NVIDIA ever achieved.\", \"- e111 [third_party_view; Danielle Liverance; original source Unspecified estimates ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] Unspecified estimates put memory at half of total data-center spending in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: Some estimates put half of all data center spend going toward memory in 2027.\", \"- e116 [fact; 247wallst.com, author Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.61 billion, up 85.2% year over year, and data center revenue of $75.25 billion.\\n    Quote: Q1 FY27 revenue came in at $81.61 billion, up 85.2% year over year, with data center revenue of $75.25 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e105, e147; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e117 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com, author Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source Omor Ibne Ehsan 2026-07-06; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] The author estimates hyperscalers accounted for about 50% of NVIDIA's Q1 FY2027 data center revenue.\\n    Quote: About 50% of that data center number comes from hyperscalers\", \"- e118 [party_statement; 247wallst.com, author Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] NVIDIA management guided Q2 FY2027 total revenue to $91.0 billion and non-GAAP gross margin to 75%.\\n    Quote: Management guided Q2 FY27 revenue to $91.0 billion with non-GAAP gross margin holding at 75%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e103; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e119 [fact; 247wallst.com, author Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] NVIDIA networking revenue was $14.8 billion, up 199% year over year; the item does not specify the quarter in this sentence.\\n    Quote: Networking revenue grew 199% year over year to $14.8 billion\", \"- e120 [fact; 247wallst.com, author Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source Amazon ; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] Amazon disclosed that its Trainium business is now worth multiple billions of dollars; no period is specified.\\n    Quote: Amazon has disclosed Trainium is now a multi-billion-dollar business\", \"- e121 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com, author Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source Omor Ibne Ehsan 2026-07-06; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] Amazon, Google, Microsoft, and Meta are building proprietary silicon, which the author says is intended to reduce costs and improve negotiating leverage against NVIDIA.\\n    Quote: Amazon, Google, Microsoft, and Meta are all building proprietary silicon to cut costs and gain negotiating leverage over NVIDIA.\", \"- e122 [party_statement; 247wallst.com, author Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source Colette Kress, NVIDIA CFO ; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] The author says NVIDIA's China data center compute revenue is effectively zero; CFO Colette Kress described the future China market as close to $50 billion and said losing it would be material.\\n    Quote: China data center compute revenue is effectively zero, and Colette Kress (Nvidia’s CFO) said losing that market, which NVIDIA sizes at “close to about $50 billion in the future,” would be material.\", \"- e123 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com, author Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source Omor Ibne Ehsan 2026-07-06; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] The author cites $119 billion of NVIDIA supply commitments and says they compound demand risk if hyperscaler orders slow; the period and definition of the commitments are not specified.\\n    Quote: Supply commitments of $119 billion compound demand risk if hyperscaler orders slow\", \"- e124 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com, author Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source Omor Ibne Ehsan 2026-07-06; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] The author cites NVIDIA data center revenue growth of 92%, gross margin of 75%, and quarterly free cash flow of $48.55 billion; the period for the growth and margin figures is not specified in this sentence.\\n    Quote: A company compounding data center revenue at 92% with 75% gross margins and $48.55 billion of quarterly free cash flow is a durable franchise.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e101; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e126 [fact; autonocion.com; original source Nvidia and Valar Atomics 2026-07-01; from gnews:417f6244f0aaa27123023deb 2026-07-06] Nvidia and Valar Atomics announced an agreement to explore nuclear-powered AI systems, including a 30-megawatt closed-loop AI factory in Utah that would use no water from the local community; the factory is under study.\\n    Quote: Alongside the demo, the two companies announced an agreement to jointly explore nuclear-powered AI systems. The concrete version under study is a 30-megawatt closed-loop AI factory in Utah, which Valar’s own announcement says “consumes no water from the local community.”\", \"- e127 [fact; DCD reporter Cristina Cueto; original source Bleeding Edge 2026-07-06; from gnews:c2924b0380602940d68de7ff 2026-07-06] Bleeding Edge launched its Querétaro AI Factory and neocloud offering, which it says is the first Blackwell-based neocloud in Mexico and Latin America.\\n    Quote: Bleeding Edge has launched an AI Factory in Querétaro, Mexico, bringing online its neocloud offering.\", \"- e128 [party_statement; DCD reporter Cristina Cueto; original source Bleeding Edge 2026-07-06; from gnews:c2924b0380602940d68de7ff 2026-07-06] Bleeding Edge said companies developing AI solutions have contracted all of the neocloud platform’s initial capacity.\\n    Quote: According to Bleeding Edge, the platform’s entire initial capacity has already been contracted by companies dedicated to developing AI solutions.\", \"- e129 [party_statement; DCD reporter Cristina Cueto; original source Bleeding Edge 2026-07-06; from gnews:c2924b0380602940d68de7ff 2026-07-06] Bleeding Edge plans to expand neocloud and AI Factory capacity in the coming months by adding Nvidia systems and deploying infrastructure in other markets.\\n    Quote: Bleeding Edge plans to expand both the capacity of its neocloud and its AI Factories in the coming months by incorporating new Nvidia systems and deploying infrastructure in other strategic markets.\", \"- e133 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia plans to make up for the Rubin Ultra shortfall by selling more Oberon-Rubin racks in the existing form factor.\\n    Quote: Nvidia plans to make up for the shortfall by selling more Oberon-Rubin racks in the existing form factor.\", \"- e139 [party_statement; Investing.com; original source Hon Hai management ; from gnews:d5c48abb470f394f86549b6b 2026-07-06] Hon Hai management forecast continued acceleration in AI demand; Mizuho analyst Jordan Klein said this was a positive sign ahead of Nvidia's Vera Rubin rack launch.\\n    Quote: Klein noted that Hon Hai management forecasted a continued acceleration in AI demand, which the analyst said was \\\"a very good sign into the NVDA launch of their new Vera Rubin rack.\\\"\", \"- e140 [third_party_view; Monica J. White, How-To Geek; original source Monica J. White 2026-07-06; from gnews:349140be6b12bf5941071947 2026-07-06] How-To Geek author Monica J. White judged that AMD's RX 9070 XT is much cheaper than Nvidia's RTX 5070 Ti while offering similar performance, except for DLSS.\\n    Quote: The RX 9070 XT is much cheaper than the RTX 5070 Ti, but it offers similar performance, bar DLSS.\", \"- e146 [third_party_view; tikr.com (analyst); original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:d4c5dc540392f8df39aee250 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis forecast NVIDIA data-center compute revenue in the second half of FY2027 to be 20% above current Wall Street expectations.\\n    Quote: SemiAnalysis actually expects Nvidia’s data-center compute revenue in the second half of fiscal 2027 to come in 20% above Wall Street’s current expectations.\", \"- e147 [fact; tikr.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:d4c5dc540392f8df39aee250 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reported quarterly total revenue of $82 billion, up 85% year over year, and data-center revenue of $75 billion; the item does not specify the quarter.\\n    Quote: In the most recent quarter, the company posted $82 billion in total revenue, up 85% year-over-year, with data center revenue alone hitting $75 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e116; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e155 [rumour; Tom's Hardware, reporting SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:c75f16a6d64cc27fc28fb571 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reportedly said NVIDIA changed Rubin Ultra from a quad-chiplet GPU to a dual-chiplet part the prior week, halving per-package compute because of manufacturing execution concerns.\\n    Quote: Nvidia dropped the quad-chiplet Rubin Ultra GPU for a dual-chiplet part last week over manufacturing execution concerns, halving the accelerator's per-package compute.\", \"- e157 [third_party_view; businesstimes.com.sg, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence’s survey; original source Bloomberg Intelligence 2026-07-07; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] Chinese executives surveyed by Bloomberg Intelligence plan to allocate 46% of their AI-accelerator budgets to domestic products over the next 12 months, up from 30% currently.\\n    Quote: Executives in the country say they will allocate 46 per cent of their budget for AI accelerators to domestic products over the next 12 months.\", \"- e158 [third_party_view; businesstimes.com.sg, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence’s survey; original source Bloomberg Intelligence 2026-07-07; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] 80% of Chinese executives surveyed said their total infrastructure spending was running over budget in 2026, mostly because of the high cost of AI-related projects.\\n    Quote: In addition, 80 per cent of executives said their total infrastructure spending is running over-budget this year, mostly because of the high cost of AI-related projects.\", \"- e159 [third_party_view; businesstimes.com.sg, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence’s survey; original source Bloomberg Intelligence 2026-07-07; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] Bloomberg Intelligence’s survey expects Nvidia’s market share in China to shrink as H20 chips become harder to find and local suppliers take over; it says Beijing has urged Chinese technology firms not to use H20 chips.\\n    Quote: While Nvidia’s products remain popular, the Santa Clara-based firm’s market share is expected to shrink as its H20 chips, which Beijing has urged its tech firms not to use , become harder to find and local firms take over, according to the survey.\", \"- e160 [fact; businesstimes.com.sg; original source The Chinese government ; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] China is allocating roughly 2 trillion yuan (US$294 billion) over five years to build data centres and expand AI use across sectors.\\n    Quote: China is allocating roughly two trillion yuan (US$294 billion) to build data centres across the country in the next five years, a government-led initiative to expand the use of AI in sectors from healthcare to city management.\", \"- e161 [third_party_view; businesstimes.com.sg, reporting Bloomberg News; original source Bloomberg News ; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] Bloomberg News reported that domestic companies will supply at least 80% of China’s core technologies, including chips.\\n    Quote: At least 80 per cent of core technologies, such as chips, will be supplied by domestic companies, Bloomberg News reported.\", \"- e162 [third_party_view; businesstimes.com.sg, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence’s report; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] Bloomberg Intelligence’s report says a global memory-chip shortage is likely to cap growth at Chinese AI firms such as SMIC, while ChangXin Memory Technologies is positioned to benefit.\\n    Quote: But a global memory chip shortage is likely to cap the growth of Chinese AI firms like Semiconductor Manufacturing International Corporation, with ChangXin Memory Technologies poised to reap the benefits.\", \"- e108 [third_party_view; Danielle Liverance; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] Bloomberg Intelligence forecast a 27% compound annual growth rate for custom ASICs through 2033, compared with 16% for AI accelerators.\\n    Quote: Broadcom’s custom ASICs for Alphabet and Meta are eating the story, with Bloomberg Intelligence forecasting a 27% CAGR for custom ASICs through 2033 versus 16% for AI accelerators.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e185; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e109 [party_statement; Danielle Liverance; original source Broadcom ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] Broadcom guided Q3 AI semiconductor revenue to $16.0 billion, more than 200% higher year over year.\\n    Quote: Broadcom guided Q3 AI semiconductor revenue to $16.0 billion, more than 200% year over year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e184; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e116 [fact; 247wallst.com, author Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.61 billion, up 85.2% year over year, and data center revenue of $75.25 billion.\\n    Quote: Q1 FY27 revenue came in at $81.61 billion, up 85.2% year over year, with data center revenue of $75.25 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e105, e147, e182; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e122 [party_statement; 247wallst.com, author Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source Colette Kress, NVIDIA CFO ; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] The author says NVIDIA's China data center compute revenue is effectively zero; CFO Colette Kress described the future China market as close to $50 billion and said losing it would be material.\\n    Quote: China data center compute revenue is effectively zero, and Colette Kress (Nvidia’s CFO) said losing that market, which NVIDIA sizes at “close to about $50 billion in the future,” would be material.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e193; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e163 [party_statement; NVIDIA Corporation; original source Perplexity ; from nvblog:nvidia-vera-max-single-threaded-cpu-at-scale 2026-07-07] Perplexity is looking to deploy NVIDIA Vera in its upcoming production system; no deployment date or amount is given.\\n    Quote: Perplexity is now looking to deploy Vera in its upcoming production system.\", \"- e164 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source NVIDIA and Hugging Face 2026-07-07; from nvblog:hugging-face-lerobot-models-frameworks-open-robotics 2026-07-07] NVIDIA and Hugging Face are integrating Isaac GR00T 1.7 and Isaac Teleop into Hugging Face’s LeRobot robotics library.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA and Hugging Face are collaborating to bring the NVIDIA Isaac GR00T 1.7 open, reasoning vision language action (VLA) model for humanoid robots and the NVIDIA Isaac Teleop framework to LeRobot — Hugging Face’s open source library for robotics\", \"- e165 [party_statement; NVIDIA Corporation; original source NVIDIA Corporation 2026-07-07; from nvblog:hugging-face-lerobot-models-frameworks-open-robotics 2026-07-07] NVIDIA plans to integrate Cosmos 3 into Hugging Face’s LeRobot library soon.\\n    Quote: with NVIDIA Cosmos 3 , a frontier model for physical AI, planned soon.\", \"- e166 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source Palantir ; from gnews:1a116fecd5de1747cc5a06b1 2026-07-07] Palantir 