ace is called AI1 and will use Nvidia chips.\", \"- e182 [fact; 24/7 Wall St.; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] NVIDIA Data Center revenue was $75.246 billion in Q1 FY2027, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue reached $75.246 billion (+92% YoY) in Q1 FY27, and CEO Jensen Huang described “the largest infrastructure expansion in human history”.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e116; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e183 [party_statement; 24/7 Wall St.; original source Lisa Su, AMD CEO ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] AMD CEO Lisa Su said customer engagement for MI450 Series and Helios is strengthening, with leading-customer forecasts above AMD’s initial expectations.\\n    Quote: CEO Lisa Su has said “customer engagement around MI450 Series and Helios is strengthening, with leading customer forecasts exceeding our initial expectations.”\", \"- e184 [fact; 24/7 Wall St.; original source Broadcom ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] Broadcom reported Q2 AI semiconductor revenue of $10.8 billion, up 143% year over year, and guided Q3 revenue to $16.0 billion.\\n    Quote: Q2 AI semiconductor revenue was $10.8 billion, +143% YoY, with Q3 guided to $16.0 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e109; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e185 [third_party_view; 24/7 Wall St.; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] Bloomberg Intelligence forecasts a 27% compound annual growth rate for the custom ASIC market through 2033.\\n    Quote: Bloomberg Intelligence forecasts 27% CAGR for the custom ASIC market through 2033.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e108; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e186 [fact; 24/7 Wall St.; original source Google ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] Google Cloud revenue rose 63%, its backlog nearly doubled to more than $460 billion, and Google guided 2026 capital expenditures to $190 billion.\\n    Quote: Google Cloud revenue rose 63% with backlog nearly doubling to over $460 billion, and 2026 capex is guided up tp $190 billion.\", \"- e188 [party_statement; NVIDIA; original source id Software and Bethesda Softworks ; from gnews:2f1cb54b7a3da28d093523b6 2026-07-07] NVIDIA said DOOM: The Dark Ages | Revelations would launch on July 7, 2026, with DLSS Multi Frame Generation, Ray Reconstruction and path tracing support.\\n    Quote: Later today, the DOOM: The Dark Ages | Revelations expansion launches with support for DLSS Multi Frame Generation and Ray Reconstruction, and path tracing.\", \"- e189 [party_statement; NVIDIA; original source Ubisoft ; from gnews:2f1cb54b7a3da28d093523b6 2026-07-07] NVIDIA said Assassin’s Creed Black Flag Resynced would launch on July 9, 2026, with DLSS Multi Frame Generation, Super Resolution and ray tracing support.\\n    Quote: On Thursday, Assassin’s Creed Black Flag Resynced launches with DLSS Multi Frame Generation and Super Resolution, and ray tracing.\", \"- e190 [fact; NVIDIA; original source MADFINGER Games ; from gnews:2f1cb54b7a3da28d093523b6 2026-07-07] NVIDIA said Gray Zone Warfare had added its latest DLSS Dynamic Multi Frame Generation and Super Resolution models for GeForce RTX GPUs.\\n    Quote: Now, the latest DLSS Dynamic Multi Frame Generation and Super Resolution models have been added to further enhance frame rates and image quality on GeForce RTX GPUs.\", \"- e191 [rumour; mlq.ai; original source Three people with knowledge of the matter, as cited by Reuters 2026-07-06; from gnews:9f430c6ce2e8d551fe1f063a 2026-07-07] DeepSeek is developing a custom AI inference chip, according to three people cited by Reuters.\\n    Quote: DeepSeek, the Hangzhou-based AI startup behind some of China's most advanced large language models, is developing its own custom AI chip, Reuters reported on Monday, citing three people with knowledge of the matter [1] . The chip is designed for inference — the phase where trained models generate responses to user queries — rather than for training new models.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e195; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e192 [fact; mlq.ai; original source The U.S. government ; from gnews:9f430c6ce2e8d551fe1f063a 2026-07-07] U.S. export controls bar Chinese companies from accessing the most advanced overseas foundries and restrict shipments of high-bandwidth memory.\\n    Quote: U.S. export controls that bar access to the most advanced overseas foundries and restrict shipments of high-bandwidth memory — a component critical to inference chip performance [2].\", \"- e193 [third_party_view; mlq.ai; original source Richard Windey ; from gnews:9f430c6ce2e8d551fe1f063a 2026-07-07] Analyst Richard Windey said U.S. export rules have effectively zeroed out Nvidia's China revenue and limit DeepSeek's ability to manufacture or sell advanced silicon outside China.\\n    Quote: Analyst Richard Windey highlighted the constraint: the same export rules that have effectively zeroed out Nvidia's China revenue also limit DeepSeek's ability to manufacture or sell advanced silicon outside China [3].\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e122, e198; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e194 [third_party_view; mlq.ai; original source Industry surveys ; from gnews:9f430c6ce2e8d551fe1f063a 2026-07-07] Industry surveys indicate Chinese firms plan to allocate 46% of their AI-accelerator budgets to domestic suppliers within 12 months, versus about 30% currently.\\n    Quote: Industry surveys indicate Chinese firms plan to shift 46% of their AI-accelerator budgets to domestic suppliers within 12 months, up from roughly 30% today [5].\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e157; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e195 [rumour; idnfinancials.com; original source Three unnamed sources familiar with DeepSeek's plans, cited by Reuters ; from gnews:2957e5c79a365952140c8cce 2026-07-07] Unnamed sources cited by Reuters said DeepSeek is developing chips specifically for AI inference.\\n    Quote: According to Reuters , citing three sources familiar with the plans, DeepSeek's chips are being designed specifically for inference, the stage where trained AI models generate responses for users.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e191; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e196 [rumour; idnfinancials.com; original source Unnamed Reuters sources ; from gnews:2957e5c79a365952140c8cce 2026-07-07] Unnamed Reuters sources said DeepSeek's early-stage chip project has involved discussions over the past year with chip design firms, foundries and memory suppliers.\\n    Quote: According to Reuters sources, DeepSeek's chip development project remains at an early stage. Over the past year, the company has been communicating with chip design firms, foundries and memory suppliers to support the development of the semiconductors.\", \"- e197 [rumour; idnfinancials.com; original source idnfinancials.com ; from gnews:2957e5c79a365952140c8cce 2026-07-07] DeepSeek increased recruitment of chip design engineers in recent months, without publicly posting the openings on general recruitment platforms.\\n    Quote: DeepSeek has also increased recruitment of chip design engineers in recent months. The hiring process has been conducted discreetly, without publicly posting job openings on general recruitment platforms.\", \"- e198 [third_party_view; Richard Windsor, Radio Free Mobile; original source Richard Windsor, Radio Free Mobile ; from gnews:2957e5c79a365952140c8cce 2026-07-07] Analyst Richard Windsor said Nvidia's position in China is effectively zero and will remain so, and