15% year-on-year, nearly twice cloud capital-expenditure growth.\\n    Quote: Sales to hyperscalers rose 115% year-on-year, nearly twice cloud capex growth.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e230; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e225 [fact; qz.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:ee0d6792b6bf98069cfe0cc6 2026-07-08] Nvidia reported FY2027 first-quarter total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: For its fiscal first quarter of 2027, Nvidia posted $81.6 billion in total revenue — an 85% increase from a year earlier\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e102; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e226 [fact; qz.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:ee0d6792b6bf98069cfe0cc6 2026-07-08] Nvidia's data center segment reported record revenue of $75.2 billion in FY2027's first quarter.\\n    Quote: while its data center segment set a record at $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e105; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e227 [party_statement; Tom’s Hardware; original source AMD ; from gnews:9fbd0f954b9cc2281da531d1 2026-07-08] AMD claimed its hardware would deliver 3.3x Vera’s performance for the projected output of a 100 kW rack; the item gives no statement date.\\n    Quote: AMD had some things to say about the Phoronix test, firing back with its own metrics of a 3.3x performance gain over Vera for the projected output of a 100 kW rack of its hardware.\", \"- e228 [third_party_view; aibusiness.com, quoting Lian Jye Su; original source Lian Jye Su, analyst at Omdia ; from gnews:21e9182d07508a6690f10419 2026-07-08] Omdia analyst Lian Jye Su said Nvidia is facing challenges from Chinese vendors as humanoid robotics vendors rise in China.\\n    Quote: “The company is facing some challenges from Chinese vendors due to the rise of humanoid robotics vendors in China ,” Su noted.\", \"- e229 [fact; aibusiness.com; original source Qualcomm and Intel ; from gnews:21e9182d07508a6690f10419 2026-07-08] Qualcomm recently entered robotics with Dragonwing IQ10, and Intel with its OpenVINO robotics offerings, challenging Nvidia’s position.\\n    Quote: In addition, Qualcomm, with its Dragonwing IQ10 and Intel, with its OpenVINO robotics offerings, have recently entered the fold to challenge Nvidia’s position.\", \"- e230 [third_party_view; moomoo.com; original source BofA ; from gnews:1b5a3359dd0644861c0fce42 2026-07-08] BofA reported that Nvidia’s hyperscaler sales rose 115% year over year, nearly twice the growth rate of cloud capital expenditures.\\n    Quote: The report also says Nvidia’s hyperscaler sales rose 115% year over year, nearly twice cloud capex growth, suggesting wallet-share gains rather than share loss.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e224; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e231 [third_party_view; moomoo.com; original source BofA ; from gnews:1b5a3359dd0644861c0fce42 2026-07-08] BofA modeled Nvidia retaining roughly 65%–70% or more of AI capital expenditures over time, with the remainder going to ASICs, AMD and other merchant vendors.\\n    Quote: BofA still models Nvidia holding roughly 65% to 70% plus of AI capex over time, with the rest split across ASICs, AMD and other merchant vendors.\", \"- e232 [rumour; Notebookcheck.net; original source Notebookcheck.net, reporting unnamed sources ; from gnews:134fc6bce6a550f5376d6f27 2026-07-08] Notebookcheck reports that Nvidia is reportedly planning to release RTX 50 Super cards in 2027 instead of launching the next-generation RTX 60 series.\\n    Quote: However, the news has been quite disappointing when it comes to the GeForce RTX 60 series cards. Rather than initiate a full-blown next-gen RTX 60 series launch, Nvidia is reportedly planning to release the RTX 50 Super series cards in 2027.\", \"- e233 [rumour; Notebookcheck.net, relaying Moore’s Law Is Dead; original source An unnamed Nvidia source, as relayed by Moore’s Law Is Dead ; from gnews:134fc6bce6a550f5376d6f27 2026-07-08] An unnamed Nvidia source told leaker Moore’s Law Is Dead that the RTX 60 series GPUs are not expected to come out in 2027.\\n    Quote: One of Moore’s Law Is Dead’s Nvidia source told the leaker that they don’t think the RTX 60 series GPUs are coming out in 2027.\", \"- e234 [third_party_view; Notebookcheck.net; original source Notebookcheck.net 2026-07-08; from gnews:134fc6bce6a550f5376d6f27 2026-07-08] Notebookcheck reports that AMD is expected to release RDNA 5 gaming GPUs in 2027, a potential competitive product launch for Nvidia.\\n    Quote: We have been hearing about the release timeline of the next-gen AMD and Nvidia GPUs for a while now. It is now clear that we approaching the end of the current-gen GPU lifecycle, as AMD is expected to release the RDNA 5 gaming GPUs in 2027.\", \"- e235 [fact; Larsen & Toubro Vyoma; original source L&T Vyoma and Fortanix 2026-07-08; from gnews:79b4840d3de4aa77ec0d0229 2026-07-08] L&T Vyoma and Fortanix announced a partnership to offer sovereign AI infrastructure and secure workloads using NVIDIA Confidential Computing; the announcement gave no amount or timeline.\\n    Quote: Through this partnership, L&T Vyoma will provide sovereign AI infrastructure, including data centres, compute and networking, while Fortanix will secure the data and AI workloads in use by leveraging NVIDIA Confidential Computing.\", \"- e27 [party_statement; fool.com analyst Justin Pope; original source Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang ; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang expects $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\\n    Quote: CEO Jensen Huang has laid out expectations for $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e252; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e252 [party_statement; fool.com (Adam Spatacco); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:931ee0196ca609e637235fad 2026-07-09] NVIDIA management cited roughly $1 trillion of revenue visibility for Blackwell and Vera Rubin processors across 2026 and 2027, anchored by multiyear customer commitments.\\n    Quote: Management has also articulated roughly $1 trillion in revenue visibility for its Blackwell and Vera Rubin processors across 2026 and 2027, anchored by multiyear commitments from hyperscalers and large enterprise customers.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e27; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e258 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Bloomberg Intelligence projects Nvidia will hold 70%–75% of the AI chip market through 2030.\\n    Quote: Bloomberg Intelligence projects the company will hold 70% to 75% of the AI chip market through 2030.\", \"- e259 [party_statement; qz.com; original source Andy Jassy, Amazon CEO ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Amazon CEO Andy Jassy said in late 2025 that Trainium2 had no spare capacity left to sell and was a multibillion-dollar business growing at a 150% quarterly clip.\\n    Quote: Amazon CEO Andy Jassy said in late 2025 that Trainium2, the previous generation, had no spare capacity left to sell. He said it had grown into a multibillion-dollar business at a 150% quarterly clip.\", \"- e263 [party_statement; qz.com; original source Meta ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Meta’s MTIA 300 is in production for ranking and recommendation, and Meta plans to build three further MTIA generations over the next two years for generative AI models.\\n    Quote: The newest version, MTIA 300, is already in production for ranking and recommendation work. Meta is set to build three more generations over the next two years with the purpose of running generative AI models.\", \"- e264 [party_statement; qz.com; original source Meta ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Meta expects its MTIA 450 chip in early 2027 and MTIA 500 later in 2027.\\n    Quote: The next one, MTIA 450, arrives in early 2027, doubling how fast the chip moves data in and out of memory. Its eventual successor, MTIA 500, is expected to come later next year, and pushes memory speed another 50% higher.\", \"- e265 [party_statement; qz.com; original source OpenAI ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] OpenAI’s planned installation of its custom AI chips is set to begin in the second half of 2026 and continue through the end of 2029.\\n    Quote: Installing them is set to begin in the second half of 2026 and run through the end of 2029.\", \"- e266 [fact; qz.com; original source Tesla ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Tesla completed the AI5 inference-chip design in April 2026 and plans production at TSMC’s Arizona plant and Samsung’s Texas plant.\\n    Quote: Tesla finished the design of its AI5 inference chip in April 2026, according to Reuters . Production is planned at both TSMC 's plant in Arizona and Samsung's plant in Texas.\", \"- e267 [party_statement; qz.com; original source Tesla ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Tesla is targeting mid-2027 to begin mass production of its AI5 chip.\\n    Quote: Tesla is targeting mid-2027 for mass production.\", \"- e274 [rumour; au.finance.yahoo.com; original source Cerebras ; from gnews:66cb0387229ac4b1390615cb 2026-07-09] Cerebras plans to build European AI data centres with combined power capacity of 200 MW by the end of 2027, adding competing AI compute capacity.\\n    Quote: The company plans to build a network of AI data centres across Europe by the end of 2027, with a combined power capacity of 200 MW.\", \"- e275 [party_statement; au.finance.yahoo.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:66cb0387229ac4b1390615cb 2026-07-09] Nvidia says its technology powers more than 90% of announced AI factory projects in Europe.\\n    Quote: The expansion comes as AI infrastructure investment accelerates across Europe, where Nvidia says its technology powers more than 90% of the continent's announced AI factory projects.\", \"- e163 [party_statement; NVIDIA Corporation; original source Perplexity ; from nvblog:nvidia-vera-max-single-threaded-cpu-at-scale 2026-07-07] Perplexity is looking to deploy NVIDIA Vera in its upcoming production system; no deployment date or amount is given.\\n    Quote: Perplexity is now looking to deploy Vera in its upcoming production system.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e295; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e169 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source Amazon and Alphabet ; from gnews:ce5daf57bdca5da657e5f677 2026-07-07] Amazon and Alphabet are extending access to their in-house processors, increasing competition for NVIDIA’s AI computing products.\\n    Quote: The move comes as the company faces rising competition from specialized AI chips from cloud providers, including Amazon and Alphabet, which are extending access to in-house processors.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e278; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e218 [third_party_view; tradingview.com; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:a09988fd9c5c1a739a14f873 2026-07-08] Bloomberg Intelligence data cited in the source puts NVIDIA's server GPU market share at 97% at the end of 2025, up from 95% at the end of 2024.\\n    Quote: The company is projected to generate $228 billion in profit on $393 billion in sales in fiscal 2027, which ends Jan. 31, representing expected growth of 90% and 82%, respectively, while its profit estimate has risen 13% over the past three months.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e277; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e277 [third_party_view; Jeran Wittenstein, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence data; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:49f225cd79fb22132f3b9ee4 2026-07-10] Bloomberg Intelligence data put NVIDIA’s server GPU market share at 97% at the end of 2025, up from 95% at the end of 2024.\\n    Quote: Nvidia had 97% of the server GPU market at the end of 2025, up from 95% at the end of 2024, according to data compiled by Bloomberg Intelligence.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e218; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e278 [third_party_view; Jeran Wittenstein; original source Jeran Wittenstein 2026-07-10; from gnews:49f225cd79fb22132f3b9ee4 2026-07-10] Alphabet and Amazon are increasingly deploying their own custom-made chips, adding to competition with NVIDIA.\\n    Quote: For now, that competition — not just from AMD and Intel but also from its biggest customers like Alphabet Inc. and Amazon.com Inc., who are increasingly deploying their own custom-made chips — is a major factor holding back Nvidia’s stock price.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e169, e291; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e280 [third_party_view; Trefis; original source Trefis 2026-07-10; from gnews:6abaf2856736877236d30f6a 2026-07-10] Trefis reports Wall Street consensus expects NVIDIA revenue to grow about 32% annually over the next few years.\\n    Quote: Wall Street consensus sees NVIDIA’s revenue growing about 32% a year for the next few years.\", \"- e291 [rumour; GuruFocus; original source GuruFocus ; from gnews:4c201dc59ba0c7579bfef4db 2026-07-10] GuruFocus reported rumors that major NVIDIA clients were accelerating development of in-house AI chips, potentially increasing competition for NVIDIA.\\n    Quote: rumors of major clients accelerating their development of in-house artificial intelligence (AI) chips\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e278; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e295 [fact; quantumzeitgeist.com; original source Perplexity ; from gnews:b666d35e5247a8ddcc2d7c72 2026-07-10] Perplexity plans to integrate NVIDIA Vera CPUs into its upcoming production systems; no amount or date was given.\\n    Quote: Perplexity is now planning to integrate Vera into its upcoming production systems, demonstrating confidence in its ability to enhance agent performance and overall system efficiency.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e163; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e297 [party_statement; theverge.com; original source Chey Tae-won ; from gnews:3839887e5ca53a0cb0e7c91e 2026-07-10] SK Group chairman Chey Tae-won said in June that SK Hynix plans to ramp up memory-chip capacity over the next five years to address a shortage that could last until 2030.\\n    Quote: SK Group chairman Chey Tae-won said in June that the company plans to ramp up its memory chip capacity over the next five years to address a shortage that could last until 2030, Bloomberg reports .\", \"- e298 [third_party_view; Thomas Richmond, quoting Kristina Partsinevelos; original source Kristina Partsinevelos 2026-07-10; from gnews:9ae96ca750b8e3962c47795f 2026-07-10] Kristina Partsinevelos said no additional HBM supply would arrive before late 2027, keeping the memory shortage and record-high prices in place until then.\\n    Quote: “None of that supply, though, arrives before late 2027, which keeps the memory shortage going and record-high prices intact for now,” Partsinevelos said.\", \"- e194 [third_party_view; mlq.ai; original source Industry surveys ; from gnews:9f430c6ce2e8d551fe1f063a 2026-07-07] Industry surveys indicate Chinese firms plan to allocate 46% of their AI-accelerator budgets to domestic suppliers within 12 months, versus about 30% currently.\\n    Quote: Industry surveys indicate Chinese firms plan to shift 46% of their AI-accelerator budgets to domestic suppliers within 12 months, up from roughly 30% today [5].\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e157, e343; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e327 [party_statement; tech-insider.org; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:8faf69f198e10f14aae67621 2026-07-12] Nvidia said AWS plans to deploy 2 million additional Nvidia GPUs during 2027–2028.\\n    Quote: Nvidia said in August 2026 that AWS plans to deploy 2 million additional Nvidia GPUs in 2027 to 2028 .\", \"- e328 [third_party_view; io-fund.com; original source Yole Research ; from gnews:2dcfaef1a91c2976a4e347da 2026-07-12] Yole Research projected that more than 90% of servers would be CXL-capable by the end of calendar 2026, up from two-thirds in Q1 2025.\\n    Quote: Yole Research estimated that in Q1 2025, two-thirds of servers were CXL-capable , and projects this figure will rise to more than 90% by the end of 2026.\", \"- e329 [party_statement; io-fund.com; original source Marvell ; from gnews:2dcfaef1a91c2976a4e347da 2026-07-12] Marvell plans to begin sampling its Structera S CXL 3.0 switch in calendar Q3 2026.\\n    Quote: Marvell expects to begin sampling its Structera S CXL 3.0 switch in calendar Q3 2026.\", \"- e331 [third_party_view; barchart.com (analyst); original source Wedbush Securities ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Wedbush Securities said Nvidia's Vera CPU could expand its addressable market beyond GPUs and create billions of dollars in additional revenue; no period was specified.\\n    Quote: Wedbush Securities recently argued that Nvidia's new Vera CPU platform could expand the company's total addressable market (TAM) well beyond graphics processors, opening the door to billions of dollars in additional revenue.\", \"- e332 [rumour; barchart.com (analyst); original source barchart.com (unnamed reports) ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Reports said Nvidia had begun offering Vera processors to cloud customers, including some in China where regulations allow; no amount or period was specified.\\n    Quote: Reports also suggest Nvidia has begun offering the new processors to cloud customers, including some in China where regulations allow.\", \"- e343 [third_party_view; barchart.com (analyst); original source Bloomberg survey ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] A Bloomberg survey found Chinese technology companies expect domestic suppliers to receive roughly 46% of their AI-chip spending over the next year, up from about 30% currently.\\n    Quote: A new Bloomberg survey showed Chinese technology companies expect to allocate roughly 46% of their AI chip spending to domestic suppliers over the next year, up from about 30% currently.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e194; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e359 [party_statement; gurufocus.com (analyst); original source Nvidia management ; from gnews:dedacecd6d2ed5192c307199 2026-07-13] Nvidia management expects sovereign AI projects and on-premise deployments to account for a larger share of future growth; no period or amount was specified.\\n    Quote: It expects sovereign AI projects and on-premise deployments to make up a larger share of future growth as AI adoption expands.\", \"- e360 [fact; GuruFocus; original source Google ; from gnews:1c47fd978ef50b1d7f48cbd8 2026-07-13] Google approached neocloud companies about using its TPUs, potentially expanding competition with Nvidia in AI chips.\\n    Quote: Google has approached so-called neocloud companies about using its tensor processing units, or TPUs, according to a report from The Information.\", \"- e361 [third_party_view; GuruFocus; original source Nscale ; from gnews:1c47fd978ef50b1d7f48cbd8 2026-07-13] Nscale reportedly told Google its active projects remain centered on GPU capacity, indicating limited near-term openness to TPU adoption at that provider.\\n    Quote: One provider, Nscale, reportedly told Google that its active projects remain centered on GPU capacity.\", \"- e362 [third_party_view; GuruFocus; original source Google and Blackstone ; from gnews:1c47fd978ef50b1d7f48cbd8 2026-07-13] Google and Blackstone are working on a cloud venture that plans to rent TPU capacity to AI labs and financial firms in 2027.\\n    Quote: Google is also working with Blackstone on a new cloud venture that plans to rent TPU capacity to AI labs and financial firms next year.\", \"- e383 [party_statement; Abhinav Raj, as reported by XDA Developers; original source AMD ; from gnews:6e27fc3ef50f99b180c6646a 2026-07-13] AMD has committed to bringing FSR 4.1 to RDNA 2 GPUs, with the rollout expected to extend into 2027.\\n    Quote: AMD, to its credit, has committed to bringing FSR 4.1 to RDNA 2 cards, but that rollout is expected to stretch into 2027, seven years after those GPUs launched and two full years behind the equivalent Nvidia moment.\", \"- e390 [third_party_view; Rich Duprey; original source Morgan Stanley ; from gnews:e0e5ab6c2aced8d5a6a688a5 2026-07-13] The article reports Morgan Stanley's forecast that Google, Amazon, Microsoft, and Meta will spend over $1 trillion on AI infrastructure and add 19.5 GW of compute capacity in calendar 2027; they added roughly 6.7 GW in 2025, while Google alone is forecast to add 6.8 GW in 2027.\\n    Quote: The analyst says Google, Amazon, Microsoft, and Meta are forecast to spend over $1 trillion on AI infrastructure next year, adding 19.5 gigawatts (GW) of incremental compute capacity. In 2025, they added roughly 6.7 GW. Google alone will add 6.8 GW, or more than the hyperscalers did combined two years ago.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e173; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e391 [third_party_view; Rich Duprey; original source Morgan Stanley ; from gnews:e0e5ab6c2aced8d5a6a688a5 2026-07-13] Morgan Stanley says hyperscalers are continuing to expand investment in proprietary silicon to improve total cost of ownership and reduce dependence on merchant GPU suppliers.\\n    Quote: Morgan Stanley says hyperscalers continue to expand their investments in proprietary silicon to improve total cost of ownership and reduce dependence on merchant GPU suppliers.\", \"- e392 [third_party_view; Rich Duprey; original source Milk Road AI ; from gnews:e0e5ab6c2aced8d5a6a688a5 2026-07-13] Milk Road AI estimates that one GW of AI infrastructure costs $6 billion–$11 billion with Broadcom- or Marvell-designed ASIC racks, versus roughly $19 billion with Nvidia GB300-based racks and $25 billion with Vera Rubin racks.\\n    Quote: Milk Road AI estimates that building one gigawatt of AI infrastructure using Broadcom- or Marvell-designed ASIC racks cost between $6 billion and $11 billion, compared with roughly $19 billion using Nvidia GB300-based racks. Under Vera Rubin, rack costs jump to $25 billion.\", \"- e28 [third_party_view; fool.com analyst Justin Pope; original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] Wall Street analysts estimate Nvidia revenue of $392 billion in FY2027, compared with trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts estimate that Nvidia's business could double over the next couple of years, from trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion to $392 billion this fiscal year, and $554 billion the following year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e401; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e401 [third_party_view; Justin Pope, The Motley Fool; original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:84e90d3da2d3779da0e7bdb0 2026-07-14] Wall Street analysts estimate NVIDIA total revenue of approximately $555 billion in FY2028, ending January 2028.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts estimate that Nvidia will generate approximately $555 billion in revenue for the company's next fiscal year, ending January 2028.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e28; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e404 [party_statement; Nokia, as reported by the outlet; original source Nokia 2026-07-15; from gnews:e153ff10e5adda87a52745a4 2026-07-14] Nokia said it developed the first commercial AI-driven radio access network platform with Nvidia.\\n    Quote: Nokia Oyj says it developed the first commercial artificial intelligence-driven radio access network platform together with Nvidia Corp to radically increase the amount of data operators can transmit using existing infrastructure.\", \"- e425 [third_party_view; sg.finance.yahoo.com; original source Zacks ; from gnews:f10cd8ddb00105698ac294cf 2026-07-14] Zacks reported that consensus analyst estimates for Nvidia increased 13.7% over the three months before 2026-07-14; the estimate measure and fiscal period are not specified.\\n    Quote: Analysts have been steadily raising their estimates for Nvidia. Over the past three months, the Zacks Consensus Estimate for the company has increased 13.7%.\"]\n{\"control\": 7, \"points_to_rule\": [\"same_question\"], \"ruler_question\": {\"question\": \"How much will the largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?\", \"unit\": \"USD\", \"due_day\": \"2028-12-31\", \"rungs\": [{\"label\": \"Below $700 billion\", \"condition\": \"Combined spending is less than $700 billion.\", \"lo\": null, \"hi\": 700000000000.0}, {\"label\": \"$700 billion to below $800 billion\", \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $700 billion and less than $800 billion.\", \"lo\": 700000000000.0, \"hi\": 800000000000.0}, {\"label\": \"$800 billion to below $900 billion\", \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $800 billion and less than $900 billion.\", \"lo\": 800000000000.0, \"hi\": 900000000000.0}, {\"label\": \"$900 billion to below $1000 billion\", \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $900 billion and less than $1000 billion.\", \"lo\": 900000000000.0, \"hi\": 1000000000000.0}, {\"label\": \"$1000 billion or more\", \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $1000 billion.\", \"lo\": 1000000000000.0, \"hi\": null}]}, \"judged_question\": {\"view_id\": \"v5\", \"question\": \"What will the big four AI hyperscalers' combined data center capital expenditures be in calendar 2027?\", \"looks_at\": \"Combined data center capital expenditures of the big four AI hyperscalers in calendar 2027\", \"due_day\": \"2028-03-31\", \"year\": \"2027\", \"kind\": \"theme\"}, \"judged_rungs\": [{\"position\": 1, \"label\": \"Lowest\", \"condition\": \"Below $850 billion\", \"lo\": null, \"hi\": 850000000000.0}, {\"position\": 2, \"label\": \"Low\", \"condition\": \"At least $850 billion but below $950 billion\", \"lo\": 850000000000.0, \"hi\": 950000000000.0}, {\"position\": 3, \"label\": \"Middle\", \"condition\": \"At least $950 billion but below $1.05 trillion\", \"lo\": 950000000000.0, \"hi\": 1050000000000.0}, {\"position\": 4, \"label\": \"High\", \"condition\": \"At least $1.05 trillion but below $1.15 trillion\", \"lo\": 1050000000000.0, \"hi\": 1150000000000.0}, {\"position\": 5, \"label\": \"Highest\", \"condition\": \"At least $1.15 trillion\", \"lo\": 1150000000000.0, \"hi\": null}]}\n{\"control\": 8, \"points_to_rule\": [\"item i295\", \"item i037\"], \"ruler_question\": {\"question\": \"What will Nvidia's total revenue be in FY2027?\", \"unit\": \"USD\", \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\", \"rungs\": [{\"label\": \"Strongly bullish\", \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $500 billion.\", \"lo\": 500000000000.0, \"hi\": null}, {\"label\": \"Bullish\", \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $400 billion and below $500 billion.\", \"lo\": 400000000000.0, \"hi\": 500000000000.0}, {\"label\": \"Neutral\", \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $350 billion and below $400 billion.\", \"lo\": 350000000000.0, \"hi\": 400000000000.0}, {\"label\": \"Bearish\", \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $300 billion and below $350 billion.\", \"lo\": 300000000000.0, \"hi\": 350000000000.0}, {\"label\": \"Strongly bearish\", \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is below $300 billion.\", \"lo\": null, \"hi\": 300000000000.0}]}, \"judged_question\": {\"view_id\": \"v9\", \"question\": \"What will NVIDIA's total revenue be in FY2027?\", \"looks_at\": \"NVIDIA total revenue in FY2027\", \"due_day\": \"2027-02-24\", \"year\": \"FY2027\", \"kind\": \"asset\"}, \"judged_rungs\": [{\"position\": 1, \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\", \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is below $300 billion.\", \"lo\": null, \"hi\": 300000000000.0}, {\"position\": 2, \"label\": \"Bullish\", \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $300 billion and below $350 billion.\", \"lo\": 300000000000.0, \"hi\": 350000000000.0}, {\"position\": 3, \"label\": \"Neutral\", \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $350 billion and below $400 billion.\", \"lo\": 350000000000.0, \"hi\": 400000000000.0}, {\"position\": 4, \"label\": \"Bearish\", \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $400 billion and below $450 billion.\", \"lo\": 400000000000.0, \"hi\": 450000000000.0}, {\"position\": 5, \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\", \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $450 billion.\", \"lo\": 450000000000.0, \"hi\": null}]}\nITEM [{\"id\": \"i295\", \"day\": \"2026-07-10\", \"title\": \"Here are Friday's biggest analyst calls: Nvidia, SpaceX, Toll, Shopify, Twilio, Seagate, Chipotle & more\", \"passage\": \"the company describing \\\"accelerating growth rates\\\" even as revenues approach the $100 bn per quarter mark\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"NVIDIA management, relayed by Morgan Stanley\", \"what\": \"revenue growth rates accelerating\", \"how_much\": \"quarterly revenue approaching $100 bn\", \"status\": \"claim\"}}]\nEVIDENCE [\"- e204 [fact; Yahoo Finance; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:b40db2c507df72ec016e99e6 2026-07-08] NVIDIA reported FY2026 revenue above $215.9 billion, up 65% year over year.\\n    Quote: The company's most recent fiscal 2026 revenue topped $215.9 billion, up 65% year over year and well ahead of the $11.7 billion it posted in 2019.\", \"- e205 [third_party_view; Yahoo Finance; original source Analysts ; from gnews:b40db2c507df72ec016e99e6 2026-07-08] Analysts anticipate NVIDIA FY2027 revenue of $392.7 billion.\\n    Quote: And analysts are anticipating further gains of $392.7 billion in its current fiscal year.\", \"- e236 [fact; FEV Group; original source FEV Group and Microsoft 2026-07-09; from gnews:c8324bfbfe7f0c60c826e72f 2026-07-09] FEV is collaborating with Microsoft to integrate in-vehicle generative AI built on NVIDIA GPU-accelerated compute and AI model microservices; no scale or completion date was given.\\n    Quote: FEV is collaborating with Microsoft to integrate powerful, in-vehicle Generative AI capabilities built on NVIDIA GPU-accelerated compute and AI model microservices.\", \"- e237 [third_party_view; TechCrunch author Russell Brandom; original source TechCrunch author Russell Brandom 2026-07-09; from gnews:3ea4e94c707ece2db2d7caec 2026-07-09] The article reports that memory makers have increased high-bandwidth memory chip prices tenfold over the past year as demand outpaced supply.\\n    Quote: For memory companies like Micron, the story is much simpler. They build high-bandwidth memory chips — specialized components designed to move data in and out of processors as fast as possible — which have been getting incrementally better for 20 years. Without the chips or the companies changing too much, the service they provide suddenly became very valuable — and since demand is growing faster t\", \"- e238 [third_party_view; TechCrunch author Russell Brandom; original source TechCrunch author Russell Brandom 2026-07-09; from gnews:3ea4e94c707ece2db2d7caec 2026-07-09] The article reports that the spot price for an hour of Nvidia H100 GPU compute peaked at around $3.20 in May 2026 and then declined steadily.\\n    Quote: Just like Nvidia’s stock price, there’s a peak in May (around $3.20 an hour) and then a steady drop-off.\", \"- e239 [third_party_view; Ornn co-founder and CTO Wayne Nelms, quoted by TechCrunch author Russell Brandom; original source Wayne Nelms ; from gnews:3ea4e94c707ece2db2d7caec 2026-07-09] Ornn co-founder and CTO Wayne Nelms said more GPU and accelerator players are entering the market and predicted that current market conditions would broadly persist absent an HBM breakthrough, a supply-demand shift, or a new memory-market entrant.\\n    Quote: “More GPU and accelerator players are entering the market.\", \"- e241 [third_party_view; barchart.com; original source Experts cited by barchart.com ; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Experts cited by barchart.com say DeepSeek's chip is unlikely to materially affect Nvidia's near-term revenue, partly because China contributes less to Nvidia sales, but custom silicon could gradually erode Nvidia's pricing power and margins.\\n    Quote: Although experts note that DeepSeek's move is unlikely to materially impact Nvidia's near-term revenue, particularly given China's shrinking contribution to Nvidia's sales, it reinforces concerns that custom silicon could gradually erode the company's pricing power and margins.\", \"- e244 [fact; barchart.com; original source Nvidia 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia reported fiscal 2027 first-quarter revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year, and net income of $58.32 billion, up 211% year over year, for the quarter ended April 26.\\n    Quote: For the quarter ended April 26, Nvidia posted record revenue of $81.6 billion, an 85% year-over-year (YOY) increase, while net income jumped 211% YOY to $58.32 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e254; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e245 [fact; barchart.com; original source Nvidia 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia Data Center revenue was $75.2 billion in fiscal 2027 first-quarter, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Moreover, the Data Center segment remained Nvidia's biggest growth driver, with revenue surging 92% YOY to a record $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e250; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e246 [fact; barchart.com; original source Nvidia 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia Data Center networking revenue was $14.8 billion in fiscal 2027 first-quarter, up 199% year over year; Data Center computing revenue was $60.4 billion.\\n    Quote: Data Center networking revenue soared 199% YOY to $14.8 billion, while computing revenue accounted for the remaining $60.4 billion.\", \"- e247 [fact; barchart.com; original source Nvidia 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia Edge Computing revenue was $6.4 billion in fiscal 2027 first-quarter, up 29% year over year.\\n    Quote: Its Edge Computing revenue increased 29% YOY to $6.4 billion, supported by demand across gaming GPUs, autonomous driving, robotics, and AI-enabled edge devices.\", \"- e248 [party_statement; barchart.com; original source Nvidia 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia forecast fiscal 2027 second-quarter revenue of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%, and non-GAAP gross margin of about 75%.\\n    Quote: Additionally, Nvidia issued another optimistic outlook for the second quarter of fiscal 2027, forecasting revenue of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%, and a non-GAAP gross margin of about 75%.\", \"- e249 [party_statement; barchart.com; original source Nvidia 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia's fiscal 2027 second-quarter guidance assumes zero China Data Center compute revenue because of U.S. export restrictions.\\n    Quote: The guidance assumes no contribution from China Data Center compute revenue due to ongoing U.S. export restrictions.\", \"- e250 [fact; fool.com (Adam Spatacco); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:931ee0196ca609e637235fad 2026-07-09] NVIDIA reported record data center segment revenue in Q1 FY2027.\\n    Quote: Revenues from Nvidia's data center segment -- the primary engine of the business -- set a record in the first quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e245; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e251 [party_statement; fool.com (Adam Spatacco); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:931ee0196ca609e637235fad 2026-07-09] NVIDIA management guided to accelerating data center segment revenue growth in Q2 FY2027.\\n    Quote: Moreover, management guided for further revenue growth acceleration for the second quarter.\", \"- e252 [party_statement; fool.com (Adam Spatacco); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:931ee0196ca609e637235fad 2026-07-09] NVIDIA management cited roughly $1 trillion of revenue visibility for Blackwell and Vera Rubin processors across 2026 and 2027, anchored by multiyear customer commitments.\\n    Quote: Management has also articulated roughly $1 trillion in revenue visibility for its Blackwell and Vera Rubin processors across 2026 and 2027, anchored by multiyear commitments from hyperscalers and large enterprise customers.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e27; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e253 [third_party_view; Rick Munarriz; original source Rick Munarriz 2026-07-09; from gnews:b412380d12c5a222545d42f1 2026-07-09] The author says Nvidia's revenue growth accelerated for three consecutive quarters.\\n    Quote: Nvidia's revenue has accelerated for three consecutive quarters.\", \"- e254 [fact; Rick Munarriz; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:b412380d12c5a222545d42f1 2026-07-09] Nvidia reported 85% year-over-year revenue growth in fiscal Q1, its strongest increase in a year and a half.\\n    Quote: The 85% top-line jump it posted in its fiscal first quarter is the strongest increase in a year and a half.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e244; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e259 [party_statement; qz.com; original source Andy Jassy, Amazon CEO ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Amazon CEO Andy Jassy said in late 2025 that Trainium2 had no spare capacity left to sell and was a multibillion-dollar business growing at a 150% quarterly clip.\\n    Quote: Amazon CEO Andy Jassy said in late 2025 that Trainium2, the previous generation, had no spare capacity left to sell. He said it had grown into a multibillion-dollar business at a 150% quarterly clip.\", \"- e260 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source qz.com 2026-07-09; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Amazon’s Trainium4 chip could arrive later in 2026.\\n    Quote: Amazon 's next chip, Trainium4, which packs three times the performance of its predecessor, could arrive later this year.\", \"- e261 [fact; qz.com; original source Microsoft ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Microsoft announced its Maia 200 inference chip in January 2026, and the chip is now reaching a handful of U.S. data centers.\\n    Quote: It announced Maia 200, a chip built for that work, in January 2026, and the chip is already reaching a handful of U.S. data centers.\", \"- e262 [party_statement; qz.com; original source Microsoft ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Microsoft’s Maia 200 chip is planned to power OpenAI’s newest models and Microsoft AI products including Copilot.\\n    Quote: The chip will power OpenAI's newest models, along with Microsoft 's own AI products, such as Copilot.\", \"- e263 [party_statement; qz.com; original source Meta ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Meta’s MTIA 300 is in production for ranking and recommendation, and Meta plans to build three further MTIA generations over the next two years for generative AI models.\\n    Quote: The newest version, MTIA 300, is already in production for ranking and recommendation work. Meta is set to build three more generations over the next two years with the purpose of running generative AI models.\", \"- e265 [party_statement; qz.com; original source OpenAI ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] OpenAI’s planned installation of its custom AI chips is set to begin in the second half of 2026 and continue through the end of 2029.\\n    Quote: Installing them is set to begin in the second half of 2026 and run through the end of 2029.\", \"- e266 [fact; qz.com; original source Tesla ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Tesla completed the AI5 inference-chip design in April 2026 and plans production at TSMC’s Arizona plant and Samsung’s Texas plant.\\n    Quote: Tesla finished the design of its AI5 inference chip in April 2026, according to Reuters . Production is planned at both TSMC 's plant in Arizona and Samsung's plant in Texas.\", \"- e268 [fact; gizmodo.com, as reported by Bruce Gil; original source Micron ; from gnews:fe9210b7b43c51e0939ecbbb 2026-07-09] Micron decided to wind down its Crucial consumer business brand to focus on data center demand; no date or amount was given.\\n    Quote: Micron even decided to wind down its consumer business brand , Crucial, to focus on data center demand.\", \"- e269 [rumour; moomoo.com; original source Meta Platforms 2026-07-09; from gnews:7b39859113d4e2b8ebd8aa86 2026-07-09] Meta reportedly plans to start manufacturing its AI chip in September 2026, according to a Reuters report citing an internal memo.\\n    Quote: Meta Platforms (META.US)$ is reportedly planning to start manufacturing its AI chip in September, Reuters reported Thursday, citing the company’s internal memo.\", \"- e270 [fact; moomoo.com; original source Quanta ; from gnews:7b39859113d4e2b8ebd8aa86 2026-07-09] Quanta's monthly sales rose to NT$385.19 billion in June 2026, more than doubling year over year; Quanta supplies AI servers powered by Nvidia GPUs.\\n    Quote: Quanta, which supplies AI servers powered by Nvidia’s GPUs, saw its monthly sales more than double to 385.19 billion New Taiwanese dollars in June from a year earlier, according to data compiled by Bloomberg.\", \"- e205 [third_party_view; Yahoo Finance; original source Analysts ; from gnews:b40db2c507df72ec016e99e6 2026-07-08] Analysts anticipate NVIDIA FY2027 revenue of $392.7 billion.\\n    Quote: And analysts are anticipating further gains of $392.7 billion in its current fiscal year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e276; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e244 [fact; barchart.com; original source Nvidia 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia reported fiscal 2027 first-quarter revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year, and net income of $58.32 billion, up 211% year over year, for the quarter ended April 26.\\n    Quote: For the quarter ended April 26, Nvidia posted record revenue of $81.6 billion, an 85% year-over-year (YOY) increase, while net income jumped 211% YOY to $58.32 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e254, e281; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e245 [fact; barchart.com; original source Nvidia 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia Data Center revenue was $75.2 billion in fiscal 2027 first-quarter, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Moreover, the Data Center segment remained Nvidia's biggest growth driver, with revenue surging 92% YOY to a record $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e250, e285, e305; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e246 [fact; barchart.com; original source Nvidia 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia Data Center networking revenue was $14.8 billion in fiscal 2027 first-quarter, up 199% year over year; Data Center computing revenue was $60.4 billion.\\n    Quote: Data Center networking revenue soared 199% YOY to $14.8 billion, while computing revenue accounted for the remaining $60.4 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e286; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e248 [party_statement; barchart.com; original source Nvidia 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia forecast fiscal 2027 second-quarter revenue of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%, and non-GAAP gross margin of about 75%.\\n    Quote: Additionally, Nvidia issued another optimistic outlook for the second quarter of fiscal 2027, forecasting revenue of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%, and a non-GAAP gross margin of about 75%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e282; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e249 [party_statement; barchart.com; original source Nvidia 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia's fiscal 2027 second-quarter guidance assumes zero China Data Center compute revenue because of U.S. export restrictions.\\n    Quote: The guidance assumes no contribution from China Data Center compute revenue due to ongoing U.S. export restrictions.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e287; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e254 [fact; Rick Munarriz; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:b412380d12c5a222545d42f1 2026-07-09] Nvidia reported 85% year-over-year revenue growth in fiscal Q1, its strongest increase in a year and a half.\\n    Quote: The 85% top-line jump it posted in its fiscal first quarter is the strongest increase in a year and a half.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e244, e290, e292; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e269 [rumour; moomoo.com; original source Meta Platforms 2026-07-09; from gnews:7b39859113d4e2b8ebd8aa86 2026-07-09] Meta reportedly plans to start manufacturing its AI chip in September 2026, according to a Reuters report citing an internal memo.\\n    Quote: Meta Platforms (META.US)$ is reportedly planning to start manufacturing its AI chip in September, Reuters reported Thursday, citing the company’s internal memo.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e284; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e276 [third_party_view; Jeran Wittenstein, reporting Bloomberg-compiled data; original source Bloomberg ; from gnews:49f225cd79fb22132f3b9ee4 2026-07-10] Bloomberg-compiled projections put NVIDIA FY2027 sales at $393 billion, up 82% year over year.\\n    Quote: The chipmaker is projected to deliver $228 billion in profits on sales of $393 billion in fiscal 2027, which ends Jan. 31. That would represent an expansion of 90% and 82%, respectively, according to data compiled by Bloomberg.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e205; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e279 [fact; AWS; original source AWS 2026-07-10; from gnews:23d831f15e3a80d6b3ba60e6 2026-07-10] AWS introduced serverless customization on SageMaker AI for NVIDIA’s Nemotron 3 Nano and Super models.\\n    Quote: Now, SageMaker AI introduces serverless model customization for NVIDIA Nemotron 3 models, starting with Nemotron 3 Nano (30B total parameters, 3B active) and Nemotron 3 Super (120B total parameters, 12B active).\", \"- e280 [third_party_view; Trefis; original source Trefis 2026-07-10; from gnews:6abaf2856736877236d30f6a 2026-07-10] Trefis reports Wall Street consensus expects NVIDIA revenue to grow about 32% annually over the next few years.\\n    Quote: Wall Street consensus sees NVIDIA’s revenue growing about 32% a year for the next few years.\", \"- e281 [third_party_view; Trefis; original source Trefis 2026-07-10; from gnews:6abaf2856736877236d30f6a 2026-07-10] Trefis says NVIDIA revenue grew 71% over the last twelve months and 85% in the most recent quarter.\\n    Quote: That figure seems high until you set it against what the company is actually delivering: revenue grew 71% over the last twelve months and 85% in the most recent quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e244; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e282 [party_statement; Trefis, relaying NVIDIA guidance; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:6abaf2856736877236d30f6a 2026-07-10] NVIDIA guided to upcoming-quarter revenue of $91 billion at the midpoint.\\n    Quote: For the upcoming quarter, the company guided revenue to a midpoint of $91.00 billion, signaling continued strong demand.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e248, e289, e293; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e283 [party_statement; Trefis, quoting NVIDIA management; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:6abaf2856736877236d30f6a 2026-07-10] NVIDIA management said its Vera CPU opens a new total addressable market of $200 billion.\\n    Quote: Management sees its new Vera CPU opening a “brand new $200 billion TAM for NVIDIA,” a market it has never addressed before.\", \"- e284 [fact; gurufocus.com (analyst); original source Meta Platforms ; from gnews:09b9d76297a57f198651c5e7 2026-07-10] Meta plans to begin manufacturing its Iris custom AI processor in September 2026, after initial testing.\\n    Quote: Reuters said Meta plans to begin manufacturing its custom AI processor, code-named Iris, in September after completing initial testing.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e269; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e285 [fact; 247wallst.com, summarizing NVIDIA’s results; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Data Center revenue of $75.246 billion, up 92% year over year, in Q1 FY2027.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue hit $75.246 billion, up 92% year over year\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e245, e299; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e286 [fact; 247wallst.com, summarizing NVIDIA’s results; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] NVIDIA networking revenue grew 199% year over year in Q1 FY2027.\\n    Quote: networking alone grew 199%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e246; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e287 [party_statement; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] NVIDIA’s Q2 FY2027 revenue guidance excluded Data Center compute revenue from China, and NVIDIA reported zero H20 shipments in Q1 FY2027.\\n    Quote: Q2 FY27 guidance explicitly excludes Data Center compute revenue from China, and there were zero H20 shipments in the quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e249; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e289 [party_statement; 247wallst.com, summarizing NVIDIA’s guidance; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] NVIDIA guided to Q2 FY2027 revenue of $91 billion.\\n    Quote: Q2 FY27 guidance points to $91 billion in revenue.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e282; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e290 [fact; Vandita Jadeja; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] The article cites NVIDIA revenue growth of 85.23% year over year and a non-GAAP gross margin of 75.0%.\\n    Quote: For a business growing revenue 85.23% year over year at 75.0% non-GAAP gross margins\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e254; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e292 [fact; 247Wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially; Data Center revenue was $75.2 billion.\\n    Quote: The company reported record revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially, with Data Center revenue reaching $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e254; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e293 [party_statement; 247Wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 non-GAAP gross margin of 75% and guided Q2 FY2027 revenue to $91 billion.\\n    Quote: Non-GAAP gross margin came in at 75%, and management guided Q2 FY2027 revenue to $91 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e282; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e296 [third_party_view; theverge.com; original source Counterpoint ; from gnews:3839887e5ca53a0cb0e7c91e 2026-07-10] Counterpoint reported that in June 2026 SK Hynix had 29% of the global DRAM market, versus Samsung at 38% and Micron at 22%.\\n    Quote: As of June 2026, SK Hynix makes up 29 percent of the global DRAM market, with Samsung at 38 percent and Micron at 22 percent, according to data from Counterpoint .\", \"- e298 [third_party_view; Thomas Richmond, quoting Kristina Partsinevelos; original source Kristina Partsinevelos 2026-07-10; from gnews:9ae96ca750b8e3962c47795f 2026-07-10] Kristina Partsinevelos said no additional HBM supply would arrive before late 2027, keeping the memory shortage and record-high prices in place until then.\\n    Quote: “None of that supply, though, arrives before late 2027, which keeps the memory shortage going and record-high prices intact for now,” Par