 original source Silicon Analysts ; from gnews:2beadbce40c7f927f33d9fc5 2026-07-12] Silicon Analysts estimated that Nvidia held 60%–75% of the AI-chip inference market in 2025, with custom silicon competition reducing its share.\\n    Quote: Its inference share sat between 60% and 75% over the same period, undercut by growing competition from custom silicon.\", \"- e316 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source TechCrunch ; from gnews:2beadbce40c7f927f33d9fc5 2026-07-12] TechCrunch reported that 1.4 million Amazon Trainium chips across three generations were deployed as of March 2026.\\n    Quote: As of March, 1.4 million Trainium chips were deployed across three generations, according to TechCrunch\", \"- e317 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source TechCrunch ; from gnews:2beadbce40c7f927f33d9fc5 2026-07-12] TechCrunch reported that Anthropic's Claude was running on more than one million Amazon Trainium2 chips as of March 2026.\\n    Quote: with Anthropic's Claude running on more than one million Trainium2 chips alone.\", \"- e318 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source Mizuho Securities and Silicon Analysts ; from gnews:2beadbce40c7f927f33d9fc5 2026-07-12] Mizuho Securities estimated Nvidia's overall AI-chip market share at 70%–95%, depending on segment; Silicon Analysts projected it would settle near 75% as the market grows beyond $200 billion.\\n    Quote: Nvidia 's overall AI chip market share, estimated by Mizuho Securities at between 70% and 95% depending on segment, is projected by Silicon Analysts to settle near 75% as the total market expands past $200 billion.\", \"- e319 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:07cf5835d106467db5448c13 2026-07-12] Nvidia revenue increased 85% in its past quarter.\\n    Quote: During its past quarter, Nvidia's revenue increased at an 85% clip.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e281; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e320 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:07cf5835d106467db5448c13 2026-07-12] Wall Street analysts expect Nvidia revenue to grow 96% in Q2.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts expect 96% growth during Q2.\", \"- e322 [third_party_view; Keithen Drury; original source Broadcom ; from gnews:f8f440b5020fec9773812b6e 2026-07-12] Broadcom plans to ramp production of custom AI chips for Meta Platforms, Anthropic, and OpenAI in late 2026 and into 2027.\\n    Quote: However, Broadcom is also making custom AI chips for Meta Platforms , Anthropic, and OpenAI, and production for those chips is scheduled to ramp up late this year and into next.\", \"- e330 [third_party_view; jpost.com; original source jpost.com 2026-07-12; from gnews:c14249088492921c802c839a 2026-07-12] The article reports that Nvidia’s server GPU market share was about 97% at the end of 2025, up from 95% at the end of 2024.\\n    Quote: Nvidia's firm grip on the server GPU market showed no signs of weakening, with its market share climbing to about 97% at the end of 2025, compared to 95% the previous year.\", \"- e333 [fact; barchart.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Nvidia reported fiscal Q1 2027 total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: For the first quarter of fiscal 2027, revenue jumped 85% year-over-year (YOY) to $81.6 billion, easily beating analyst expectations.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e292, e344; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e334 [fact; barchart.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Nvidia reported fiscal Q1 2027 Data Center revenue of $75.2 billion, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue climbed 92% YOY to $75.2 billion, highlighting that AI infrastructure remains the company's primary growth engine.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as