27, Nvidia generated record revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year-over-year (YOY).\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e333, e364, e372, e384; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e345 [party_statement; barchart.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] NVIDIA management guided FY2027 Q2 revenue to approximately $91 billion, assuming zero China data-center revenue because of export restrictions.\\n    Quote: Looking ahead, management guided Q2 revenue to approximately $91 billion, despite assuming zero China data-center revenue because of export restrictions.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e335, e388; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e349 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Nvidia automotive chief Xinzhou Wu estimated that autonomous driving accounts for about 0.006% of all miles driven, without specifying a measurement period.\\n    Quote: Right now the percentage of autonomous miles among all the mileage driven is probably negligible. I think it’s 0.006%, or something like that.\", \"- e350 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said Nvidia hopes to earn a share of ecosystem revenue for each autonomously driven mile, which he described as a potential trillion-dollar opportunity; he gave no timing.\\n    Quote: We hope that we can get a percentage of the revenue that the ecosystem can get from every mile that is driven autonomously in the future. This is where the trillion-dollar opportunity can come from.\", \"- e351 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said Tesla is ahead of other companies in L2++ advanced driver-assistance technology and that competitors are trying to catch up.\\n    Quote: For the basic L2++ technology, Elon is probably ahead of everybody. He had a division a long time ago and he has stuck to the vision for a long time to develop and test the technology among a massive fleet. Nobody would argue that Elon is ahead of everybody in the ADAS market and everybody is playing a catch-up game, essentially.\", \"- e352 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu forecast that Level 4 self-driving could become a mainstream experience in less than five years; he did not give a specific date.\\n    Quote: I would say if I need to give a time, I wouldn’t say five years, but less than five years.\", \"- e353 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said Nvidia chip prices would most likely need to rise because demand for chips is intense; he did not specify timing or the size of any increase.\\n    Quote: Actually, most likely even the chip price will need to go up, because of this intense demand for every chip everybody can grab onto.\", \"- e354 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said Nvidia offers two Hyperion 10 sensor configurations: a base version with 10 cameras and three radars and no lidar, and a high-end version with 14 cameras, three lidars, and seven radars for Level 4 driving.\\n    Quote: In Hyperion 10, for example, we really offer two versions. One is a base, which is mostly cameras: 10 cameras, three radars, no lidar. It’s a very cost-effective way to build a L2++ ADAS kind of vehicle. And on the other hand, for the high end, is what we call the Hyperion High: we provide the sensor set required, which has, I think, 14 cameras, three lidars, and seven radars to have enough sensor\", \"- e355 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said Nvidia planned to roll out its ADAS technology in all Mercedes vehicles and in vehicles from some other partners across the United States by the end of 2026.\\n    Quote: First of all, by the end of this year, we are rolling out our technology on the ADAS side in all Mercedes vehicles and some other partners as well, all over the United States.\", \"- e356 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said Nvidia and Uber were working toward rolling out an L4 service in the next few years; he did not give a specific date.\\n    Quote: Meanwhile, we are also working closely with our partners, for example, Uber. We announced that at GTC, we are trying to roll out our L4 service in the next few years.\", \"- e357 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said 80% of mass-production automakers were in Nvidia’s Hyperion ecosystem for Level 4 driving; he did not specify a measurement date.\\n    Quote: Right now, I would say 80% of the mass-production OEMs are in Nvidia’s Hyperion ecosystem for L4.\", \"- e358 [third_party_view; gurufocus.com (analyst); original source Citi ; from gnews:dedacecd6d2ed5192c307199 2026-07-13] Citi said Nvidia has strong access to high-bandwidth DRAM memory, a critical component for AI systems.\\n    Quote: The bank pointed to Nvidia's strong access to high-bandwidth DRAM memory, a critical component for AI systems.\", \"- e363 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:f4eb5206f2995f5dbb86c5e9 2026-07-13] Nvidia reported quarterly revenue of $81.6 billion for the quarter ended April 26, 2026, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: In its most recent quarter (ended April 26), it made $81.6 billion in revenue (up 85% year over year)\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e244; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e364 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original sou