fcd3515 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 Data Center revenue of $75.246 billion, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue hit $75.246 billion , up 92% YoY.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e285, e420; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e376 [fact; Vandita Jadeja; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:b68c019528300c6a1fcd3515 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 Data Center networking revenue of $14.8 billion, up 199% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data Center networking alone did $14.8 billion, up 199%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e246, e406, e421; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e377 [fact; Vandita Jadeja; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:b68c019528300c6a1fcd3515 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.615 billion, up 85.2% year over year.\\n    Quote: Total revenue was $81.615 billion, growing 85.2%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e372, e405; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e393 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source CoreWeave ; from nvblog:performance-per-watt-ai-infrastructure-efficiency 2026-07-14] CoreWeave deployed Kimi K2.6 on NVIDIA GB300 NVL72, using NVFP4 quantization and EAGLE3 speculative decoding.\\n    Quote: CoreWeave has deployed Kimi K2.6 on NVIDIA GB300 NVL72, combining NVFP4 quantization and EAGLE3 speculative decoding to maximize inference performance.\", \"- e394 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source Perplexity ; from nvblog:performance-per-watt-ai-infrastructure-efficiency 2026-07-14] Perplexity runs Qwen3 235B and post-trained Qwen3.5-397B-A17B on NVIDIA GB200 NVL72 for its AI agent platform, serving millions of queries daily.\\n    Quote: Perplexity runs Qwen3 235B and post-trained Qwen3.5-397B-A17B on NVIDIA GB200 NVL72 for its AI agent platform, serving millions of queries daily with the latency and reliability that consumers need.\", \"- e395 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source Fireworks AI ; from nvblog:performance-per-watt-ai-infrastructure-efficiency 2026-07-14] Fireworks AI deploys GLM 5.2 on the NVIDIA Blackwell platform for production deployments, including for Cursor and Factory AI.\\n    Quote: Fireworks AI deploys GLM 5.2 on the NVIDIA Blackwell platform, enabling production deployments for customers including Cursor and Factory AI.\", \"- e399 [fact; news.xbox.com; original source NVIDIA, Xbox and The Coalition 2026-07-14; from gnews:49d69b4a25983f1ee26710fc 2026-07-14] NVIDIA announced it is the exclusive PC partner for Gears of War: E-Day, collaborating with Xbox and The Coalition on GeForce RTX integration, performance optimization, and launch support.\\n    Quote: As the exclusive PC partner of Gears of War: E-Day , NVIDIA is collaborating closely with XBOX and The Coalition to enhance the game’s PC experience through deep integration with GeForce RTX technologies, performance optimization, and launch support. From the earliest stages of development through release, this partnership is focused on delivering a first-class PC experience, while the game contin\", \"- e402 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reported data-center networking revenue of $14.8 billion in the fiscal 2027 period referenced in the article, triple the year-earlier amount.\\n    Quote: with networking revenue tripling year-over-year to $14.8 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e246; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e405 [fact; Vandita Jadeja; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:1e1fa5a194198eaf05d90c9e 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.615 billion, up 85.23% year over year.\\n    Quote: It delivered $81.615 billion in Q1 FY27 revenue, up 85.23% year over year\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e377, e419; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e406 [fact; Vandita Jadeja; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:1e1fa5a194198eaf05d90c9e 2026-07-14] NVIDIA Data Center Networking revenue grew 199% year over year to $14.8 billion in Q1 FY2027.\\n    Quote: with Data Center Networking alone growing 199% YoY to $14.8 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e376; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e408 [third_party_view; Vandita Jadeja; original source Vandita Jadeja 2026-07-14; from gnews:1e1fa5a194198eaf05d90c9e 2026-07-14] The author calculates NVIDIA's forward P/E at 25x using a $203.53 share price and $8 forward EPS, and cites revenue growth above 85% year over year and a 75% gross margin.\\n    Quote: At $203.53 against forward EPS of $8, Nvidia’s forward P/E 25x is not expensive for a company compounding revenue north of 85% YoY with 75% gross margins.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e290; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e409 [party_statement; Vandita Jadeja; original source NVIDIA for Q2 revenue guidance; Vandita Jadeja for the quarterly earnings-growth figure ; from gnews:1e1fa5a194198eaf05d90c9e 2026-07-14] The author cited quarterly earnings growth of 214.5% year over year and NVIDIA's Q2 FY2027 revenue guidance of $91 billion.\\n    Quote: With quarterly earnings growth of 214.5% YoY and Q2 FY27 revenue guided to $91 billion, the 12-month models remain anchored to yesterday’s earnings power.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e366, e418; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e410 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Unnamed third-party estimates ; from gnews:37d2648cf990f4943cad6208 2026-07-14] Third-party estimates put Nvidia’s share of the AI chip market at 80%.\\n    Quote: Nvidia still controls an impressive 80% of the AI chip market, according to third-party estimates.\", \"- e411 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Harsh Chauhan 2026-07-14; from gnews:37d2648cf990f4943cad6208 2026-07-14] The author attributes Nvidia’s 8% share-price rise in 2026, despite continued growth, to the shift from AI training to inference and emerging chip competition.\\n    Quote: The shift from AI training to inference and the emergence of competing chip technologies explain why Nvidia stock has risen just 8% this year despite sustaining impressive growth levels.\", \"- e412 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Harsh Chauhan 2026-07-14; from gnews:37d2648cf990f4943cad6208 2026-07-14] The author says demand for custom AI processors has increased as AI data-center computing shifts toward inference.\\n    Quote: This has led to increased demand for custom AI processors that are designed to perform specific tasks.\", \"- e413 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Harsh Chauhan 2026-07-14; from gnews:37d2648cf990f4943cad6208 2026-07-14] Marvell controls 20% to 25% of the custom AI processor market, according to the article.\\n    Quote: Marvell is one of the key players in custom AI processors, controlling 20% to 25% of this market.\", \"- e414 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Marvell Technology ; from gnews:37d2648cf990f4943cad6208 2026-07-14] Marvell says it has more than 50 potential custom AI chip opportunities across over 10 customers, with potential lifetime revenue of $75 billion.\\n    Quote: In all, Marvell notes that it can tap into more than 50 custom AI chip opportunities across over 10 customers in the long run, leading to potential lifetime revenue of $75 billion.\", \"- e415 [rumour; Tom's Hardware, relaying a Financial Times report; original source Nvidia, according to sources cited by the Financial Times ; from gnews:2a41a34c16f5280b624481fb 2026-07-14] Nvidia reportedly cut its authorized-client roster in Asia by more than half and tightened verification, including data-center inspections, contract checks, and end-user interviews, to reduce the risk of chips being diverted into China.\\n    Quote: According to the Financial Times , this roster cuts the number of authorized clients by more than half, with those remaining having passed tougher compliance inspections to ensure that they are genuine businesses, not shell companies designed to forward Nvidia GPUs and servers into China. Some of the steps that Nvidia took to help safeguard its chips reportedly included sending staff to customer d\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e444, e447; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e416 [fact; 247wallst.com, citing NVIDIA; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ac8a489e54fbb1b85a1c7a2c 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85.2% year over year.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA’s Q1 FY27 revenue hit $81.6 billion, up 85.2% YoY\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e344; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e417 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ac8a489e54fbb1b85a1c7a2c 2026-07-14] NVIDIA Data Center Networking revenue grew 199% year over year in Q1 FY2027, attributed to InfiniBand, NVLink, and Spectrum-X pull-through.\\n    Quote: Data Center Networking alone growing 199% on InfiniBand, NVLink, and Spectrum-X pull-through.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e286; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e418 [party_statement; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ac8a489e54fbb1b85a1c7a2c 2026-07-14] NVIDIA guided to Q2 revenue of $91 billion.\\n    Quote: unusual for a company guiding to $91 billion in Q2 revenue.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e409; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e419 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:184645c8d683d95b684bd6da 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.615 billion, up 85.23% year over year.\\n    Quote: Revenue hit $81.615 billion, up 85.23% YoY\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e405; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e420 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:184645c8d683d95b684bd6da 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 Data Center revenue of $75.246 billion, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data Center alone contributing $75.246 billion (+92% YoY).\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e375; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e421 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:184645c8d683d95b684bd6da 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 networking revenue of $14.8 billion, up 199% year over year.\\n    Quote: Networking was the sleeper hit at $14.8 billion (+199% YoY), driven by InfiniBand, Spectrum-X, and NVLink.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e376; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e423 [party_statement; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:184645c8d683d95b684bd6da 2026-07-14] NVIDIA guided Q2 revenue to $91 billion, assuming zero China Data Center compute revenue.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA guided Q2 to $91 billion in revenue, which assumes zero China Data Center compute.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e368; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e424 [fact; Vandita Jadeja; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:386a294bd395bde25e3f4a11 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.61 billion, up 85.2% year over year, and Data Center revenue of $75.25 billion, up 92%.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA’s Q1 FY27 revenue hit $81.61B, up 85.2% YoY, with Data Center at $75.25B (+92%).\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e285; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e425 [third_party_view; sg.finance.yahoo.com; original source Zacks ; from gnews:f10cd8ddb00105698ac294cf 2026-07-14] Zacks reported that consensus analyst estimates for Nvidia increased 13.7% over the three months before 2026-07-14; the estimate measure and fiscal period are not specified.\\n    Quote: Analysts have been steadily raising their estimates for Nvidia. Over the past three months, the Zacks Consensus Estimate for the company has increased 13.7%.\", \"- e426 [third_party_view; sg.finance.yahoo.com; original source Zacks ; from gnews:f10cd8ddb00105698ac294cf 2026-07-14] Zacks reported expected Nvidia earnings of $9.10 per share for the fiscal year ending January 2027, unchanged from the year-ago reported figure.\\n    Quote: For the fiscal year ending January 2027, this maker of graphics chips for gaming and artificial intelligence is expected to earn $9.10 per share, which is unchanged compared with the year-ago reported number.\", \"- e427 [fact; Reuters; original source U.S. authorities, as reported from documents and sources familiar with the matter 2026-07-14; from gnews:24268bfaab6ef1d7876b188c 2026-07-14] U.S. authorities permitted ZTE Kangxun Telecom and server maker Maginfra to purchase Nvidia H200 chips; a Kingsoft subsidiary was cleared to use some AMD chips.\\n    Quote: ZTE Kangxun Telecom and server maker Maginfra have been permitted to purchase Nvidia's H200 chips, while Zhuhai Hengqin Yunxiang Zhisheng Network Technology, a subsidiary of cloud computing company Kingsoft, has ‌been cleared to use some ⁠AMD chips that rival the H200, according to the documents and the sources.\", \"- e428 [rumour; Reuters; original source Unnamed sources familiar with the matter 2026-07-14; from gnews:24268bfaab6ef1d7876b188c 2026-07-14] Unnamed sources said some Chinese cloud firms recently told partners and clients they may soon be able to obtain Nvidia H200 chips, indicating progress in Chinese authorities' import reviews.\\n    Quote: However, some Chinese cloud firms have recently told partners and clients they may soon be able to obtain H200 chips, the sources said, indicating some progress in import reviews by Chinese authorities.\", \"- e429 [fact; Rest of World; original source Saudi Arabia 2026-06-01; from gnews:01a49ffd41f6abe24538da65 2026-07-14] Saudi Arabia agreed on June 1, 2026, to use self-driving taxis that run on Nvidia technology.\\n    Quote: Saudi Arabia agreed on June 1 to use self-driving taxis that run on Nvidia technology — from the computer inside each car to the software that steers it.\", \"- e430 [fact; Rest of World; original source Humain ; from gnews:01a49ffd41f6abe24538da65 2026-07-14] Humain is building data centers in Riyadh and Dammam, planned to be powered by several hundred thousand Nvidia chips.\\n    Quote: Humain is also building data centers in Riyadh and Dammam, powered by several hundred thousand Nvidia chips.\", \"- e431 [fact; Rest of World; original source G42 ; from gnews:01a49ffd41f6abe24538da65 2026-07-14] G42’s first stage of its Stargate data center in Abu Dhabi is planned to run on 400,000 Nvidia chips.\\n    Quote: Its first stage will run on 400,000 Nvidia chips .\", \"- e432 [party_statement; Rest of World; original source Peng Xiao, G42 CEO ; from gnews:01a49ffd41f6abe24538da65 2026-07-14] G42 CEO Peng Xiao said Stargate’s machines would be mostly Nvidia despite G42’s efforts to spread orders among suppliers.\\n    Quote: G42 has spent months trying to spread its orders among several suppliers, yet the machines inside Stargate would be “mostly” Nvidia, CEO Peng Xiao said in an interview in January.\", \"- e434 [third_party_view; Tom's Hardware; original source Reuters ; from gnews:3221eba2826b001b12b82770 2026-07-14] Reuters said Chinese technology firms had more than 2 million Nvidia H200 chips on order about six months before 2026-07-14, exceeding Nvidia's available inventory at the time.\\n    Quote: But even with those domestic production initiatives, the Chinese hunger for AI silicon is so deep that six months ago, Reuters said the nation's tech firms had more than two million H200 chips on order, far more than what Nvidia had on hand at the time.\", \"- e438 [fact; mlq.ai; original source FBI ; from gnews:ca7564a0dc63b215f5d49402 2026-07-14] The FBI published an RFI seeking market input on AI supercomputer hardware for its CJIS Division, including Nvidia Blackwell Ultra GPUs and Google TPUs; the RFI does not commit the FBI to a procurement.\\n    Quote: The FBI has published a Request for Information on SAM.gov seeking market input on AI supercomputer hardware for its Criminal Justice Information Services (CJIS) Division in Clarksburg, West Virginia. The RFI outlines four distinct categories of accelerator systems spanning training, inference, and analytics workloads — including both Nvidia Blackwell Ultra GPUs and Google TPUs [1].\", \"- e439 [third_party_view; mlq.ai; original source mlq.ai 2026-07-14; from gnews:ca7564a0dc63b215f5d49402 2026-07-14] Federal AI spending obligations reached $7.2 billion in 2026, up from $675 million in 2024, while potential contract awards reached $91.8 billion, up from $4.6 billion in 2024.\\n    Quote: Federal AI spending obligations reached $7.2 billion in 2026, up from $675 million in 2024 — a 966% increase. Potential contract awards ballooned to $91.8 billion, up 1,912% from 2024's $4.6 billion [2].\", \"- e440 [party_statement; Jakarta Globe; original source Airlangga Hartarto ; from gnews:e001119c6342373f6b1f3cf4 2026-07-14] Indonesia’s Chief Economic Affairs Minister Airlangga Hartarto said investors are planning data center projects with a combined capacity of about 1.3 GW, in addition to roughly 580 MW already operating; no project period was specified.\\n    Quote: Chief Economic Affairs Minister Airlangga Hartarto said investors are planning data center projects with a combined capacity of about 1.3 gigawatts (GW), on top of the roughly 580 megawatts (MW) currently in operation.\", \"- e444 [rumour; Reuters; original source Unnamed sources cited by the Financial Times 2026-07-14; from gnews:dc642adc9738cb72e71bf4cd 2026-07-14] The Financial Times reported on July 14 that NVIDIA had more than halved its authorised Asian AI-chip customer list after creating a new whitelist to prevent chips reaching China.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA has more than halved the number of Asian customers authorised to buy its AI chips after creating a new “white list” of companies that have passed tougher compliance checks aimed at preventing the products from reaching China, the Financial Times reported on Monday (Jul 14).\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e415; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e445 [rumour; Reuters; original source Three unnamed people familiar with the matter, cited by the Financial Times 2026-07-14; from gnews:dc642adc9738cb72e71bf4cd 2026-07-14] Three people familiar with the matter told the Financial Times that NVIDIA intensified customer due diligence in Singapore, Malaysia and Japan over the past few months.\\n    Quote: Over the past few months, the chipmaker has intensified due diligence in Singapore, Malaysia and Japan, the report added, citing three people familiar with the matter.\", \"- e446 [fact; Reuters; original source US Commerce Department ; from gnews:dc642adc9738cb72e71bf4cd 2026-07-14] The US Commerce Department issued guidance in May to curb advanced AI-chip transfers to overseas subsidiaries of Chinese companies, citing concern that Blackwell processors may have reached Chinese-linked entities in countries including Malaysia despite US restrictions.\\n    Quote: The US Commerce Department issued guidance in May aimed at curbing advanced AI chips from reaching overseas subsidiaries of Chinese companies, highlighting concerns that Nvidia’s cutting-edge Blackwell processors may have been exported to Chinese-linked entities in countries such as Malaysia despite US restrictions.\", \"- e447 [rumour; Reuters; original source Unnamed sources cited by the Financial Times 2026-07-14; from gnews:dc642adc9738cb72e71bf4cd 2026-07-14] The Financial Times reported that NVIDIA tightened compliance procedures after pressure from Washington, with staff now visiting customers’ data centres, verifying contracts and interviewing end users.\\n    Quote: Nvidia has tightened compliance procedures following pressure from Washington, the FT said, adding that staff now visit customers’ data centres, verify contracts and interview end users as part of the checks.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e415; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e448 [rumour; Reuters; original source Unnamed sources cited by the Financial Times 2026-07-14; from gnews:dc642adc9738cb72e71bf4cd 2026-07-14] The Financial Times reported that the US Department of Commerce is providing oversight and political backing for the compliance checks.\\n    Quote: The US Department of Commerce is also involved, providing oversight and political backing, the report said.\"]\nITEM [{\"id\": \"i037\", \"day\": \"2026-07-02\", \"title\": \"Microsoft vs. Nvidia: Which Is the Better AI Stock to Own for the Next 3 Years?\", \"passage\": \"from trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion to $392 billion this fiscal year, and $554 billion the following year\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"Wall Street analysts\", \"what\": \"NVIDIA total revenue estimates\", \"how_much\": \"$392 billion this fiscal year, $554 billion next year (from $253 billion trailing twelve months)\", \"period\": \"this fiscal year (FY2027) and the following year (FY2028)\", \"status\": \"forecast\"}}]\nEVIDENCE [\"- e204 [fact; Yahoo Finance; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:b40db2c507df72ec016e99e6 2026-07-08] NVIDIA reported FY2026 revenue above $215.9 billion, up 65% year over year.\\n    Quote: The company's most recent fiscal 2026 revenue topped $215.9 billion, up 65% year over year and well ahead of the $11.7 billion it posted in 2019.\", \"- e205 [third_party_view; Yahoo Finance; original source Analysts ; from gnews:b40db2c507df72ec016e99e6 2026-07-08] Analysts anticipate NVIDIA FY2027 revenue of $392.7 billion.\\n    Quote: And analysts are anticipating further gains of $392.7 billion in its current fiscal year.\", \"- e236 [fact; FEV Group; original source FEV Group and Microsoft 2026-07-09; from gnews:c8324bfbfe7f0c60c826e72f 2026-07-09] FEV is collaborating with Microsoft to integrate in-vehicle generative AI built on NVIDIA GPU-accelerated compute and AI model microservices; no scale or completion date was given.\\n    Quote: FEV is collaborating with Microsoft to integrate powerful, in-vehicle Generative AI capabilities built on NVIDIA GPU-accelerated compute and AI model microservices.\", \"- e237 [third_party_view; TechCrunch author Russell Brandom; original source TechCrunch author Russell Brandom 2026-07-09; from gnews:3ea4e94c707ece2db2d7caec 2026-07-09] The article reports that memory makers have increased high-bandwidth memory chip prices tenfold over the past year as demand outpaced supply.\\n    Quote: For memory companies like Micron, the story is much simpler. They build high-bandwidth memory chips — specialized components designed to move data in and out of processors as fast as possible — which have been getting incrementally better for 20 years. Without the chips or the companies changing too much, the service they provide suddenly became very valuable — and since demand is growing faster t\", \"- e238 [third_party_view; TechCrunch author Russell Brandom; original source TechCrunch author Russell Brandom 2026-07-09; from gnews:3ea4e94c707ece2db2d7caec 2026-07-09] The article reports that the spot price for an hour of Nvidia H100 GPU compute peaked at around $3.20 in May 2026 and then declined steadily.\\n    Quote: Just like Nvidia’s stock price, there’s a peak in May (around $3.20 an hour) and then a steady drop-off.\", \"- e239 [third_party_view; Ornn co-founder and CTO Wayne Nelms, quoted by TechCrunch author Russell Brandom; original source Wayne Nelms ; from gnews:3ea4e94c707ece2db2d7caec 2026-07-09] Ornn co-founder and CTO Wayne Nelms said more GPU and accelerator players are entering the market and predicted that current market conditions would broadly persist absent an HBM breakthrough, a supply-demand shift, or a new memory-market entrant.\\n    Quote: “More GPU and accelerator players are entering the market.\", \"- e241 [third_party_view; barchart.com; original source Experts cited by barchart.com ; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Experts cited by barchart.com say DeepSeek's chip is unlikely to materially affect Nvidia's near-term revenue, partly because China contributes less to Nvidia sales, but custom silicon could gradually erode Nvidia's pricing power and margins.\\n    Quote: Although experts note that DeepSeek's move is unlikely to materially impact Nvidia's near-term revenue, particularly given China's shrinking contribution to Nvidia's sales, it reinforces concerns that custom silicon could gradually erode the company's pricing power and margins.\", \"- e244 [fact; barchart.com; original source Nvidia 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia reported fiscal 2027 first-quarter revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year, and net income of $58.32 billion, up 211% year over year, for the quarter ended April 26.\\n    Quote: For the quarter ended April 26, Nvidia posted record revenue of $81.6 billion, an 85% year-over-year (YOY) increase, while net income jumped 211% YOY to $58.32 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e254; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e245 [fact; barchart.com; original source Nvidia 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia Data Center revenue was $75.2 billion in fiscal 2027 first-quarter, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Moreover, the Data Center segment remained Nvidia's biggest growth driver, with revenue surging 92% YOY to a record $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e250; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e246 [fact; barchart.com; original source Nvidia 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia Data Center networking revenue was $14.8 billion in fiscal 2027 first-quarter, up 199% year over year; Data Center computing revenue was $60.4 billion.\\n    Quote: Data Center networking revenue soared 199% YOY to $14.8 billion, while computing revenue accounted for the remaining $60.4 billion.\", \"- e247 [fact; barchart.com; original source Nvidia 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia Edge Computing revenue was $6.4 billion in fiscal 2027 first-quarter, up 29% year over year.\\n    Quote: Its Edge Computing revenue increased 29% YOY to $6.4 billion, supported by demand across gaming GPUs, autonomous driving, robotics, and AI-enabled edge devices.\", \"- e248 [party_statement; barchart.com; original source Nvidia 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia forecast fiscal 2027 second-quarter revenue of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%, and non-GAAP gross margin of about 75%.\\n    Quote: Additionally, Nvidia issued another optimistic outlook for the second quarter of fiscal 2027, forecasting revenue of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%, and a non-GAAP gross margin of about 75%.\", \"- e249 [party_statement; barchart.com; original source Nvidia 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia's fiscal 2027 second-quarter guidance assumes zero China Data Center compute revenue because of U.S. export restrictions.\\n    Quote: The guidance assumes no contribution from China Data Center compute revenue due to ongoing U.S. export restrictions.\", \"- e2