idia reported total revenue of $82 billion, up 85% year over year, in the quarter; this was its third consecutive quarter of accelerating growth.\\n    Quote: The company posted $82 billion in total revenue, up 85% year-over-year, marking its third straight quarter of accelerating growth.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e299; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e305 [fact; TIKR.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] Nvidia reported data center revenue of $75 billion, up 92% year over year, in the quarter; the exact period was not specified.\\n    Quote: Data center revenue alone hit $75 billion, up 92% year over year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e245; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e306 [party_statement; TIKR.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] Nvidia expects its Vera CPU line to generate $20 billion in sales by the end of the fiscal year; the article date places that year in FY2027.\\n    Quote: Nvidia also highlighted a new growth driver: its Vera CPU line, which the company expects to generate $20 billion in sales by the end of this fiscal year, a notable push into a market historically dominated by Intel and AMD.\", \"- e307 [fact; TIKR.com; original source Nvidia and Valar Atomics ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] Nvidia and Valar Atomics have a deal to build a nuclear-powered data center in Utah to support AI computing and reduce water use; no capacity or completion date was specified.\\n    Quote: Beyond the CPU expansion, Nvidia has been striking new partnerships, including a deal with Valar Atomics to build a nuclear-powered data center in Utah aimed at reducing water use for AI computing.\", \"- e308 [fact; TIKR.com; original source Perplexity ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] Perplexity chose to use Nvidia’s new CPUs for AI agent tasks; no deployment date or scale was specified.\\n    Quote: AI startup Perplexity has also chosen to use Nvidia’s new CPUs for AI agent tasks.\", \"- e309 [third_party_view; TIKR.com; original source Mark Zuckerberg ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] Meta CEO Mark Zuckerberg commented that progress in AI agents was slower than expected; the article gives no specific measure or period.\\n    Quote: Comments from Meta’s Mark Zuckerberg about slower-than-expected progress in AI agents have also added caution to the broader AI narrative.\", \"- e310 [third_party_view; TIKR.com; original source Bank of America ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] Bank of America views the recent semiconductor-sector pullback as a temporary adjustment rather than evidence that AI demand is fading.\\n    Quote: Still, firms like Bank of America view the recent semiconductor sector pullback as a temporary adjustment rather than a sign that AI demand is fading, keeping names like Nvidia stock in focus for investors watching this space closely.\", \"- e311 [third_party_view; es.tradingview.com; original source Morgan Stanley ; from gnews:1bfc0e875ab1f26dcf48fb06 2026-07-11] Morgan Stanley estimated that AI laboratories account for roughly 20% of Nvidia’s demand; no period was specified.\\n    Quote: The bank noted that AI laboratories now account for roughly 20% of Nvidia’s demand, highlighting how enterprise AI adoption is expanding beyond hyperscale cloud providers.\", \"- e281 [third_party_view; Trefis; original source Trefis 2026-07-10; from gnews:6abaf2856736877236d30f6a 2026-07-10] Trefis says NVIDIA revenue grew 71% over the last twelve months and 85% in the most recent quarter.\\n    Quote: That figure seems high until you set it against what the company is actually delivering: revenue grew 71% over the last twelve months and 85% in the most recent quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e244, e319; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e285 [fact; 247wallst.com, summarizing NVIDIA’s results; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Data Center revenue of $75.246 billion, up 92% year over year, in Q1 FY2027.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue hit $75.246 billion, up 92% year over year\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e245, e299, e334; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e292 [fact; 247Wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially; Data Center revenue was $75.2 billion.\\n    Quote: The company reported record revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially, with Data Center revenue reaching $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e254, e333; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e293 [party_statement; 247Wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 non-GAAP gross margin of 75% and guided Q2 FY2027 revenue to $91 billion.\\n    Quote: Non-GAAP gross margin came in at 75%, and management guided Q2 FY2027 revenue to $91 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e282, e335; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e314 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source Silicon Analysts ; from gnews:2beadbce40c7f927f33d9fc5 2026-07-12] Silicon Analysts estimated that Nvidia held more than 90% of the AI-chip training market in 2025.\\n    Quote: Nvidia 's share exceeded 90% in training in 2025.\", \"- e315 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source Silicon Analysts ; from gnews:2beadbce40c7f927f33d9fc5 2026-07-12] Silicon Analysts estimated that Nvidia held 60%–75% of the AI-chip inference market in 2025, with custom silicon competition reducing its share.\\n    Quote: Its inference share sat between 60% and 75% over the same period, undercut by growing competition from custom silicon.\", \"- e316 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source TechCrunch ; from gnews:2beadbce40c7f927f33d9fc5 2026-07-12] TechCrunch reported that 1.4 million Amazon Trainium chips across three generations were deployed as of March 2026.\\n    Quote: As of March, 1.4 million Trainium chips were deployed across three generations, according to TechCrunch\", \"- e317 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source TechCrunch ; from gnews:2beadbce40c7f927f33d9fc5 2026-07-12] TechCrunch reported that Anthropic's Claude was running on more than one million Amazon Trainium2 chips as of March 2026.\\n    Quote: with Anthropic's Claude running on more than one million Trainium2 chips alone.\", \"- e318 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source Mizuho Securities and Silicon Analysts ; from gnews:2beadbce40c7f927f33d9fc5 2026-07-12] Mizuho Securities estimated Nvidia's overall AI-chip market share at 70%–95%, depending on segment; Silicon Analysts projected it would settle near 75% as the market grows beyond $200 billion.\\n    Quote: Nvidia 's overall AI chip market share, estimated by Mizuho Securities at between 70% and 95% depending on segment, is projected by Silicon Analysts to settle near 75% as the total market expands past $200 billion.\", \"- e319 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:07cf5835d106467db5448c13 2026-07-12] Nvidia revenue increased 85% in its past quarter.\\n    Quote: During its past quarter, Nvidia's revenue increased at an 85% clip.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e281; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e320 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:07cf5835d106467db5448c13 2026-07-12] Wall Street analysts expect Nvidia revenue to grow 96% in Q2.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts expect 96% growth during Q2.\", \"- e322 [third_party_view; Keithen Drury; original source Broadcom ; from gnews:f8f440b5020fec9773812b6e 2026-07-12] Broadcom plans to ramp production of custom AI chips for Meta Platforms, Anthropic, and OpenAI in late 2026 and into 2027.\\n    Quote: However, Broadcom is also making custom AI chips for Meta Platforms , Anthropic, and OpenAI, and production for those chips is scheduled to ramp up late this year and into next.\", \"- e330 [third_party_view; jpost.com; original source jpost.com 2026-07-12; from gnews:c14249088492921c802c839a 2026-07-12] The article reports that Nvidia’s server GPU market share was about 97% at the end of 2025, up from 95% at the end of 2024.\\n    Quote: Nvidia's firm grip on the server GPU market showed no signs of weakening, with its market share climbing to about 97% at the end of 2025, compared to 95% the previous year.\", \"- e333 [fact; barchart.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Nvidia reported fiscal Q1 2027 total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: For the first quarter of fiscal 2027, revenue jumped 85% year-over-year (YOY) to $81.6 billion, easily beating analyst expectations.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e292, e344; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e334 [fact; barchart.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Nvidia reported fiscal Q1 2027 Data Center revenue of $75.2 billion, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue climbed 92% YOY to $75.2 billion, highlighting that AI infrastructure remains the company's primary growth engine.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e285; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e335 [party_statement; barchart.com (analyst); original source Nvidia management ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8