tly, signing a multi-year technology partnership. It involves SK Hynix supplying memory across a broad range of areas, from AI infrastructure to personal AI and robotics .\", \"- e340 [party_statement; Jensen Huang, quoted by fool.com (analyst); original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:03c38d2fe2e6e02ba5736307 2026-07-12] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said SK Hynix had been NVIDIA's largest memory partner and would continue to be its largest memory partner.\\n    Quote: \\\"SK Hynix has been Nvidia's largest memory partner and will continue to be our largest memory partner,\\\" Nvidia chief Jensen Huang said at the time.\", \"- e344 [fact; barchart.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] NVIDIA reported record FY2027 first-quarter revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: During the fiscal first quarter of 2027, Nvidia generated record revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year-over-year (YOY).\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e333; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e345 [party_statement; barchart.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] NVIDIA management guided FY2027 Q2 revenue to approximately $91 billion, assuming zero China data-center revenue because of export restrictions.\\n    Quote: Looking ahead, management guided Q2 revenue to approximately $91 billion, despite assuming zero China data-center revenue because of export restrictions.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e335; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e347 [fact; barchart.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] NVIDIA expanded partnerships with Alphabet and Marvell.\\n    Quote: expanded partnerships with companies such as Alphabet (GOOGL) and Marvell (MRVL)\", \"- e244 [fact; barchart.com; original source Nvidia 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia reported fiscal 2027 first-quarter revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year, and net income of $58.32 billion, up 211% year over year, for the quarter ended April 26.\\n    Quote: For the quarter ended April 26, Nvidia posted record revenue of $81.6 billion, an 85% year-over-year (YOY) increase, while net income jumped 211% YOY to $58.32 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e254, e281, e363; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e246 [fact; barchart.com; original source Nvidia 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia Data Center networking revenue was $14.8 billion in fiscal 2027 first-quarter, up 199% year over year; Data Center computing revenue was $60.4 billion.\\n    Quote: Data Center networking revenue soared 199% YOY to $14.8 billion, while computing revenue accounted for the remaining $60.4 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e286, e376; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e285 [fact; 247wallst.com, summarizing NVIDIA’s results; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Data Center revenue of $75.246 billion, up 92% year over year, in Q1 FY2027.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue hit $75.246 billion, up 92% year over year\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e245, e299, e334, e373, e375; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e287 [party_statement; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] NVIDIA’s Q2 FY2027 revenue guidance excluded Data Center compute revenue from China, and NVIDIA reported zero H20 shipments in Q1 FY2027.\\n    Quote: Q2 FY27 guidance explicitly excludes Data Center compute revenue from China, and there were zero H20 shipments in the quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e249, e368, e380; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e292 [fact; 247Wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially; Data Center revenue was $75.2 billion.\\n    Quote: The company reported record revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially, with Data Center revenue reaching $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e254, e333, e367; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e293 [party_statement; 247Wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 non-GAAP gross margin of 75% and guided Q2 FY2027 revenue to $91 billion.\\n    Quote: Non-GAAP gross margin came in at 75%, and management guided Q2 FY2027 revenue to $91 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e282, e335, e366, e381; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e305 [fact; TIKR.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] Nvidia reported data center revenue of $75 billion, up 92% year over year, in the quarter; the exact period was not specified.\\n    Quote: Data center revenue alone hit $75 billion, up 92% year over year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e245, e365; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e344 [fact; barchart.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] NVIDIA reported record FY2027 first-quarter revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: During the fiscal first quarter of 2027, Nvidia generated record revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year-over-year (YOY).\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e333, e364, e372, e384; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e345 [party_statement; barchart.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] NVIDIA management guided FY2027 Q2 revenue to approximately $91 billion, assuming zero China data-center revenue because of export restrictions.\\n    Quote: Looking ahead, management guided Q2 revenue to approximately $91 billion, despite assuming zero China data-center revenue because of export restrictions.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e335, e388; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e349 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Nvidia automotive chief Xinzhou Wu estimated that autonomous driving accounts for about 0.006% of all miles driven, without specifying a measurement period.\\n    Quote: Right now the percentage of autonomous miles among all the mileage driven is probably negligible. I think it’s 0.006%, or something like that.\", \"- e350 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said Nvidia hopes to earn a share of ecosystem revenue for each autonomously driven mile, which he described as a potential trillion-dollar opportunity; he gave no timing.\\n    Quote: We hope that we can get a percentage of the revenue that the ecosystem can get from every mile that is driven autonomously in the future. This is where the trillion-dollar opportunity can come from.\", \"- e351 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said Tesla is ahead of other companies in L2++ advanced driver-assistance technology and that competitors are trying to catch up.\\n    Quote: For the basic L2++ technology, Elon is probably ahead of everybody. He had a division a long time ago and he has stuck to the vision for a long time to develop and test the technology among a massive fleet. Nobody would argue that Elon is ahead of everybody in the ADAS market and everybody is playing a catch-up game, essentially.\", \"- e352 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu forecast that Level 4 self-driving could become a mainstream experience in less than five years; he did not give a specific date.\\n    Quote: I would say if I need to give a time, I wouldn’t say five years, but less than five years.\", \"- e353 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said Nvidia chip prices would most likely need to rise because demand for chips is intense; he did not specify timing or the size of any increase.\\n    Quote: Actually, most likely even the chip price will need to go up, because of this intense demand for every chip everybody can grab onto.\", \"- e354 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said Nvidia offers two Hyperion 10 sensor configurations: a base version with 10 cameras and three radars and no lidar, and a high-end version with 14 cameras, three lidars, and seven radars for Level 4 driving.\\n    Quote: In Hyperion 10, for example, we really offer two versions. One is a base, which is mostly cameras: 10 cameras, three radars, no lidar. It’s a very cost-effective way to build a L2++ ADAS kind of vehicle. And on the other hand, for the high end, is what we call the Hyperion High: we provide the sensor set required, which has, I think, 14 cameras, three lidars, and seven radars to have enough sensor\", \"- e355 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said Nvidia planned to roll out its ADAS technology in all Mercedes vehicles and in vehicles from some other partners across the United States by the end of 2026.\\n    Quote: First of all, by the end of this year, we are rolling out our technology on the ADAS side in all Mercedes vehicles and some other partners as well, all over the United States.\", \"- e356 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said Nvidia and Uber were working toward rolling out an L4 service in the next few years; he did not give a specific date.\\n    Quote: Meanwhile, we are also working closely with our partners, for example, Uber. We announced that at GTC, we are trying to roll out our L4 service in the next few years.\", \"- e357 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said 80% of mass-production automakers were in Nvidia’s Hyperion ecosystem for Level 4 driving; he did not specify a measurement date.\\n    Quote: Right now, I would say 80% of the mass-production OEMs are in Nvidia’s Hyperion ecosystem for L4.\", \"- e358 [third_party_view; gurufocus.com (analyst); original source Citi ; from gnews:dedacecd6d2ed5192c307199 2026-07-13] Citi said Nvidia has strong access to high-bandwidth DRAM memory, a critical component for AI systems.\\n    Quote: The bank pointed to Nvidia's strong access to high-bandwidth DRAM memory, a critical component for AI systems.\", \"- e363 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:f4eb5206f2995f5dbb86c5e9 2026-07-13] Nvidia reported quarterly revenue of $81.6 billion for the quarter ended April 26, 2026, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: In its most recent quarter (ended April 26), it made $81.6 billion in revenue (up 85% year over year)\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e244; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e364 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:3a9054a950c410e249837c91 2026-07-13] Nvidia reported FY2027 Q1 revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% quarter over quarter.\\n    Quote: For its fiscal 