nsensus analyst estimates for Nvidia increased 13.7% over the three months before 2026-07-14; the estimate measure and fiscal period are not specified.\\n    Quote: Analysts have been steadily raising their estimates for Nvidia. Over the past three months, the Zacks Consensus Estimate for the company has increased 13.7%.\", \"- e426 [third_party_view; sg.finance.yahoo.com; original source Zacks ; from gnews:f10cd8ddb00105698ac294cf 2026-07-14] Zacks reported expected Nvidia earnings of $9.10 per share for the fiscal year ending January 2027, unchanged from the year-ago reported figure.\\n    Quote: For the fiscal year ending January 2027, this maker of graphics chips for gaming and artificial intelligence is expected to earn $9.10 per share, which is unchanged compared with the year-ago reported number.\", \"- e427 [fact; Reuters; original source U.S. authorities, as reported from documents and sources familiar with the matter 2026-07-14; from gnews:24268bfaab6ef1d7876b188c 2026-07-14] U.S. authorities permitted ZTE Kangxun Telecom and server maker Maginfra to purchase Nvidia H200 chips; a Kingsoft subsidiary was cleared to use some AMD chips.\\n    Quote: ZTE Kangxun Telecom and server maker Maginfra have been permitted to purchase Nvidia's H200 chips, while Zhuhai Hengqin Yunxiang Zhisheng Network Technology, a subsidiary of cloud computing company Kingsoft, has ‌been cleared to use some ⁠AMD chips that rival the H200, according to the documents and the sources.\", \"- e428 [rumour; Reuters; original source Unnamed sources familiar with the matter 2026-07-14; from gnews:24268bfaab6ef1d7876b188c 2026-07-14] Unnamed sources said some Chinese cloud firms recently told partners and clients they may soon be able to obtain Nvidia H200 chips, indicating progress in Chinese authorities' import reviews.\\n    Quote: However, some Chinese cloud firms have recently told partners and clients they may soon be able to obtain H200 chips, the sources said, indicating some progress in import reviews by Chinese authorities.\", \"- e429 [fact; Rest of World; original source Saudi Arabia 2026-06-01; from gnews:01a49ffd41f6abe24538da65 2026-07-14] Saudi Arabia agreed on June 1, 2026, to use self-driving taxis that run on Nvidia technology.\\n    Quote: Saudi Arabia agreed on June 1 to use self-driving taxis that run on Nvidia technology — from the computer inside each car to the software that steers it.\", \"- e430 [fact; Rest of World; original source Humain ; from gnews:01a49ffd41f6abe24538da65 2026-07-14] Humain is building data centers in Riyadh and Dammam, planned to be powered by several hundred thousand Nvidia chips.\\n    Quote: Humain is also building data centers in Riyadh and Dammam, powered by several hundred thousand Nvidia chips.\", \"- e431 [fact; Rest of World; original source G42 ; from gnews:01a49ffd41f6abe24538da65 2026-07-14] G42’s first stage of its Stargate data center in Abu Dhabi is planned to run on 400,000 Nvidia chips.\\n    Quote: Its first stage will run on 400,000 Nvidia chips .\", \"- e432 [party_statement; Rest of World; original source Peng Xiao, G42 CEO ; from gnews:01a49ffd41f6abe24538da65 2026-07-14] G42 CEO Peng Xiao said Stargate’s machines would be mostly Nvidia despite G42’s efforts to spread orders among suppliers.\\n    Quote: G42 has spent months trying to spread its orders among several suppliers, yet the machines inside Stargate would be “mostly” Nvidia, CEO Peng Xiao said in an interview in January.\", \"- e434 [third_party_view; Tom's Hardware; original source Reuters ; from gnews:3221eba2826b001b12b82770 2026-07-14] Reuters said Chinese technology firms had more than 2 million Nvidia H200 chips on order about six months before 2026-07-14, exceeding Nvidia's available inventory at the time.\\n    Quote: But even with those domestic production initiatives, the Chinese hunger for AI silicon is so deep that six months ago, Reuters said the nation's tech firms had more than two million H200 chips on order, far more than what Nvidia had on hand at the time.\", \"- e438 [fact; mlq.ai; original source FBI ; from gnews:ca7564a0dc63b215f5d49402 2026-07-14] The FBI published an RFI seeking market input on AI supercomputer hardware for its CJIS Division, including Nvidia Blackwell Ultra GPUs and Google TPUs; the RFI does not commit the FBI to a procurement.\\n    Quote: The FBI has published a Request for Information on SAM.gov seeking market input on AI supercomputer hardware for its Criminal Justice Information Services (CJIS) Division in Clarksburg, West Virginia. The RFI outlines four distinct categories of accelerator systems spanning training, inference, and analytics workloads — including both Nvidia Blackwell Ultra GPUs and Google TPUs [1].\", \"- e439 [third_party_view; mlq.ai; original source mlq.ai 2026-07-14; from gnews:ca7564a0dc63b215f5d49402 2026-07-14] Federal AI spending obligations reached $7.2 billion in 2026, up from $675 million in 2024, while potential contract awards reached $91.8 billion, up from $4.6 billion in 2024.\\n    Quote: Federal AI spending obligations reached $7.2 billion in 2026, up from $675 million in 2024 — a 966% increase. Potential contract awards ballooned to $91.8 billion, up 1,912% from 2024's $4.6 billion [2].\", \"- e440 [party_statement; Jakarta Globe; original source Airlangga Hartarto ; from gnews:e001119c6342373f6b1f3cf4 2026-07-14] Indonesia’s Chief Economic Affairs Minister Airlangga Hartarto said investors are planning data center projects with a combined capacity of about 1.3 GW, in addition to roughly 580 MW already operating; no project period was specified.\\n    Quote: Chief Economic Affairs Minister Airlangga Hartarto said investors are planning data center projects with a combined capacity of about 1.3 gigawatts (GW), on top of the roughly 580 megawatts (MW) currently in operation.\", \"- e444 [rumour; Reuters; original source Unnamed sources cited by the Financial Times 2026-07-14; from gnews:dc642adc9738cb72e71bf4cd 2026-07-14] The Financial Times reported on July 14 that NVIDIA had more than halved its authorised Asian AI-chip customer list after creating a new whitelist to prevent chips reaching China.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA has more than halved the number of Asian customers authorised to buy its AI chips after creating a new “white list” of companies that have passed tougher compliance checks aimed at preventing the products from reaching China, the Financial Times reported on Monday (Jul 14).\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e415; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e445 [rumour; Reuters; original source Three unnamed people familiar with the matter, cited by the Financial Times 2026-07-14; from gnews:dc642adc9738cb72e71bf4cd 2026-07-14] Three people familiar with the matter told the Financial Times that NVIDIA intensified customer due diligence in Singapore, Malaysia and Japan over the past few months.\\n    Quote: Over the past few months, the chipmaker has intensified due diligence in Singapore, Malaysia and Japan, the report added, citing three people familiar with the matter.\", \"- e446 [fact; Reuters; original source US Commerce Department ; from gnews:dc642adc9738cb72e71bf4cd 2026-07-14] The US Commerce Department issued guidance in May to curb advanced AI-chip transfers to overseas subsidiaries of Chinese companies, citing concern that Blackwell processors may have reached Chinese-linked entities in countries including Malaysia despite US restrictions.\\n    Quote: The US Commerce Department issued guidance in May aimed at curbing advanced AI chips from reaching overseas subsidiaries of Chinese companies, highlighting concerns that Nvidia’s cutting-edge Blackwell processors may have been exported to Chinese-linked entities in countries such as Malaysia despite US restrictions.\", \"- e447 [rumour; Reuters; original source Unnamed sources cited by the Financial Times 2026-07-14; from gnews:dc642adc9738cb72e71bf4cd 2026-07-14] The Financial Times reported that NVIDIA tightened compliance procedures after pressure from Washington, with staff now visiting customers’ data centres, verifying contracts and interviewing end users.\\n    Quote: Nvidia has tightened compliance procedures following pressure from Washington, the FT said, adding that staff now visit customers’ data centres, verify contracts and interview end users as part of the checks.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e415; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e448 [rumour; Reuters; original source Unnamed sources cited by the Financial Times 2026-07-14; from gnews:dc642adc9738cb72e71bf4cd 2026-07-14] The Financial Times reported that the US Department of Commerce is providing oversight and political backing for the compliance checks.\\n    Quote: The US Department of Commerce is also involved, providing oversight and political backing, the report said.\"]\n{\"control\": 9, \"points_to_rule\": [\"same_question\"], \"ruler_question\": {\"question\": \"Will NVIDIA sign a guarantee of OpenAI's Ohio data-center lease by 2027-06-30?\", \"unit\": \"yes/no\", \"due_day\": \"2027-06-30\", \"rungs\": [{\"label\": \"Yes\", \"condition\": \"NVIDIA has signed the guarantee by the due day.\"}, {\"label\": \"No\", \"condition\": \"It has not.\"}]}, \"judged_question\": {\"view_id\": \"v2\", \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA sign a financial guarantee for OpenAI’s Ohio data-center lease by 2027-07-01?\", \"looks_at\": \"NVIDIA guarantee for OpenAI’s Ohio data-center lease\", \"due_day\": \"2027-07-01\", \"year\": \"2027\", \"kind\": \"asset\"}, \"judged_rungs\": [{\"position\": 1, \"label\": \"No\", \"condition\": \"NVIDIA has not signed the guarantee by 2027-07-01.\", \"lo\": null, \"hi\": null}, {\"position\": 2, \"label\": \"Yes\", \"condition\": \"NVIDIA has signed the guarantee by 2027-07-01.\", \"lo\": null, \"hi\": null}]}\n{\"control\": 10, \"points_to_rule\": [\"item i202\"], \"ruler_question\": {\"question\": \"Will Nvidia begin shipping its Rubin generation by December 31, 2026?\", \"unit\": \"yes/no\", \"due_day\": \"2026-12-31\", \"rungs\": [{\"label\": \"Yes\", \"condition\": \"Nvidia has begun shipping Rubin by December 31, 2026.\", \"lo\": null, \"hi\": null}, {\"label\": \"No\", \"condition\": \"Nvidia has not begun shipping Rubin by December 31, 2026.\", \"lo\": null, \"hi\": null}]}, \"judged_question\": {\"view_id\": \"v3\", \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA begin shipping Rubin by 2026-12-31?\", \"looks_at\": \"Whether NVIDIA begins shipping its Rubin-generation platform by the end of 2026.\", \"due_day\": \"2026-12-31\", \"year\": \"2026\", \"kind\": \"asset\"}, \"judged_rungs\": [{\"position\": 1, \"label\": \"Yes\", \"condition\": \"NVIDIA begins shipping Rubin on or before 2026-12-31.\", \"lo\": null, \"hi\": null}, {\"position\": 2, \"label\": \"No\", \"condition\": \"NVIDIA has not begun shipping Rubin by 2026-12-31.\", \"lo\": null, \"hi\": null}]}\nITEM [{\"id\": \"i202\", \"day\": \"2026-07-06\", \"title\": \"Nvidia's Kyber rack for Rubin Ultra reportedly delayed to 2028, stopgap solution also axed due to customer pushback — Analyst firm SemiAnalysis says PCB midplane problems led to the delay [Updated]\", \"passage\": \"Nvidia's 2026 Rubin GPUs, which reuse the current Oberon rack, aren't part of the reported delay.\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"Tom's Hardware\", \"what\": \"scope of the reported delay: Rubin Ultra/Kyber only; 2026 Rubin on Oberon unaffected\", \"period\": \"2026\", \"status\": \"claim\"}}]\nEVIDENCE [\"- e29 [third_party_view; fool.com; original source fool.com 2026-07-02; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] The article says NVIDIA’s Vera Rubin platform is in full production and could begin shipping in 2026.\\n    Quote: Vera Rubin, Nvidia's next-generation AI chip platform, is in full production and could begin shipping later this year.\", \"- e30 [party_statement; fool.com; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang expects $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\\n    Quote: CEO Jensen Huang has laid out expectations for $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\", \"- e30 [party_statement; fool.com; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang expects $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\\n    Quote: CEO Jensen Huang has laid out expectations for $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e34; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e34 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst), quoting Jensen Huang; original source Jensen Huang, NVIDIA CEO ; from gnews:e4e5f1b5c0c68381e4c486e1 2026-07-03] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang forecast $1 trillion in combined Blackwell and Vera Rubin chip sales from March through the end of 2027.\\n    Quote: In March, CEO Jensen Huang said he expects the company's Blackwell and Vera Rubin chips to generate $1 trillion in sales between that time and the end of 2027.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e30; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e39 [fact; BGR.com, reporting on NVIDIA's blog post by Josh Parker; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:a8fab49de53d125314a6688a 2026-07-04] NVIDIA announced that its DSX AI factories are hosting Rubin AI infrastructure, using a design with no fans or cold aisles.\\n    Quote: In Nvidia's blog post by Josh Parker, head of corporate sustainability at Nvidia, it was announced that Nvidia DSX AI factories are hosting Nvidia's Rubin AI infrastructure with no fans or cold aisles.\", \"- e47 [rumour; CNBC; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA’s Kyber rack-scale architecture, designed for Rubin Ultra, had been delayed by more than 12 months to 2028.\\n    Quote: Nvidia 's next marquee product — the Kyber rack-scale architecture designed to house its 2027 Rubin Ultra chips — has been delayed by more than 12 months to 2028, according to research firm SemiAnalysis\", \"- e48 [party_statement; CNBC, quoting NVIDIA; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] NVIDIA rejected SemiAnalysis’s report and said its product roadmap remained intact.\\n    Quote: Nvidia rejected the SemiAnalysis report and said, \\\"Our roadmap is intact.\\\"\", \"- e49 [rumour; CNBC, quoting SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis said the Kyber NVL144 rack architecture was delayed to 2028 because its PCB midplane remained difficult to manufacture.\\n    Quote: \\\"Kyber NVL144 rack architecture has been delayed to 2028 as the PCB midplane remains challenging from a manufacturability standpoint,\\\" the firm said\", \"- e50 [rumour; CNBC; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis said NVIDIA’s NVL576 system, which links eight racks, was likely to be delayed or produced in only small volumes.\\n    Quote: NVL576 — a larger system linking eight racks via optical connections — is also likely delayed or limited to small volumes, the research firm said.\", \"- e51 [rumour; CNBC, quoting SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis said NVIDIA scrapped its backup plan to bolt two current-generation racks together after cloud providers and hyperscalers objected to the design and operating burden.\\n    Quote: A backup plan — bolting two of Nvidia's current-generation racks together for similar power — has also been scrapped after cloud customers rejected the design as awkward and costly to operate. \\\"It has since been cancelled due to heavy pushback from CSPs [cloud service providers] and hyperscalers over its odd design and heavy operational burden,\\\" SemiAnalysis said.\", \"- e52 [third_party_view; CNBC, quoting SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis said NVIDIA had no proven solution to expand Rubin Ultra’s scale-up system size and that this could give AMD and Google a technical opening in the high-end market.\\n    Quote: That leaves Nvidia with \\\"no proven solution to expand the scale-up world size for Rubin Ultra,\\\" SemiAnalysis said, predicting that could give rivals Advanced Micro Devices and Google , whose in-house chips are already winning business from top AI labs, a rare technical opening at the high end of the market.\", \"- e53 [fact; CNBC; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] NVIDIA’s current-generation Rubin systems were in full production and were scheduled to begin shipping in fall 2026 to eight cloud partners, including AWS, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud.\\n    Quote: Nvidia's current-generation Rubin systems are in full production and begin shipping this fall to eight cloud partners, including Amazon Web Services, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud.\", \"- e55 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:2f953a56cd06571ab0afc348 2026-07-05] NVIDIA plans to launch its first stand-alone CPU this fall as part of the Vera Rubin platform.\\n    Quote: In fact, it's launching its first-ever stand-alone CPU this fall as part of the Vera Rubin platform.\", \"- e51 [rumour; CNBC, quoting SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis said NVIDIA scrapped its backup plan to bolt two current-generation racks together after cloud providers and hyperscalers objected to the design and operating burden.\\n    Quote: A backup plan — bolting two of Nvidia's current-generation racks together for similar power — has also been scrapped after cloud customers rejected the design as awkward and costly to operate. \\\"It has since been cancelled due to heavy pushback from CSPs [cloud service providers] and hyperscalers over its odd design and heavy operational burden,\\\" SemiAnalysis said.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e125; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e52 [third_party_view; CNBC, quoting SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis said NVIDIA had no proven solution to expand Rubin Ultra’s scale-up system size and that this could give AMD and Google a technical opening in the high-end market.\\n    Quote: That leaves Nvidia with \\\"no proven solution to expand the scale-up world size for Rubin Ultra,\\\" SemiAnalysis said, predicting that could give rivals Advanced Micro Devices and Google , whose in-house chips are already winning business from top AI labs, a rare technical opening at the high end of the market.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e119, e120; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e53 [fact; CNBC; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] NVIDIA’s current-generation Rubin systems were in full production and were scheduled to begin shipping in fall 2026 to eight cloud partners, including AWS, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud.\\n    Quote: Nvidia's current-generation Rubin systems are in full production and begin shipping this fall to eight cloud partners, including Amazon Web Services, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e129; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e76 [third_party_view; MarketScale; original source MarketScale 2026-07-06; from gnews:f66e1689ec2e27e7eab2a2dd 2026-07-06] First shipments of the Vera Rubin VR200 are scheduled for Q3 2026, with volume ramping in Q4.\\n    Quote: First shipments are scheduled for the third quarter of 2026, with volume ramping in the fourth.\", \"- e79 [rumour; datacenterdynamics.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:98a4e8ff0c0260d8dc9e531d 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis had reported that NVIDIA canceled its four-die Rubin Ultra design in favor of a two-chiplet design, citing manufacturing execution concerns.\\n    Quote: The news comes a week after SemiAnalysis separately reported that Nvidia had canceled the four-die Rubin Ultra design in favor of the two-chiplet design, also due to “manufacturing execution concerns.”\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e116; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e90 [rumour; 247wallst.com (Danielle Liverance); original source Unnamed reports cited by 247wallst.com ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] Reports said NVIDIA's upcoming Vera Rubin server systems were delayed; the item does not specify the extent or timing.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA shares are under pressure on reports of delays across their upcoming lineup of Vera Rubin server systems.\", \"- e116 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA had canceled the four-compute-die version of its upcoming Rubin Ultra chip.\\n    Quote: The more powerful version of the upcoming Rubin Ultra chip with four compute dies has also been canceled.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e79, e126; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e117 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis said only the two-die Rubin Ultra version remained, with roughly half the real-world compute performance of the canceled four-die version.\\n    Quote: Only the smaller two-die version remains, delivering roughly half the real-world compute performance.\", \"- e118 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA's CPO-NVSwitch interconnect technology would not arrive until the Feynman generation, the generation after next.\\n    Quote: A key interconnect technology called CPO-NVSwitch, which links many chips into a single large system, won't arrive until the generation after next, called Feynman.\", \"- e119 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis said NVIDIA currently lacked a proven way to scale Rubin Ultra to very large systems.\\n    Quote: That means Nvidia lacks a proven way to scale Rubin Ultra to very large systems for now.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e52; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e120 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis said the gap in NVIDIA's ability to scale Rubin Ultra could give AMD's MI500X and Google's TPUv8i Broadfly room to compete.\\n    Quote: The gap could give competitors like AMD's MI500X or Google's TPUv8i Broadfly room to move in.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e52; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e121 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA planned to offset the shortfall by selling more Oberon-Rubin racks in the existing form factor.\\n    Quote: Nvidia plans to make up for the shortfall by selling more Oberon-Rubin racks in the existing form factor.\", \"- e125 [rumour; Investing.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:d5c48abb470f394f86549b6b 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis alleged that NVIDIA cancelled an alternative back-to-back rack design after operational pushback from hyperscale cloud clients.\\n    Quote: The research firm further alleged that Nvidia cancelled an alternative back-to-back rack design following heavy operational pushback from hyperscale cloud clients.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e51; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e126 [rumour; Investing.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:d5c48abb470f394f86549b6b 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis claimed NVIDIA scrapped a four-die configuration of its upcoming Rubin Ultra platform in favor of a downsized version.\\n    Quote: Additionally, the report pointed to a downsized version of the upcoming Rubin Ultra platform, claiming a crucial four-die configuration had been scrapped.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e116; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e129 [third_party_view; tikr.com (analyst); original source tikr.com (analyst) 2026-07-06; from gnews:d4c5dc540392f8df39aee250 2026-07-06] NVIDIA’s current-generation Rubin systems are in full production and are scheduled to begin shipping in fall 2026 to eight major cloud partners, including AWS, Microsoft Azure, and Google Cloud.\\n    Quote: That’s likely because the company’s current-generation Rubin systems are already in full production and set to start shipping this fall to eight major cloud partners, including Amazon Web Services, Microsoft Azure, and Google Cloud.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e53; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e278 [third_party_view; Vandita Jadeja; original source Vandita Jadeja 2026-07-10; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] The author said the $300 NVIDIA share-price case depended on Blackwell Ultra and Vera Rubin shipping on schedule, gross margins remaining at 75%, and a sovereign or hyperscaler deal being upsized.\\n    Quote: Three things need to go right: Blackwell Ultra and Vera Rubin ship on schedule, gross margins hold the 75% line, and one sovereign or hyperscaler deal gets upsized in a headline print.\", \"- e350 [fact; barchart.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] NVIDIA recently launched its Vera Rubin AI platform.\\n    Quote: Nvidia recently launched its Vera Rubin AI platform, released the AI PC platform RTX Spark, expanded partnerships with companies such as Alphabet (GOOGL) and Marvell (MRVL), and further invested in networking, CPUs, and AI infrastructure.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e90 (); both are in force: Reports said NVIDIA's upcoming Vera Rubin server systems were delayed; the item does not specify the extent or timing.\", \"- e351 [fact; en.sedaily.com; original source LG Electronics ; from gnews:bf96def37a9c3a5f19f5d43c 2026-07-12] LG Electronics completed a Vera Rubin-specification AI server rack prototype in the first half of 2026 and plans to seek orders after second-half reliability evaluations, with mass production planned for 2027.\\n    Quote: According to the semiconductor industry on the 12th, LG Electronics' Production Research Institute (PRI) completed development of an AI server rack prototype matching the compute tray specifications of Nvidia's \\\"Vera Rubin\\\" in the first half of the year. LG plans to secure orders from global big tech companies after reliability evaluations in the second half and begin mass production next year.\", \"- e359 [party_statement; gurufocus.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:dedacecd6d2ed5192c307199 2026-07-13] NVIDIA said development of its next-generation Rubin Ultra platform remains on schedule.\\n    Quote: The company said development of its next-generation Rubin Ultra platform remains on schedule\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e90 (); both are in force: Reports said NVIDIA's upcoming Vera Rubin server systems were delayed; the item does not specify the extent or timing.\", \"- e427 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com; original source 247wallst.com 2026-07-14; from gnews:ac8a489e54fbb1b85a1c7a2c 2026-07-14] NVIDIA’s Blackwell 300 was ramping, with the Vera Rubin platform queued behind it.\\n    Quote: Blackwell 300 is ramping, and the Vera Rubin platform is queued behind it.\", \"- e445 [party_statement; ebc.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f83ae0a4f01c18d48f20a629 2026-07-14] NVIDIA’s Vera Rubin architecture remains on track for late-2026 delivery, according to the article.\\n    Quote: the Vera Rubin architecture remains officially on track for late 2026\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e90 (); both are in force: Reports said NVIDIA's upcoming Vera Rubin server systems were delayed; the item does not specify the extent or timing.\"]\n{\"control\": 12, \"points_to_rule\": [\"same_question\"], \"ruler_question\": {\"question\": \"How much will the largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?\", \"unit\": \"USD\", \"due_day\": \"2028-12-31\", \"rungs\": [{\"label\": \"Below $700 billion\", \"condition\": \"Combined spending is less than $700 billion.\", \"lo\": null, \"hi\": 700000000000.0}, {\"label\": \"$700 billion to below $800 billion\", \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $700 billion and less than $800 billion.\", \"lo\": 700000000000.0, \"hi\": 800000000000.0}, {\"label\": \"$800 billion to below $900 billion\", \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $800 billion and less than $900 billion.\", \"lo\": 800000000000.0, \"hi\": 900000000000.0}, {\"label\": \"$900 billion to below $1000 billion\", \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $900 billion and less than $1000 billion.\", \"lo\": 900000000000.0, \"hi\": 1000000000000.0}, {\"label\": \"$1000 billion or more\", \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $1000 billion.\", \"lo\": 1000000000000.0, \"hi\": null}]}, \"judged_question\": {\"view_id\": \"v5\", \"question\": \"How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?\", \"looks_at\": \"Calendar 2027 data-center capital expenditures by the four largest AI hyperscalers\", \"due_day\": \"2028-03-31\", \"year\": \"2027\", \"kind\": \"theme\"}, \"judged_rungs\": [{\"position\": 1, \"label\": \"Lowest range\", \"condition\": \"Combined spending is below $800 billion.\", \"lo\": null, \"hi\": 800000000000.0}, {\"position\": 2, \"label\": \"Lower-middle range\", \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $800 billion but below $900 billion.\", \"lo\": 800000000000.0, \"hi\": 900000000000.0}, {\"position\": 3, \"label\": \"Neutral comparison: around NVIDIA's reported $1 trillion projection\", \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $900 billion but below $1.1 trillion.\", \"lo\": 900000000000.0, \"hi\": 1100000000000.0}, {\"position\": 4, \"label\": \"Upper-middle range\", \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $1.1 trillion but below $1.2 trillion.\", \"lo\": 1100000000000.0, \"hi\": 1200000000000.0}, {\"position\": 5, \"label\": \"Highest range\", \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $1.2 trillion.\", \"lo\": 1200000000000.0, \"hi\": null}]}\n{\"control\": 14, \"points_to_rule\": [\"item i202\"], \"ruler_question\": {\"question\": \"Will Nvidia begin shipping its Rubin generation by December 31, 2026?\", \"unit\": \"yes/no\", \"due_day\": \"2026-12-31\", \"rungs\": [{\"label\": \"Yes\", \"condition\": \"Nvidia has begun shipping Rubin by December 31, 2026.\", \"lo\": null, \"hi\": null}, {\"label\": \"No\", \"condition\": \"Nvidia has not begun shipping Rubin by December 31, 2026.\", \"lo\": null, \"hi\": null}]}, \"judged_question\": {\"view_id\": \"v3\", \"question\": \"Will Nvidia's Rubin platform begin shipping by December 31, 2026?\", \"looks_at\": \"Whether Nvidia's Rubin platform begins shipping by the end of 2026.\", \"due_day\": \"2026-12-31\", \"year\": \"2026\", \"kind\": \"asset\"}, \"judged_rungs\": [{\"position\": 1, \"label\": \"Yes\", \"condition\": \"Nvidia begins shipping the Rubin platform on or before December 31, 2026.\", \"lo\": null, \"hi\": null}, {\"position\": 2, \"label\": \"No\", \"condition\": \"Nvidia has not begun shipping the Rubin platform by December 31, 2026.\", \"lo\": null, \"hi\": null}]}\nITEM [{\"id\": \"i202\", \"day\": \"2026-07-06\", \"title\": \"Nvidia's Kyber rack for Rubin Ultra reportedly delayed to 2028, stopgap solution also axed due to customer pushback — Analyst firm SemiAnalysis says PCB midplane problems led to the delay [Updated]\", \"passage\": \"Nvidia's 2026 Rubin GPUs, which reuse the current Oberon rack, aren't part of the reported delay.\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"Tom's Hardware\", \"what\": \"scope of the reported delay: Rubin Ultra/Kyber only; 2026 Rubin on Oberon unaffected\", \"period\": \"2026\", \"status\": \"claim\"}}]\nEVIDENCE [\"- e24 [third_party_view; fool.com (Justin Pope); original source fool.com (Justin Pope) 2026-07-02; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] The author says Vera Rubin is in full production and could begin shipping later in 2026.\\n    Quote: Vera Rubin, Nvidia's next-generation AI chip platform, is in full production and could begin shipping later this year.\", \"- e57 [fact; CNBC; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] Nvidia’s current-generation Rubin systems are in full production and are scheduled to begin shipping in fall 2026 to eight cloud partners, including AWS, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud.\\n    Quote: Nvidia's current-generation Rubin systems are in full production and begin shipping this fall to eight cloud partners, including Amazon Web Services, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud.\", \"- e59 [party_statement; fool.com analyst; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:2f953a56cd06571ab0afc348 2026-07-05] Nvidia plans to launch its first stand-alone CPU as part of the Vera Rubin platform in fall 2026.\\n    Quote: In fact, it's launching its first-ever stand-alone CPU this fall as part of the Vera Rubin platform.\", \"- e60 [party_statement; fool.com analyst; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:2f953a56cd06571ab0afc348 2026-07-05] Nvidia plans to release a personal-computing superchip that combines a GPU and a CPU in fall 2026.\\n    Quote: And at the same time, Nvidia is targeting the personal computing market with a superchip -- also set for fall release -- that includes a GPU and a CPU.\", \"- e64 [rumour; finance.yahoo.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:68a3ed21f77b935d9fa7ec5e 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis claimed the Rubin Ultra high-density rack design was delayed by more than 12 months because of persistent manufacturing problems with its PCB midplane.\\n    Quote: SemiAnalysis claims the high-density rack design built for Rubin Ultra GPUs has slipped by more than 12 months. The firm blamed persistent manufacturing problems with the system's complex PCB midplane.\", \"- e65 [rumour; finance.yahoo.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:68a3ed21f77b935d9fa7ec5e 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis claimed Nvidia scrapped its NVL72x2 back-to-back rack after hyperscaler customers pushed back.\\n    Quote: The firm also claimed Nvidia scrapped its NVL72x2 back-to-back rack after pushback from hyperscaler customers.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e54, e130, e145, e146; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e66 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:68a3ed21f77b935d9fa7ec5e 2026-07-06] Nvidia told media outlets that its roadmap remains intact, rejecting claims of delays to its next-generation AI rack systems.\\n    Quote: Nvidia rejected the claims, telling media outlets that its roadmap remains intact.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e56, e90, e134; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e80 [third_party_view; MarketScale; original source Morgan Stanley Research ; from gnews:f66e1689ec2e27e7eab2a2dd 2026-07-06] Morgan Stanley estimated the Vera Rubin VR200 NVL72 rack would cost hyperscale cloud providers about $7.8 million per unit, versus about $4 million for the GB300 NVL72.\\n    Quote: Morgan Stanley Research estimates that Nvidia 's Vera Rubin VR200 NVL72 rack will cost hyperscale cloud providers around $7.8 million per unit, up from roughly $4 million for the current GB300 NVL72 generation.\", \"- e81 [third_party_view; MarketScale; original source Morgan Stanley Research ; from gnews:f66e1689ec2e27e7eab2a2dd 2026-07-06] Morgan Stanley estimated Nvidia would charge about $55,000 per Rubin GPU and $5,000 per Vera CPU at volume.\\n    Quote: The bank estimates Nvidia will charge about $55,000 per Rubin GPU and $5,000 per Vera CPU when sold in volume.\", \"- e82 [third_party_view; MarketScale; original source Morgan Stanley Research ; from gnews:f66e1689ec2e27e7eab2a2dd 2026-07-06] Morgan Stanley estimated memory content in a Vera Rubin rack at about $2 million, up 435% from the prior generation, including roughly $1 million or more of 3D NAND storage.\\n    Quote: Morgan Stanley puts memory content per rack at about $2 million, a 435% jump from the prior generation, driven by a threefold increase in LPDDR5X capacity to 54 terabytes per rack plus roughly $1 million or more in 3D NAND storage that was virtually absent from earlier systems.\", \"- e83 [third_party_view; MarketScale; original source Morgan Stanley Research ; from gnews:f66e1689ec2e27e7eab2a2dd 2026-07-06] The article reported Morgan Stanley's estimate that memory's share of the bill of materials rose from 5–10% on GB200 to 25–30% on VR200, while the GPU share fell from about 63% to 51%.\\n    Quote: As a share of the bill of materials, memory rose from 5 to 10 percent on the GB200 to 25 to 30 percent on the VR200, while the GPU's share fell from roughly 63 percent to 51 percent.\", \"- e84 [third_party_view; MarketScale; original source MarketScale 2026-07-06; from gnews:f66e1689ec2e27e7eab2a2dd 2026-07-06] First shipments of Nvidia's Vera Rubin VR200 NVL72 rack were scheduled for Q3 2026, with volume ramping in Q4 2026.\\n    Quote: First shipments are scheduled for the third quarter of 2026, with volume ramping in the fourth.\", \"- e85 [third_party_view; MarketScale; original source Morgan Stanley Research ; from gnews:f66e1689ec2e27e7eab2a2dd 2026-07-06] Morgan Stanley estimated that hyperscalers self-sourcing certain memory modules could reduce the Vera Rubin rack price to around $6.7 million.\\n    Quote: Morgan Stanley notes that a hyperscaler self-sourcing certain memory modules could bring the rack price down to around $6.7 million, a reminder that procurement structure now materially moves the number.\", \"- e86 [rumour; datacenterdynamics.com, reporting SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:98a4e8ff0c0260d8dc9e531d 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia delayed production of its Kyber rack-scale architecture by more than 12 months, pushing its release to 2028.\\n    Quote: Nvidia has delayed production of its Kyber rack-scale architecture by more than 12 months, pushing its release date to 2028, SemiAnalysis has reported.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e144; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e87 [rumour; datacenterdynamics.com, quoting SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:98a4e8ff0c0260d8dc9e531d 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis said Kyber NVL144 was delayed to 2028 because of PCB midplane manufacturing challenges, and Nvidia scrapped its alternative two-Oberon-rack design after cloud companies and hyperscalers objected to it.\\n    Quote: “Kyber NVL144 rack architecture has been delayed to 2028 as the PCB midplane remains challenging from a manufacturability standpoint,” SemiAnalysis said, adding that Nvidia’s alternative plan, which involved placing two Oberon racks back-to-back in order to achieve a similar power output, has also been scrapped after cloud companies and hyperscalers pushed back against its “odd design and heavy op\", \"- e88 [rumour; datacenterdynamics.com, reporting SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:98a4e8ff0c0260d8dc9e531d 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis said manufacturing issues would likely delay Nvidia’s planned NVL576 system or limit it to small volumes.\\n    Quote: The manufacturing issues will also impact the planned NVL576 system, which connects 8x Oberon racks over CPO between the NVSwitches, meaning that the system will also likely be delayed or limited to small volumes, the firm noted.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e147; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e89 [rumour; datacenterdynamics.com, reporting SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:98a4e8ff0c0260d8dc9e531d 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia canceled the four-die Rubin Ultra design in favor of a two-chiplet design because of manufacturing execution concerns.\\n    Quote: The news comes a week after SemiAnalysis separately reported that Nvidia had canceled the four-die Rubin Ultra design in favor of the two-chiplet design, also due to “manufacturing execution concerns.”\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e131, e148; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e90 [party_statement; Nvidia spokesperson, quoted by datacenterdynamics.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:98a4e8ff0c0260d8dc9e531d 2026-07-06] An Nvidia spokesperson said the company’s roadmap was intact in response to questions about the Kyber claims.\\n    Quote: In response to a request for comment from DCD regarding the Kyber claims, a spokesperson for Nvidia said: \\\"Our roadmap is intact.\\\"\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e66; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e97 [rumour; Danielle Liverance; original source Danielle Liverance 2026-07-06; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] The author reported that NVIDIA’s upcoming Vera Rubin server systems were reportedly delayed; no timing or scale was specified.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA shares are under pressure on reports of delays across their upcoming lineup of Vera Rubin server systems.\", \"- e131 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia canceled the four-die Rubin Ultra version, leaving only the two-die version, which it said delivers roughly half the real-world compute performance.\\n    Quote: The more powerful version of the upcoming Rubin Ultra chip with four compute dies has also been canceled. Only the smaller two-die version remains, delivering roughly half the real-world compute performance.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e89, e135; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e134 [party_statement; NVIDIA spokesperson, in a statement emailed to Investing.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-07-06; from gnews:d5c48abb470f394f86549b6b 2026-07-06] An NVIDIA spokesperson said the company's product roadmap remained intact.\\n    Quote: Our roadmap is intact.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e66, e149; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e135 [rumour; Investing.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:d5c48abb470f394f86549b6b 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis claimed that NVIDIA had scrapped a four-die configuration for the upcoming Rubin Ultra platform and would use a downsized version instead.\\n    Quote: Additionally, the report pointed to a downsized version of the upcoming Rubin Ultra platform, claiming a crucial four-die configuration had been scrapped.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e131; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e138 [party_statement; Investing.com, reporting Mizuho analyst Jordan Klein's note; original source Hon Hai Precision Industry management 2026-07-03; from gnews:d5c48abb470f394f86549b6b 2026-07-06] Hon Hai management forecast continued acceleration in AI demand; Mizuho analyst Jordan Klein said this was a positive sign ahead of NVIDIA's Vera Rubin rack launch.\\n    Quote: Klein noted that Hon Hai management forecasted a continued acceleration in AI demand, which the analyst said was \\\"a very good sign into the NVDA launch of their new Vera Rubin rack.\\\"\", \"- e144 [rumour; Tom's Hardware, reporting SemiAnalysis's X thread; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:c75f16a6d64cc27fc28fb571 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia’s Kyber NVL144 rack for Rubin Ultra would not ship until 2028, more than 12 months later than planned.\\n    Quote: Nvidia reportedly won't ship its Kyber NVL144 rack until 2028, a delay of more than 12 months that pushes the cabinet meant for 2027's Rubin Ultra GPUs into the following year, according to a SemiAnalysis thread on X.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e86; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e145 [rumour; Tom's Hardware; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:c75f16a6d64cc27fc28fb571 2026-07-06] Nvidia reportedly abandoned the NVL72x2 stopgap rack intended to provide Rubin Ultra scale-up in 2027; the report says no proven alternative is available.\\n    Quote: Nvidia is also understood to have killed NVL72x2, a stopgap rack designed to tide customers over, and that no proven alternative is now available to widen Rubin Ultra's scale-up in 2027.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e65; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e146 [rumour; Tom's Hardware, reporting SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:c75f16a6d64cc27fc28fb571 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis said Nvidia’s largest customers objected to operating two linked Oberon racks as one unit, prompting Nvidia to abandon the NVL72x2 stopgap for Rubin Ultra scale-up.\\n    Quote: NVL72x2 would have bolted two Oberon racks back-to-back to reach Kyber-class density over copper NVLink, per SemiAnalysis, which said Nvidia abandoned the stopgap after its largest customers balked at running two linked cabinets as a single unit.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e65; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e147 [third_party_view; Tom's Hardware; original source Tom's Hardware 2026-07-06; from gnews:c75f16a6d64cc27fc28fb571 2026-07-06] Tom's Hardware reported that the NVL576 configuration for Rubin Ultra may be delayed or ship in low volumes until co-packaged optics matures.\\n    Quote: NVL576, a separate configuration tying eight racks together through co-packaged optics, is likely to slip too or ship in low volume until that optical technology matures.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e88; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e148 [rumour; Tom's Hardware; original source Tom's Hardware ; from gnews:c75f16a6d64cc27fc28fb571 2026-07-06] Nvidia reportedly changed Rubin Ultra from a quad-chiplet GPU to a dual-chiplet part the week before publication, halving per-package compute because of manufacturing execution concerns.\\n    Quote: Nvidia dropped the quad-chiplet Rubin Ultra GPU for a dual-chiplet part last week over manufacturing execution concerns, halving the accelerator's per-package compute.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e89; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e149 [party_statement; Nvidia representative, quoted by Tom's Hardware; original source NVIDIA 2026-07-06; from gnews:c75f16a6d64cc27fc28fb571 2026-07-06] An Nvidia representative said the company’s roadmap was intact in response to Tom's Hardware; the company gave no further details.\\n    Quote: An Nvidia representative responded with a short statement to Tom's Hardware : \\\"Our roadmap is intact.\\\"\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e134; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e202 [rumour; The Straits Times; original source The Straits Times 2026-07-08; from gnews:c8c39f971721fd820aab5c1c 2026-07-08] Nvidia is reported to be working toward releasing its Rubin lineup in the second half of 2026.\\n    Quote: Nvidia is now working to release an even more powerful line-up called Rubin in the second half of 2026 .\", \"- e223 [third_party_view; Investing.com, reporting Vivek Arya's note; original source Vivek Arya, Bank of America 2026-07-08; from gnews:266c882eea8c686ee7aafac7 2026-07-08] Bank of America analyst Vivek Arya estimated that HBM content per rack may increase by $0.2–0.3 million from Blackwell to Rubin, while rack pricing could increase by $2–3 million because of compute, networking, and software upgrades.\\n    Quote: While HBM content per rack may rise by approximately $0.2-0.3 million from Blackwell to Rubin, Arya noted that rack pricing could increase by $2-3 million, driven by upgrades across compute, networking and software.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e230; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e230 [third_party_view; moomoo.com; original source BofA ; from gnews:1b5a3359dd0644861c0fce42 2026-07-08] BofA estimated HBM content per rack could increase by $0.2 million to $0.3 million from Blackwell to Rubin, while total rack pricing could rise from about $3 million–$4 million to $6 million–$7 million.\\n    Quote: The report estimates HBM content per rack could rise by about $0.2 million to $0.3 million from Blackwell to Rubin, while total rack pricing could increase by $2 million to $3 million, from roughly $3 million to $4 million for Blackwell to $6 million to $7 million for Vera Rubin.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e223; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e66 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:68a3ed21f77b935d9fa7ec5e 2026-07-06] Nvidia told media outlets that its roadmap remains intact, rejecting claims of delays to its next-generation AI rack systems.\\n    Quote: Nvidia rejected the claims, telling media outlets that its roadmap remains intact.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e56, e90, e134, e270; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e270 [party_statement; moomoo.com, reporting NVIDIA’s statement to Bloomberg; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:7b39859113d4e2b8ebd8aa86 2026-07-09] NVIDIA told Bloomberg that it had no technical delay and that its product roadmap remained intact.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA recently issued a statement to Bloomberg denying claims of a technical delay, confirming that its product roadmap remains intact.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e66; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e353 [fact; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] Nvidia recently launched its Vera Rubin AI platform.\\n    Quote: Nvidia recently launched its Vera Rubin AI platform, released the AI PC platform RTX Spark, expanded partnerships with companies such as Alphabet (GOOGL) and Marvell (MRVL), and further invested in networking, CPUs, and AI infrastructure.\", \"- e354 [rumour; en.sedaily.com; original source Unnamed semiconductor-industry sources, as reported by en.sedaily.com 2026-07-12; from gnews:bf96def37a9c3a5f19f5d43c 2026-07-12] LG Electronics completed a Vera Rubin-specification AI server rack prototype in the first half of 2026 and plans to seek orders after second-half reliability evaluations and begin mass production in 2027.\\n    Quote: According to the semiconductor industry on the 12th, LG Electronics' Production Research Institute (PRI) completed development of an AI server rack prototype matching the compute tray specifications of Nvidia's \\\"Vera Rubin\\\" in the first half of the year. LG plans to secure orders from global big tech companies after reliability evaluations in the second half and begin mass production next year.\", \"- e66 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:68a3ed21f77b935d9fa7ec5e 2026-07-06] Nvidia told media outlets that its roadmap remains intact, rejecting claims of delays to its next-generation AI rack systems.\\n    Quote: Nvidia rejected the claims, telling media outlets that its roadmap remains intact.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e56, e90, e134, e270, e364; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e364 [party_statement; gurufocus.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:dedacecd6d2ed5192c307199 2026-07-13] Nvidia said development of its Rubin Ultra platform remains on schedule.\\n    Quote: The company said development of its next-generation Rubin Ultra platform remains on schedule\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e66; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e24 [third_party_view; fool.com (Justin Pope); original source fool.com (Justin Pope) 2026-07-02; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] The author says Vera Rubin is in full production and could begin shipping later in 2026.\\n    Quote: Vera Rubin, Nvidia's next-generation AI chip platform, is in full production and could begin shipping later this year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e456; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e456 [third_party_view; ebc.com; original source ebc.com 2026-07-14; from gnews:f83ae0a4f01c18d48f20a629 2026-07-14] Nvidia’s Vera Rubin architecture remains on track for shipment in late 2026, according to the article.\\n    Quote: the Vera Rubin architecture remains officially on track for late 2026\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e24; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\"]\n{\"control\": 15, \"points_to_rule\": [\"item i295\"], \"ruler_question\": {\"question\": \"What will Nvidia's total revenue be in FY2027?\", \"unit\": \"USD\", \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\", \"rungs\": [{\"label\": \"Strongly bullish\", \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $500 billion.\", \"lo\": 500000000000.0, \"hi\": null}, {\"label\": \"Bullish\", \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $400 billion and below $500 billion.\", \"lo\": 400000000000.0, \"hi\": 500000000000.0}, {\"label\": \"Neutral\", \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $350 billion and below $400 billion.\", \"lo\": 350000000000.0, \"hi\": 400000000000.0}, {\"label\": \"Bearish\", \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $300 billion and below $350 billion.\", \"lo\": 300000000000.0, \"hi\": 350000000000.0}, {\"label\": \"Strongly bearish\", \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is below $300 billion.\", \"lo\": null, \"hi\": 300000000000.0}]}, \"judged_question\": {\"view_id\": \"v4\", \"question\": \"What will Nvidia's total revenue be in FY2027?\", \"looks_at\": \"Nvidia total revenue in FY2027.\", \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\", \"year\": \"FY2027\", \"kind\": \"asset\"}, \"judged_rungs\": [{\"position\": 1, \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\", \"condition\": \"Total revenue is above $430 billion.\", \"lo\": 430000000000.0, \"hi\": null}, {\"position\": 2, \"label\": \"Bullish\", \"condition\": \"Total revenue is above $392 billion and at or below $430 billion.\", \"lo\": 392000000000.0, \"hi\": 430000000000.0}, {\"position\": 3, \"label\": \"Neutral\", \"condition\": \"Total revenue is at or below $392 billion and at or above $350 billion.\", \"lo\": 350000000000.0, \"hi\": 392000000000.0}, {\"position\": 4, \"label\": \"Bearish\", \"condition\": \"Total revenue is below $350 billion and at or above $300 billion.\", \"lo\": 300000000000.0, \"hi\": 350000000000.0}, {\"position\": 5, \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\", \"condition\": \"Total revenue is below $300 billion.\", \"lo\": null, \"hi\": 300000000000.0}]}\nITEM [{\"id\": \"i295\", \"day\": \"2026-07-10\", \"title\": \"Here are Friday's biggest analyst calls: Nvidia, SpaceX, Toll, Shopify, Twilio, Seagate, Chipotle & more\", \"passage\": \"the company describing \\\"accelerating growth rates\\\" even as revenues approach the $100 bn per quarter mark\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"NVIDIA management, relayed by Morgan Stanley\", \"what\": \"revenue growth rates accelerating\", \"how_much\": \"quarterly revenue approaching $100 bn\", \"status\": \"claim\"}}]\nEVIDENCE [\"- e25 [party_statement; fool.com (Justin Pope); original source Jensen Huang, Nvidia CEO ; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] The author reports that Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang expects $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\\n    Quote: CEO Jensen Huang has laid out expectations for $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\", \"- e26 [third_party_view; fool.com (Justin Pope); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] Wall Street analysts estimate Nvidia revenue of $392 billion in FY2027.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts estimate that Nvidia's business could double over the next couple of years, from trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion to $392 billion this fiscal year, and $554 billion the following year.\", \"- e25 [party_statement; fool.com (Justin Pope); original source Jensen Huang, Nvidia CEO ; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] The author reports that Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang expects $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\\n    Quote: CEO Jensen Huang has laid out expectations for $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e35; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e30 [fact; storagereview.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-07-01; from gnews:8c9d215416b714064de3b095 2026-07-03] NVIDIA removed the AI Enterprise subscription requirement for Omniverse production use and redistribution; the change was announced July 1, 2026, and the licensing documentation says it took effect in May 2026.\\n    Quote: The new terms remove that requirement entirely; anything built with Omniverse can also be redistributed under the same free terms, which is a substantive impact for ISVs and integrators who embed Omniverse applications inside their own products.\", \"- e31 [third_party_view; storagereview.com; original source storagereview.com 2026-07-03; from gnews:8c9d215416b714064de3b095 2026-07-03] The Mercedes-Benz CLA with NVIDIA's DRIVE platform reached the US market in 2026, described as the platform's first production deployment.\\n    Quote: The first production deployment, the Mercedes-Benz CLA on the DRIVE platform, reached the US market this year.\", \"- e33 [party_statement; Ben Wodecki, SDxCentral, recounting Aldo Kamper's remarks to investors; original source Aldo Kamper, AMS-Osram CEO ; from gnews:1740f3733eedc34d8bac9b65 2026-07-03] AMS-Osram CEO Aldo Kamper said the company was working toward developing microLED optical interconnects for inside racks and for chip-to-chip communication between GPUs and high-bandwidth memory.\\n    Quote: AMS-Osram’s efforts, meanwhile, will see work toward developing microLED optical interconnects for inside the rack as well as chip-to-chip communication between graphic processing units (GPUs) and high-bandwidth memory, CEO Aldo Kamper told investors during its Q1 2026 earnings call back in May.\", \"- e34 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:e4e5f1b5c0c68381e4c486e1 2026-07-03] Nvidia’s revenue grew 85% year over year in fiscal Q1 2027.\\n    Quote: In the first quarter of Nvidia's fiscal year 2027, ending April 26, the company grew revenue 85% year over year\", \"- e35 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Jensen Huang, Nvidia CEO ; from gnews:e4e5f1b5c0c68381e4c486e1 2026-07-03] In March, CEO Jensen Huang expected Nvidia’s Blackwell and Vera Rubin chips to generate $1 trillion in sales from then through the end of 2027.\\n    Quote: In March, CEO Jensen Huang said he expects the company's Blackwell and Vera Rubin chips to generate $1 trillion in sales between that time and the end of 2027.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e25; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e36 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia management ; from gnews:e4e5f1b5c0c68381e4c486e1 2026-07-03] Nvidia management said it thinks the company can generate nearly $20 billion in CPU sales; no period was specified.\\n    Quote: Management said they think they can generate nearly $20 billion of CPU sales, making it an instant industry leader.\", \"- e37 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source Palantir and NVIDIA ; from gnews:bdcb0ed0921c2e9ae241083c 2026-07-03] Palantir is making a deal to use NVIDIA's Nemotron to build government AI models; no amount or timing is specified.\\n    Quote: With Palantir now inking a deal to use Nvidia's Nemotron to build models for the government\", \"- e38 [third_party_view; Jim Cramer, as quoted by finance.yahoo.com; original source Google and Amazon, as reported by Jim Cramer ; from gnews:a96a4cbf6aae35d01d0d285b 2026-07-03] Jim Cramer said Google and Amazon claim their chips are better than NVIDIA’s, despite using NVIDIA products.\\n    Quote: The first two claim that they have better chips than NVIDIA, even as they use NVIDIA.\", \"- e39 [party_statement; Jim Cramer, as quoted by finance.yahoo.com; original source Hock Tan, Broadcom CEO ; from gnews:a96a4cbf6aae35d01d0d285b 2026-07-03] Broadcom CEO Hock Tan said Broadcom can compete with NVIDIA and take share from it.\\n    Quote: Plus, there's Broadcom, vicious competitor, and CEO Hock Tan's out there saying it can compete; it can take share from NVIDIA.\", \"- e43 [fact; mlq.ai; original source Sharon AI ; from gnews:9e0d5b0d6b3e603c60340128 2026-07-03] Sharon AI plans to deploy up to 40,000 NVIDIA Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs under a six-year agreement with NVIDIA.\\n    Quote: Sharon AI, which listed on the Nasdaq in February 2026 via a $125 million IPO, is deploying up to 40,000 Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs under a six-year agreement with Nvidia [2] [6] .\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e28; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e44 [fact; mlq.ai; original source Firmus Technologies ; from gnews:9e0d5b0d6b3e603c60340128 2026-07-03] Firmus Technologies is constructing a DSX-aligned campus in Batam, Indonesia, expected to scale to 360 MW and house up to 170,000 NVIDIA GPUs.\\n    Quote: Firmus Technologies, a private company, is constructing a campus in Batam, Indonesia, built to Nvidia's DGX SuperPOD (DSX) reference architecture specifications. The facility is expected to scale to 360MW and house up to 170,000 Nvidia GPUs [1] [3] .\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e5; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e44 [fact; mlq.ai; original source Firmus Technologies ; from gnews:9e0d5b0d6b3e603c60340128 2026-07-03] Firmus Technologies is constructing a DSX-aligned campus in Batam, Indonesia, expected to scale to 360 MW and house up to 170,000 NVIDIA GPUs.\\n    Quote: Firmus Technologies, a private company, is constructing a campus in Batam, Indonesia, built to Nvidia's DGX SuperPOD (DSX) reference architecture specifications. The facility is expected to scale to 360MW and house up to 170,000 Nvidia GPUs [1] [3] .\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e5, e51; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e47 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568 2026-07-04] Wall Street analysts project Nvidia revenue growth of 82% in FY2027 and 41% in FY2028.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts project 82% revenue growth for this year and 41% next year, so there's another external source that's projecting even more growth for Nvidia.\", \"- e48 [third_party_view; fool.com analyst; original source fool.com analyst 2026-07-04; from gnews:068a24e2743bab750f43f048 2026-07-04] The author calculated that NVIDIA revenue increased 1,033% from Q1 2024 through Q1 FY2027, which ended April 26.\\n    Quote: Just in the last three years, from Q1 2024 to the first quarter of fiscal 2027 (ended April 26), Nvidia's revenue soared 1,033%.\", \"- e50 [fact; datacenters.economictimes.indiatimes.com; original source Sharon AI ; from gnews:1e7a9c953f3ad70093b67ae4 2026-07-04] Sharon AI plans to deploy up to 40,000 NVIDIA Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs under the financing model.\\n    Quote: Sharon AI plans to deploy up to 40,000 Nvidia Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs,\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e28; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e51 [fact; datacenters.economictimes.indiatimes.com; original source Firmus ; from gnews:1e7a9c953f3ad70093b67ae4 2026-07-04] Firmus is developing a DSX AI factory campus in Batam, Indonesia, expected to reach 360 MW and accommodate up to 170,000 NVIDIA GPUs.\\n    Quote: Firmus is developing a DSX AI factory campus in Batam, Indonesia, which is expected to scale to 360 megawatts and accommodate up to 170,000 Nvidia GPUs.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e44; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e58 [third_party_view; CNBC, reporting SemiAnalysis’s projection; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis projected Nvidia data-center compute revenue in the second half of FY2027 to be 20% above Wall Street consensus.\\n    Quote: SemiAnalysis also projects Nvidia's data-center compute revenue will run 20% above Wall Street consensus in the second half of fiscal 2027.\", \"- e61 [third_party_view; fool.com analyst; original source fool.com analyst 2026-07-05; from gnews:2f953a56cd06571ab0afc348 2026-07-05] The author describes Nvidia's goal as dominating a CPU market estimated at $200 billion, without specifying a period.\\n    Quote: I'll start with the goal, and this is to dominate the $200 billion CPU market -- a market where Nvidia has not been greatly present in the past.\", \"- e62 [party_statement; fool.com analyst; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:2f953a56cd06571ab0afc348 2026-07-05] Nvidia forecasts $20 billion in stand-alone CPU sales in 2026.\\n    Quote: Nvidia already forecasts $20 billion in stand-alone CPU sales this year.\", \"- e34 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:e4e5f1b5c0c68381e4c486e1 2026-07-03] Nvidia’s revenue grew 85% year over year in fiscal Q1 2027.\\n    Quote: In the first quarter of Nvidia's fiscal year 2027, ending April 26, the company grew revenue 85% year over year\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e95, e122; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e43 [fact; mlq.ai; original source Sharon AI ; from gnews:9e0d5b0d6b3e603c60340128 2026-07-03] Sharon AI plans to deploy up to 40,000 NVIDIA Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs under a six-year agreement with NVIDIA.\\n    Quote: Sharon AI, which listed on the Nasdaq in February 2026 via a $125 million IPO, is deploying up to 40,000 Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs under a six-year agreement with Nvidia [2] [6] .\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e28, e74; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e58 [third_party_view; CNBC, reporting SemiAnalysis’s projection; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis projected Nvidia data-center compute revenue in the second half of FY2027 to be 20% above Wall Street consensus.\\n    Quote: SemiAnalysis also projects Nvidia's data-center compute revenue will run 20% above Wall Street consensus in the second half of fiscal 2027.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e142; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e67 [third_party_view; SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis 2026-07-06; from gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis says market estimates for Nvidia shipment volumes and revenue in the second half of 2026 are materially below its supply-chain-tracking estimates.\\n    Quote: Nvidia revenue is skyrocketing, and even 3 years into the build out, the general market is still materially lower on shipment volumes and revenue estimates for Nvidia in the 2nd half of this year versus our through supply chain tracking in the Accelerator Model .\", \"- e69 [third_party_view; SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis 2026-07-06; from gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis says data-center supply improved by early 2026, chip production became the limiting constraint, and financing was a significant obstacle to expanding compute by mid-2026.\\n    Quote: In 2025, we wrote extensively about how datacenter capacity was the bottleneck for AI compute growth. By early 2026, the datacenter supply situation improved considerably, but it became clear that chip production was now the limiting constraint. Now – mid-way through the year – it is clear that financing will now be one of the most significant obstacles to ramping large scale compute broadly avail\", \"- e74 [fact; SemiAnalysis; original source SharonAI ; from gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6 2026-07-06] SharonAI’s June 2026 Australia AI-factory deal includes a six-year backstop for up to 40,000 GB300 GPUs valued at $4.88 billion; SharonAI plans a 132 MW footprint, 102 MW contracted, and more than 55,000 Nvidia GPUs by mid-2027.\\n    Quote: The first is SharonAI’s 72MW AI factory in Australia. Announced in June 2026, the deal has SharonAI scaling up to as many as 40,000 GB300s under a six-year backstop. Sharon disclosed a total backstop value of $4.88B, which works out to an implied floor of about $2.33/hr/GPU on average over the six year period. Sharon AI’s footprint is now set to grow to 132MW with 102MW contracted, and the company\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e43; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e92 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:71df54965281684cc500960f 2026-07-06] Wall Street analysts expect Nvidia revenue growth of 82% for the rest of 2026 and 41% in 2027.\\n    Quote: For the rest of this year, they expect 82% growth. For 2027, that figure rises to 41%.\", \"- e93 [fact; fool.com; original source Nvidia and Palantir Technologies ; from gnews:0e3cbf453958ce83fabf7a65 2026-07-06] Nvidia and Palantir announced a collaboration to bring open AI models into classified environments.\\n    Quote: Nvidia ( NVDA +2.48% ) and Palantir Technologies ( PLTR +1.34% ) announced a collaboration designed to bring powerful open AI models into highly sensitive, classified environments.\", \"- e94 [fact; tradingview.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] NVIDIA's Data Center segment generated $75.25 billion in revenue in FY2027 Q1, 92% of total sales, up 92% year over year and 21% sequentially.\\n    Quote: During the first quarter of fiscal 2027, the Data Center segment generated $75.25 billion in revenues, accounting for 92% of total sales. Revenues from the segment surged 92% year over year and grew 21% sequentially, driven by the rapid ramp-up of Blackwell 300 systems and robust networking demand.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e98, e115; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e95 [fact; tradingview.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reported FY2027 Q1 revenue of $81.62 billion, up 85% year over year, and non-GAAP EPS of $1.87, up 140%.\\n    Quote: First-quarter fiscal 2027 revenues climbed 85% year over year to $81.62 billion, while non-GAAP earnings per share jumped 140% to $1.87.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e34; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e96 [party_statement; tradingview.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] NVIDIA guided FY2027 Q2 revenue to approximately $91 billion, nearly 95% above the year-earlier quarter.\\n    Quote: For the second quarter of fiscal 2027, NVIDIA projects revenues of approximately $91 billion, representing nearly 95% year-over-year growth.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e117; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e97 [rumour; Danielle Liverance; original source Danielle Liverance 2026-07-06; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] The author reported that NVIDIA’s upcoming Vera Rubin server systems were reportedly delayed; no timing or scale was specified.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA shares are under pressure on reports of delays across their upcoming lineup of Vera Rubin server systems.\", \"- e98 [fact; Danielle Liverance; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] NVIDIA revenue was $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year; data-center revenue was $75.2 billion, up 92%.\\n    Quote: Revenue rose 85% year over year to $81.6 billion, with data center up 92% to $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e94, e114; the argument counts one claim, on