ture capital expenditures could reach $765 billion in 2026 and grow to $1.6 trillion by 2031, with cumulative spending of about $7.6 trillion from 2026 through 2031.\", \"- e126 [fact; DCD; original source Bleeding Edge ; from gnews:c2924b0380602940d68de7ff 2026-07-06] Bleeding Edge launched its Querétaro AI Factory and neocloud offering using Nvidia Blackwell B300 systems.\\n    Quote: Bleeding Edge has launched an AI Factory in Querétaro, Mexico, bringing online its neocloud offering.\", \"- e127 [party_statement; DCD; original source Bleeding Edge ; from gnews:c2924b0380602940d68de7ff 2026-07-06] Bleeding Edge said AI companies had contracted the entire initial capacity of its neocloud platform.\\n    Quote: According to Bleeding Edge, the platform’s entire initial capacity has already been contracted by companies dedicated to developing AI solutions.\", \"- e128 [party_statement; DCD; original source Bleeding Edge ; from gnews:c2924b0380602940d68de7ff 2026-07-06] Bleeding Edge plans to expand neocloud and AI Factory capacity in the coming months, adding Nvidia systems and deploying infrastructure in other markets.\\n    Quote: Bleeding Edge plans to expand both the capacity of its neocloud and its AI Factories in the coming months by incorporating new Nvidia systems and deploying infrastructure in other strategic markets.\", \"- e130 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia scrapped its planned NVL72x2 design, which would have placed two Oberon racks back to back, after cloud providers and large data center operators objected to its form factor and operational overhead.\\n    Quote: A planned alternative design called NVL72x2, which would have placed two Oberon racks back to back, has been scrapped entirely. Cloud providers and large data center operators pushed back against the unusual form factor and the high operational overhead.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e65; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e131 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia canceled the four-die Rubin Ultra version, leaving only the two-die version, which it said delivers roughly half the real-world compute performance.\\n    Quote: The more powerful version of the upcoming Rubin Ultra chip with four compute dies has also been canceled. Only the smaller two-die version remains, delivering roughly half the real-world compute performance.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e89, e135; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e132 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia’s CPO-NVSwitch interconnect technology will not arrive until the Feynman generation, two generations from the current one.\\n    Quote: A key interconnect technology called CPO-NVSwitch, which links many chips into a single large system, won't arrive until the generation after next, called Feynman.\", \"- e133 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia plans to offset the product shortfall by selling more Oberon-Rubin racks in the existing form factor.\\n    Quote: Nvidia plans to make up for the shortfall by selling more Oberon-Rubin racks in the existing form factor.\", \"- e135 [rumour; Investing.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:d5c48abb470f394f86549b6b 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis claimed that NVIDIA had scrapped a four-die configuration for the upcoming Rubin Ultra platform and would use a downsized version instead.\\n    Quote: Additionally, the report pointed to a downsized version of the upcoming Rubin Ultra platform, claiming a crucial four-die configuration had been scrapped.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e131; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e136 [third_party_view; Investing.com, citing analysts quoted by Bloomberg; original source Analysts cited by Bloomberg ; from gnews:d5c48abb470f394f86549b6b 2026-07-06] Analysts cited by Bloomberg said the rumored technical setbacks could severely limit the scale-up capacity of NVIDIA's future hardware.\\n    Quote: According to analysts cited by Bloomberg, these rumored technical setbacks could severely cap the scale-up capacity of Nvidia's future hardware.\", \"- e137 [third_party_view; Investing.com, citing analysts quoted by Bloomberg; original source Analysts cited by Bloomberg ; from gnews:d5c48abb470f394f86549b6b 2026-07-06] Analysts cited by Bloomberg said perceived weaknesses in NVIDIA's future hardware could give AMD's MI500X and Broadcom-backed custom TPUs a wider competitive opportunity.\\n    Quote: This perceived vulnerability may create a wider competitive window for alternative AI platforms, specifically AMD's MI500X and Broadcom-backed custom TPUs.\", \"- e138 [party_statement; Investing.com, reporting Mizuho analyst Jordan Klein's note; original source Hon Hai Precision Industry management 2026-07-03; from gnews:d5c48abb470f394f86549b6b 2026-07-06] Hon Hai management forecast continued acceleration in AI demand; Mizuho analyst Jordan Klein said this was a positive sign ahead of NVIDIA's Vera Rubin rack launch.\\n    Quote: Klein noted that Hon Hai management forecasted a continued acceleration in AI demand, which the analyst said was \\\"a very good sign into the NVDA launch of their new Vera Rubin rack.\\\"\", \"- e142 [third_party_view; tikr.com (analyst); original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:d4c5dc540392f8df39aee250 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis expects Nvidia data-center compute revenue in the second half of FY2027 to be 20% above Wall Street’s current expectations.\\n    Quote: SemiAnalysis actually expects Nvidia’s data-center compute revenue in the second half of fiscal 2027 to come in 20% above Wall Street’s current expectations.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e58; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e150 [third_party_view; Business Times, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence’s survey; original source Bloomberg Intelligence survey respondents 2026-07-07; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] Chinese executives surveyed by Bloomberg Intelligence said domestic products would receive 46% of their AI-accelerator budgets over the next 12 months, up from 30% currently.\\n    Quote: Executives in the country say they will allocate 46 per cent of their budget for AI accelerators to domestic products over the next 12 months.\", \"- e151 [third_party_view; Business Times, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence’s survey; original source Bloomberg Intelligence survey respondents 2026-07-07; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] 80% of surveyed Chinese executives said their total infrastructure spending was running over budget in 2026, mostly because of AI-project costs.\\n    Quote: In addition, 80 per cent of executives said their total infrastructure spending is running over-budget this year, mostly because of the high cost of AI-related projects.\", \"- e152 [third_party_view; Business Times, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence’s survey; original source Bloomberg Intelligence survey respondents 2026-07-07; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] A large pool of surveyed Chinese executives was evaluating AI accelerators from Hygon Information Technology and Cambricon Technologies.\\n    Quote: AI accelerators produced by Hygon Information Technology and Cambricon Technologies were also being evaluated by a large pool of respondents to the survey.\", \"- e153 [third_party_view; Business Times, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence’s survey; original source Bloomberg Intelligence survey respondents 2026-07-07; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] Bloomberg Intelligence survey respondents expected Nvidia’s market share in China to shrink as H20 chips became harder to find and local suppliers took over.\\n    Quote: While Nvidia’s products remain popular, the Santa Clara-based firm’s market share is expected to shrink as its H20 chips, which Beijing has urged its tech firms not to use , become harder to find and local firms take over, according to the survey.\", \"- e154 [fact; Business Times; original source China ; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] China is allocating about 2 trillion yuan (US$294 billion) over five years to build data centres and expand AI use across sectors.\\n    Quote: China is allocating roughly two trillion yuan (US$294 billion) to build data centres across the country in the next five years, a government-led initiative to expand the use of AI in sectors from healthcare to city management.\", \"- e155 [third_party_view; Business Times, citing Bloomberg News; original source Bloomberg News ; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] Bloomberg News reported that domestic companies would supply at least 80% of core technologies, including chips, for China’s data-centre initiative.\\n    Quote: At least 80 per cent of core technologies, such as chips, will be supplied by domestic companies, Bloomberg News reported.\", \"- e156 [third_party_view; Business Times, reporting the survey report; original source Bloomberg Intelligence survey report ; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] The report said a global memory-chip shortage was likely to cap growth at Chinese AI firms such as SMIC, with high-bandwidth memory supply becoming the bottleneck.\\n    Quote: But a global memory chip shortage is likely to cap the growth of Chinese AI firms like Semiconductor Manufacturing International Corporation, with ChangXin Memory Technologies poised to reap the benefits.\", \"- e37 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source Palan