:f8191f5bb960d79e47c73d6c 2026-07-07] The author forecasts that Nvidia will report another blowout quarter in late August 2026, citing no shift in its core clients' actual spending habits.\\n    Quote: Even if it doesn't, Nvidia reports earnings in late August and will likely report another blowout quarter, as there hasn't been any shift in actual spending habits from Nvidia's core clients yet.\", \"- e165 [fact; CNBC; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:784c556d2e58ed09dd8aa7fc 2026-07-07] NVIDIA reported automotive revenue grew 39% year over year in FY2026, driven by adoption of its self-driving platforms.\\n    Quote: In its latest annual filing, Nvidia reported automotive revenue for fiscal year 2026 was up 39% from a year prior, driven by the adoption of its self-driving platforms.\", \"- e166 [party_statement; fool.com (Keithen Drury); original source Micron Technology ; from gnews:d0f3f83296df884fae64921e 2026-07-07] Micron said tight memory-market conditions could last until 2028.\\n    Quote: Micron recently announced another jaw-dropping quarter with huge growth and incredible expectations for the following quarter, dropping huge news that tight market conditions could last until 2028.\", \"- e167 [third_party_view; fool.com (Keithen Drury); original source fool.com (Keithen Drury) 2026-07-07; from gnews:d0f3f83296df884fae64921e 2026-07-07] The author says new capacity across the memory-chip industry will not be online until 2027 or later, leaving inventory supply low for at least the next year and a half.\\n    Quote: As mentioned, new capacity for many in this industry won't be online until 2027 or later, creating a low supply of inventory for at least the next year and a half.\", \"- e169 [third_party_view; fool.com (Keithen Drury); original source fool.com (Keithen Drury) 2026-07-07; from gnews:d0f3f83296df884fae64921e 2026-07-07] The author estimates Nvidia will generate about $100 billion in revenue next quarter, based on Micron's expected $50 billion being about half that amount.\\n    Quote: Next quarter, it expects $50 billion in revenue, or about half of what Nvidia is expected to generate.\", \"- e173 [fact; 24/7 Wall St.; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] NVIDIA Data Center revenue was $75.246 billion in Q1 FY2027, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue reached $75.246 billion (+92% YoY) in Q1 FY27\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e115; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e175 [fact; 24/7 Wall St.; original source Broadcom ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] Broadcom AI semiconductor revenue was $10.8 billion in Q2, up 143% year over year, and the company guided to $16.0 billion for Q3.\\n    Quote: Q2 AI semiconductor revenue was $10.8 billion, +143% YoY, with Q3 guided to $16.0 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e100; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e176 [party_statement; 24/7 Wall St.; original source Google ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] Google Cloud revenue rose 63%, its backlog nearly doubled to more than $460 billion, and Google guided 2026 capital expenditures to $190 billion.\\n    Quote: Google Cloud revenue rose 63% with backlog nearly doubling to over $460 billion, and 2026 capex is guided up tp $190 billion.\", \"- e177 [fact; NVIDIA; original source id Software and Bethesda Softworks 2026-07-07; from gnews:2f1cb54b7a3da28d093523b6 2026-07-07] id Software and Bethesda Softworks launched the DOOM: The Dark Ages | Revelations expansion on July 7, 2026, with support for NVIDIA DLSS Multi Frame Generation, Super Resolution, and path tracing with Ray Reconstruction on supported GeForce RTX GPUs.\\n    Quote: DOOM: The Dark Ages | Revelations launches today with native support for DLSS Multi Frame Generation (up to 6X mode), Super Resolution, and path tracing enhanced with Ray Reconstruction on supported GeForce RTX GPUs, which was used to great effect in the base game .\", \"- e178 [party_statement; NVIDIA; original source Ubisoft 2026-07-07; from gnews:2f1cb54b7a3da28d093523b6 2026-07-07] Ubisoft planned to launch the PC release of Assassin’s Creed Black Flag Resynced on July 9, 2026, with ray tracing and support for NVIDIA DLSS Multi Frame Generation, Frame Generation, and Super Resolution on GeForce RTX GPUs.\\n    Quote: Launching July 9th, the PC release of Assassin’s Creed Black Flag Resynced includes support for ray-traced reflections and ray-traced lighting for realistic reflections, shadows, and water/lighting interactions across the Caribbean, which can be accelerated by DLSS Multi Frame Generation, Frame Generation and Super Resolution on GeForce RTX GPUs.\", \"- e179 [fact; NVIDIA; original source MADFINGER Games 2026-07-07; from gnews:2f1cb54b7a3da28d093523b6 2026-07-07] MADFINGER Games added NVIDIA’s latest DLSS Dynamic Multi Frame Generation and Super Resolution models to Gray Zone Warfare, for use on GeForce RTX GPUs.\\n    Quote: Now, the latest DLSS Dynamic Multi Frame Generation and Super Resolution models have been added to further enhance frame rates and image quality on GeForce RTX GPUs.\", \"- e180 [rumour; mlq.ai, relaying Reuters; original source Three unnamed sources cited by Reuters 2026-07-06; from gnews:9f430c6ce2e8d551fe1f063a 2026-07-07] Reuters, citing three unnamed sources, reported that DeepSeek is developing a custom AI inference chip rather than a training chip.\\n    Quote: DeepSeek, the Hangzhou-based AI startup behind some of China's most advanced large language models, is developing its own custom AI chip, Reuters reported on Monday, citing three people with knowledge of the matter [1] . The chip is designed for inference — the phase where trained models generate responses to user queries — rather than for training new models.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e186; the