 has grown approximately 700 times since 2015.\\\"\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e233; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e225 [third_party_view; Investing.com, reporting Bank of America's note; original source Bank of America 2026-07-08; from gnews:266c882eea8c686ee7aafac7 2026-07-08] NVIDIA sales to hyperscalers rose 115% year-on-year, nearly twice the growth in cloud capital expenditures; the period is not specified.\\n    Quote: Sales to hyperscalers rose 115% year-on-year, nearly twice cloud capex growth.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e231; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e226 [fact; qz.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:ee0d6792b6bf98069cfe0cc6 2026-07-08] Nvidia reported FY2027 first-quarter total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: For its fiscal first quarter of 2027, Nvidia posted $81.6 billion in total revenue — an 85% increase from a year earlier\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e98; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e228 [fact; aibusiness.com; original source Nvidia and Hugging Face 2026-07-06; from gnews:21e9182d07508a6690f10419 2026-07-08] Nvidia and Hugging Face announced a collaboration unveiled July 6, integrating Nvidia’s Isaac GR00T 1.7 models and Isaac Teleop framework into LeRobot, with Cosmos 3 planned for future integration.\\n    Quote: Nvidia and Hugging Face entered into a new collaboration for open source robotics, integrating the chipmaker’s models onto LeRobot, Hugging Face’s open source library for physical AI developers. Under the deal, unveiled on July 6, the companies added Nvidia's Isaac GR00T 1.7 open reasoning vision-language-action (VLA) models for humanoid robotics and the Isaac Teleop framework for robotics data co\", \"- e229 [fact; aibusiness.com; original source Qualcomm and Intel ; from gnews:21e9182d07508a6690f10419 2026-07-08] Qualcomm recently entered robotics with its Dragonwing IQ10 and Intel with its OpenVINO offerings, adding named competitors to Nvidia in robotics.\\n    Quote: In addition, Qualcomm, with its Dragonwing IQ10 and Intel, with its OpenVINO robotics offerings, have recently entered the fold to challenge Nvidia’s position.\", \"- e230 [third_party_view; moomoo.com; original source BofA ; from gnews:1b5a3359dd0644861c0fce42 2026-07-08] BofA estimated HBM content per rack could increase by $0.2 million to $0.3 million from Blackwell to Rubin, while total rack pricing could rise from about $3 million–$4 million to $6 million–$7 million.\\n    Quote: The report estimates HBM content per rack could rise by about $0.2 million to $0.3 million from Blackwell to Rubin, while total rack pricing could increase by $2 million to $3 million, from roughly $3 million to $4 million for Blackwell to $6 million to $7 million for Vera Rubin.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e223; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e231 [third_party_view; moomoo.com; original source BofA ; from gnews:1b5a3359dd0644861c0fce42 2026-07-08] BofA reported that Nvidia’s hyperscaler sales rose 115% year over year, nearly twice the growth in cloud capital expenditures.\\n    Quote: The report also says Nvidia’s hyperscaler sales rose 115% year over year, nearly twice cloud capex growth, suggesting wallet-share gains rather than share loss.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e225; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e232 [third_party_view; moomoo.com; original source BofA ; from gnews:1b5a3359dd0644861c0fce42 2026-07-08] BofA modeled Nvidia holding roughly 65% to 70% or more of AI capital expenditures over time, with the remainder going to ASICs, AMD and other merchant vendors.\\n    Quote: BofA still models Nvidia holding roughly 65% to 70% plus of AI capex over time, with the rest