d3de4aa77ec0d0229 2026-07-08] L&T Vyoma and Fortanix announced a strategic partnership to jointly deliver sovereign AI and security offerings, with Fortanix leveraging NVIDIA Confidential Computing; they plan to develop solutions, co-sell and support customer engagements in India.\\n    Quote: Larsen & Toubro Vyoma (L&T Vyoma), L&T’s next-generation sovereign AI cloud and digital infrastructure business, has entered a strategic partnership with Fortanix Inc, a US-headquartered global leader in data and AI security and a pioneer in Confidential Computing. They will jointly deliver sovereign, secure software-as-a-service offerings for enterprises and government organisations in India.\", \"- e25 [party_statement; fool.com (Justin Pope); original source Jensen Huang, Nvidia CEO ; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] The author reports that Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang expects $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\\n    Quote: CEO Jensen Huang has laid out expectations for $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e35, e253; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e95 [fact; tradingview.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reported FY2027 Q1 revenue of $81.62 billion, up 85% year over year, and non-GAAP EPS of $1.87, up 140%.\\n    Quote: First-quarter fiscal 2027 revenues climbed 85% year over year to $81.62 billion, while non-GAAP earnings per share jumped 140% to $1.87.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e34, e255; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e240 [party_statement; NVIDIA Corporation; original source NVIDIA Corporation 2026-07-09; from nvblog:geforce-now-thursday-toronto-expansion 2026-07-09] NVIDIA said it plans to roll out a new RTX 5080-powered GeForce NOW server in Toronto within days, exp