re outlet.\", \"- e307 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:07cf5835d106467db5448c13 2026-07-12] Nvidia's revenue grew 85% in its past quarter.\\n    Quote: During its past quarter, Nvidia's revenue increased at an 85% clip.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e283; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e308 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:07cf5835d106467db5448c13 2026-07-12] Wall Street analysts expect Nvidia's revenue to grow 96% in Q2.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts expect 96% growth during Q2.\", \"- e311 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Broadcom ; from gnews:f8f440b5020fec9773812b6e 2026-07-12] The author says Broadcom plans to ramp production of custom AI chips for Meta, Anthropic, and OpenAI in late 2026 and into 2027, a competitive development for Nvidia.\\n    Quote: Broadcom is also making custom AI chips for Meta Platforms , Anthropic, and OpenAI, and production for those chips is scheduled to ramp up late this year and into next.\", \"- e312 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source the market ; from gnews:f8f440b5020fec9773812b6e 2026-07-12] The author reports that the market expects Nvidia to retain its growth lead for the full fiscal year, while Broadcom is closing the gap.\\n    Quote: Looking ahead, the market still expects Nvidia to maintain its lead for the full fiscal year, though Broadcom is starting to close the gap.\", \"- e313 [third_party_view; Keithen Drury; original source Keithen Drury 2026-07-12; from gnews:f8f440b5020fec9773812b6e 2026-07-12] The author expects Nvidia to remain the fastest-growing of AMD, Nvidia, and Broadcom for some time.\\n    Quote: AMD is still well behind Nvidia, and while I think Broadcom is still a strong pick, Nvidia will likely retain its rapid-growth title for some time.\", \"- e314 [rumour; tech-insider.org; original source The Information ; from gnews:8faf69f198e10f14aae67621 2026-07-12] The Information reported that Nvidia shelved the RTX 50 Super refresh in December 2025, including a completed-design 24GB RTX 5080 Super, and that the RTX 60-series is pushed back to 2028.\\n    Quote: According to The Information, Nvidia quietly shelved its planned RTX 50 “Super” refresh back in December 2025 — including a 24GB RTX 5080 Super that had reportedly reached completed-design stage — and reporting corroborated through September 2026 confirms the company’s next-generation RTX 60-series remains pushed back to 2028.\", \"- e315 [rumour; tech-insider.org; original source CNBC ; from gnews:8faf69f198e10f14aae67621 2026-07-12] CNBC reported in January 2026 that Samsung, SK Hynix, and Micron had sold out their entire 2026 HBM output under long-term contracts to customers including hyperscalers.\\n    Quote: The root cause sits one layer below Nvidia entirely. Hyperscalers including Microsoft, Google, Meta, and Amazon are buying up high-bandwidth memory as fast as Samsung, SK Hynix, and Micron can produce it, and all three manufacturers have reportedly sold out their entire 2026 HBM output under long-term contracts, according to CNBC’s reporting from January 2026.\", \"- e316 [rumour; tech-insider.org; original source Unnamed supply-chain sources ; from gnews:8faf69f198e10f14aae67621 2026-07-12] Nvidia is reportedly cutting RTX 50-series production by an estimated 15% to 20% through at least Q3 2026.\\n    Quote: Nvidia is reportedly cutting production of existing RTX 50-series cards already on shelves by an estimated 15% to 20% through at least Q3 2026 , which helps explain why street prices on cards like the RTX 5070 Ti and RTX 5080 have stayed stubbornly above MSRP for most of 2026\", \"- e317 [rumour; tech-insider.org; original source Unnamed supply-chain sources ; from gnews:8faf69f198e10f14aae67621 2026-07-12] The RTX 5060 has reportedly been pulled from retail for at least six months.\\n    Quote: The entry-level RTX 5060 has taken the hardest hit, reportedly pulled from retail entirely for at least six months .\", \"- e318 [third_party_view; tech-insider.org; original source PCWorld-cited reporting ; from gnews:8faf69f198e10f14aae67621 2026-07-12] PCWorld-cited reporting estimated Nvidia AI-accelerator profit margins at about 65%, versus roughly 40% for consumer gaming GPUs.\\n    Quote: According to reporting cited by PCWorld, Nvidia’s AI accelerators carry profit margins near 65% , compared with roughly 40% for consumer gaming GPUs.\", \"- e319 [party_statement; tech-insider.org; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:8faf69f198e10f14aae67621 2026-07-12] Nvidia told Tom’s Hardware that it faced memory supply constraints, without confirming the reported 2026 gaming GPU skip.\\n    Quote: Nvidia has still not issued a full on-the-record confirmation of the 2026 gaming GPU gap, and the company continues to sell existing RTX 50-series inventory. Its only public acknowledgment to date remains the statement it gave to Tom’s Hardware confirming memory supply constraints, without confirming the broader skip outright.\", \"- e320 [third_party_view; I/O Fund / io-fund.com; original source Yole Research ; from gnews:2dcfaef1a91c2976a4e347da 2026-07-12] Yole Research estimated that CXL-capable servers will exceed 90% of servers by the end of calendar 2026, up from two-thirds in Q1 2025.\\n    Quote: Yole Research estimated that in Q1 2025, two-thirds of servers were CXL-capable , and projects this figure will rise to more than 90% by the end of 2026.\", \"- e321 [party_statement; I/O Fund / io-fund.com; original source Marvell ; from gnews:2dcfaef1a91c2976a4e347da 2026-07-12] Marvell plans to begin sampling its Structera S CXL 3.0 switch in calendar Q3 2026.\\n    Quote: Marvell expects to begin sampling its Structera S CXL 3.0 switch in calendar Q3 2026.\", \"- e324 [third_party_view; I/O Fund / io-fund.com; original source I/O Fund 2026-07-12; from gnews:2dcfaef1a91c2976a4e347da 2026-07-12] I/O Fund analysts said Nvidia’s modular STX architecture could make CMX a new revenue driver.\\n    Quote: STX is modular, which is key to CMX being a new revenue driver for Nvidia.\", \"- e325 [third_party_view; I/O Fund / io-fund.com; original source I/O Fund 2026-07-12; from gnews:2dcfaef1a91c2976a4e347da 2026-07-12] I/O Fund analysts said Nvidia’s CMX could gain significant traction but was unlikely to be a stock catalyst given Nvidia’s market capitalization.\\n    Quote: Nvidia’s CMX could gain significant traction, but is unlikely to be a stock catalyst at such a high market cap.\", \"- e328 [third_party_view; barchart.com (author); original source Wedbush Securities ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Wedbush Securities said Nvidia’s Vera CPU platform could expand its addressable market beyond graphics processors and create billions of dollars in additional revenue; no period was specified.\\n    Quote: Wedbush Securities recently argued that Nvidia's new Vera CPU platform could expand the company's total addressable market (TAM) well beyond graphics processors, opening the door to billions of dollars in additional revenue.\", \"- e329 [rumour; barchart.com (author); original source Unnamed reports ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Reports suggest Nvidia has begun offering Vera processors to cloud customers, including some in China where regulations allow; no date or amount was specified.\\n    Quote: Reports also suggest Nvidia has begun offering the new processors to cloud customers, including some in China where regulations allow.\", \"- e330 [fact; barchart.com (author); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Nvidia reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: For the first quarter of fiscal 2027, revenue jumped 85% year-over-year (YOY) to $81.6 billion, easily beating analyst expectations.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher re