arter, indicating the scale of Nvidia’s key memory supplier.\\n    Quote: SK Hynix held 58% share globally of the HBM market as of the end of the first quarter, according to Counterpoint Research.\", \"- e338 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia and SK Hynix ; from gnews:03c38d2fe2e6e02ba5736307 2026-07-12] Nvidia and SK Hynix recently signed a multi-year technology partnership under which SK Hynix will supply memory for AI infrastructure, personal AI and robotics.\\n    Quote: The two companies even reinforced their relationship recently, signing a multi-year technology partnership. It involves SK Hynix supplying memory across a broad range of areas, from AI infrastructure to personal AI and robotics .\", \"- e339 [party_statement; Jensen Huang; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:03c38d2fe2e6e02ba5736307 2026-07-12] Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang said SK Hynix has been Nvidia’s largest memory partner and will continue to be its largest memory partner.\\n    Quote: \\\"SK Hynix has been Nvidia's largest memory partner and will continue to be our largest memory partner,\\\" Nvidia chief Jensen Huang said at the time.\", \"- e340 [fact; fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:635f19578778394086009f6f 2026-07-12] NVIDIA reported record total revenue of $81.6 billion in its fiscal quarter ended in late April, up 85% year over year and 20% quarter over quarter.\\n    Quote: In its most recent fiscal quarter (ended in late April), revenue hit a record $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% from the prior quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e293; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e342 [fact; fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source Broadcom ; from gnews:635f19578778394086009f6f 2026-07-12] Broadcom reported AI chip revenue of $10.8 billion last quarter, up 143% year over year.\\n    Quote: Its AI chip revenue jumped 143% year over year last quarter to $10.8 billion\\