ement ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Nvidia guided to approximately $91 billion in Q2 FY2027 revenue, assuming no China data-center sales because of export restrictions.\\n    Quote: Management also issued strong guidance, forecasting approximately $91 billion in Q2 revenue despite assuming no China data-center sales because of export restrictions.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e291, e380, e396; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e340 [fact; fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:635f19578778394086009f6f 2026-07-12] NVIDIA reported record total revenue of $81.6 billion in its fiscal quarter ended in late April, up 85% year over year and 20% quarter over quarter.\\n    Quote: In its most recent fiscal quarter (ended in late April), revenue hit a record $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% from the prior quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e293, e373; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e355 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu, quoted by The Verge; original source Xinzhou Wu, Nvidia head of automotive ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Nvidia automotive head Xinzhou Wu said the company has limited internal GPU compute and reviews its allocation across teams almost weekly, sometimes with CEO Jensen Huang’s help.\\n    Quote: Even Nvidia has a limited supply of GPU for compute. We have an internal priority, and I’m working with my colleagues basically almost on a weekly basis to decide how to set aside the different compute, sometimes for training, sometimes for testing, or resources for a different thread of work in the company. And sometimes we need Jensen [Huang, Nvidia CEO] to help, but yeah.\", \"- e356 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu, quoted by The Verge; original source Xinzhou Wu, Nvidia head of automotive ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said Nvidia’s Hyperion 10 