ng Nvidia GB300-based racks. Under Vera Rubin, rack costs jump to $25 billion.\", \"- e399 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com (Rich Duprey); original source Morgan Stanley ; from gnews:e0e5ab6c2aced8d5a6a688a5 2026-07-13] Morgan Stanley’s forecast, as reported by the author, put the four hyperscalers’ 2027 AI-infrastructure spending above $1 trillion and incremental compute capacity at 19.5 GW; Google was forecast to add 6.8 GW, compared with about 6.7 GW added by the four in 2025.\\n    Quote: The analyst says Google, Amazon, Microsoft, and Meta are forecast to spend over $1 trillion on AI infrastructure next year, adding 19.5 gigawatts (GW) of incremental compute capacity. In 2025, they added roughly 6.7 GW. Google alone will add 6.8 GW, or more than the hyperscalers did combined two years ago.\", \"- e301 [fact; Thomas Richmond, citing NVIDIA’s report; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:9ae96ca750b8e3962c47795f 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.62 billion, up 85.2% year over year.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.62 billion, up 85.2% year over year, with Data Center revenue of $75.25 billion and total supply-related commitments of $119.0 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e226, e418; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e333 [party_statement; barchart.com (author); original source Nvidia management ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Nvidia guided to approximately $91 billion in Q2 FY2027 revenue, assuming no China data-center sales because of export restrictions.\\n    Quote: Management also issued strong guidance, forecasting approximately $91 billion in Q2 revenue despite assuming no China data-center sales because of export restrictions.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e291, e380, e396, e437; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e384 [fact; 247wallst.com, citing NVIDIA’s reported results; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:b68c019528300c6a1fcd3515 2026-07-13] NVIDIA Data Center revenue was $75.246 billion in Q1 FY2027, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue hit $75.246 billion , up 92% YoY.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e341, e433; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e385 [fact; 247wallst.com, citing NVIDIA’s reported results; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:b68c019528300c6a1fcd3515 2026-07-13] NVIDIA Data Center networking revenue was $14.8 billion in Q1 FY2027, up 199% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data Center networking alone did $14.8 billion, up 199%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e294, e411, e419, e434; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e408 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reported fiscal 2026 Data Center revenue of $193.7 billion.\\n    Quote: For comparison, Nvidia's data center revenue in fiscal 2026 (which ended in January this year) was $193.7 billion.\", \"- e409 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] NVIDIA generated $162.3 billion of fiscal 2026 Data Center revenue from compute chips; the remaining Data Center revenue came from networking components.\\n    Quote: It is worth noting that $162.3 billion of its fiscal 2026 data center revenue came from sales of compute chips, while the rest was from networking components.\", \"- e410 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reported fiscal 2026 networking revenue of $31.4 billion, up 142% year over year.\\n    Quote: The company reported a 142% year-over-year increase in networking revenue in fiscal 2026 to $31.4 billion.\", \"- e411 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] NVIDIA's networking revenue tripled year over year to $14.8 billion in the opening quarter of fiscal 2027.\\n    Quote: networking revenue tripling year-over-year to $14.8 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e385; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e419 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:1e1fa5a194198eaf05d90c9e 2026-07-14] NVIDIA’s Data Center Networking revenue was $14.8 billion in Q1 FY2027, up 199% year over year.\\n    Quote: with Data Center Networking alone growing 199% YoY to $14.8 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e385, e428; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e421 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Third-party estimates ; from gnews:37d2648cf990f4943cad6208 2026-07-14] Third-party estimates put Nvidia's share of the AI chip market at 80%; the period is not specified.\\n    Quote: The good news is that Nvidia still controls an impressive 80% of the AI chip market, according to third-party estimates.\", \"- e422 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-07-14; from gnews:37d2648cf990f4943cad6208 2026-07-14] The author says the shift toward inference and competing chip technologies are weighing on Nvidia's stock performance; the period is 2026.\\n    Quote: The shift from AI training to inference and the emergence of competing chip technologies explain why Nvidia stock has risen just 8% this year despite sustaining impressive growth levels.\", \"- e423 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-07-14; from gnews:37d2648cf990f4943cad6208 2026-07-14] The author says inference requires less computing power than training, a shift that could reduce demand for Nvidia's data center products; no period is specified.\\n    Quote: As a result, the inference phase doesn't require as much computing power as the training phase.\", \"- e424 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-07-14; from gnews:37d2648cf990f4943cad6208 2026-07-14] The author estimates Marvell controls 20% to 25% of the custom AI processor market; the period is not specified.\\n    Quote: Marvell is one of the key players in custom AI processors, controlling 20% to 25% of this market.\", \"- e425 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Marvell Technology ; from gnews:37d2648cf990f4943cad6208 2026-07-14] Marvell says it has more than 50 custom AI chip opportunities across over 10 customers, with potential lifetime revenue of $75 billion; no completion period is specified.\\n    Quote: In all, Marvell notes that it can tap into more than 50 custom AI chip opportunities across over 10 customers in the long run, leading to potential lifetime revenue of $75 billion.\", \"- e428 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ac8a489e54fbb1b85a1c7a2c 2026-07-14] NVIDIA’s Data Center Networking revenue grew 199% year over year in Q1 FY2027.\\n    Quote: with Data Center Networking alone growing 199% on InfiniBand, NVLink, and Spectrum-X pull-through.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e419; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e433 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:184645c8d683d95b684bd6da 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 Data Center revenue of $75.246 billion, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: with Data Center alone contributing $75.246 billion (+92% YoY).\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e384, e439; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e434 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:184645c8d683d95b684bd6da 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 Networking revenue of $14.8 billion, up 199% year over year.\\n    Quote: Networking was the sleeper hit at $14.8 billion (+199% YoY), driven by InfiniBand, Spectrum-X, and NVLink.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e385; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e439 [fact; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:386a294bd395bde25e3f4a11 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 Data Center segment revenue of $75.25 billion, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data Center at $75.25B (+92%).\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e433; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e440 [party_statement; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source Broadcom management ; from gnews:386a294bd395bde25e3f4a11 2026-07-14] Broadcom guided to Q3 revenue of $29.4 billion, up 84% year over year, and stated a goal of exceeding $100 billion in AI sales by 2027.\\n    Quote: Broadcom guided Q3 revenue to $29.4B (+84% YoY), and management’s stated goal is to exceed $100B in AI sales by 2027.\", \"- e441 [fact; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source Broadcom ; from gnews:386a294bd395bde25e3f4a11 2026-07-14] Broadcom reported AI semiconductor revenue of $10.8 billion last quarter, up 143% year over year.\\n    Quote: AI semi revenue grew 143% YoY to $10.8B last quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e342; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e451 [fact; Tom's Hardware, reporting Reuters; original source U.S. government 2026-07-14; from gnews:3221eba2826b001b12b82770 2026-07-14] The U.S. approved ZTE and Maginfra to buy Nvidia H200 chips on July 14, 2026.\\n    Quote: Today, Reuters reports that Chinese telecoms giant ZTE and server firm Maginfra have received U.S. approval to buy Nvidia's last-gen H200 \\\"Hopper\\\" chips.\", \"- e452 [third_party_view; Tom's Hardware; original source Tom's Hardware 2026-07-14; from gnews:3221eba2826b001b12b82770 2026-07-14] U.S. policy allows case-by-case sales of Nvidia Hopper-family chips, but not Blackwell chips, to Chinese firms and imposes a 25% export tariff.\\n    Quote: The current status of the AI chip trade situation is roughly that the U.S. allows Chinese firms to buy AI chips up to and including the Hopper family (meaning no Blackwell chips), with a 25% export tariff, though final decisions are made on a case-by-case basis.\", \"- e453 [party_statement; Tom's Hardware, citing CNBC; original source U.S. trade official 2026-07-14; from gnews:3221eba2826b001b12b82770 2026-07-14] A U.S. trade official said very few shipments had taken place against licenses for H200 chips and equivalents as of July 14, 2026.\\n    Quote: CNBC cites a U.S. trade official who today stated that \\\"very few shipments against licenses for H200s and equivalents have taken place. It’s a very small quantity of chips\\\" during a congressional hearing.\", \"- e458 [fact; mlq.ai; original source FBI ; from gnews:ca7564a0dc63b215f5d49402 2026-07-14] The FBI's RFI specifies a single-node training-server category with one Nvidia HGX B300 eight-GPU assembly and Nvidia BlueField-3 data processing units; the RFI does not commit the FBI to a procurement.\\n    Quote: Category 1 covers single-node training servers built around Intel Xeon 6767P processors with 2-4 TB of RAM, one Nvidia HGX B300 eight-GPU assembly, SSD storage, 25Gb Ethernet, and Nvidia BlueField-3 data processing units for network offload and security [1] .\", \"- e459 [fact; mlq.ai; original source FBI ; from gnews:ca7564a0dc63b215f5d49402 2026-07-14] The FBI's RFI specifies an integrated rack-scale system category requiring one GB300 NVL72 equivalent with high-speed interconnect, Spectrum-X networking and in-rack cooling; the RFI does not commit the FBI to a procurement.\\n    Quote: Category 2 steps up to integrated rack-scale systems, specifying one GB300 NVL72 equivalent — Nvidia's flagship 72-GPU liquid-cooled rack — along with high-speed interconnect fabric, Spectrum-X networking architecture, and in-rack cooling [1] .\", \"- e460 [fact; mlq.ai; original source FBI ; from gnews:ca7564a0dc63b215f5d49402 2026-07-14] The FBI's RFI specifies an AI pod category with performance matching five GB300 NVL72 systems, while allowing Google TPU v8 or v7L or better; the RFI does not commit the FBI to a procurement.\\n    Quote: Category 3 is the most ambitious: an AI pod architecture equivalent to Google TPU v8 or v7L, or better, with performance matching five GB300 NVL72 systems.\", \"- e461 [fact; mlq.ai; original source FBI ; from gnews:ca7564a0dc63b215f5d49402 2026-07-14] The FBI's RFI specifies Nvidia L40-S accelerators or equivalent for an inference category, with 48GB of GPU memory; the RFI does not commit the FBI to a procurement.\\n    Quote: Category 4 targets inference workloads specifically, calling for Nvidia L40-S accelerators or equivalent with 48GB of GPU memory and support for FP32, FP16, BF16, and INT8 precision formats [1] .\", \"- e462 [third_party_view; mlq.ai; original source mlq.ai 2026-07-14; from gnews:ca7564a0dc63b215f5d49402 2026-07-14] Federal AI spending obligations reached $7.2 billion in calendar 2026, compared with $675 million in 2024, according to the article.\\n    Quote: Federal AI spending obligations reached $7.2 billion in 2026, up from $675 million in 2024 — a 966% increase.\"]\n{\"control\": 21, \"points_to_rule\": [\"same_question\"], \"ruler_question\": {\"question\": \"Will Nvidia begin shipping its Rubin generation by December 31, 2026?\", \"unit\": \"yes/no\", \"due_day\": \"2026-12-31\", \"rungs\": [{\"label\": \"Yes\", \"condition\": \"Nvidia has begun shipping Rubin by December 31, 2026.\", \"lo\": null, \"hi\": null}, {\"label\": \"No\", \"condition\": \"Nvidia has not begun shipping Rubin by December 31, 2026.\", \"lo\": null, \"hi\": null}]}, \"judged_question\": {\"view_id\": \"v3\", \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA confirm that first shipments of its Vera Rubin AI chip platform to customers have begun by December 31, 2026, through a press release, earnings call, or quarterly filing?\", \"looks_at\": \"First shipments of Vera Rubin to customers, confirmed by NVIDIA.\", \"due_day\": \"2026-12-31\", \"year\": \"2026\", \"kind\": \"asset\"}, \"judged_rungs\": [{\"position\": 1, \"label\": \"Yes\", \"condition\": \"NVIDIA confirms that first shipments of Vera Rubin to customers have begun by December 31, 2026.\", \"lo\": null, \"hi\": null}, {\"position\": 2, \"label\": \"Ruled out\", \"condition\": \"NVIDIA formally announces after July 2, 2026, that it has canceled or abandoned the Vera Rubin platform before any first shipment to a customer. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-02 and stands on 2026-12-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\", \"lo\": null, \"hi\": null}, {\"position\": 3, \"label\": \"Still open\", \"condition\": \"Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2026-12-31.\", \"lo\": null, \"hi\": null}]}\n{\"control\": 26, \"points_to_rule\": [\"same_question\"], \"ruler_question\": {\"question\": \"Will Nvidia begin shipping its Rubin generation by December 31, 2026?\", \"unit\": \"yes/no\", \"due_day\": \"2026-12-31\", \"rungs\": [{\"label\": \"Yes\", \"condition\": \"Nvidia has begun shipping Rubin by December 31, 2026.\", \"lo\": null, \"hi\": null}, {\"label\": \"No\", \"condition\": \"Nvidia has not begun shipping Rubin by December 31, 2026.\", \"lo\": null, \"hi\": null}]}, \"judged_question\": {\"view_id\": \"v2\", \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA make revenue-generating first shipments of its Vera Rubin platform by December 31, 2026, as confirmed by an official NVIDIA shipment announcement or company filing?\", \"looks_at\": \"Whether Vera Rubin begins shipping in 2026, as the item reports it 'could begin shipping later this year'.\", \"due_day\": \"2026-12-31\", \"year\": \"2026\", \"kind\": \"asset\"}, \"judged_rungs\": [{\"position\": 1, \"label\": \"Yes\", \"condition\": \"NVIDIA makes revenue-generating first shipments of its Vera Rubin platform by December 31, 2026, confirmed by an official NVIDIA shipment announcement or company filing.\", \"lo\": null, \"hi\": null}, {\"position\": 2, \"label\": \"Ruled out\", \"condition\": \"After July 2, 2026, NVIDIA formally announces that it has abandoned Vera Rubin or postponed its first shipments until after 2026. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-02 and stands on 2026-12-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\", \"lo\": null, \"hi\": null}, {\"position\": 3, \"label\": \"Still open\", \"condition\": \"Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2026-12-31.\", \"lo\": null, \"hi\": null}]}\n{\"control\": 28, \"points_to_rule\": [\"same_question\"], \"ruler_question\": {\"question\": \"Will NVIDIA begin shipping its Rubin Ultra generation, in Kyber NVL144 racks, by December 31, 2027?\", \"unit\": \"yes/no\", \"due_day\": \"2027-12-31\", \"rungs\": [{\"label\": \"Yes\", \"condition\": \"NVIDIA has begun shipping Rubin Ultra systems by December 31, 2027.\", \"lo\": null, \"hi\": null}, {\"label\": \"No\", \"condition\": \"NVIDIA has not begun shipping Rubin Ultra systems by December 31, 2027.\", \"lo\": null, \"hi\": null}]}, \"judged_question\": {\"view_id\": \"v5\", \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA make first shipments of the Kyber NVL144 rack with Vera Rubin Ultra during calendar 2027, as determined by NVIDIA shipment confirmations, earnings-call disclosures, or independently confirmed customer deployments?\", \"looks_at\": \"Whether the Kyber rack debuts and ships with Vera Rubin Ultra in calendar 2027 (consistent with NVIDIA's 'roadmap is intact') or is delayed to 2028 (SemiAnalysis), and when first shipments actually occur.\", \"due_day\": \"2027-12-31\", \"year\": \"2027\", \"kind\": \"asset\"}, \"judged_rungs\": [{\"position\": 1, \"label\": \"Yes\", \"condition\": \"NVIDIA makes first shipments of the Kyber NVL144 rack with Vera Rubin Ultra by 2027-12-31.\", \"lo\": null, \"hi\": null}, {\"position\": 2, \"label\": \"Ruled out\", \"condition\": \"After 2026-07-05, NVIDIA announces that it has canceled Kyber or formally deferred its first shipments with Vera Rubin Ultra until 2028. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-05 and stands on 2027-12-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\", \"lo\": null, \"hi\": null}, {\"position\": 3, \"label\": \"Still open\", \"condition\": \"Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-12-31.\", \"lo\": null, \"hi\": null}]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; p=json.load(open(\\\"/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/full-eligibility/third-reader-packet.json\\\"));\nfor x in p:\n print(\\\"CONTROL\\\",x[\\\"control\\\"],\\\"POINTS\\\",x[\\\"points_to_rule\\\"]); print(\\\"RULER\\\",x[\\\"ruler_question\\\"][\\\"question\\\"],x[\\\"ruler_question\\\"][\\\"due_day\\\"]); print(\\\"JUDGED\\\",x[\\\"judged_question\\\"][\\\"question\\\"],x[\\\"judged_question\\\"][\\\"due_day\\\"]);\n for pt in x[\\\"points_to_rule\\\"]:\n  if pt.startswith(\\\"item \\\"):\n   print(\\\"ITEM\\\",json.dumps([i for i in x[\\\"reader_b_decisive_items\\\"] if i[\\\"id\\\"]==pt[5:]],ensure_ascii=False))'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
